        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl70' => 'As always, your patronage is greatly appreciated.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl80' => 'As always, your patronage is greatly appreciated.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl40' => 'All identified Fallen Stars have been accounted for and dealt with.

We must remain ever vigilant for new sightings.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl52' => 'All identified Fallen Stars have been accounted for and dealt with.

We must remain ever vigilant for new sightings.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl64' => 'All identified Fallen Stars have been accounted for and dealt with.

We must remain ever vigilant for new sightings.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl70' => 'All identified Fallen Stars have been accounted for and dealt with.

We must remain ever vigilant for new sightings.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl80' => 'All identified Fallen Stars have been accounted for and dealt with.

We must remain ever vigilant for new sightings.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Main' => 'These fallen stars are changing everything on our island. Who knows what other secrets they may hold? We must stay vigilant, and consider the possibility that one day, we too must venture beyond the horizon.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1' => 'I will examine and process the explorers\' reports and get back to you as soon as possible, Mayor.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part10' => 'Every time we need to produce equipment, we shall resupply.

She is a capable vessel, but not perfect... Not yet.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part11' => 'These wonders of medieval engineering can sit on top of a fallen star and drill away with minimal oversight needed.

Amazing, aren\'t they? I designed them myself!',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part12' => 'Good grief! That’s a lot more noise than I expected. And those fumes are concerning.

Maybe some fine tuning, tinkering, and a bit of good old fashion spit and polish is needed.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part13' => 'Finally! Done. Disaster averted, and I have a notebook full of observations for future upgrades and improvements.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part14' => 'You deserve to keep some for yourself, Mayor, as a token of appreciation for all the efforts you’ve made.

We couldn\'t have done any this without your support.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part15' => 'For better or worse, if our calculations are correct, these events are just the beginning.

We should continue our efforts to better understand the nature of the fallen stars, and prevent any harm.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1_A' => 'From reading their resumes... 

I’d say they might even be overqualified for the job!
Some make me look like a rookie.

I couldn’t have picked a better team myself.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1_B' => 'You already have the search reports? So soon? Fantastic!

Hmmm, it’s just as I feared...',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2' => 'I have an idea. A crazy idea. But often the best ideas are the craziest ones.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_A' => 'Great! We should take this to the Provision House to better study it.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_B' => 'Those don\'t look half bad...

It could be worse. We could be handling this material bare-handed.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_C' => 'Careful now. We don\'t know what might be inside of those.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3' => 'This does not bode well, Mayor.

I\'m afraid the foreign objects are having an adverse effect on the environment around them.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3_A' => 'Safely delivered!

Let’s allow our top minds to work their magic.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3_B' => 'The reports are in?

Let’s see...

Oh... I was hoping for better news.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4' => 'Hull parts... checked.
Lift and control surfaces... checked
Propulsion and lift chemical agents... checked.

We have everything we need to start the construction. How exciting!',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_A' => 'Do instruct the workers to wear gloves. Splinters are horrible.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_A2' => 'Great!

I can already picture these fitting together.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_B' => 'Ah, freshly ironed, perfumed and softened.

A shame really, given the fact of how we’re planning to use these.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_B2' => 'Please save those leftover scraps for me!

I\'m not only a world class explorer, but I’m also an amateur scrapbooker in my free time.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_C' => 'Do wear some sort of face mask when handling these.

The odor can be quite overpowering.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_C2' => 'Make sure that gas is properly stored.

Just don’t be too concerned about its volatility. I’ve formulated it to be flame proof.

The unfortunate side effect is that it smells like... well, there are no words to describe it.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part5' => 'These fallen stars have the capacity to change everything we know - but this beauty can give us a chance to set things right.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part6' => 'Love the name. It has a "portending" tone to it.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7' => 'We can now study these dust motes to accurately trace the impact site of larger fallen stars.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7_A' => 'Oh my... These look sharp. 

Much better than the ones we put together at the Provision House last time.

No offense.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7_B' => 'These collected dust motes will now be inspected at the onboard lab.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part8' => 'Fascinating. Just as expected, the dust motes have the same energy signature as the larger fallen star fragments, which should allow us to reliably find them.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part9' => 'Fragments spotted, and course set.

While we’re on our way, we should prepare the tools and contraptions we’ll need to get rid of these nuisances.',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_Granite' => 'You have received additional rewards for completing the Bonus Quest!',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_Salpeter' => 'You have received additional rewards for completing the Bonus Quest!',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_TitaniumOre' => 'You have received additional rewards for completing the Bonus Quest!',
        'TheSiegeQ1' => 'The last of the bandits\' forces are scattered on the island, and will most likely never regroup again. 
Another successful operation, even with the added difficulty of synchronizing with an ally!',
        'TombRaidersQ1' => 'Excellent! 

The altars lie in ruins and the dark, ominous chanting has been replaced with cries for mercy. 

Time to end this madness for good!',
        'TombRaidersQ2' => 'With a great rumble, giant slabs of stone are repositioned to seal the tomb\'s entrance. 

A small bird has already perched itself on the top of a statue, as if reclaiming the land for nature once more. 

Time to return home, victorious once again!',
        'TutAddSector' => 'That went as expected. The remaining sectors will probably be the same. A great battle lies before us. I hope you will face this challenge!',
        'TutAdditionalForester' => 'Very good. These two foresters should be enough to refill your wood deposits. Maybe you\'ve seen that we\'re producing surplus wood. Another sawmill might be useful.',
        'TutAdditionalSawmill' => 'Nice. That doubles our plank production. But now we have negative pinewood production, don\'t we? It is not easy to keep the production chains balanced…',
        'TutAdvanced1001NightsRaid' => 'That was an extremely impressive feat, my lord! Your settlers will be singing about this conquest for generations to come!',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsChain' => 'You have managed to explore and occupy new lands! Your responsibilities doubled, if not tripled! Go my lord, rule your lands!',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsExploration' => 'Berim Khalar\'s forces have been defeated! My islands had been liberated! Thank you for your help!',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsUnlock' => 'My lord! You\'ve done everything I have asked you for! But I need to be honest with you - I\'m really very tired. This exciting adventure we had has made me wish for years of rest. I\'d like you to look after my islands for me, as I simply cannot handle running them myself. I trust you will do your best!',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicine01' => 'You provided the obsidian ore? Good job!',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicine02' => '“Thank you! I can make some great massage oil using this oilseed!”',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicineChain' => 'Well done! Everybody\'s grateful that you provided the materials your practitioner needed, who can now happily continue to treat your settlers.',
        'TutAdvancedArmouredMarksmanTraining' => 'The armoured marksmen are ready for duty! They do look… err… hard to kill?',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsFirst' => 'A bit of training never hurts! Your men stay in shape and now we have more land to cover. Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsSecond' => 'Ahh! Your general returned! The area is bandit free! Now I can have that pie in peace.',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsThird' => 'Good! Maybe now those bandits will learn their lesson and leave us be!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerChain' => 'No walls will be able to hold back our advance! I wish I could see the face of your enemies when they spot your army!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerFoundry' => 'The foundry is ready, and it will be lit by nightfall! Great!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerMortar' => 'How magnificent! I wonder if we should keep one of these as decoration? Put it in the middle of the settlement? No?',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerTraining' => 'I can\'t even begin to imagine how these huge machines are moved! Imagine the enemies\' faces when they see this… ha ha!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerWagonMaker' => 'The man sure knows his profession! I may ask him to build a custom wagon for me, too… strictly for work related tasks, of course.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_CompleteSnowWhite' => 'You\'re a very kind person. Meeting with different cultures, and helping the people with their needs. You earned this blueprint.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_Main' => 'That is all I can tell you about the epic farmyard. I wish you good luck on your travels, and in the hunt for more blueprints.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_UnlockChain' => 'The expansion is complete, and it\'s turned into a nice new well. Just look at how deep it is - and so much water!',
        'TutAdvancedEpicTreasureHuntUse' => 'The explorer is back! He claims Ali Baba was hiding from forty robbers. An oddly specific estimate, if you ask me.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksChain' => 'Being prepared for the worst is not pessimistic! Being careful just makes you, my lord, a better leader! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksExoticWood' => 'This is exactly the amount I need in order to start rebuilding! Thank you, my lord.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksProduce' => 'Thank you my lord, the planks are ready!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodChain' => 'Outstanding results my lord! The storehouse is filled with wood, and now we can plan ahead! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodCutter' => 'How nice these huts are! Woodcutters are truly strong people!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodForester' => 'I see that your foresters have learned how to harvest more seeds from the woodland. Good stuff!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodOptimize' => 'There! The storehouse master took the lamp away and had the men return to their work!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodProduce' => 'Great, the wood\'s been transported to the storehouse.',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonaberti01' => 'Good job on these impressive buildings!',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonaberti02' => 'Oh my, the interiors turned out magnificently! Thank you for your support!',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonabertiChain' => 'The Bonabertis are highly impressed with their quarters. They even sent some of their homeland’s finest obsidian ore as a way of saying thanks. Nice job!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteChain' => 'All the granite in the area has been mined and our warehouse is full! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteDeposit' => 'The mason is ready to start working!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteMason' => 'The scouts have returned, and they\'ve marked the location of the deposits on this map here. Good job!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteOptimize' => 'The miners are happy and the production is back on track! Great!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteProduce' => 'I think that\'s enough granite for now - but you can decide to mine for more if you\'d prefer.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightBattleHorses' => 'So much elegance in these horses. They reminded me of my own beautiful horse, Jasmin… I mean, technically she was a camel but still… Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightChain' => 'We now have a proper cavalry! The horsemen are ready to go into battle! They look most intimidating, if you ask me!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightEliteStable' => 'The horses are equipped with the finest saddles, and are ready to ride! Or to be ridden… or… never mind.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightMountedSwordsman' => 'These mounted swordsmen will be a great addition to your army! Even I\'m scared of them! Well done!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightSaddleMaker' => 'Have you felt the quality of these saddles? I think I want one myself! Make it violet!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightShepard' => 'The shepherd promised me that he will do his best to produce the finest wool! Good man!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightTraining' => 'The knights are ready! Every war needs its heroes.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightWeaver' => 'The man takes the wool and produces cloth! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyChain' => 'You\'ve outdone yourself, my lord! We have all the wood we need! I now understand why your settlers respect you so much!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyGather' => 'Do you smell that? Freshly cut mahogany wood! The best of the best!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyPlanks' => 'They\'re so beautiful, these planks! I think I\'ll have one of your carpenters build me a new bed. My back hurts too, you know.',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganySawmill' => 'The sawmill\'s ready? So soon? That\'s great news! Now we can produce some planks!',
        'TutAdvancedManorBuild' => 'How splendid! This is one of the most beautiful manors I have ever seen in my life! It is also the first.',
        'TutAdvancedManorChain' => 'You are a provider my lord! Your mansions bring a tear to my eye! You should consider tourism, you know? Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedManorPopulation' => 'Look at the people moving into the new settlement! They will have a wonderful life here, I promise!',
        'TutAdvancedMarksmanTraining' => 'Your artisan is currently holding a speech regarding the proper use of ranged weapons. Your marksmen are eager to learn more. Good job!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanArchebuse' => 'This is fantastic craftsmanship! Look at the shape of this weapon. Truly spectacular! Job well done!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanArchebuseMaker' => 'The artisan is ready to make the weapons! He does not speak our language though. Where did you find him, if I may ask?',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanChain' => 'Our ranged company is reporting for duty! Their arrows are sharp and their aim is deadly! Good work, my lord!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanEpicTutentureSearch' => 'The explorer is back, and he found a new adventure for us! Ready your men!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanTraining' => 'Your mounted marksmen are ready! Aiming from a running horse must be a difficult task!',
        'TutAdvancedNewCoatOfPaint' => 'Oh, yes! Now that it\'s been upgraded, the mayor’s house looks stunning. Good job!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorBandits' => 'What an amazing battle that was! Your men are indeed great fighters! I bet you have no opponents in your homelands.',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorChain' => 'Our adventures are not finished yet! We have many lands to explore!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorDeed' => 'Excellent! Remember that you can get additional sector deeds from the black market in the shop. Now let\'s dig up an underground tunnel and take the first of our settlers to it. How exciting!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorExploration' => 'Ahh! Well done! This seems to be the perfect spot to start a new settlement. Look at the beautiful grass, how green it looks, how fresh it smells!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorPrepare' => 'Thank heavens we were prepared to fight those nasty bandits. How did I know they were there, you ask? The hairs on the back of my neck tingle when there\'s danger nearby. My uncle Ben told me it\'s a family trait!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorWarehouse' => 'Magnificent! A beautiful building! Maybe we can upgrade it later. I need my own quarters you know?',
        'TutAdvancedOptions' => 'Fantastic! I promise, I won\'t bother you with the options menu anymore. You\'ve now learned everything there is to know about it. I am most grateful for your undivided attention!',
        'TutAdvancedPlatinumOptimize' => 'Ahh the stories that young woman tells, beautiful. Maybe one day you will also have the time to listen to her stories.',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffChain' => 'Delicious food is the best cure for the hungry soul! Now, if you excuse me, I have a dinner to catch!',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffOwn' => 'One of the baskets landed on my table, and I must be honest with you - I have never eaten anything this tasty! Aunt Irma works miracles!',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffUse' => 'I saw one of your workers lick his fingers clean after eating those delicious cookies! You made them happy!',
        'TutAdvancedReadyArmy' => 'Mighty fine weapons, these. I wonder if our new friends from the eastern lands have ever seen weapon crafting like this? Our blacksmiths are definitely deserving of our praise!',
        'TutAdvancedRecruitArmy' => 'I knew it, my lord! Our scouts have spotted bandit camps ahead! Take our generals through the underground tunnel that connects the storehouses to the new islands, and prepare for the offensive!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterChain' => 'Wild Peter told me that the quality of the gunpowder surpassed his expectations! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterDeposit' => 'The mine is ready, but your miners seemed less than willing to share their techniques with me! Maybe later!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterMine' => 'They have returned and none of them are missi- I mean they\'re all safe and sound! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterOptimize' => 'I\'ve made sure that every saltpetre mine has a huge barrel of water near the entrance from this day on! No fire shall interrupt their work anymore!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterProduce' => 'We have enough saltpetre now! When the time comes, we can make a lot of gunpowder!',
        'TutAdvancedStockMaterials' => 'Great work! With these materials we\'ll be able to at least get started on our constructions in the new land. If we have spares we can always trade them, right?',
        'TutAdvancedStory01' => 'The rescue party returned, and they brought with them an old man. He\'s currently being treated at the hospital. As soon as he\'s able to speak, we\'re going to bring him over to the town hall. Good work saving him - I have a suspicion he\'s a very important person...',
        'TutAdvancedStory02' => 'Now that we have some knights, we can use them to help with the first steps of building that home for Captain Mapparan.',
        'TutAdvancedStory03' => 'Ahh! The platinum swords are so shiny! Ouch! They seem to be very sharp as well!',
        'TutAdvancedStory04' => 'Wagons! Use them well to transport the exotic wood! Ships need a lot of it!',
        'TutAdvancedStory05' => 'The floors may be made of granite, but I hope he has a good pair of slippers - it\'ll be freezing under foot otherwise.',
        'TutAdvancedStory06' => 'My lord! How are we going to safely transport so much gunpowder? Ohh!',
        'TutAdvancedStory07' => 'There is no curse that could break through these quality book fittings! The captain will be pleased!',
        'TutAdvancedStory08' => 'I\'m not sure this is a good idea, but still - I bring good news. The captain no longer needs the coin! His men unearthed some treasure on skull island. Lucky him…',
        'TutAdvancedStory09' => 'I… I think I ate too much. I cannot move. Help!',
        'TutAdvancedStory10' => 'So many adventures, so much experience! Next time Captain Mapparan invites us for some storytelling, we will have our own to tell!',
        'TutAdvancedStory11' => 'We have all the ore we need! It\'s time for me to visit Captain Mapparan and offer him the citizenship. Well done, my lord!',
        'TutAdvancedStoryChain' => 'Captain Mapparan has declared that he will never leave a great leader like you! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanChain' => 'We\'ve used up all the platinum to create more supplies! A good economy can only work if the people who run it know exactly what to do! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanEliteBarracks' => 'It is done! What a spectacular architecture! So elite!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPaltinumSmelter' => 'No, I won\'t go near that smelting plant, I might get burned! But good work nonetheless.',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumOre' => 'We didn\'t build a smelter for nothing! Now we can smelt that ore and begin producing weapons.',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumSwords' => 'First class quality! I expected nothing less!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumWeaponsmith' => 'The smith is ready! Is it just me, or did the weaponsmith give me a funny look? I just wanted to give him some advice... I do have a diploma in weapon crafting, you know...',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanTraining' => 'The swordsmen are ready to serve… I mean mingle. The time will come when they will be needed for combat, I\'m sure.',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingBuild' => 'Done! What a magnificent house…I mean ship!! Let\'s take a look around, and see what quests await our attention!',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingChain' => 'We\'re done! The majestic ship is ready, and now we\'re closer to our goals! If you ever have need for a new quest, visit Captain Mapparan!',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingUse' => 'Ahh! The Captain indeed has a great knowledge of this world we live in! Make sure to visit him as often as possible!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniuimProduce' => 'The titanium ore is ready for you to use! Great!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumChain' => 'I never doubted you for a second, my lord! Titanium may be hard to find, but you collected it in plenty of time! Good work!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumDeposit' => 'The mine looks like a true piece of art! I\'m sure it\'s safe, too, but I don\'t have the time to venture deep.',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumMine' => 'There are quite a few deposits around this area - and now we know where some of them are located. Good job.',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumOptimize' => 'The titanium chunks were restored and work can now continue! Great job!',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperity01' => 'Oh, what a talented merchant you are. We are very impressed!',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperity02' => 'Nothing beats the beauty of your newly produced gold coins. Your treasurer just can’t take his eyes off them. Good job!',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperityChain' => 'Your hard work really paid off; the archipelago is a real display of wealth and prosperity.',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorses01' => 'Those wild horses were a handful, that’s for sure. I\'m so glad we tamed them!',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorses02' => 'Look at our gorgeous battle horses - a true sight to behold!',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorsesChain' => 'You did an amazing job with those wild horses – very well done, my lord!',
        'TutAdventure' => 'That was really a good effort for your first adventure, but don\'t think all adventures will be this easy. They will get increasingly difficult as time goes on. On your maps, you\'ll find an estimation of the difficulty, indicated with skulls.',
        'TutAdventureMaster' => 'You made it. You really made it. You\'ve done everything a person can achieve in one lifetime. Our meeting went fine. We decided to meet once and again and do something. Tomorrow we will go to the firing range. It will be fun!',
        'TutArmies' => 'Great!
Your Army is now ready to do battle.',
        'TutArmiesNew' => 'And so, everything is settled for you to send your troops to battle. Have you spotted any bandit camps already?',
        'TutBakery' => 'Wow, I am really impressed. Finally we can produce bread by ourselves. Since you arrived, everything has improved. Thank you very much.',
        'TutBanditLeader' => 'You general was victorious. The sector is free and can be captured. I hope you know how that works… Just in case you don\'t, start by building a storehouse in the sector.',
        'TutBandits' => 'You have just won your first battle.

You gain Experience for every defeated enemy unit. 

Unlocked:
- New building: Bakery
- New building: Mill
- New building: Bowmaker

- New unit: Bowman',
        'TutBanditsNew' => 'Wow, I wouldn\'t have credited you with so much command potential. My compliments, that worked out really well.',
        'TutBarracks' => 'Good!
Sectors with bandits can\'t be used in any way. Before you are able to expand to these sectors you have to wipe out the bandits.',
        'TutBarracksNew' => 'Well, that\'s a start, but looking around we have still a way to go. First check out the barracks. You\'ll need a lot of them in the future.',
        'TutBattleReport' => 'With it you can see which enemy units can defeat your units, and which is the most effective against the other. You should always refer to it.',
        'TutBeer' => 'Good job!
Brew is required for each military unit so keep a good stock if you want to increase your troops.',
        'TutBigArmy' => 'Now your army is on the right track. In my opinion, an army is never too big. Remember to have a variety of units. Having only recruits or bowmen will not suffice.',
        'TutBigArmy2' => 'Good, now my work here is done. Your military is near perfect - I\'ve taught you everything I know and all nearby enemies have been fought back. With your permission, I will draw back. Contact me if you need my help again.',
        'TutBigArmy3' => 'Are you satisfied with your preparations? Do you have enough units and supplies in stock? As soon as you think you are correctly prepared, just contact me and we\'ll get going.',
        'TutBonusAddFriend' => 'Very good - strong allies will definitely prove useful. Social skills are very important. You should never underestimate that.',
        'TutBonusAdventuresBought' => 'Not a bad offer, is it? You should really take a regular look at what the merchant has to offer. It changes from time to time. By the way, this adventure box contains a random adventure. Mystical…',
        'TutBonusAdventuresOwned' => 'Wow, you have a lot more than me. I suppose I\'ll have to go and search a bit more, so that\'s what I\'m going to do, straight away. Until next time!',
        'TutBonusAdventuresPlayed' => 'And how did you like them? Experiencing adventures is a lot of fun, isn\'t it? And you can discover the coolest things during them. Also, you may occasionally find new adventures that even your explorer can\'t.',
        'TutBonusAuntIrmasGiftBasket' => 'Exactly these ones I meant. As you probably know already, you can allocate the baskets to your production buildings, and these will produce more effectively for a certain time.',
        'TutBonusBattle' => 'Hmm… I wasn\'t expecting that. I have to admit, that wasn\'t bad. But you have not arrived at the Mount Olympus of adventures just yet. There\'s still a long way to go.',
        'TutBonusBattle2' => 'Quite difficult, isn\'t it? But that is how you should always try to do your adventures - consume as little as possible to get the most out of the adventure. Anyway, I have to go before someone spots me.',
        'TutBonusBattle3' => 'Wow, that was really good. As a reward, here\'s a so-called decoration object. It is the latest fashion at the king\'s yard. To be more specific, it\'s a flower bed. You can place it on your island to beautify your city. You\'ll find it in your star menu.',
        'TutBonusBattle4' => 'That was really exciting. I think in the long run it would be too much for my old heart. I prefer to stay in my office and support you from there. Speaking of my office, I\'ll go check whether it is free again.',
        'TutBonusBattle5' => 'Ha! I just said that. I won the bet. That will teach him to stop underestimating you. To thank you, I\'d like to give you something from my reward. Buy yourself something beautiful with it.',
        'TutBonusBattle6' => 'I\'m so very grateful. The help requests were all taken care of, and all the soldiers who requested vacation were able to return home safely too. I couldn\'t have done it without you. Thank you very much.',
        'TutBonusBattle7' => 'So, what do you think about the cannoneers? I think they are fabulous. If you\'re ever forced to fight against buildings, they\'ll be your most effective weapon.',
        'TutBonusBow' => 'Why did I insist on helping him? I made a bet with another former student that the time will come when he would need my help. Back then, he had rich parents and bragged about it, but I knew it was nothing but hot air.',
        'TutBonusBread' => 'Thank you very much. Now my relatives can come. I am convinced they will be enthusiastic about your generosity and spread word of it across the whole land.',
        'TutBonusBuffCoalMines' => 'You see? Always pay attention when you are adjusting your production chains. Unless of course you buff your buildings all the time. But in this case, an additional building of the same kind might be a better alternative.',
        'TutBonusBuffFarm' => 'Now we should have enough wheat to supply them, should they decide to rest here. In case they decide otherwise, we can still use the wheat ourselves.',
        'TutBonusBuffFriend' => 'The king has noted your efforts appreciatively. I congratulate you. You are really doing excellently. Keep it up!',
        'TutBonusBuffGoldmine' => 'Just like that! In doing so you can get way more resources out of the mine. By now, you probably know where to get or produce buffs. The merchant has some more effective ones for sale too.',
        'TutBonusBuffLvl1' => 'I brought him the plate and I was asked to tell you thank you, and that a bright future awaits you, with a huge army, great city and lots of capital. However, that\'s what they always tell you.',
        'TutBonusBuffRealwoodCutter' => 'It\'s much better that way. Don\'t forget to keep an eye on your weapon production, as you need your army when expanding your land. And even if you have enough units, weapons are a fantastic good to trade with.',
        'TutBonusBuffSteelforge' => 'With the additional steel you produce, you can make more steel swords, and with additional steel swords you can train more soldiers.',
        'TutBonusBuffWellFarm' => 'Super! Thank you very much. You will not regret this, believe me. I will begin to help with the harvest immediately.',
        'TutBonusBuffs' => 'That is correct. You can do a lot with this. Don\'t forget that you need resources to create buffs, such as fish in this case. Do you have enough left?',
        'TutBonusBuildingQueue' => 'Do you like it? It is always a good option to have an important building at the end of the construction queue. By the way, temporary building slots can be bought from the bottom of the list, and permanent ones can be acquired at the merchant\'s.',
        'TutBonusCannoneers' => 'I just knew you didn\'t need any help. It\'s a mystery why Lord Sardin always thinks you have to have someone standing by your side for the slightest thing. The man\'s such a worrier.',
        'TutBonusCannonsStock' => 'Thank you for listening to my advice. Now you can train cannoneers. Unfortunately, I have to go on a journey, which is why I won\'t be able to oversee training. I asked the little man… what\'s his name? Oliver? The little fat one. Anyway, I asked him to help you.',
        'TutBonusCoal' => 'That is very kind of you. The king sends you his best wishes and regards.',
        'TutBonusCoalDeposit' => 'Maybe you\'re wonder why you were supposed to search for a coal deposit. Well, Henry told me he is now able to build coal mines, and they are way more effective than the coking plant. This is a good time to try out the new mines.',
        'TutBonusCoalDepositsFound' => 'Don\'t get me wrong. I just wanted to inform you before you run out of coal, and the other production chains that need it also stop producing. I wish you the best of luck for your coin production.',
        'TutBonusCoalmine' => 'I just returned from the barracks. The troops had all painted their faces black. Looked really frightening. I think it\'s camouflage training. Very strange.',
        'TutBonusCoinTrade' => 'So, what do you think? Did you get an impression? With coins, you can do a lot of different things, not just trade but also hire new specialists. For the moment though, it\'s a little early to you build your own means of production.',
        'TutBonusCoinage' => 'Now you are producing coins. Congratulations. I am eager to see how your coin production will go in the future. Try to upgrade these buildings as soon as possible, as it will make coin production more effective.',
        'TutBonusCoins' => 'So, in conclusion, what do you think of your coin production? Are you satisfied? As I said, it takes some time, but when it is upgraded and becomes more effective, it will also become indispensable. If necessary, you can also purchase gold ore at the trader\'s.',
        'TutBonusCopperDeposit' => 'It\'s good that you claimed that sector. It seems to be rich in copper. I\'m already excited about what the other sectors might hold.',
        'TutBonusCopperMine' => 'As you may have noticed, storehouses are not cheap, but having them pays off as they can shorten production times for several buildings at once. If you ever find yourself with a number of buildings whose production times are too long, just place a warehouse nearby.',
        'TutBonusCrossbows' => 'It\'s not easy to produce crossbows on your own, is it? However, they do have a lot of advantages. Not only do crossbowmen have the highest damage output, but crossbows also bring a high price when traded.',
        'TutBonusDekorationBuildings' => 'So I was right, they are just decorative buildings. It seems you can find them from time to time during adventures. By the way, the merchant also has some of these buildings. Some of them can be somewhat complex.',
        'TutBonusEpicDecorationBuilding' => 'Perfect! Now, your island is complete. I think that last touch makes your island one of the most beautiful of all time. By the way, the king thinks so too, and has sent you something as appreciation. Things couldn\'t get any better!',
        'TutBonusExoticWoodStock' => 'I\'ve just returned from my storage inspection, and I have to admit that freshly cut wood smells really fantastic. I also checked the wood for woodworm. Luckily, there isn\'t any.',
        'TutBonusExoticwoodPlanksStock' => 'Oh, that was quick. Thank you very much. I always feel better when I know the most important building materials are in stock. Now I can turn my attention back to the construction plans for the new buildings. Bye for now.',
        'TutBonusFarmUpgraded' => 'The farmers just told me that your materials have arrived and are already being utilized. Since the machines can work better now, and there is more space, they produce a lot more.',
        'TutBonusFarmfield' => 'That\'s really generous of you. With so many wheat fields, we should definitely win the bet.',
        'TutBonusFarms' => 'Thank you for following my advice. I\'m looking forward to the bread production already. Please contact me if you need my help with it.',
        'TutBonusFishProduction' => 'Your fishermen were really hard working. Seems like they are really satisfied under your leadership. Now the first part of your economy is finished, we can go a step further.',
        'TutBonusFollowUpAdventure' => 'Oh, you just returned from a follow-up adventure? So, how was it? Of course, you won\'t always find construction plans, but a decent amount of coins is common.',
        'TutBonusGainCoins' => 'You\'ve really managed to gather quite a solid amount of capital. Did you have any difficulties? Sleep on it, it and if you still want coin production, we\'ll start work on it. Meanwhile, you should be able to evaluate it yourself.',
        'TutBonusGenerals' => 'The more generals you have, the more effectively you can transport your troops to adventures, and the faster you can defeat bandits. This is why having multiple generals is always a good idea.',
        'TutBonusGoldDeposit' => 'I don\'t believe it - we really do have gold on this island. That is fantastic! Before we begin to bank it, we should check whether we have multiple deposits and how rich they are. Coin production is quite expensive.',
        'TutBonusGoldbar' => 'Well, the report is finished. I really only have good things to say about you. The pre-production of gold bars is also complete, I see. This means we can commence the last step in your coin production.',
        'TutBonusGoldmine' => 'To keep the mine replenished, you can buy refills from the merchant. If you are unable to keep the mine going, just destroy it shortly before it collapses. That way, the craftsmen can recuperate some of the construction resources.',
        'TutBonusGoldore' => 'That should suffice. I never thought production would take that long, but gold ore is always very deep in the mountain. That explains why settlers take so long to extract it.',
        'TutBonusGoldsmelter' => 'Now we have nearly everything we need for coin production. Pretty intensive, don\'t you think? I told you. However, coins are one of the most valuable resources you can have, so it does pay off.',
        'TutBonusGraniteStock' => 'Wow, that much granite in one place is definitely rare, I have to say. I mean, I don\'t know much about this sort of thing, but just by looking you can see how valuable granite is. Take good care of your granite.',
        'TutBonusGraniteThroughAdventures' => 'It is really a lot of work gathering granite, but it\'s essential so don\'t pay it any further thought. Just one thing - I\'m pretty sure you can also obtain granite through trade. Furthermore, one of our explorers told me that he once found a small amount of granite during his journey, but really not very much.',
        'TutBonusHugeCapital' => 'You really taught the other king something. He\'ll never criticize the trade network again. Even I was surprised how much gold you can earn through it. You\'ve done really well.',
        'TutBonusHugeCapital2' => 'Just as I said it would be. The king had to let someone read out a plea of guilt, taking back everything he had said. It was a complete success. To show his gratitude for your help, the king has sent you a big present.',
        'TutBonusIronDeposit' => 'Thank you for your help, but please hurry. We don\'t have much time. Maybe the child is trapped and cannot breath.',
        'TutBonusIronOre' => 'Thank goodness, we found the child. That was close. I will go immediately and tell everybody to stay away from the mines.',
        'TutBonusMarbleDeposit' => 'Of course that also applies to stone deposits. You should always have multiple deposits on your island.',
        'TutBonusMarbleStock' => 'That was a really exciting competition. Thank you very much for your help. Although this competition is held only once every ten years, I would be very happy for you to take part again next time too. If you need to find me, I\'ll be back at my work.',
        'TutBonusMoreAdventures' => 'Ha! I was really in front of you by a nose. However, I didn\'t win either. Little matter - we both qualified for the next round, which means you\'ll have a chance to get your revenge.',
        'TutBonusMoreMasons' => 'Pretty useful features, am I right? Keeping the quests in sight is particularly handy. But I have kept you from your business long enough. Don\'t let me delay you any further.',
        'TutBonusMoreMines' => 'So, what do you think? Did it pay off? Of course you have to consider that prices always differ for many different reasons, for example depending on the time of day. So, even if prices are not good one day, they can change completely the next.',
        'TutBonusMoreWood' => 'Hmm… I just told him we would help him, and straight away he asked for more bows. He\'s always been like that - you give him your pinky and he takes off the whole hand.',
        'TutBonusMultiplayerAdventure' => 'I\'m really impressed. Not only were you better than me, you also won the whole competition. There\'s no shame in losing to the best. My congratulations. I\'m looking forward to competing against you again next time.',
        'TutBonusOptimizeCoalChain' => 'So, how is coal production doing? Everything fine? That\'s comforting. In which case, I will report back to my craftspeople. They will be relieved too, I hope. Thank you very much.',
        'TutBonusPlanks' => 'You are developing quickly. This should be enough for wood production to get started. Let\'s get on with the next resource.',
        'TutBonusPlayAdventures' => 'Very good! Then we know where to get our granite from. I assume the amount of granite will differ a lot from adventure to adventure, but at least we know where to get it from generally.',
        'TutBonusPopulation1' => 'Works fine, right? By the way, you can hire different numbers of settlers for bread. You can even store them in your star menu, meaning that you can produce them ahead of time.',
        'TutBonusProductionTime' => 'That\'s how it works! When you have a little deficit in your economic overview you don\'t necessarily have to build a new building. Sometimes simply upgrading or repositioning a building, like just now, is sufficient.',
        'TutBonusPurchaseGeologist' => 'See? It\'s dead easy. You can do this with all specialist tasks. It will pay off, especially for the treasure search, but we will come to that later. For now, let\'s continue with our plan.',
        'TutBonusRaiseStockBread' => 'Not bad is it? Now, you just have to use the buff on the mayor\'s house, and you\'ll have 75 extra settlers immediately. If you need to bump up your numbers quickly, you can use this method any time to gain settlers.',
        'TutBonusRaiseStockCoal' => 'Very good. Now we will be able to work, and steel production can begin. I will return to my work and make sure production goes smoothly.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodPlanks' => 'Thank you. Now I can continue working without problems. I have a feeling that a lot of new construction orders are about to come in.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodStock' => 'Good. Now the woodworm is probably gone for good. It would have been annoying for it to spread to the exotic wood and be obliged to start the whole process again. I\'ll tell the sawmills they should keep an eye out for these things.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodforester' => 'Good, the construction of the forester was well received. I was concerned whether that would suffice. For the future we should consider something else, because I think this will not be the last time we hear about this initiative.',
        'TutBonusResourceBuff' => 'Very strange… Usually, your brother doesn\'t give things away for free. Let\'s hope he is not up to something bad. Anyway, we should get back to your settlers. There are still important things missing in the basic services.',
        'TutBonusSawmill' => 'Of course, the sawmill isn\'t the only building to have such a window. You should always take a look at the information on each building.',
        'TutBonusSpecialAdventures' => 'Oh no! This time you were in front of me. I assume I wasn\'t paying enough attention. Never mind, once again we both qualified for the next round. This one will decide who is the better explorer.',
        'TutBonusSteel' => 'Well, you seem to have everything under control, even during your adventures. I just wanted to be sure. Very well then, we\'ll soon be able to begin training the soldiers.',
        'TutBonusSteelswords' => 'Cool, thank you. With that I can realise my project. What? Oh, nothing special. I just want to help a village defend itself against constant attacks.',
        'TutBonusStone' => 'Very good. This amount of stone should be sufficient for the upcoming buildings. However, you should always continue producing stone.',
        'TutBonusStoneDeposit' => 'Of course this is true for every deposit, not just stone. Always remember that deposits become depleted after a certain time, so it\'s good to have another one as a replacement.',
        'TutBonusTavern' => 'Wow, did you see how fast that was? Amazing! And I heard it works with all buildings. Furthermore, it also functions for building upgrades - you just have to click on the specific building. Just keep an eye on the prices, as they can differ.',
        'TutBonusToolStock' => 'So, was the production chain still balanced? Don\'t forget the resources not included in the economic overview, such as building costs or upgrade costs. You should always try to produce a bit more than you need of everything.',
        'TutBonusTools' => 'I see you have everything under control. I just wanted to be sure, but it looks like I worry too much.',
        'TutBonusTradeStone' => 'Wow, that functions quite well. I am really amazed. So now everything is possible for you. By the way, the mayor sends you his thanks. You really helped him out.',
        'TutBonusTradeWater' => 'And how did it go? Not bad, right? By the way, they say the merchant sells a watermill which produces water from an inexhaustible water deposit. However, it is not particularly cheap.',
        'TutBonusTradeWeapons' => 'It\'s amazing how fast the consumption of brew and swords has increased. But you should not, of course, neglect your production for trade, because selling extra production is also a good source of income.',
        'TutBonusVisitFriend' => 'And did you like the islands? Of course you should always go your own way, but considering suggestions doesn\'t hurt.',
        'TutBonusWater' => 'I see that water production seems to be quite effective. Don\'t neglect it, or the cavalry training will cease.',
        'TutBonusWell' => 'Ha ha! That made him look really stupid. He didn\'t bargain with that. I thank you very much. Please take some of my gains as a sign of my gratitude.',
        'TutBonusWell2' => 'The construction of the wells you ordered is completed. It\'s nice that you always take my advice seriously. I appreciate it.',
        'TutBonusWheat' => 'So, the advice from the farmer was good after all. With this production we are well prepared for the horse breeding that will soon be upon us.',
        'TutBonusWood' => 'Having a little stock is never a bad thing. Don\'t forget to check your storehouses regularly to see if anything is missing.',
        'TutBowmaker' => 'Well, the bows are a bit small but they will suffice for the start of our bowmen training.',
        'TutBowman' => 'Perfect!

In an army, bowmen are only attacked once all melee or cavalry units have been defeated.

Additionally bowmen deal high damage to enemy armies.',
        'TutBowmanNew' => 'So, you\'ve created the basis of your weapon production. Just remember that bow production consumes additional pinewood. You know what that means, don\'t you?',
        'TutBranchOffice' => 'Oh, what a beautiful building. Isn\'t it noble? That is your ticket to becoming a mighty, influential merchant. I am excited to see how you will use this.',
        'TutBread' => 'Fantastic! You bakery is ready to produce fresh bread...',
        'TutBrewery' => 'Excellent. It\'s nearly impossible to convince a recruit to fight for you without brew. But of course, brew alone is not enough to recruit units - we need more… correct! - weapons!',
        'TutBronzeDeposit' => 'Your geologist has found a copper deposit.',
        'TutBronzeDepositNew' => 'The rumours really were true, luckily! You will be needing copper for further city development. We should make the most of it!',
        'TutBronzeMine' => 'Perfect!
Now your workers can start mining for copper ore',
        'TutBronzeMineNew' => 'Well, I\'ve settled everything. All deposits you find on this island are your property now. You\'ve also been busy, I see, so let\'s get on with it.',
        'TutBronzeSmelter' => 'Bronze bars are very important. If we have to deal with bandits, we can process them into weapons. But first, we need to use them for something else: tools.',
        'TutBronzeSword' => 'Perfect!
A bronze sword is the most basic weapon, but it is still sharp enough to teach the bandits some respect!',
        'TutBronzeSwordNew' => 'Good, production is working fine. That\'s a relief. Recruits are the cheapest unit, which is why you should take them into every battle.',
        'TutBronzeWeaponChainOptimize' => 'Good - that should suffice to help your brother out. I\'d like to know who this ominous attacker is. Perhaps we will know soon enough.',
        'TutBronzeWeaponsmith' => 'Well, it\'s about time! As soon as we have enough brew and weapons we can begin training.',
        'TutBuildingLicenze' => 'Good! Celebrate your victory. For personal reasons I have to go on a journey for some time. When I return, I will help you to increase the size of your military.',
        'TutButcher' => 'That really looks tasty. Our settlers will be very happy with their new rations. If we also supply the explorers with sausages, they might be able to search more effectively.',
        'TutBuyGoodsViaTrade' => 'Uh, thank you. Finally I can get my own back on him! What? No, I don\'t mean you. As a reward, I can give you some map fragments which I found during my travels.',
        'TutCannonforge' => 'So, did I promise too much? Even Lord Sardin complimented me, and that surely means something. I think I\'ve helped you as much as I can. I will now return to my work. Do not hesitate to ask for my help if you are ever in need of it.',
        'TutCapital' => 'You\'ve mastered that really well, but I have to admit I expected nothing less. By the way, have you seen Lord Sardin lately? Since the incident with his daughter he has kind of disappeared.',
        'TutCarpenter' => 'We are finished. Definitely one of our best constructions. Do you like it? By the way, I\'ve heard rumours about the carriages being able to carry cannons. I\'ll check whether I can find plans for that.',
        'TutCavalry' => 'You should remember that cavalry always attacks first, targeting the weakest enemy unit first. This will be very useful in your upcoming battles.',
        'TutCavalryFight' => 'Not that I couldn\'t do it on my own… but thank you. With that, he has already lost the second bet, the blockhead. He will never learn his lesson.',
        'TutClaimAnotherSector' => 'You were really good. Lord Sardin seems to have prepared you very well. I am truly impressed.',
        'TutCoin' => 'You managed to complete the main campaign for this milestone.

We hope you had fun ;-)',
        'TutCokingPlant' => 'Very well!
Coal is used in many production processes so make sure you\'ve always got plenty of coal.',
        'TutCokingPlantNew' => 'There\'s the coking plant. You\'ll need coal for many different things, which is why you should always keep an eye on your production.',
        'TutCollectionAdvItem' => 'You\'re quite the explorer!',
        'TutCollectionComplete' => 'At long last! It is completed!',
        'TutCollectionGather' => 'How fortuitous!',
        'TutCollectionTab' => 'You\'ve found it! Amazing!',
        'TutCollectionsChain' => 'Congratulations on your first collection.',
        'TutContentGeneratorCompleteDailyQuest' => 'Aren\'t they beautiful? Shining so bright, with all those colours, and yet so mysterious to the touch.',
        'TutContentGeneratorCompleteQuestBuff' => 'Well, that was exciting! And there\'s so much more to discover, I\'m getting goosebumps just thinking about it.',
        'TutContentGeneratorMain' => 'Finally! Thank you so much for your help! I owe you one. Now, let\'s get to the exciting part, and use those crystals to reveal the truth about the world we\'re living in.',
        'TutContentGeneratorRollShortLetter' => 'Ahhh, I thought this would grab your attention! Some people call it the "Forge of Truth" - a bit of a silly name if you ask me. But there\'s one thing we know for sure - this is the heart of The Excelsior. I designed it to translate, analyze and piece together snippets of text. It usually works like a charm, but there are still some kinks to iron out: like how the primal energy of the crystals it uses for fuel occasionally transform the paper into completely different objects and resources.
Here are some snippets I was able to translate - maybe some of them belong together?',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_EpicForge' => 'The forge looks incredible... And it\'s incredibly useful, too! Not only will we be able to manufacture a lot of our weapons here, but we\'ll also save a lot of space, which we can use for other productions! 

But what should we use that space for? That\'s up to you to decide!',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Expedition' => 'All prepared. The expedition crew is ready to leave. Let\'s head out at once!',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Main' => 'You managed this crisis beautifully. Not only have you averted disaster, but now we also have the most impressive Forge the world has ever seen, right on our island!

I\'m sure all our neighbors will look on in envy!',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_MountainClan' => 'At last, we´re home again. After spending so long in the cold, I can\'t wait to relax with the sun on my skin again, and sip a cool, refreshing Red Flying Settler. And maybe a grilled steak too. But I digress. 

You did a great job, you know. The battles you fought, the weather you endured, and the value of the work you did for the Mountain Clan cannot be expressed by words. 

Congratulations! But we\'re not quite done yet...',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Prediction' => 'Finally, your residents can relax and get a good night´s sleep. You can see the relief in their eyes. 

However, we do still have to find a way to mollify the troublemaker in our backyard. Luckily, I think I might have an idea for that!',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Sector' => 'Splendid! As the path is now clear, we can get a better look at this mountainous menace. We\'d better hurry!',
        'TutCreateBuff' => 'You\'ve just created your first food package.',
        'TutCreateBuffNew' => 'There are a lot of different buffs. They differ in duration and effect, and you cannot produce all of them yourself. While playing, more possibilities will become available, so take a regular look at your provisions house.',
        'TutCrossbowsmith' => 'As I said, you can manage that all by yourself. If you still have any questions, feel free to ask, any time. In the meantime, I\'ll have a talk with my daughter.',
        'TutDetailsTab' => 'But now I shall myself retreat. I wish you lots of luck with the bandits. Hopefully, they will not make too much trouble.',
        'TutEconomyOverview' => 'It\'s fantastic, isn\'t it? Use this overview as you wish. I will try to keep it up to date as best I can. However, we have to do something about your tree deposits. You should always try to keep your resource production in a green area.',
        'TutEliteSoldiers' => 'I have to say that adventures are really exciting. I never thought I\'d say that. And what do you think about our soldiers? Phenomenal, don\'t you think? They can take much and deal out a lot. For big challenges you should always take some of them with you.',
        'TutEpicAdventures' => 'Wow, you really made them pay. You are becoming a veritable bandit\'s nightmare. The only thing left to hope for is that the king will not hear about it. It would be a shame to be forced to give the gold back to him.',
        'TutEpicWorkyards1' => 'Great! You started up the machines!',
        'TutEpicWorkyards2' => 'Wow! Such productivity!',
        'TutEpicWorkyards3' => 'Extraordinary! It really does do so much more!',
        'TutEpicWorkyards4' => 'Excellent! Look at the size of that building!',
        'TutExoticWood' => 'The smell alone is simply sensational. By the way, you can also obtain this wood by trading with other settlers, although the cost is obviously higher.',
        'TutExoticWoodPlanks' => 'I have good news. We\'ve found a way to get rid of the wood worm. Now, we can store the wood safely again.',
        'TutExoticWoodSawmill' => 'Very good, but it was about time. These little monsters feed on everything they can find. Let\'s hurry and begin processing the wood. It\'s still free of woodworm.',
        'TutExploreClaim' => 'Very nice!

You can explore any sector adjacent to one of your owned sectors.',
        'TutExploreClaimNew' => 'The explorer has just returned. He discovered a new sector. Each sector has its own deposits and provides additional building space. So, if you are in need of new deposits or space, don\'t hesitate to search for new sectors.',
        'TutExplorer' => 'Your Explorer is ready for his first mission',
        'TutFarm' => 'The farm is the most important building for successful bread production. Theoretically, all farms can harvest from the same wheat field - but the fields will deplete faster that way.',
        'TutFarmfield' => 'The fields are harvested continuously, and when they are depleted, a new field has to be built. In order to avoid a shortage you can place several fields.',
        'TutFishRefill' => 'Easy, isn\'t it? You can refill all deposits to greater than their original amount. But you can only produce refills for meat and fish by yourself. If you want to refill another deposit, you have to take a look at the merchant.',
        'TutFisher' => 'OK!
Your fish production has started.',
        'TutFisherNew' => 'Your fisherman has already begun his work. A lot of things can be made from the fish caught, but most importantly your settlers can work more effectively using them. I\'ll show you, what I mean.',
        'TutForester' => 'Good!
Keeping your forests healthy is important to secure a constant supply of wood.',
        'TutForesterNew' => 'This forester will refill your wood deposits so you always have enough wood. However, refilling usually takes more time than cutting down. To see whether you need an additional forester, you can take a look at the economy overview.',
        'TutForum' => 'In the archive you can re-read all the help window texts, and if you still have questions, try the forum where a lot of other settlers are willing to help you with their experience.',
        'TutFreeHomezone' => 'That will teach them a lesson. We\'ll see if they dare rob the settlers again. But we should build our forces up so we can strike back if they try again.',
        'TutFreeHomezone2' => 'You are becoming a very good leader, which is why I would like to share another tip with you: If you defeat the leader camp of a sector, the remaining enemies in the same sector become very demoralized and give up. They too are defeated, if you will.',
        'TutFreeHomezone3' => 'Victory! You\'ve defeated them all and freed your island. Your settlers have reacted with jubilation. I have to admit, I am rather proud of myself. I guided you quite well.',
        'TutGarrison' => 'Nice!
These garrisons represent your armies.',
        'TutGarrisonNew' => 'A nice garrison! Each of your generals has his own garrison where you can assign units to him. You can place them on any green field.',
        'TutGeneral' => 'Good!
All specialists you hire in the tavern are found in the star menu.',
        'TutGeneralLost' => 'Did you figure out how it happened? Did you sent too few units with him or did you send your general through an additional agro radius so that he was distracted? Always remember that you have to wait a long time until your general recovers after a defeat.',
        'TutGeneralNew' => 'A beautiful tavern. I just visited it and you really have fabulous taste. However, let\'s now take care of your new general.',
        'TutGeologist' => 'Your geologist has successfully discovered a stone deposit.

Geologists can search for various deposits later on. Be sure to check his abilities often!',
        'TutGeologistNew' => 'That was really fast. Please remember that resources other than stone might take longer to find. But enough chat, let\'s get to work!',
        'TutGraniteTrade' => 'Very well. That should be enough to do something useful with. What? My father? Oh, he\'s just sobbing in a dark corner where nobody can see him. It is always the same. Don\'t worry, he\'ll soon reappear.',
        'TutGreatCapital' => 'Unbelievable! You really made it. I\'ve just received the letter from the king via express messenger, approving your independence. I congratulate you. You are the first person I know who has managed to do this.',
        'TutGuildBank' => 'The bank lets you transfer resources both to and from your guild. Perhaps it\'d be nice to leave them a little gift? Here, why not give it a try with these resources.',
        'TutGuildBankUI' => 'The guild bank gives you a lot of options for sharing and trading resources and items. To see what\'s stored in the bank, click on the building. Because there are so many possibilities, the architects left a manual in the building, which explains how the bank works. You can find the manual by clicking on the question mark.',
        'TutGuildMarketVote' => 'That was a nice trip! I hope you got the information you were looking for. If you have any more questions, or are looking for some more information, you should try the archive. There you\'ll find everything you could ever want to know about the guild market.',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteParticipation' => 'Good Job! Your vote has been submitted, and we\'ll see the final results soon.',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteReset' => 'Your new vote has been submitted. You can withdraw it at any time.',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteResults' => 'Ohh, I didn\'t expect people would vote like that!',
        'TutHarbour_Building' => 'Oh, wow. I knew it would be a masterpiece, but what I\'m seeing surpasses even my wildest dreams. I just knew we were missing something from our shores!',
        'TutHarbour_Emigration' => 'Have you also been struck by gold fever? It seems a huge amount of our settlers are willing to travel out to Tavos. I guess it\'s just in our blood to head out to far-away lands, and start settling in unknown territories...',
        'TutHarbour_Main' => 'Fantastic! Now we\'ve established a new method of travel. Who knows what we\'ll be able to find in the future!',
        'TutHarbour_Population' => 'Alright - this should get things started! But we can\'t stop here - the opportunity is just too good to ignore.',
        'TutHarbour_Reach13' => 'Good work! We\'re one step closer to being able to help the new band of pioneers on their merry way.',
        'TutHorse' => 'Great!
Note that archers can deal high damage to your armies, but they are not very durable. Use your cavalry units to counter enemy archers.',
        'TutHunter' => 'Thank you for finding a hunter. I hope the problems caused by the wild animals will improve soon.',
        'TutIronChainOptimize' => 'You are getting better and better, I have to admit. It\'s probably no longer necessary to treat you with so much care. If you continue like that, you will achieve everything you desire.',
        'TutIronmine' => 'So our information was correct - we have iron deposits. Lucky for us. We will be able to make a lot of beautiful things from them.',
        'TutIronsmelter' => 'Strange… What? Oh nothing. I just received a weird letter from my daughter, but never mind. You know what to do next.',
        'TutIronweaponsmith' => 'This is music to my ears. Solid weapon production is always a good base for a successful kingdom. But enough chatter - now action is needed.',
        'TutLongAdventureSearch' => 'Excuse your explorer when he sometimes comes back without an adventure - this route is quite dangerous and sometimes falling back is the better alternative. I have no further routes I can give you. Have fun!',
        'TutLongTreasureSearch' => 'So, did your explorer find something interesting? I told you it would pay off. Anyway, I must go quickly. Until next time.',
        'TutLongbowmaker' => 'I see you know exactly what I am talking about. These longbows cause a lot more damage. I hope they will suffice to drive our enemies back.',
        'TutLongbowmen' => 'Hi, hi, thank you. I will contact you when it is safe to talk and tell you more about the other islands. You will not regret this.',
        'TutLongbows' => 'Good - with this quantity of longbows we should be able to equip quite a lot of longbowmen. I would suggest we do this next. I\'m going to start looking for that suspicious person again.',
        'TutMainAdventure' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know the basics about adventures, and have had your first experience with them.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainAdventureMaster' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know everything about adventures, including the various types and difficulties.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainBattle' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have your first experience of fighting bandits.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainBattleMaster' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have well balanced weapon production and a huge army.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainBeerProductionChain' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have stable brew production and can concentrate on other tasks.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainBetterProductionBuff' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to produce and use a new buff on your workyards or on your friend\'s workyards.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainEpicWorkyards' => 'Your Epic Workyard is now operating at full speed! 
You should focus on upgrading it for maximum benefits.',
        'TutMainFirstStrikeUnits' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to produce and recruit cavalry.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainFishAndMeat' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know everything about fish and meat.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainFreeHomezone' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You have dealt with the bandits, and they no longer pose a threat.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainLastUnits' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to recruit all kinds of different unit types.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainLuxuryMaterials' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know about special luxury materials, where to get them, and how to process them.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainMoreUnits' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to produce and recruit militia.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainNewBuildingMaterials' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have stable production of new building materials and can concentrate on other tasks.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainNewLands' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know the most important facts about claiming new sectors.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainParanoid' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Your brother is now safe and sound.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainPlankProductionChain' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have stable pinewood plank production and can concentrate on other tasks.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainPopulationCap' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You have continuously increased your population capacity.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainPopulationCapPreparations' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know the issues concerning population, and how to handle them.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainProvisionerBuffs' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to produce and use a simple buff on your workyards or on your friend\'s workyards.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01' => 'The preparations are ready. We can start our expedition.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Generals' => 'With our specialists ready we are well on our way to exploring new lands.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Help' => 'Good thing you checked out the archive!

Remember to come back here, whenever you need help with the colony mode.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Production' => 'Nice work. We\'re ready to start preparing the troops we\'ll need for our future explorations.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Recovery' => 'Great! Now that you\'ve produced some medipacks, we\'ll be able to instantly revive our marshals when they get defeated. I, er, I mean if. If...',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Troops' => 'Our troops are ready to set off on an exploration, just give the word!',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Weapons' => 'Great, you got all the weapons we require to equip our troops! Well done!',
        'TutMainPvPStage02' => 'Congratulations! You have completed your first expedition.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_Exp' => 'Great! We\'ve defeated the leader of this colony. Now we can claim its riches!',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_Progression' => 'Look at all those rewards. You can get extra fame and loot by sending your troops to expedition islands. Remember, you\'ll earn PvP XP for each unit you defeat.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_SendArmy' => 'Good work. Your marshals are on their way to this mysterious island. They will arrive there shortly.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_WaterCastle' => 'Well, look at that! Even it is still small, the expedition water castle is quite a sight, isn\'t it? Remember to upgrade it when you level up!',
        'TutMainPvPStage03_Troops' => 'Very good! Now we have a large enough force to set out, and discover our first real Colony.',
        'TutMainPvPstage03' => 'You have just conquered your first colony. Now we can claim it as our own!',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_Conquer' => 'Great work! Now we have a new colony to claim for its resources.',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_Explorers' => 'Great, you have chosen a new expedition.',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_SendArmy' => 'Good, our troops are travelling to the new expedition point as we speak. They should arrive there soon.',
        'TutMainPvPstage04' => 'The colony is producing goods nicely!',
        'TutMainPvPstage04_ClaimColony' => 'We have a new colony! It\'s already started producing resources for our kingdom.',
        'TutMainPvPstage04_Defence_Mode' => 'You\'ve inspected the bandits\' defences. I hope you managed to improve the weak points we exploited to conquer them.',
        'TutMainRangedUnits' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to recruit any kind of bowman.
Medium duration quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainSoldiers' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to produce and recruit soldiers.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainStoneProduction' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have stable stone production and can concentrate on other tasks.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainStorage' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You have continuously increased your storage capacity.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainSupport' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know the most important comfort functions of the game.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainToolProductionChain' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You now have stable tool production and can concentrate on other tasks.
Short quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainTrade' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now able to trade.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainTreasureSearch' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You have discovered all the treasure searches, and have had experience of using them.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainUpdateOldChains' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. Now you know all important facts about updating older production chains.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMainWealthy' => 'You\'ve managed to finish all the subquests. You are now a true master of trading, and your riches are almost limitless.
Long quest chain finished.',
        'TutMapparts' => 'Map fragments are a good thing. I have… Oh no, someone is opening the door. What should I do? Darn it! I\'m trapped.',
        'TutMarble' => 'With hardwood planks and marble you are now set to create more buildings.',
        'TutMarbleNew' => 'So, now we can relax and wait. As soon as we have enough hardwood planks and marble, we can start building new buildings and expand your economy further.',
        'TutMason' => 'Very good!
Your mason takes up his employment.',
        'TutMasonNew' => 'Good, the stone cutter has begun work. Since he does not supply any other buildings, there is no need to check whether you can perfect his methods. The more masons you have, the more your stock of stone increases.',
        'TutMeat' => 'That worked really well. The potion made from wheat and fish made the bear sleep long enough for us to take him to another island. Now the settlers can enter the woods safely again.',
        'TutMeatFishOptimize' => 'Well, was an adjustment necessary? At least the butcher is satisfied, so whatever you have done, it was a success.',
        'TutMediumAdventureSearch' => 'So, did your explorer find something useful? Don\'t forget, the adventures you\'ll find on this route might be more difficult to handle, so always take enough units with you.',
        'TutMediumTreasureSearch' => 'He really found coins lying unclaimed on the street. Unbelievable how careless people are with their cash. But we can make good use of them, so who cares…',
        'TutMilitia' => 'Very good!
Militias are better melee fighters than recruits.',
        'TutMilitiaFight' => 'So what do you think? Not bad is it? That is the result of the splendid training program I personally arranged. Feel free to keep training more units.',
        'TutMilitiaNew' => 'Training the militia really isn\'t easy. By the way, you should keep an eye on your population because regardless of what you do, you\'ll always need settlers, whether they\'re military units, mine workers or woodcutters.',
        'TutMiller' => 'Isn\'t the mill beautiful? I love the sound of its sails turning. A friend of mine is in charge of it now. I also have another one for the bakery.',
        'TutMoreCapital' => 'So, now I\'m eager to see whether it works. It\'s really very exciting. I admire you for taking care of your settlers so conscientiously. Now I\'ll mingle and see whether it works.',
        'TutMoreEconomyOverview' => 'Now, you have it in black and white that efficiency has been improved. Using this method, you can perfect all your production chains. Oh, that reminds me of something: may I introduce you to our new geologist?',
        'TutMoreEconomyOverviewAgain' => 'As you can see, your pinewood consumption has risen rapidly, so it is recommended you take countermeasures.',
        'TutMoreExplorer' => 'Very good. It would be best to send them out immediately to find something. By the way, the explorer you hire from the merchant needs only half the time the normal ones from the tavern take.',
        'TutMoreMasons' => 'Very good. More buildings of one type produce more, of course. Still, there are other ways of increasing production… Hey, a courier is coming. Please, wait a moment.',
        'TutMoreNobleResidences' => 'Of course, you can also upgrade already existing residences to expand your population capacity if you need to save on building licences. Another possibility is to buy a residence at the merchant\'s, where construction does not consume building licences.',
        'TutMorePopulation' => 'I have to admit, you have a really nice little town there. Carry on like that and the king will happily support you. Anyway, that\'s enough relaxing. Let us get on.',
        'TutMoreRealwood' => 'Unfortunately, I could not find out who the suspicious person was, but I think it was a blonde woman. Anyway, how is the hardwood production going?',
        'TutMoreResidences' => 'Hmm… I am not sure whether I like the residences being built so close together, but as long as the king is happy... By the way, he has given you a small reward.',
        'TutMoreTrades' => 'You really have a talent for trading. I\'m sure the king will recognize that too. Once we\'ve improved your skills a bit, maybe you\'ll become one of the most successful traders of the country.',
        'TutMoreWoodCutter' => 'Well, now the basics have been built. By the way, this proportion applies not only to pinewood but to all the different types of wood. When in doubt, produce more rather than less.',
        'TutMoveBuilding' => 'Well, that works fine. So, no problem if you ever get yourself stuck. However, moving buildings costs resources, so keep that in mind.',
        'TutNewMaterialChainsOptimize' => 'Very well, it can stay like this for now. I have already told you this, but it\'s very important: older production chains need to be updated over and over again, as many resources are consumed by multiple production circles.',
        'TutNobleResidence' => 'Don\'t they look fabulous? From now on you can build them and make even more space for your settlers. However, remember that residences also need building licences. If you need a building without obtaining a licence, go see the merchant.',
        'TutOpenShop' => 'Did you find anything suitable? There are some beautiful things... but enough of that. The merchant is accessible at any time through the treasure chest in the bottom right-hand corner, in case you need something.',
        'TutOptimizeWeaponChains' => 'My father prepared you really well. You worked well, and quickly. You have erased all my final doubts about you becoming the greatest explorer of all times.',
        'TutPlayAdventures' => 'Thank you for leaving us alone for a moment. Seraphina is my daughter. We don\'t exactly have the best relationship. She left a while ago without even saying goodbye. At least I know where she is now.',
        'TutPopulation1' => 'Just like that! You get a new settler every 15 minutes. If you have less time and you need new settlers fast, you cannot only buy settlers directly from the merchant but also buy buffs to shorten the time it takes to train new settlers. But always keep in mind that to get new settlers you need adequate free space.',
        'TutPopulationCap' => 'It seems demand is high. There are a lot of people who want to settle on your island. You have a good reputation, but deservedly so.',
        'TutPopulationCap2' => 'What, you\'re not allowed to tell me the subject of the letter? That\'s a shame, but I suppose I\'ll have to get used to it. It must be very important if you get a personal, secret letter from the king.',
        'TutPopulationCap3' => 'Hmm… Your face reveals a certain anxiety. I\'m sure you can handle whatever\'s written in this letter. Anyway, I have to leave fast before someone spots me. Until next time.',
        'TutPopulationCap4' => 'Wow - a very generous delivery has just arrived from the king. Whatever it is you did, the king seems very satisfied. Well done!',
        'TutPopulationCap5' => 'Hmm… I wonder if that will be enough? Maybe I should go and spy a bit more to make sure you are sufficiently well prepared. \'llI contact you as soon as I am convinced.',
        'TutPopulationCap6' => 'Yes, these are really strapping young men, perfect for the military. Now we can take the next step in perfecting your army, and increase the amount of units.',
        'TutPopulationCap7' => 'Wow, people are flocking to your city. You seem to have a really good reputation. Hardly surprising, considering your good relationship with the king. This means we\'ll be able to continue quickly.',
        'TutPopulationCap8' => 'Wow, people are flocking to your city. You seem to have a really good reputation. No wonder, seeing as you have such a good relationship with the king. Now we can continue quickly.',
        'TutPowderhut' => 'Hmm, that was a lot of work, but the powderhut really looks pretty. Now I shall leave and prepare the construction of the cannon forge. See you later.',
        'TutProduceFishRefill' => 'I am very grateful. You are really very kind. We have put the fish refiller in your star menu.',
        'TutProduceRecruits' => 'The message that the recruits are on their way seems to have calmed him down a bit, though he still doesn\'t want to tell us who this possible attacker might be.',
        'TutProduceSoldiers' => 'I don\'t believe this. It would seem your brother\'s \'frightening fiend\' is simply a lady he was rather ungentlemanly with. She hasn\'t even threatened him with soldiers, just thrown rotten eggs at his carriage. Unbelievable.',
        'TutProduceSteelswords' => 'You are really very generous. I hope your brother appreciates it, but most likely not. Hopefully, he is satisfied after taking receipt of the soldiers.',
        'TutProduceTools' => 'Now we should be prepared for the new buildings. I\'m going back to study the new plans so we can begin construction as soon as you give the signal. Goodbye.',
        'TutProvisionHouse' => 'Good job!
The provision house can change resources into a variety of useful items.',
        'TutProvisionHouseNew' => 'Ah, the provisions house has already been built. You should take a look. You can commission a lot of nice things there.',
        'TutPurchaseGeologist' => 'You can find your purchased specialists in your star menu. You can have multiple specialists of one kind, but the allocation of specialists you can hire from the tavern is limited. When it is exhausted.you have to get additional ones from the merchant.',
        'TutQualityFoodBuff' => 'That\'s it! A workyard buffed with the Quality Food buff will work much faster than usual. Watch out for more buffs in the shop or quest rewards

NOTE:
Visit your friends and buff their buildings. Buffs applied to friends\' workyards will last longer.',
        'TutRaiseGranite' => 'Could you get hold of some granite? It\'s quite expensive because it\'s rare, but there really is nothing better. Some people offer granite through the trade and, in an emergency, there is always the merchant. I heard that sometimes even explorers find granite during their treasure hunts.',
        'TutRealWood' => 'Great!
Hardwood planks will allow you to create new and advanced buildings.',
        'TutRealWoodNew' => 'It\'s great that we have enough hardwood trees on this island. Your hard working settlers are already producing hardwood and hardwood planks. Now, let\'s get on with producing marble.',
        'TutRecruit' => 'Well done!
Your recruits are now ready for duty.',
        'TutRecruitNew' => 'As you might have gathered, to train units takes quite a lot of time. The better the unit, the longer it takes, but when you upgrade your barracks, the time decreases a little. In addition, there are drill plans that can speed the process up. I\'ll let the merchant tell you more.',
        'TutSausage' => 'We won, thanks to your bountiful sausage supply. As promised, we would like to give you a part of our reward. Now I have to go back to work. Thanks again.',
        'TutSawmill' => 'Great!
You are now able to produce pinewood planks.',
        'TutSawmillNew' => 'The sawmill converts wood into planks, with which you can build new buildings. Now I\'ll show you where you can find your produced goods.',
        'TutSelectBarracks' => 'Good.
All military units are trained in the barracks.
As you can see, each unit has different requirements.',
        'TutSelectBarracksNew' => 'In the beginning there are only recruits to train, but others will come over time. However, training takes time, so plan for it.',
        'TutSelectMayorhouse' => 'Workers bring the goods they produce to the storehouses, and needed resources are always taken from the storehouses.',
        'TutSelectMayorhouseNew' => 'As you can see, the Mayor\'s house has different pages where you can see different things. The same is true of storehouses. Anyway, enough theory for now - let\'s focus on your economy again.',
        'TutSellGoodsViaTrade' => 'At some point, you will almost certainly have a resource that\'s no use to you anymore. However, before you tear down a building you should always consider selling it through trade instead.',
        'TutShortAdventureSearch' => 'So, were you lucky? Sometimes the explorer finds only single map pieces, but you can piece them together too. Just visit the merchant.',
        'TutSimpleResidence' => 'Good.
Every workyard needs 1 worker in order to produce goods.
Keep an eye on your available living space and population when expanding your town.',
        'TutSimpleResidenceNew' => 'You\'ve just built your first residence and hopefully created the basis for a successful settlement. May many residences follow and your settlement flourish.',
        'TutSolidSandwich' => 'Hmm… A buff. And how is that supposed to help the military? They don\'t need sandwiches! They need something more consistent!',
        'TutStable' => 'The travellers were really pleased about the stable. One of your settlers is taking care of the stable and has begun to raise horses, just in case you need some in the future.',
        'TutSteelWeaponChainOptimize' => 'As soon as you think that production is okay, we can continue training the soldiers. Do you think Theodor is really in danger? Maybe he is just imagining things.',
        'TutSteelWeaponsmith' => 'Very good. The military expansion has worked. In which case, I shall get back to searching for the suspicious person. Keep an eye open and report to me if you see her.',
        'TutSteelforge' => 'Steel is very important for weapon manufacture. By the way, I saw the shadow from earlier again. She disappeared in your direction. Did you see her, by any chance?',
        'TutStorage' => 'You passed this test. I will contact the king immediately. As soon as I have an answer, and am notified of his next demand, I will inform you.',
        'TutStorage2' => 'Yes, much better. I hate rats, but at least they have helped us be better prepared for the king\'s next task.',
        'TutStorage3' => 'It seems that we had the right idea about this. I\'ve heard that the king really appreciated our initiative. As a reward, he has sent us some resources to support us.',
        'TutStorage4' => 'Wow, that was a really generous reward. I hope no envious individual will try to tarnish your success. We better keep our eyes open, just in case.',
        'TutStorage5' => 'Oh wonderful. Now we can store the items way better. I\'m sorry I always seem to ask you for something when I come for a visit. Next time I promise we\'ll just have a nice chat.',
        'TutStorage6' => 'Excellent! The king was enthusiastic and has commissioned delivery of the reward, a really generous reward! Congratulations. In any case, you have definitely secured the king\'s favor.',
        'TutStorage7' => 'Well, that looks way better. I\'m surprised how fast you did this. Now, there is only a little bit of work left to do to make your city perfect.',
        'TutStorage8' => 'So, you\'ve mastered everything there is to do with the store. When we began settling I could never imagined such success. I am glad I was allowed to assist you.',
        'TutSurveyQuest' => 'Good work! You\'ve finished making your first self-produced resources. What does it feel like? Just wait until we can build huge houses with our own resources!',
        'TutTavern' => 'From now on, you can hire an unlimited number of Specialists in the Tavern.',
        'TutTavernNew' => 'What a wonderful place. The people there are always cheerful and ready for a good talk. Take a look when you have the possibility. It\'ll be worth it!',
        'TutTitanium' => 'Hmm… I just saw my daughter in the courtyard. It seems she wants to speak with you. I\'m surprised she\'s helping you so much. Maybe I have misjudged her.',
        'TutTitaniumForge' => 'Titanium is a good metal; solid, but light and able to take a lot of strain. We should be able to produce effective weapons from it. However, it is not cheap.',
        'TutTitaniumWeapon' => 'I just took a look at weapon production. Very beautiful swords I have to admit. What? No, I am not sure where my daughter might be. She tends to keep out of my sight, rather successfully in fact.',
        'TutTitaniumWeaponSmith' => 'Right, that is what we need! No carriages to push around the area. We will be able to make fantastic weapons out of it. You will see!',
        'TutToolProductionChainOptimize' => 'Very well, I will stop bothering you now so you concentrate on your military concerns.',
        'TutToolResourceBuff' => 'That was fast. Now, you have enough tools in stock. We should think about producing them ourselves, only one by one.',
        'TutTools' => 'Good job!
Each workyard needs tools to operate.
Make sure you always have enough tools available when expanding your town.

NOTE:
Take a look at the production times of your workyards.
A Coppermine produces twice as fast as a Coppersmelter. So a Coppermine delivers enough resources to deploy two Coppersmelters.

The production times are shown in the details tab of each workyard.',
        'TutToolsNew' => 'Good, tool production works… Unfortunately, I have bad news. The rumour about the bandits is true. We need to take action. We also need a specialist.',
        'TutTrade' => 'So, how do you like trading? You can always use it to get missing resources or to get rid of those you have in excessive quantities. And remember always to keep an eye on prices - you may find a bargain here or there.',
        'TutTradeWeapons' => 'A good option, isn\'t it? You should always keep trade in mind as a viable alternative. In the right moment, it can save you a lot of time. But always compare prices so that you get a good offer.',
        'TutTreasure' => 'I am really curious as to what the explorer will find. He will be returning in 6 hours, so you can give him some new orders then. Just remember you cannot cancel the search.',
        'TutUpgrade' => 'Good!
Note that buildings stop working while they are being upgraded.',
        'TutUpgradeNew' => 'You can upgrade nearly all buildings so they produce faster, or make more goods. Upgrading storehouses increases your stock capacity, but the time and resources required increases with every level.',
        'TutUpgradedBuildings' => 'Just like that! It looks a lot better that way. I am sure the king will also be satisfied when he hears of your efforts to please him.',
        'TutUpgradedNobleResidences' => 'Thank you for your trust. I will not disappoint you. Hmm? Did I hear a noise? I think someone is approaching. I had better disappear. Until next time.',
        'TutUseBuff' => 'Good!
You\'ve increased the productivity of your workyard for the first time.',
        'TutUseBuffNew' => 'You have doubled the production of this building for 30 minutes. You should always buff your workyards when you temporarily need more of one specific resource.',
        'TutUseControls' => 'I see you have the hang of it. Don\'t hesitate to change the options if anything bothers you. Additionally, you can look up all my notes in the archive in case you forget anything.',
        'TutUseFishRefill' => 'My friend the fisherman has come to me and told me he has been catching fish better than ever. He has asked me to convey his thanks. You have mine also - thank you.',
        'TutUseShop' => 'The merchant is reliable. Maybe you have seen the other resources he has on offer. This makes him a good place to go whenever you need something urgently.',
        'TutUseSolidSandwich' => 'I think I have underestimated you in certain areas. That was a clever move. You should go now and look after your production. You always have to keep an eye on the people.',
        'TutVeryLongTreasureSearch' => 'So, were you successful? Adventures like these are not easy to find. Be patient. Sooner or later you\'ll find one. While you\'re waiting, use the time to expand your army.',
        'TutWarehouse' => 'You\'ve just claimed your first new sector.',
        'TutWarehouseNew' => 'This sector is yours now. You are progressing really fast. I will now write my report for the king. It\'s very pleasing to have only good things to report.',
        'TutWell' => 'Really beautiful wells. Wells and wheat fields only contain a certain amount of resources. As you progress, you will gain access to higher capacity wells and wheat fields.',
        'TutWheatProductionOptimize' => 'I have spoken to the stable manager once again, and he is now receiving enough wheat to feed his horses. Soon the first horses will be ready.',
        'TutWheelmaker' => 'Wow, what a beautiful building. It really adds something to the city. Can\'t have been cheap, I\'m sure. I\'m excited to see how things develop with the carriages. Just remember we need a carpenter before we can use the carriages.',
        'TutWoodChainOptimize' => 'I knew you would make it. The king will be proud of you. I will report to him immediately.',
        'TutWoodCutter' => 'You\'ve constructed your first building.',
        'TutWoodCutterNew' => 'Very well. You\'ve now finished the first step in creating a basic stable economy. Let\'s move on to the next one!',
        'TutZoneWideBuffs1' => 'The window might have been empty. We\'ll take care of that in the next step!',
        'TutZoneWideBuffs2' => 'See how the buff\'s listed in the window now? You can even cancel it early if you want to get rid of the effect.
I\'ll give you some more to play around with.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_0' => 'Oh, right - there\'s a town behind those rocks! Is this Laeylorn? But... it seems there are ongoing fights. Another group of bandits seemingly arrived shortly before us. We should intervene!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_1' => 'Good solid work. Not like those bandits really stood a chance, but still.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_10' => 'As always, an immensely good job. I expected nothing less of you! Thank you so much.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_11' => 'Oh, those are some sturdy barricades! They might not look like much, but with these, our enemies have only one path they can take to enter the town. And we can much more easily defend it. They tried to stop us building up these barricades, but you were far too fast. I guess it\'s not your first time building and repairing things far away from home?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_2' => 'Ah, finally someone opens the door! You know, it\'s rather unpleasant standing outside and knocking weirdly on so many doors and windows.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_20' => 'Don\'t forget to send the troops! Without them, we cannot dare rebuild the town. Who\'d want to start building a smithery if they fear a spear in their back at any time? Only with safety will we be able to return the town to its former glory, and repay you for your help!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_21' => 'Did you use some kind of special fertilizer? These wheat fields are growing faster and stronger than I\'d ever imagined. Thank you for this - this wheat should prevent any immediate threat of starving, at the very least.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_22' => 'It almost looks like a normal village now, doesn\'t it? People are coming out of their houses, and even daring to sit on the benches around town again. Remarkable.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_23' => 'Oh, I get the shivers when I even so much as see those towers... But can I still call you if anyone tries attacking us again?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_25' => 'Why is no-one able to speak for themselves! Everyone just sends us to the mayor without exception. They were reluctant to tell us a lot about Kaedric to begin with, but they practically stopped talking the instant I\'ve mentioned him. Are they afraid of us? Or of Kaedric? Well, at least they confirmed he was here...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_26' => 'It\'s good to have proof that Kaedric was here. And not only that, it seems he was looking for something around the village and the island. It sounds like he went outside the village, even though Ferri clearly warns everybody against doing so. There are many aggressive and dangerous wild animals on the island, and Ferri doesn\'t want them to be drawn to the village.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_27' => 'At least his explanation wasn\'t that bad. As he told us before, the monsters around the island are dangerous, and he doesn\'t want us to get hurt - especially since we became twin towns. He also thinks Kaedric was the explorer that visited some time ago, and that he went westward for something. He did intend to send out his own search party first, as they know the land, and know how to avoid any potential trouble, but it seems he has other priorities he needed to deal with first.
On top of that, he mentioned some ancient ruins and treasures he doesn\'t want to get stolen. It seems he trusts us now, at least... Let\'s see for ourselves.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_28' => 'Now that these beasts are off our backs, let\'s take a look around.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_29' => 'I thought so. But it\'s always better to be sure. Now we know the direction he went in, and we also have a bit of a clue what he was interested in, don\'t we?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_3' => 'See, this is why we cannot divert any attention to searching for missing people right now. We ourselves are also still missing our tailor and one of our healers. Due to constant attacks on our town for a nigh on decade, only a small village remains, and even this is shrinking faster than we can hope to rebuild. There are many villagers who\'ve fled to nearby hideouts and have been left homeless.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_30' => 'This is really strange... The building is perfectly fine. Not a scratch. It\'s even been cleaned recently! But it doesn\'t look like anyone\'s living here. There isn\'t even a bed - just some tools for digging and research. Maybe Kaedric\'s using the house? Hmm, or perhaps not... I guess he\'d be too organized to leave such a mess behind. Let\'s continue along the path.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_31' => 'Aha! It seems there are some small crevasses in the mountains here. Big enough for someone to squeeze through if they really wanted to. And Kaedric\'s the kind of guy who\'d be so curious he couldn\'t NOT do it... I just hope he didn\'t suffocate in a small hole underground... I suggest we see if we can get rid of some rock here, and take a look at what\'s behind these crevasses a bit more safely.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_32' => 'Oookaaay. I was expecting we might find some kind of ruin - not a huge cave entrance like this! You wait here for minute - I\'m going to have a little peek inside. If the cave\'s a bit unstable,  I don\'t want you getting buried because of my curiosity...

Waaaaaaaaahh. Oh my... OK, no... It\'s not OK! Let\'s get away from here. Fast! And gather our troops. We\'ll need lots of troops before we can explore this cave. When I went inside, I just kept going down and down forever, until I turned a corner and saw this huge underground cave. It was so incredible, I stopped to catch my breath - which probably also saved my life. The very next second, some huge - aehm - something rushed past me, hunting something else in the dark. I\'ve never seen anything like it. I hope you don\'t think I\'m exaggerating when I say it was some kind of monster...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_33' => 'Oh, how wonderful! I\'ll see we sell our share of the resources, and put the proceeds to good use in Laeylorn. That should secure our town\'s food supply further. Maybe we could even afford some herbs and seasonings now? We haven\'t had anything like that in a while...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_34' => 'As soon as our economy is back in the black, we can try to expand our city. If the pirates return, I trust I\'ll be able to count on our allies again? I\'ll see you get the "gifts" I told you about earlier as soon as possible. If it\'s not too much trouble, come visit, OK?

Goodbye, my friends!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_35' => 'Hmm... It seems the mad scientist found several interesting things - but he also said it\'s too early to come to any conclusions. That said, he was maniacally grinning and laughing when he was talking about the experiments he\'s going to be doing next. Just... don\'t expect to hear anything from him soon. I think he\'s a little bit... busy.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_4' => 'Thank you so much for this. Now we have enough room for the majority of people, and we don\'t have to cram everyone into the left-over buildings.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_5' => 'My sincerest thanks. It\'s... harder than you can imagine. Especially since I have to maintain my composure. I fear the people would give up completely and surrender their lives if there was no-one there to provide hope.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_6' => 'I will accompany you to your ships personally. We were really lucky you came. Once the situation has calmed down, we\'ll be more than happy to help you find your friend. When you return, I think it might be a good idea to bring some more troops with you - though I doubt there will be as many bandits as last time.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_7' => 'Wow! I\'m impressed. I thought you might try to lure them away or something - I didn\'t realize you had such an incredible force behind you! I must remember not to get on your bad side, huh?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_8' => 'Phew! Those beasts looked really dangerous, but you seem to take care of such threats with ease!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_9' => 'Impressive! OK - now we should have some time to recuperate. But I fear the pirates will return soon... Maybe even tomorrow! I will be sure to send for you if we need help, so there\'s no need to remain on the island. But don\'t wait too long before you send your troops... I don\'t want to see everything we\'ve rebuilt so far just crumble away. Not again.

And thank you, for all you\'ve done. I have a feeling I\'ll have reason to say this again and again in future.',
        'TwinTown_El_Chupacabra_Tracks' => 'Looking a little closer, Kaedric was digging holes here and there as he went. He was digging for something specific, that much is clear. Let\'s take some samples too.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main1' => 'I think I\'ve thanked you so often by now, you must be growing tired of my voice. You are a true friend! Although I am still unsure how any of this will turn out, with your help I\'m sure we will be able to find Kaedric, and discover what all this was about!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2' => 'At least we\'ve found some traces of Kaedric now... Even if we haven\'t yet found him, we at least know he\'s still alive. But if he doesn\'t want to be found, there must be a reason... I hope we\'ll be able to find out what\'s behind all of this.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_1' => 'Friggin\' unbelievable! Excuse my outburst, but none of the explorers could find a thing! Kaedric\'s apparently never visited any known town, fishing village or hermit\'s house! So now what do we do? If we\'ve already searched so far and wide, how are we ever going to find anything? Unless... wait a second...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_10' => 'Your specialists have gone through the samples we provided, and what they found is a bit worrisome. It\'s the same reddish powder that was found in our mines some time ago - but they\'re still unable to identify it. At a glance, it just looks like normal dirt - it\'s just the color that\'s unusual.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_11' => 'Great. So after much time and effort, we find ourselves back exactly where we started. Kaedric is still missing, we have no lead on where he went, and we have even less of an idea on how to proceed. I really hope he\'s OK. I guess we\'ll just have to wait until a new lead shows up. I\'ll ask the explorers\' guild to have everyone keep their eyes and ears open. I\'m afraid there\'s not much else we can do - flying around aimlessly in the Excelsior won\'t help anyone. But I\'m sure this won\'t be the last we hear about all this...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_2' => 'Still no clues as to Kaedric\'s whereabouts... I think we ought to go back to Laeylorn and ask around there.

Hmm... You know, it doesn\'t really help us with the search, and it might just be a random detail, but nonetheless... During several of the searches, we found some red dust. None of the geologists knows what this is - they\'ve never seen anything like it before. But your experts all agreed that this mineral, or whatever it is, would usually reside very deep in the ground.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_3' => 'Hmm... Do you also have the strange feeling that something isn\'t quite right? Are the people of Laeylorn hiding something?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_4' => 'OK. Everyone\'s certain that Kaedric hasn\'t returned, and no-one\'s heard anything from him since he went to Laeylorn. Can we take a look over there ourselves? Maybe if we promise not to let any beasts reach the town, he\'ll allow us to take a look around the island?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_5' => 'I truly did not expect this outcome. Let\'s continue.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_6' => 'Every single storage building on Laeylorn is filled to the brim with things people can\'t really use at the moment, but Ferri has ensured us it\'s fine for now, as he knows we\'ll take care of it in future. Also, apparently most of the island\'s weapons are stored in and below the Mayor\'s House. Turn out there\'s an unexpectedly large cellar with lots of room directly below it. I guess with all the fighting, they must think it\'s safer to build under the buildings rather than above ground.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_7' => 'Well, that was new. I mean, those creatures, and the trees and the crystals. But there\'s also this constant feeling of... dread. As if there\'s always something standing behind you, but when you turn around, there\'s nothing there. Once, I even thought I felt someone\'s breath on my nape, but apparently it was just a gust of wind.
Though there were some hints that Kaedric had been there, it looks like it was already some time ago. Still, we did find a list of places Kaedric was apparently going to visit. It looks like Kaedric left it there on purpose, so someone - like us - could follow his tracks.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_8' => 'After sifting through the clues, it looks like Kaedric was looking for something specific. And he was mostly looking at the mountainous areas, if we\'ve drawn the correct conclusions. Still, that doesn\'t exactly tell us a lot. Let\'s carry on to the next item on the list.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_9' => 'Well, it\'s clear that Kaedric is heading towards the rocks. And it looks like he\'s taken several samples from different ones. But we still don\'t know what he did with those samples. Off to the next item on the list!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3' => 'Now it\'s official. Laeylorn has become your partner town. We\'re definitely counting on you and your help, but I hope we\'ve already proven that we can become a worthy partner in future. All this aside, I think the most important thing is that you\'ve been able to help so many good people! Don\'t you agree?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_1' => 'Thanks again. We couldn\'t have dealt with them on our own.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_1_Starter2' => 'You showed those damned invaders! They shouldn\'t go to other people\'s islands in the first place!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_2' => 'Thanks for returning the scrolls and books. They\'re precious remnants of our past - we wouldn\'t have got them back without you.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_3' => 'This is such a relief. The people and I can finally feel somewhat safe. Even during ongoing attacks, the noise doesn\'t reach the village anymore, and everyone can finally rest. All thanks to you.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_4' => 'Good choice!

For now, our town needs to rest and catch up with all the improvements we\'ve been able to install thanks to you. We\'ll need to gather up all the people that are still scattered around the island, and assign them rooms in the residences. We\'ll also need to fill all the positions to take care of the farm and food supply, and get to know all the people you stationed here better. Even if they are soldiers, they\'re still people, and some of them will settle down here for good - and get all the former productions running again. With the protection we have now, we should be able get back into a routine in a few months, I\'d say. We\'ll let you know when we\'re ready to continue building up this beautiful town once more.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main4' => 'Laeylorn, now finally able to defend itself, will slowly but surely be able to return to its former glory. That being said, the people might need your help again sooner than you might think - and Kaedric\'s whereabouts are still a mystery that begs to be solved.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Start_1' => 'Ok... He\'s not here. Let\'s ask around, and see where he might have ended up. It\'s really not like him to invite us but then not be there. He\'s more of an orderly, punctual type of guy.

Oh, it looks like he left us a message?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_1' => 'Finally, we have a clue about what Laeylorn might be. It seems to be an island - one further away from our home than we\'ve ever traveled. It is beyond the stormy regions to the west. Even I have rarely visited these areas, as the Excelsior isn\'t capable of travelling there. Believe me, we tried, and we almost paid with our lives. I assume the only way to get there is by ship. Or by some kind of underwater vessel, if something so ludicrous should exist. Either way, we have to find a way to go either below, or around these heavy and unpredictable thunderstorms.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_10' => 'We\'ve got some weird things onboard now... But it can\'t be helped, I guess!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_11' => 'Nice! I think we\'re finally prepared for what\'s yet to come. I think I\'d have gone crazy if these preparations had taken any longer!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_12' => 'A great day to start an epic adventure, wouldn\'t you agree?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_13' => 'Good, good! That puts my mind at rest, at least a little. I thought I\'d go crazy pondering over it...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_14' => 'OK! Now let\'s go back to Laeylorn, continue conquering this new adventure, and find out what happened to Kaedric! Remember, you\'ll always find the coordinates for Laeylorn in your mailbox after deferring this adventure.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_15' => 'It seems our island is THE birthplace of thrillseeking adventurers. Maybe that has something to do with you? 
There were more than enough volunteers after all. I shouldn\'t have been worried.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_16' => 'OK! The troops should have arrived by now. Ever since we created some proper maps of the area, and improved our ships by borrowing some of the engineering feats from the Excelsior, we\'ve been able to get to Laeylorn much quicker!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_17' => 'Oh wow, that really was a lot of supplies! I was watching the dockworkers for hours. If you looked closely, you could see the ships sink a little deeper with every crate and barrel that was loaded on board. These supplies are going to help people that are truly in need. You can be content with your work today.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_2' => 'Look at all those carts to transport the materials. That is quite a sight to behold!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_3' => 'I already feel safer! Even though there was never a lot of crime here, I doubt anyone will try anything foolish while we\'re gone now.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_4' => 'Equally spread across all the ships, this amount of food still fills their holds to the brim. But this won\'t last for long when we\'re out at sea. Oh, it\'s been a long time since I was aboard a ship... One that isn\'t flying, I mean.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_5' => 'Good, good. This setup should keep everything in order until we return.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_6' => 'OK, these ships are getting fuller and fuller...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_7' => 'OK! It seems we have all the basics, but our entourage has recommended we bring along quite a few more things in order to be fully prepared.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_8' => 'Another huge load of resources... I really hope we\'ll be able to get through the storms and find Laeylorn. I was able to get a better map showing the way to the island, but it\'s very old, and only parts are visible. Still, it seems Laeylorn has been a very rich country with lots of trading relationships.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_9' => 'OK, that should be enough! I\'ve always liked seeing everything sparkling!',
        'TwinTown_Outlaws_Tracks' => 'Hmm. Look at how clear these tracks are... I mean, I know I\'ve probably got better at tracking Kaedric\'s movements over the last few weeks... But these almost look like he left them behind intentionally. They almost look like hints, or clues to some kind of riddle... I wonder if I\'m just imagining it... I mean, he\'d have been in a hurry - and he\'d have had to stay hidden from any foes...',
        'TwinTown_RoaringBull_Tracks' => 'It looks like Kaedric travelled over the entire island... Perhaps he was in disguise? Hmmm, that could have been possible...',
        'TwinTown_TheHeroicLittleTailor_Tracks' => 'Well, that\'s strange... The tracks were almost exactly the same as the ones we\'ve followed before. But this time, there\'s clearly more of them. And if I\'m not mistaken, it looks like someone else either followed Kaedric directly, or followed his tracks just like we did. But then, suddenly, all of the tracks just stop. No more clues, no new list, nothing. But there\'s also no sign of a fight, or anything similar. It\'s like the earth just swallowed him up.',
        'Unity_Final' => 'Oh and make sure to check your mailbox... Wink... Wink...',
        'Unity_Main' => 'As unexpectedly as he showed up, Mr. Foozler leaves, convinced that his work and influence will prove essential to keeping your island running happily and optimally for years to come.

He was pleased with what the two of you achieved together, and as a token of approval from him, and on behalf of the king, he\'s rewarded you with this treasure chest.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1' => 'Oh! Hi, I didn\'t see you there.

I\'m anxious to get to work, so... I went ahead and unpacked my own insta-build accommodations.

I hope you don\'t mind. Hehe.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub1' => 'Nice house! But, something\'s not quite right... I don\'t know...',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub2' => 'Much better! The right amount of shade, not too crowded, not too isolated, the right amount of silence.

Yes, I believe I can work here.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub3' => 'There are my clothes... Here are my tools... And my undergarments...  Yes, everything is accounted for.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2' => 'Oh dear! Not quite the results I expected.

But I have an idea. I have the coordinates of a nearby deserted island where we can carry out our tests in complete safety.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub1' => 'I see... Most interesting. The shape of the scales... The physiology of the gills... Just sad that they do not survive when removed from the water.

Still, that should be enough for aquatic life. Now, let us focus on another group.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub2' => 'Great work! It is a shame that you weren\'t able to get healthy wild specimens, though. That is to say, the sort that are still alive.

I suppose I\'ll have to make do with what we have.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub3' => 'Huh... Not exactly what I expected.

Are you sure the ingredients provided were fresh?

Judging by the smell, there might have been a bit of rot in the materials.

Perhaps too much fish was used?

Back to the drawing board',
        'Unity_Main_Part3' => 'Oh! There isn\'t a shipyard available?

Never fear, I\'m sure you are quite capable of finding a use for these materials.

Here. Have a ticket for a ride on one of the royal fleet ships. No harm done.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub1' => 'Make sure everything is well sanded down. Getting splinters in your fingers is a dreadful prospect.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub2' => 'Ah, good, good. I knew you\'d nail this task.

Now, I shall put all of these materials to good use.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub3' => 'What do you mean there\'s no shipyard here?',
        'Unity_Main_Part4' => 'Good, you\'re back, and your clothes are dry!

While you were busy looking for the lost city of Atlantis - erm, I mean, saving the sailors - I had an epiphany.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5' => 'Ha ha! Yes! I believe we\'re on the verge of a production revolution, powered by all the advancements in science I\'m bringing you.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub1' => 'That\'ll be enough for the mineral part of the formula.

Next, we\'ll need some veggies.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub2' => 'You don\'t suppose I should separate the chaff from the wheat all by myself, do you?

Oh! You do? 

I guess I\'d better get working, then.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub3' => 'Here. Crystal clear instructions.

It is child\'s play!

Not in the literal sense of course. This is very much adult-like, official business. Super serious. Seriously.

I... I should just stop talking...',
        'Unity_Main_Part6' => 'Funny story: the numbers didn\'t lie, but it seems I gave you the work-in-progress version of the formula and not the final one.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7' => 'I believe my duty here has been fulfilled.

I will now sail back to the mainland and report back to the king.

He\'ll be pleased to hear what took place here.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub1' => 'When you thought you\'d had enough with water in our latest expedition...',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub2' => 'No animals were harmed during the making of this procedure. 

In fact, I think I made lots of new friends. I can\'t seem to get away from these animals anymore...',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub3' => 'In case you were curious what these were for, well, I do get hungry after a long day of work.

They\'ll make for great dumplings, yum yum!',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub4' => 'Behold my greatest creation! Yes, I did it! This is it, this is the one.',
        'Unity_Main_Reach20' => 'Great - everything is prepared. You\'ll surely make a great first impression.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1' => 'You can almost feel their edges just by looking at them.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p1' => 'The masters have gathered!',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p2' => 'The security is so tight you couldn\'t slide a paper between two guards!',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p3' => 'They\'re ... beautiful. They should\'ve sent a poet!',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2' => 'They polish so fast it\'ll char lesser wood!',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p1' => 'If this doesn\'t say "commitment" - what will?',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p2' => 'The stacks of paper reach the ceiling in some halls.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p3' => 'Smooth, heavy and warm to the touch - these tools radiate immense power.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1' => 'The ovens may be cool to the touch, but inside it\'s a firey hell!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1_p1' => 'The scaffolding\'s impressive enough - just imagine how spectacular the actual buildings will be.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1_p2' => 'The ovens look like they\'re made from a single granite block. Exquisite masonry!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2' => 'One blast can turn an entire cart of wood to coal!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2_p1' => 'It looks like fairy dust mixed with black powder! Handle with care!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2_p2' => 'Nobody thought the granite ovens could look any more impressive - but the titanium reinforcements managed that.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2' => 'Great job! Look at those blades sliding through the wood!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2_p1' => 'The crew has gathered - time to move on to the next step!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2_p2' => 'They\'re so sharp and precise, they can slice to a hair\'s depth.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3' => 'Look at them spinning! The technology at work here... It\'s magic!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p1' => 'The Magic Beans are secured now. The container is holding and is also well-guarded.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p2' => 'Clear as water, yet extremely flammable! Keep it contained at any costs!',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p3' => 'They look beautiful, even in their delivery boxes.',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2' => 'The foliage even blots out the sun!',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p1' => 'The foresters we have will provide ample supplies of the required seeds. Great job!',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p2' => 'It looks like a spider\'s web of bronze tubing!',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p3' => 'Watching this machinery work is truly hypnotic.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2' => 'The furnaces look much more ornate, too!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2_p1' => 'The masons have pledged their support for the project! Onwards and upwards!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2_p2' => 'Beautifully worked marble with iron braces in a spectacular lattice pattern - the craftsmen have truly outdone themselves.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3' => 'Watch those logs closely - blink! - they\'re coal!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3_p1' => 'The containment box looks like it could withstand a volcano itself. Great job!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3_p2' => 'KA-BOOM! A resounding success!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2' => 'This type of blade shows great improvement over the usual kind.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2_p1' => 'Great, the workers have been gathered!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2_p2' => 'The materials have been delivered and the production can begin. Great job!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3' => 'This is science, harnessing the magic!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3_p1' => 'It seems the casing is holding strong! We can proceed to the next step.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3_p2' => 'The materials have been delivered and the blades are under construction! Great job!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialArchive' => 'As you can see, spreading flowers around isn\'t too tricky, but it  still requires some effort!

I hope I can count on you my dear!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialEnding' => 'I can´t believe we made it. I just received a message from my love. It won´t be long before my sweetheart is finally home again.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerBouquet' => 'Nothing is more beautiful than getting flowers! Apart from seeing ones loved ones, of course... No, I will not cry... I will not cry! Stay strong, Flora - stay strong...',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerFarm' => 'Oh, they\'re so lovely... The smell, the colors... even the feel of these blossoms is phenomenal already. When the flowers are ready, they can be spread all over the world in different ways. By making flower bouquets out of them, you can help them reach other islands very quickly, but if you trade them, or spend them at the merchant, they´re sure to cover a long distance! I hope my love will find them!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerSeed' => 'Nice job refilling the flower farms! Plenty more flowers will be blooming soon, in all the most spectacular colors. Keep it up, and keep growing plenty of new flowers! And don´t forget - they don´t need long to grow!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialMain' => 'Oh, thank you so, so much! I don\'t know what I\'d have done without you... Now, my sweetheart and I can be together again, and celebrate our love the way it should be.

Just between us, I think this year will be pretty special... It might just be the year when we finally get engaged!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialReach16' => 'Good job, my dear. Now, let us meet properly. Please visit me as soon as you have the time.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialValentineCard' => 'Aren´t they lovely! I cannot read them often enough. The poetry, the feelings, the expressions of love! They make my heart race, even though some are already years old.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Main' => 'One game down, only four to go!',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Main1' => 'Congratulations! Now you know how to handle yourself on the field!',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub1' => 'Now you know your opponent\'s skills, you should put your knowledge to good use.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub2' => 'One striker less to worry about!',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub3' => 'You defeated the midfielder! Congratulations!',
        'WMEventAdvQ2' => 'Congratulations! We won the first group stage match. If we can win the second one too, we might advance to the last 16.',
        'WMEventAdvQ2Sub1' => 'Well done! These are some pretty advanced tactics! Remember, you can see the order in which an opponent\'s skills will be removed in the tactical item’s tooltip.',
        'WMEventAdvQ3' => 'That was really a good performance! Thanks to your excellent tactics, it\'s now official: we\'ve reached the final 16!',
        'WMEventAdvQ4' => 'What a thrilling game! I\'m glad we could beat the Shire of Oxwater – the underdogs triumph again! Let’s see which opponent is awaiting us next.',
        'WMEventAdvQ4Sub1' => 'Well done! These are some pretty advanced tactics! Remember, you can see the order in which an opponent\'s skills will be removed in the tactical item’s tooltip.',
        'WMEventAdvQ5' => 'Unbelievable! You made it! We\'re through to the semi-finals and are amongst the four best teams in the competition!',
        'WMEventAdvQ6' => 'We\'re in the finals! I can\'t believe it! We reached the finals! What a match! I always hoped we\'d go far with this team, but to actually reach the finals!! I\'m thrilled!',
        'WMEventAdvQ7' => 'We did it! We are the champions! WE ARE THE CHAMPIONS! I cannot believe it! Champions…',
        'WM_Main' => 'Excellent! Now you know everything you need to know to be able to shine at the Settlers Football World Championship. I\'ve just announced our official participation. Let the matches begin!',
        'WM_Main02' => 'The last weeks have been very exciting, haven\'t they? I still can\'t believe that we actually won the finals.
I think you\'ve earned yourself the right to build a monument to commemorate our victory!',
        'WM_Sub01' => 'Well done! You reached level 16. This is our ticket to the World Championship!',
        'WM_Sub02' => 'Great! Come back here any time if there\'s anything else you want to know about the event.',
        'WM_Sub03' => 'So, this is the World Championship fixture list. You know where to find it, and how to use it. And now we have our first opponents! As a reward, you also get your first useful item: a Red Card!',
        'WM_Sub04' => 'Good work! Now let\'s finish that match!',
        'WM_Sub05' => 'Good work! Now you know everything about how to produce tactical tools and how to find the right resources.',
        'WM_Sub05a' => 'Well done! Bananas are used to produce the Foul item in the Provision House. Did we collect all the other remaining ingredients?',
        'WM_Sub05b' => 'Excellent! Wet Grass. The best way to produce a Foul in the Provision House.',
        'WM_Sub06' => 'Yes! Now that we have the Foul, we should return to the playing pitch.',
        'WM_Sub07' => 'You won your first match! Congratulations!',
        'WM_Sub08' => 'Congratulations! We won the first group stage match. If we can win the second one as well, we might advance to the last 16.',
        'WM_Sub09' => 'That was really a good performance! Thanks to your excellent tactics, it\'s now official: We reached the last 16!',
        'WM_Sub10' => 'What a thrilling match! I\'m glad we could beat the Shire of Oxwater – even if it was a close call. Let’s see which opponent is awaiting us next.',
        'WM_Sub11' => 'Unbelievable! You made it! With this victory we reached the semi-finals and are amongst the four best teams of the competition!',
        'WM_Sub12' => 'We\'re in the finals! I cannot believe it! We reached the finals! What a game! I always hoped we\'d go far with this team, but to actually reach the finals!! I am thrilled!',
        'WM_Sub13' => 'We did it! We are world champions! WE ARE WORLD CHAMPIONS! I cannot believe it! World champions…',
        'WM_Sub14' => 'Unbelievable! We won the tournament! We won, we won, WE WON!!! Congratulations, now we are officially the Settlers Football World Champions! We wooooooooooon!',
        'WeeklyChallange_Defence_ThirdRecruitment_lvl26' => 'That was a tough exercise for the conscripts, but they managed to learn everything.',
