        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_Legacy_Sub1' => 'Ancient buildings resemble the architecture of Rome itself. Restore their splendour and search for signs that the expedition finally reached its long-awaited destination.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_Legacy_Sub2' => 'A thriving colony has been discovered, founded by survivors of the expedition. Strengthen your own settlement to honour those who carved out a new home so far from Rome.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_Legacy_Sub3' => 'Octavianus\'s final journal is incomplete. Gather the resources needed to restore its damaged pages and reveal what became of the expedition\'s leader.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_Legacy_Sub4' => 'We gathered every surviving record of the expedition. Complete the final preparations and help preserve Octavianus\'s story for future generations.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Main' => 'The expedition ventured into waters no Roman map had ever shown. What happened there? Did Octavianus brave terrible storms, make unexpected discoveries, or even find new allies? Help me find out what shaped the fate of Octavianus and his companions.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Sub1' => 'The journal speaks of peaceful encounters with distant peoples. Gather valuable goods to honour the friendships that helped the expedition continue its journey.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Sub2' => 'A violent storm scattered the fleet across the open sea. Assemble the resources needed to prepare for such hardships and understand how the expedition endured.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Sub3' => 'Reports suggest several crews founded small settlements after the storm. Make your community thrive to honour those who refused to surrender.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Sub4' => 'A battered Roman standard has been found, a symbol that the expedition stood its ground even in desperate times. Prepare your forces to preserve its legacy.',
        'Birthday2018plus_LostExpedition_62-80_UnknownSeas_Sub5' => 'The last known route leads through a mountain pass. Clear the way and gather the materials needed to follow Octavianus beyond the natural barrier.',
        'BirthdayBasicsMain' => 'Hello there! Tee hee hee… Have you already heard about the big party coming up? The king himself has sent me to find out which server is the most suitable. So, help your server to become the best. How? Oh, it\'s easy. I will explain! Hee hee…',
        'BirthdayBasicsSub1' => 'It is all about gathering the most balloons! The king loves balloons you know. Tee hee… You can see the number of balloons you have in your mayor\'s house under the new event tab. Feel free to take a look.',
        'BirthdayBasicsSub2' => 'There are actions you can perform, which generate balloons with a certain percentage, for example using buffs. So go ahead - produce some buffs in your provision house and use them.',
        'BirthdayBasicsSub3' => 'Another great possibility is trade! Whether you\'re buying or selling, each completed transaction earns them. One remark: this only works for trades via the trade office, not with friends. Hee hee hee… so, what are you waiting for? Trade!',
        'BirthdayBasicsSub4' => 'When you have gathered some balloons, you have to donate them in order to make them count for your server. You can do this from your storage. Just click on the resource in your mayor house and choose to donate them. After that, you will see a window which looks similar to your trade window. Decide how much to donate, and confirm.',
        'BirthdayBasicsSub5' => 'Remember the control panel beneath your avatar? It\'s where you can turn the sound off. Tee hee hee... Click on it and you\'ll see a new button - the Event Window button. Open the Event Window and you\'ll see all necessary information about the event, including a button allowing you to see how the servers are performing.',
        'BirthdayMain' => 'Hello there. Your achievements are really impressive. Maybe you can help me. I have a little prob… eh… concern. Nothing serious, really, but I can\'t do it by myself. You will be rewarded, of course. I\'ll make it worth your while. Tee hee hee…',
        'BirthdaySub1' => 'While we take care of my tiny little issue, you should continue gathering and donating the balloons for our celebration party. At least when I choose your server. Tee hee hee…',
        'BirthdaySub2' => 'Have you already heard about the strange buildings appearing on other islands? I too have received strange messages from one of them, but it seems the problem there is a bit bigger. You should prepare an army to be ready for any situation.',
        'BirthdaySub3' => 'Well, the settler couldn\'t give me details, so I guess we\'ll have to check out the situation once we\'re there, but it seems it\'s something to do with buildings that look different from the others. Let\'s go and see what\'s happening.',
        'BirthdaySub4' => 'Some of the settlers from the adventure we were on have asked whether they can join you. It seems you made a pretty big impression. They will come to your island a few at a time, so just lean back and relax. Tee hee hee…',
        'BirthdaySub5' => 'Now that we have fresh settlers on the island, we can start training some new units. I\'ve found another island exhibiting this strange phenomenon. We should be prepared for anything.',
        'BirthdaySub6' => 'So, I was successful and found the map. We should get going as soon as possible. I\'m not sure what the problem is there, but I assume it can\'t really wait. Also, the faster we\'re done, the faster we can continue relaxing. Tee hee hee…',
        'BirthdaySub7' => 'Now that all the side effects of our party preparations have been dealt with, we can once again concentrate on gathering balloons. So, play and spend as much as possible. Make your server the winner!',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main1' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy and highly influential family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers. It appears that there are many benefits in it, both small and more substantial, for you and the Bonabertis alike. I highly recommend working together - the Bonabertis are well known for being very generous to their partners and friends.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main1_Sub1' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The first thing to do would be to trade some customs with them.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main1_Sub2' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family’s chief trader is not happy about how wool fares on the market. Please sell wool to other players to stimulate the market’s activity.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main1_Sub3' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family would love to get some insight into your military training. Please send them some of your military units.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main1_Sub4' => 'The Bonabertis need your help on one of their islands. Please play the adventure “Bonaberti Business”.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main2' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy and highly influential family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers. It appears that there are many benefits in it, both small and more substantial, for you and the Bonabertis alike. I highly recommend working together - the Bonabertis are well known for being very generous to their partners and friends.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main2_Sub1' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

Trade some more customs with them.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main2_Sub2' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family’s chief trader is not happy about how exotic planks fare on the market. Please sell exotic planks to other players to stimulate the market’s activity.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main2_Sub3' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family would love to get some insight into your military training. Please send them some of your military units.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main2_Sub4' => 'The Bonabertis need your help on one of their islands. Please play the adventure “Bonaberti Business”.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main3' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy and highly influential family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers. It appears that there are many benefits in it, both small and more substantial, for you and the Bonabertis alike. I highly recommend working together - the Bonabertis are well known for being very generous to their partners and friends.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main3_Sub1' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

Trade some more customs with them.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main3_Sub2' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family’s chief trader is not happy about how iron fares on the market. Please sell iron to other players to stimulate the market’s activity.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main3_Sub3' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family would love to get some insight into your military training. Please send them some of your military units.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main3_Sub4' => 'The Bonabertis need your help on one of their islands. Please play the adventure “Bonaberti Business”.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main4' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy and highly influential family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers. It appears that there are many benefits in it, both small and more substantial, for you and the Bonabertis alike. I highly recommend working together - the Bonabertis are well known for being very generous to their partners and friends.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main4_Sub1' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

Trade some more customs with them.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main4_Sub2' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family’s chief trader is not happy about how bread fares on the market. Please sell bread to other players to stimulate the market’s activity.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main4_Sub3' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy family from the islands in the far south, want to create and deepen a bilateral relationship with you and your settlers.

The family would love to get some insight into your military training. Please send them some of your military units.',
        'BonabertiConnection_Main4_Sub4' => 'The Bonabertis need your help on one of their islands. Please play the adventure “Bonaberti Business”.',
        'BonusAdvancedAForeignThreat' => 'There are rumors about a belligerent tribe on a nearby island who are on the brink of developing seafaring. Your settlers are afraid - reassure them of your army’s strength by training new elite soldiers!',
        'BonusAdvancedCloth' => 'Some of the soldiers are worried we might not have enough cloth! I think we should put their minds at rest, and produce more cloth, just to be on the safe side.',
        'BonusAdvancedEpicAdventureComplete' => 'The land of the fairies seems to be a perfect place to train our troops, and collect rare resources! Order your general to engage in more fairytale adventures!',
        'BonusAdvancedExoticPlank' => 'Now that we have plenty of exotic wood, you should order your settlers to prepare it! Have them make some exotic wood planks!',
        'BonusAdvancedExoticWoodProduce' => 'My lord must have noticed that the winds on these islands are much stronger than they should be. These winds may actually cause some damage to the buildings. I advise you to produce some more exotic wood that can be used for the eventual repairs.',
        'BonusAdvancedExoticWoodRefill' => 'I have bad news! There\'s been a fire in one of the exotic woods nearby. The woodcutter\'s requested our help! Refill the affected exotic wood deposits!',
        'BonusAdvancedFairytailAdventure' => 'We now have a map that shows us where the adventure is! Ready your general, and send him out to gather the precious resources!',
        'BonusAdvancedFairytailSearch' => 'These adventures are amazing! I think we should send our troops on regular adventures so they can train for battle against our enemies. But first things first: send out one of your explorers to find a fairytale epic adventure!',
        'BonusAdvancedFairytaleAdventure' => 'My lord! I have learned that there are many magical creatures out there. Would you be so kind as to take me on an adventure, so that I can see these creatures with my own eyes? Please, play a fairytale adventure.',
        'BonusAdvancedGraniteProduce' => 'Heavy wagons and horseshoes cause extensive damage to the roads we\'re using. There are already several holes already on the main roads that need filling! You should have your men produce more granite!',
        'BonusAdvancedLetFlowersSpeak' => '“Oh my darling, I love sunflowers so much! Make sure that we never run out of them, and my love will always be yours!” You\'d better stock up on that fertilizer!',
        'BonusAdvancedMahoganyPlank' => 'I know I keep saying it, but mahogany is very rare! Therefore, I would advise you to engage in more adventures and gather more mahogany wood!',
        'BonusAdvancedMahoganyWood' => 'I see your men at the sawmill were impressed by the quality of the mahogany wood. Do not let them down - have them produce more mahogany planks!',
        'BonusAdvancedMajorGeneral' => 'Armies are lead by captains and generals, but who knows what names they have in other lands? Your army needs a major general, so it would be best to send for one!',
        'BonusAdvancedMoreNewWeapons' => 'Our army needs to use real weapons for their training, and with all the adventures we\'ve been going on, there\'s a small chance that the weapons may be unusable once the troops have returned. To avoid any awkward situations, I would suggest we make an extra order of weapons!',
        'BonusAdvancedOiledMachine' => 'True friends always make sure things are running smoothly, not only for themselves, but for each other. Use machine oil on a friend’s island.',
        'BonusAdvancedPlatinumOreSearch' => 'I had a word with your alchemist, and he shared his concerns with me. Apparently, he thinks that the platinum we\'re mining is not of the best quality. He says he\'s heard that there\'s a deposit of perfect quality platinum out there. I think you should send out one of your explorers on an epic treasure search so he can look for that special platinum ore.',
        'BonusAdvancedPlatinumProduce' => 'We have a new master at the storehouse. While he was doing his first inspection, he found that our platinum supplies were running low. I think it\'s time to produce more platinum ore.',
        'BonusAdvancedPrincessAdventure' => 'Your generals have been in many battles, but I heard that there is one more adventure that\'s worth trying. Return to the deserts and complete the final "1001 Nights" Adventure.',
        'BonusAdvancedSaddleCloth' => 'A horseman pointed out that it\'s very important to have saddles of all shapes and sizes. They have small horses and big horses, after all… I think we should produce more saddle cloth!',
        'BonusAdvancedSalpeterProduce' => 'Our miners use dynamite and all other kinds of explosives to dig deeper into their mines. Just to be sure, have your men produce some saltpetre, so if there\'s need for more gunpowder, your alchemists can make it quickly. Produce saltpetre!',
        'BonusAdvancedStory01' => 'I believe I\'ve told you about my trades with the most honoured King Schahri already! Every year I send him a gift to show him my gratitude. But this year I have nothing! I beg you, my lord, help me! I have to send him three items! One of them is a silver hunter gun. I have the gun recovered, but I will need quality gunpowder! Refill a saltpetre deposit and then upgrade your saltpetre mines so we get the best quality!',
        'BonusAdvancedStory02' => 'My friend, King Schahri is a man of a thousand tastes. He loves good food more than anything! I have met your Aunt Irma, and her cooking is out of this world! I would like to ask you to have her produce some food for me, as a gift - the famous Aunt Irma\'s Baskets!',
        'BonusAdvancedStory03' => 'The third gift I want to send to King Schahri is a bit complicated. It\'s not a something - it\'s a somebody. I usually send him some of my best fighters to serve at the king\'s court as bodyguards! Could my lord spare some of his knights? Train them so one day we can send them to the king!',
        'BonusAdvancedStory04' => 'My lord, my eyes have seen wonderful places and people. I\'ve travelled the world, seen the snowy fields of the north and the mountains to the east. I\'ve seen the jungles of the west and the deserts of the south. In each of these countries, each of their capitals had a so called "royal neighbourhood". If you want King Schahri to consider visiting us, we should build a royal neighbourhood too. Have your settlers build manors, and make sure they\'re upgraded accordingly.',
        'BonusAdvancedStory05' => 'King Schahri is here! I will personally make sure his needs are tended to! After all, I know how to treat royalty! The king\'s first wish is to visit the most expensive looking place we have! I think a gold mine fits the bill! Select a gold mine for the king to visit, but make sure it\'s upgraded!',
        'BonusAdvancedStory06' => 'My lord! Before agreeing to be our friend and ally, the king would like to see how generous you are! I think the best way is to prepare some gifts for your friends! Let the king see how generous you are, prepare some buffs and help out your friends.',
        'BonusAdvancedTailorAdventure' => 'I heard there\'s a land far away, where there\'s a man who can create the most unique garments in the whole empire. I would like to ask you to send me, along with your general, on the tailor adventure!',
        'BonusAdvancedTaskComplete' => 'I have spoken with the captain from the ship. He\'s challenged us to complete a certain number of tasks! I love a challenge! Accept and complete tasks.',
        'BonusAdvancedTheGreatestGood' => 'As a very intelligent man once said: “Education is the most powerful weapon which you can use to change the world.” Make sure that you make good use of it.',
        'BonusAdvancedTheLocustPlague' => 'A severe and totally unexpected locust plague is threatening to destroy your wheat fields. Your settlers are in a panic, and are calling for you to help. Fortunately, your best scientist has worked out a formula for a highly effective insecticide. You should provide the necessary materials as soon as possible.',
        'BonusAdvancedTitaniumProduce' => 'Eh? The latest report from the storehouse claims we\'re low on titanium! But this cannot be! Have your settlers produce more titanium!',
        'BonusAdvancedWoodcutterAdventure' => 'My lord! Have you ever heard of the land of endless deserts? There are many mysteries between the dunes, and many treasures to be found! I urge you to send your generals into the adventure of the 1001 nights!',
        'BonusAdvancedWool' => 'You know, my family had a very costly habit: they liked to coat everything in gold. I know it sounds silly, but… when I was a child, I had a woolen blanket that was coloured gold. It reminds me of my dear mother. Can you produce some more wool please?',
        'BuccaneerRoundupQ1' => 'We made landfall, now we must be swift!
Strike at the pirate forts and their barricades will fall. If you all work together, you can clear a way to the cove!',
        'BuccaneerRoundupQ2' => 'The Red Ship is here! And it\'s moored for repairs at the docks. What a great opportunity! 
Make haste, torch every hut in your path, and burn the ship to the ground. This will be a heavy blow to the pirate activity in these seas!',
        'BuffAd4_Construction_Area_Sub2' => 'Before we can construct our mining post, we\'ll have to clear some space. At the moment, there\'s just no room for construction. Let\'s get rid of some trees and stones.',
        'BuffAd4_Miner_Catering_Sub5' => 'Good stuff! The miners are hard at work, and everything\'s going according to plan. However, they\'ll soon need some food and support. We\'re still working on a food supply line, but could you help bring the first provisions?

Hint: If you\'ve already applied the food provision, wait 10 minutes, then you can apply them a second time.',
        'BuffAd4_Mining_Post_Sub3' => 'This is the important bit. With the ground cleared, we can build the outpost. Please provide us with a tavern, a storehouse and some masons.',
        'BuffAd4_Opening_the_Shaft_Sub4' => 'Most of the ore is hidden deep in the mountain. That means we\'ll need to make a hole in the mountain, and we\'ll need something to stabilize the hole, so that mountain doesn\'t collapse.',
        'BuffAd4_Proof_of_Purity_Sub1' => 'I\'m glad we have you on board! We need to check the quality of the ore on this island. Take a look around, and let\'s find some sample mountain ore.',
        'BuffAd4_Riches_of_the_Mountain_Main1' => 'Hello there! I\'m glad you agreed to help us! Allow me to introduce myself - my name\'s Oliver, and I\'m the mining supervisor. Still, there\'s no time to waste - let\'s get stuck in!

Hint: All required buffs can be produced in the provision house.',
        'BuffAd4_Sabotage_Sub6' => 'We have a problem. A nearby village sent some forces to sabotage our mining efforts. Please, stop them, before they can do us any harm or everything we\'ve achieved here will have been in vain!',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Main' => 'This must be the place. According to the people of this land, the Dragon calls itself Flafir. Could it be the same Flafir who terrorized these islands a hundred years ago? Incredible!
As much as I want to study a live dragon, I\'m afraid we cannot tolerate the destruction he is wreaking.',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Sub1' => 'The island is teeming with the Flafir\'s minions. Not only does his presence corrupt the wildlife, but he\'s even amassed a following of cultists! Who would be crazy enough to worship a dragon? You\'ll have to fight them to get to Flafir.',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Sub2' => 'Flafir is clever. His lair is at the top of the highest mountain, and your army\'s path is blocked by many obstacles.
We\'ll need bridges to get through the swamp. We can find the basic materials here, but you\'ll have to use some of your own resources as well. 
The path up the mountain is littered with large boulders. Nothing that some strong soldiers with pickaxes can\'t handle, but you\'ll need to supply said pickaxes.',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Sub3' => 'If this really is the same Flafir from a hundred years ago, then the legends speaking of dragons\' immortality must be true! Which presents something of a problem for us. However, I did some research on local folklore, and might have found a way to slay one for good - a sword enchanted according to a specific ritual. The main ingredient, the dragonsbane herb, grows on this very island.',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Sub4' => 'It is time to face Flafir himself. I won\'t lie, I\'m actually kind of excited to see him. Don\'t let yourself be intimidated though - he may be an incredible sight, but he\'s still the enemy!',
        'BuffAd_Dragons_Roost_Sub5' => 'Your scouts have returned. The dragon is lying dormant in a cave that was hidden behind the castle. That must be why he hasn\'t been seen in over a hundred years after he was believed to be slain.
Do you have the enchanted sword on you? With it, you can end his tyranny for real this time.',
        'BuffAd_HeartOfTheWoods_Main' => 'I\'m glad you\'ve answered our call for help. This sickness has infested the forest, and it keeps spreading. It seems to be coming from the center of the forest, where the heart tree, the magical tree that keeps everything green, has started to wither. We need to treat all the trees and animals, before they all die out!

Hint: All required buffs can be produced in the provision house.',
        'BuffAd_HeartOfTheWoods_Sub1' => 'The sickness from the woods is spreading to the local wildlife. Some of the animals are so sick that they can\'t even find the strength to leave their caves!
We need to feed them up, so that they can build up their strength. 

I know of a special medicinal plant you can find on our island. Gather it, and use it to make some animal feed, so we can treat the animals in those caves.',
        'BuffAd_HeartOfTheWoods_Sub2' => 'Most of the living things on our island depend on the magic of the heart tree. 
You\'ve probably seen this massive tree in the middle of the forest. That is the heart tree, a plant that brings life to the forest itself.

While you were away taking care of the animals, we found the cause of the disease. Our heart tree is ill, and now, rather than life, it\'s been spreading its disease to the other trees. We need to cure it.

We need to gather some special flowers and make a potion that might revive it.',
        'BuffAd_HeartOfTheWoods_Sub3' => 'Now that the heart tree has been healed, we need to take care of the other trees. Especially some of the older ones. They will not be able to recover all by themselves. 

You\'ll have to use the heart fruits from the heart tree to rejuvenate them.',
        'BuffAd_HeartOfTheWoods_Sub4' => 'Sadly, some of the trees were too far gone, and could not be saved. Could you please cut them down? Maybe we can at least find a good use for their wood. 
We could use the dead wood to make some special fertilizer that should strengthen the heart tree for the future.',
        'BuffAd_Lost_City_Main' => 'Have you heard the ancient stories about the grand City of Glory? All my research regarding its location points to this very island. But except for some altars and the odd building, there is no trace of it to be found.
Let us not give up too easy though. We will unearth the truth, and get access to the city\'s secrets together!',
        'BuffAd_Lost_City_Sub1' => 'Bandits have set up camp on the island, and have been interfering with our research. We won\'t be able to properly investigate until we take care of them.',
        'BuffAd_Lost_City_Sub2' => 'Have you noticed the altars scattered around the island? No wonder the bandits seem drawn to them. They seem to hold some sort of mysterious power. If we were to perform the proper rites at one of them, it could make it easier to liberate the others.
Clear all bandits from a site\'s sector, produce the proper ritual item and offer it at the altar. You won\'t be disappointed!',
        'BuffAd_Lost_City_Sub3' => 'I\'ve had another look at the old reports and tales about the City of Glory. It should be located at the center of this island, but alas, there is nothing to be seen there but the desert.
The only explanation I can come up with is that it must be buried beneath the sand. So, let\'s grab some shovels and get digging!',
        'BuffAd_Lost_City_Sub4' => 'The glyphs hint that there\'s some sort of a connection between the six altars... If I understand this correctly, you have to activate all of them. Once that is taken care of, I will be able to lift the wards.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Main' => 'Come, allow me to introduce you to an unusual acquaintance I made the last time I traveled to this island. This is King Roxy, ghost musician extraordinaire!
When we first met, I helped him and his spectral band perform their songs again

Unfortunately, it seems their ghostly status has given their music some unintended qualities, and it\'s brought a curse upon the island! Fog has engulfed us, the sun has not risen in weeks, and all sorts of mishaps are befalling the populace.

However, legend speaks of a magic song hidden somewhere on this island - the "Serenade of Joy". If they were to perform this melodic masterpiece, I\'m sure we could break the curse and restore the island to how it was.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub1' => 'We have no clue as to the whereabouts of this song. We should ask the people who live in the town in the center of the island.

It looks like the guards are on edge though... We might have to overpower them for them to let us in. I will tell your men to avoid lethal force.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2' => 'Bad news - it looks like the song has been somewhat scattered around. In fact, single pages have been passed down through the families of the composer and original performers. 

I have identified the individuals who own the pages now, but they aren\'t willing to part with them for free. Maybe we can help them out in some way, and ask for the sheets in exchange?
I don\'t think we need all of them. King Roxy used to be a talented composer himself. He should be able to fill in some of the blanks if we jog his memory.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Cultists' => 'The local priest is concerned about the cultists that, lured by the dark energies unleashed by the curse, have landed on the northern shore and started manipulating the local bandits. They perform all sorts of hideous rituals at their twisted place of worship.
The town\'s church treasury holds two pages of the Serenade of Joy, and the priest is willing to part with them provided you disband the evil cult.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Forest' => 'The Woodson siblings are running the community\'s wood industry, but they\'ve been hit by the curse in more than one way. Woodcutter Jane misplaced her axe, John\'s sawmill\'s saw has rusted away, and forester Toby claims that the soil has been sapped of all nutrients. And as if that wasn\'t enough, the forest has been overrun by some unnaturally aggressive predators!

The Woodsons have promised to hand over their family\'s page of the Serenade of Joy if you can help them out.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Hermit' => 'An old hunter claims that he has a page of the song in his hut on the south-eastern shore. We can keep the page if we defeat the bandits who drove him out of his home.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Ruins1' => 'The curse hit a small fishing hamlet on the south-western coast particularly hard. The buildings crumbled as if they were ancient. 
The fishermen had to withdraw to this town, and lost their livelihoods in the process. One of them owns a page of the Serenade, and will part with it if we help to rebuild the village.

However, it looks like a band of low-life bandits have turned the ruins into their base!',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Ruins2' => 'This place is even more wrecked than I\'d thought. You\'ll have to rebuild it from the ground up. They can make do with only the most essential buildings for now, though.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub2_Scraps' => 'Due to a bout of bad luck, one page was blown away by a chill wind when the curse set upon the island. It was seen getting torn to shreds by a pack of wolves. 
The pieces have probably been scattered all over the island by now - and that\'s if they haven\'t been lost to the sea already.',
        'BuffAd_Of_Songs_And_Curses_Sub3' => 'King Roxy lets you know that he has studied the Serenade and managed to fill in the blanks suitably

He also said that if they are going to perform a legendary, magic song, we might as well assemble an audience. It’s not even a joke; the magic will allegedly be more potent the more people listen to the song!',
        'BuffAd_Raid_of_the_Nords_Main' => 'Look at all this destruction! The Nords have gone too far this time! I\'ve spoken to the chief of the native villages, and he says the raiders stopped at nothing. They destroyed the people\'s dwellings, plundered their winter stocks and are now hunting the wildlife for sport.
If you don\'t step in, the natives are doomed.',
        'BuffAd_Raid_of_the_Nords_Sub1' => 'The Nords have built encampments all around the coast. Before we can fix the damage they\'ve done, you must send them off the island.',
        'BuffAd_Raid_of_the_Nords_Sub2' => 'You\'ve dealt the Nords a heavy blow, but they refuse to surrender. They have taken refuge on their ships and continue to take potshots and send raiding parties.
Lucky for us, the ships appear to be laden with black powder. If a lone saboteur can sneak on board, he may be able to set fire to them, and detonate them. 
I have a design for a timed fuse that will ensure the saboteur\'s safety. You\'ll need to provide some metal from your own storage, and collect some of the highly flammable wood found on this island.',
        'BuffAd_Raid_of_the_Nords_Sub3' => 'Good news! The ships were carrying the pelts of the animals the Nords had slaughtered. We can use those to repair the villagers\' tents. The bad news is that the explosions scattered them all over the island…',
        'BuffAd_Raid_of_the_Nords_Sub4' => 'The natives are on the brink of starvation, but the wildlife needs time to recover from the Nords\' thoughtless poaching. I\'m afraid their survival hinges on your generosity.',
        'BuffAd_SafeTheTowns_Main' => 'The guilds in both towns used to share their grain harvest. 
They used to meet in the Grain House to negotiate and distribute it equally - but one day, an argument began over who\'d produced the best products, and who deserved the most grain. Since that day, the Grain House has gone unused, and each guild has simply fought to keep the most grain.
Maybe you can help the two guilds to re-enter negotiations?

Hint: All required buffs can be produced in the provision house.',
        'BuffAd_SafeTheTowns_Sub1' => 'Oh, hi there! I\'m the administrator of this estate... or what\'s left of it. It was me who called you here for help!
Those stubborn Grain Islanders - bakers, brewers, the lot of \'em - have been driving me insane!
They used to negotiate the grain split here, but they can\'t do much more than bicker recently...

If we want to get them back at the table and start negotiating again, we need to fix up this... place...
I wouldn\'t mind seeing the old place tarted up a bit either...',
        'BuffAd_SafeTheTowns_Sub2' => 'Alrighty then! Now that we have a place where we can sit the brewers and bakers back together again, we get to the most delicate part:
Actually getting them here in the first place!
I\'ll leave it up to your expert negotiation skills to convince each party to come back to the table. The origin of all this fighting is that each party claimed they would create the best product. We need a ruse to get them back at the table:

Help me produce some bread and beer. Then, all we need to do is to feed it to the opposing party, and sell it like it was yours! If they love it like I think they will, we\'ll just tell them the truth - that this kind of quality has been on that island all along!',
        'BuffAd_SafeTheTowns_Sub3' => 'Alright then! We\'ve got everybody coming to the Grain House\'s reopening. This time, I really want to make sure that everything goes smoothly... No, not just smoothly! Everything needs to be perfect!
Nobody likes to negotiate on an empty stomach. Thus, I was wondering if you could delight us with a specialty of your own kingdom?',
        'BuffAd_twins_Main' => 'Thank you for the help. However, I did have another urgent task. Two children from our town are missing. They\'re twins and were last seen yesterday. We have a big, dangerous swamp nearby, and we\'re worried they may have strayed nearby... You have to find them!

Hint: All required buffs can be produced in the provision house.',
        'BuffAd_twins_Sub1' => 'First of all, we need to create a safe path for our rescue team. There aren\'t too many areas of firm ground in the swamp. Please, set up bridges over these impassable areas, so that our rescue team can cross the swamp.',
        'BuffAd_twins_Sub2' => 'While the search patrols are combing the area, we should check with the villagers to see if anyone\'s seen something. Let\'s make some broadsheets and ask around. Maybe we\'ll get lucky?!

Hint: If you\'ve already applied the broadsheets, wait 10 minutes, then you can apply them a second time.',
        'BuffAd_twins_Sub3' => 'We found them! Thanks to the hints, we managed to find the twins - but they\'re trapped in an old ruin within the swamps and cannot come out on their own. Please, help the patrol get them out of there.',
        'BuffAdv_El_Chupacabra_Main' => 'The Chupacabra is a creature that I\'ve long thought was a myth. Dog-like in appearance, it is said to spread a curse that turns even the most mild-mannered people into frenzied berserkers.
The beast seems to have made its lair in a cave at the center of the jungle. Get there and take it out!',
        'BuffAdv_El_Chupacabra_Sub1' => 'The natives have erected palisades to trap the Chupacabra and stop the madness from spreading. However, it looks like it was too little too late.
The island\'s whole population has been affected, and they won\'t let us approach the monster\'s cave safely. We have no choice but to clear the whole sector of them if we want to reach the Chupacabra.
Your soldiers have been instructed not to use lethal force. But could there be way to handle the situation without fighting them at all?',
        'BuffAdv_El_Chupacabra_Sub2' => 'The Chupacabra and the pack of wolves he leads are hiding in that large cave right ahead of us. 
You know what you have to do to end this nightmare.',
        'BuffAdv_El_Chupacabra_Sub3' => 'You know, I noticed something about the apes you were fighting just now. While they fought fiercely, they did not appear to be affected by the Chupacabra\'s curse.
Could the key to a cure lie in their diet? They mainly feed on the mushrooms that grow between the roots of those large trees they inhabit. 
If we defeat more apes and collect enough mushrooms, we might be able to produce medicine for the natives!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Main1' => 'The fisherman\'s wife, blinded by power, has gone completely mad. She\'s used her newfound influence to seize control of this island, and has devised plans to take over other lands too! He laments that it\'s not the Ilsebille he married. We must stop her!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Sub1' => 'Ever since Ilsebille became the queen, the wildlife has become even more hostile. They\'re not going to make reaching the castle any easier... I suspect that Ilsebille may have obtained even darker powers, and is influencing them somehow.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Sub2' => 'The leader of the huntsmen works for Ilsebille, and he\'s guarding the pond where the cursed prince is. If we are to have a chance of defeating the Queen, we need to save the prince!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Sub3' => 'The only way we can be completely sure that the prince will be safe from his wife is if we can break the curse. He says that the only way to do that is to use a very specific potion, made using some herbs that can be found nearby. Let\'s get to it.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Sub4' => 'The prince is extremely grateful for your efforts in lifting the curse. Unfortunately, there is no time to rejoice. The curse may be gone, but so too are his powers, which were reducing her influence! If we are to stop her, we need to press forward to her castle!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Fisherman_Sub5' => 'The Queen is trenched up with the remainder of her forces in this area, and did not reply to our surrender request. There\'s no other way - we\'ll have to take it by force.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Main1' => 'The woodcutter is very worried about his children. He needs our help! We must be ready for anything. Who knows what we\'ll encounter in this dark forest?',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub1' => 'In order to find the missing children, our engineers have devised a detector that can locate the white pebbles that Hansel has been leaving. We\'ll need to provide him with the correct materials to create it.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub2' => 'It seems the wildlife in the area has suddenly become more aggressive... There may be no choice but to make our way through the forest by force.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub3' => 'Our scouts have discovered a suspicious gingerbread house. We heard strange noises coming from within, and suspect that the children are trapped inside!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub4' => 'The Dark Cult? Something\'s fishy... These guys mean trouble, and, if my suspicion\'s correct, something much more terrible awaits us inside. Prepare your troops!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub5' => 'The woodcutter is relieved that the children are safe, but unfortunately, the problem persists. He\'s not a hunter, so the need for food is a real problem for him and his family. Let\'s hunt some animals for them and provide them with some sustenance!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Hansel_Gretel_Sub6' => 'As I suspected... It\'s her! Queen Ilsebille is here! She\'s the one that brought the Dark Cult here! This may be our only chance to capture the Queen and end this all. Let\'s plan our attack! We must succeed!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Piper_of_Hamelin_Main1' => 'We\'ve received a message that the Evil Queen has been here causing trouble. However, the scouts report there\'s been no sign of her. No matter. This region is in trouble, and it\'s our duty to help them out!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Piper_of_Hamelin_Sub1' => 'The town of Hamelin is being plagued by rats! Apparently, the inhabitants hired a specialist to get rid of the pests with an enchanted flute, but it seems he was double-crossed by the mayor, and is now refusing to cooperate. Maybe we can have a go? Let\'s clear them out!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Piper_of_Hamelin_Sub2' => 'We spotted the disgruntled piper in one of the caves. It seems unleashing the rats wasn\'t good enough, so he kidnapped the children of Hamelin as well! This is a line that should never be crossed. We must help those children!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Piper_of_Hamelin_Sub3' => 'With the pest problem solved, I thought that we should pay a visit to the mayor and demand an explanation. Unfortunately, he seems to have deployed his military in order to deny us entry! Something fishy is going on, and we must get to the bottom of it. Push forward!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Piper_of_Hamelin_Sub4' => 'The closer we get to the city hall, the more people I hear asking if we came "to save them from the mayor". Strange. Most of these citizens claim that the mayor had always been nice, up until now. It\'s time we confront the mayor, and figure out what\'s going on.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Main1' => 'We caught wind that the Evil Queen Ilsebille has established herself on this island. Once again, we must resolve the situation, and ensure her actions cause no harm to the inhabitants of this region.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Sub1' => 'It looks like we\'re on the right track. The wildlife in this area seems more aggressive than usual, which is very likely related to her dark presence. We must make our way through!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Sub2' => 'The girl says that a big, bad wolf had tricked her grandma and eaten her, and was planning to do the same to Red! A passing lumberjack said that we may be able to get grandma out of the wolf\'s belly, but we\'ll have to find something to fill the wolf\'s stomach with. I know! Some heavy rocks should do!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Sub3' => 'Grandma has seen things that would have broken stronger folk. She\'s a real trooper. However, she\'s still extremely nervous, and is refusing to talk. My own grandma gave me a recipe for a relaxing tea made with grated heart fruit core. Maybe this will help her regain her composure?',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Sub4' => 'The Dark Cult is supporting Queen Ilsebille\'s evil deeds. She must have promised them power, riches, or something even darker. We have to get our troops moving towards the Queen\'s castle, and we must not let the Dark Cult stand in our way!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Red_Riding_Hood_Sub5' => 'The Queen lies in wait in her castle, readying her final defence. Tell our generals to prepare for battle. We must not give her the chance to escape!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Main1' => 'The Queen has decreed that she wants to be considered the fairest maiden in all of the land - and, in order to achieve that goal, she intends to murder her beautiful, innocent step-daughter Snow White. It seems that Queen Ilsebille is not the only one who deserves to be called an "Evil Queen". This will not be tolerated!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Sub1' => 'Snow White was last seen around the forest, but it\'s dangerous for her to go around alone. The wildlife has been unusually aggressive lately. We need to find her!',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Sub2' => 'He doesn\'t seem to be willing to stop, but I have the feeling that deep down, he\'s a good person. The Dark Cult has been spotted nearby, probably keeping an eye on him. We need to clear this area.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Sub3' => 'Snow White has found shelter in a little hut in the forest, inhabited by seven dwarfs. The dwarfs have promised to protect her with their lives, but they\'ve asked for us to take care of the pest problem they\'ve been having in their houses in return.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Sub4' => 'Snow White\'s stepmother will definitely try again, unless we do something about it. Sometimes the best defence is a good offence. If we clear this land of Dark Cultists, we will have a clear path to the Queen\'s castle.',
        'BuffAdv_Evil_Queen_Snow_White_Sub5' => 'The path is now clear, and the Queen has been barricaded inside her castle, along with the final remnants of the Dark Cult. Gather your troops once more, and let\'s put an end to this absurd affair.',
        'BuffAdv_OneStepAhead_Main' => 'Alright, we\'ve reached our destination. Your navigators have taken a look at my maps and confirmed that this is the only island at which the pirates\' fleet can restock. 
As you know, their ships are laden with treasure that belongs to your allies - and probably that of other parties, too.
We shall reclaim it and return it to its rightful owners.',
        'BuffAdv_OneStepAhead_Sub1' => 'The sailors encamped on the island bear the same emblems as the pirates we were told of. First, let us take care of their leaders. Not only will that teach them a lesson, but they may also reveal some details of the rendezvous with the fleet.',
        'BuffAdv_OneStepAhead_Sub2' => 'If we want to get the jump on the ships, we must know the exact time and place they\'ll be docking. 
If we piece together whatever information we can get out of the sailors\' leaders, we should be able to surprise and board them.',
        'BuffAdv_OneStepAhead_Sub3' => 'Now that we know when and where to expect the ship in the harbor, we can engage its crew in combat before they even land. They won\'t know what\'s hit them.',
        'BuffAdv_OneStepAhead_Sub4' => 'Looks like that ship\'s load is already equivalent to what was taken from your friends. However, the fleet is larger than that, and if you want to reclaim all the stolen treasure, feel free to attack all four ships. The rightful owners of the treasure will be grateful, I\'m sure.',
        'BuffAdv_SplitCityFall_Sub1' => 'Let\'s get to it. We\'ll go about this in much the same way as last time. It seems the land hasn\'t changed all that much since last we were here.
Apparently, there are many underground caves and waterways which the people use for hiding. But not all of them are safe. In some, the evil creatures roam like moths to the flame, while others stay completely untouched. But what\'s the difference? Again, the closer to the town you go, the more concentrated the evil becomes. I will have to investigate this situation thoroughly once the area has been cleared.',
        'BuffAdv_SplitCityFall_Sub2' => 'Our enemies are, once again, seemingly randomly cobbled together. They don\'t seem to know what it is they are looking for. They just push relentlessly towards the city, as if infected by some kind of disease. But why aren\'t we affected as well? Or... maybe... are we affected too? I mean, we are also pushing towards the city. And yes, we have a goal, but... is there something more to it?
Or is the reason these bandits go berserk coming from somewhere else? Hmm... There are apes hailing from far-away jungles. There are bandits from the desert that usually stay outside of the city, but when they get close enough, they are drawn here. And also Vikings? What is the connection between them? This is driving me crazy. Ohh... I have to calm down... Excuse me...',
        'BuffAdv_SplitCity_Sub1' => 'First, we need to get further inland and close in on both sides of the city.

All this trouble apparently began roughly a decade ago, when a landslide split their city in two. Nowadays, the two halves of the former city have to use boats if they want to get together or share resources. The ground where the landslide occurred is too unstable to cross. They don\'t want to leave their homes, but now they\'re on the verge of obliteration, and they need our help to survive.

Defeat the foes on the way to the village, and be prepared for some unusual encounters.',
        'BuffAdv_SplitCity_Sub2' => 'Have you noticed the strange mix of enemies we\'re encountering? It doesn\'t look like they have a clear leader who strategically arranges the troops in each camp. It looks like they just... I don\'t know... like they just banded together on their way to the city. I also don\'t get why they aren\'t attacking each other? Thugs and wild animals unite to attack a harmless, impoverished and secluded city without harming the inhabitants? Sure...

Well, at least our task is clear. Defeat the enemies on our way to the city.',
        'BuffAdv_TF_Introduction_Main1' => 'Welcome to Puerto Sombrío. I heard that your local spy has not reported back for a while... There\'s not much to the island except for a small port - and yet its governor seems to be living the good life.
Something shady is going on here, and we will find out what it is!',
        'BuffAdv_TF_Introduction_Sub1' => 'Apparently, the governor has hired a load of thugs to guard the route to his mansion and the harbour. You\'ll have to fight your way through if we want to find your subject.',
        'BuffAdv_TF_Introduction_Sub2' => 'Do you see those stone towers that are blocking the way? They\'re certainly well-guarded - but that\'s not our only problem. Your enemies have smartened up, and have locked the doors! You should be able to craft some lockpicks in your provision house though. 
Let\'s open those gates and conquer the watchtowers!',
        'BuffAdv_TF_Introduction_Sub3' => 'The spy must be being held in the mansion. If we beat up the governor\'s guards, I\'m sure we\'ll find he can be persuaded to let your man go.
I cannot wait to hear what your spy has learned!',
        'BuffAdv_TF_Introduction_Sub4' => 'The spy found several clues about the docking schedule. You can collect his findings by the ruins of the mansion. There may be even more clues scattered around the island. If you can find them and piece them together at your Provision House, we can get the jump on the ships at the northern piers.
Intercepting one of them should be enough to teach them a lesson. But why stop at one when we can get our hands on two?',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Main1' => 'An unknown village was shortly visible when we flew over the Mountain Range. Due to this unusually dense fog, we couldn\'t make out who they were. But maybe they know something about the mysterious Mountain Clan. 

One of our scouts has reported the village is surrounded by bandits and closed off by barricades. A voice over the barricades told us to get rid of the bandits if we want to meet with them.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Main2' => 'One step forward, two steps back. To progress any further, we will have to build some sturdy bridges. Our new friends told us the path into the mountains should be located to the northeast of the village. But where do the other paths lead? As knowledge is power, maybe we should check out the other paths as well...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Side1' => 'With my spyglasses, I can make out the ruins of what might have been a flourishing village decades ago. Let\'s take a closer look - we might discover something useful.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Side2' => 'Some abandoned houses and remnants of fields are visible between the trees. What information could this place be hiding?',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_SideSub1' => 'If we decide to prolong our stay and explore the region further, we\'ll have to repair the bridge first.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_SideSub2' => 'Wild creatures inhabit the ruins now, and they don\'t look too friendly. If we even want to try and gain some knowledge of the Mountain Clan, we\'ll have to deal with the wildlife first.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_SideSub3' => 'Repair the bridge or don\'t repair the bridge. For me, that\'s not a question. I want to see what we can discover! But in the end, it\'s your choice!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_SideSub4' => 'This area was abandoned some time ago. Long enough for the wildlife to move in and get in our way, anyway... Let\'s clear the ruins!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub1' => 'Groups of Nord bandits have settled around the foot of the mountains. If we want to explore the region, we\'ll have to get past them. We\'d better be careful though - those long beards look like they could be hiding extra weapons!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub2' => 'The people here seem to stem from a totally different Nord tribe, and welcomed us to their town of Varaldsvik. After we freed them from the Bandits they lost their initial reluctance. They say they are willing to assist us, but they need our help first. We have agreed to rebuild their village - and in return, they will provide us with all the information and help they can offer.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub3' => 'Now that the people of Varaldsvik have become our friends, they have entrusted us with the key to the path up north. We were told not to let any bandits through the gate when we depart, and to be especially careful not to let any "dreadful creatures" through. They seemed to be even more frightened of the creatures than the bandits. I wonder why that is...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub4' => 'Those caves over there are emitting a very strong smell. I believe we should approach them carefully. There was a time when I studied the smells of hundreds of animals and beasts, and came to the conclusion that the stronger the smell, the higher the danger. But this particular smell, I do not recognize.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub5' => 'This region apparently hasn\'t seen a carpenter in a while. In order to proceed, we\'ll have to build a sturdy bridge that can withstand both the cold, and the strong winds here. The Nords village will benefit if we reconstruct the bridges here - and with their newly built smith, they\'ve provided us with the right materials for the job.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V1_Sub6' => 'Something seems definitely off with this group of bandits. How do they even survive surrounded by these beasts? We should approach them carefully to avoid running into a trap!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Main' => 'We are woefully unprepared for this weather! And it looks like it\'ll get even worse farther north. . Apparently, these local phenomena even affect the performance of your troops! I\'ve summarized the effects in your zone-wide buff window.

Our objective, for now, seems clear: find the proper equipment, possibly from the locals, and get out of this valley safely. Just keep in mind that we can only carry up to 3 types of equipment at max.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Optional' => 'There are enough beasts and pelts around that we can begin trading with a third village. The weather\'s not going to get any better on this campaign of yours, believe me.

You should consider your options before you defeat those bandits and continue your journey.

If you rush forward without setting up trade with a third village, you\'ll face a tougher challenge further up the mountains - but on the plus side, your senses will sharpen, resulting in higher rewards from any subsequent mountain ventures!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_OptionalSub1' => 'If you need more equipment, you\'ll have to pay a visit to another village. I\'m sure they\'ll appreciate us getting rid of the beasts too.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Sub1' => 'Well met, strangers! Found yourself in a bit of trouble, eh? It\'s pretty apparent you have no idea how to survive up here. What you really need is some Nord-made gear.

I\'m just a lone hermit, but the villages nearby trade gear all the time.

Gullhaugr produces Snow Shoes, Sjorheimr offers Spikes for your boots, Skaustad makes Warm Clothes, and Jarnbu is famous for its Snow Goggles.

You\'ll want to get at least two of those for your army, or you\'re gonna send them to their certain death.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Sub2' => 'Before you can deal with the villages, you\'ll have to get to them. As you can see, the valley is filled with vicious beasts. 

The villainous Mountain Clan sends them down to torment us other Nords folk every so often, but these numbers are unusual and concerning...

Anyhoo, visibility is bad, so I\'m afraid you\'ll have to clear the area sector by sector to see what\'s up ahead.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Sub3' => 'If you want to survive the north, you\'ll need more than one type of equipment. 
You should visit another village to get more. Hope your soldiers are ready!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_Sub4' => 'What is this?! Are those the bandits you battled earlier? They must have known we\'d be traveling farther north and  laid a trap to get their revenge!

There\'s no way around it: you\'ll have to fight your way through!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_TradeA' => 'The villagers of Gullhaugr produce wooden  snow shoes. Daily labor there involves carrying gold between the mines, the smiths, and the manufacturers, so not getting slowed down by the deep snow is a huge benefit!

The village has agreed to equip your army in exchange for a stack of pelts and resources from your home island.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_TradeB' => 'Sjorheimr sustains itself by fishing in that large lake. When it\'s frozen, the fishermen and women just cut holes through the ice! When that happens, they attach metal spikes to their boots so they can safely walk on the slippery surface.

Since they aren\'t hunters, they\'re running low on pelts. Hunt some wildlife, throw in some resources, and they will gladly trade.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_TradeC' => 'While all clans know how to make decent fur clothing, Skaustad\'s is of the quality you\'ll need if you want to head deeper into the mountains. Even the most piercing cold will feel like a gentle autumn breeze if you wear a set of these.

The villagers usually hunt for the pelts themselves, but the wildlife has become a lot more dangerous recently. You\'ll have to supply them with the necessary pelts to equip your troops, and compensate them for their labor.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_TradeD' => 'Jarnbu is known for their blacksmiths and weaponsmiths. They even developed some special glasses that protect their eyes from the embers. All you need to know is, they also keep wind and snow out of your eyes in a storm!

The people of Jarnbu love decorating their homes with hunting trophies. They would happily trade some "goggles" for pelts, and a few other resources.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V2_TradeTutorial' => 'If it\'s pelts they want, you might have to battle more beasts. 
Us Nords have an eye for quality, though. You\'ll want to defeat the leader caves. 
You can pick up the pelts there after the battle and pack them up with the other goods the villagers asked for in your provision house.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_Main1' => 'There\'s nothing but canyons and valleys as far as the eye can see. It seems only very experienced climbers will be able to get through here. Needless to say, our armies are anything but. Let\'s see what we can find in this area. I certainly don\'t want to double back, as we\'re well past the point of no return.

As our scouts can\'t see very well in this fog, climbing higher up could be deadly. The best way forward is probably to tackle each challenge step by step. If only we knew someone who knows the ropes around here...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_Side1' => 'You\'ve probably already heard the terrifying stories about the folk from the mountains. I would advise gathering as much information as possible before we meet them. Maybe we can find some clues in anything they\'ve left behind in this region.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_SideSub1' => 'Have you heard the terrible tale Nord parents tell their children? 
They say if a child misbehaves, the parents ring a bell, and a cart collecting badly behaved children would take them away to work in the Mountain Clan mines. Want to go and see if you can find any proof of it, eh?',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_SideSub2' => 'Rumors about people being seen in boiling hot water spread like wildfire decades ago.

A long time ago a Nord hunter reported watching a group of unknown people from afar, shrouded in thick fog. The rumor goes that the hunter witnessed how one person threw another into the bubbling water.

The result was many wild theories about the Mountain Clan, and more stories for  parents to tell their kids.

Still sure you don´t want to abandon your expedition? Bwahaha...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_SideSub3' => 'The Nord explorers returned exhausted and scared. They told stories of bodies that were left hanging on the cliffsides near some Mountain Clan Ruins. Supposedly as a warning to anyone who wanted to enter the Mountain Clan realm.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_Sub1' => 'So you still want to continue your journey into the bloody cold mountains, eh? 
The only clue I can give you is that somewhere to the north, there should be some kind of structure. I\'ve got no idea what it could be.
Unfortunately for you, all the paths seem to be blocked. Probably the doings of this diabolic Mountain Clan.
 
Maybe we should try and find out more about the bearded Mountain Clan women...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V3_Sub2' => 'It feels like the path you need to follow now leads to the east. How do I know this? Obviously, we Nords can smell the path through the mountains.
But I have no idea what\'s waiting for us in that direction. I have never been this far into the mountains...',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Click1' => 'Welcome to the Mountain Clan\'s city fortress, Skjoldrborg!

Let us visit the main hall first. The Clan Elders can brief us on the current situation, and I can report back from my exploratory mission.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Click2' => 'Alright. We\'ve managed to defuse the situation, but this alone won\'t help us back on our feet. We have to restore our basic supplies first. Let me check with the Clan Elders on what needs to be done.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Gate' => 'Look around this war-ravaged land. This was once the majestic and flourishing city fortress Skjoldrborg. But not any more. Now it is much more of a provision base.

The reason we withdrew to the mountains was to make a stand against an ancient evil, the jötnar. Our clan has been fighting these frost giants for a long time now, and while we couldn\'t defeat them, we at least managed to confine them to these mountains.

But this conflict has started to wear on us. Not just our spirit, but our defenses as well! It looks like the gates to the north of our city fortress have been broken.

If we cannot repair and reinforce them with obsidian, it will only be a matter of time until the jötnar overrun us!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Main' => 'Now that you\'ve proven yourself, there is something I have to tell you. I myself am a member of the Mountain Clan.

Do not be alarmed! The stories about us are all a fiction - one that we ourselves spread to keep the other clans away... Look. We really need your help. I\'ll tell you all the details as we go.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian1a' => 'When the giants broke into this area, we had to abandon our stone quarry in the south west of the city fortress.

We used to find obsidian there on occasion, so there might just be some left. The clan has developed a method to harden obsidian into an incredibly durable state - something which would be perfect for reinforcing the gates.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian1b' => 'The clan elders are eager to put that stone quarry back to work, but it\'s suffered substantial damage. 
If you can repair it, we might be able to find more Obsidian.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian2a' => 'Some beasts got past our defences and are harassing our farms!

We\'ll need all the food we can get if the siege drags on any longer... Though we trust you can break the siege soon, we could always repurpose the obsidian tools for reinforcing our gates.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian2b' => 'The clan wants to restore the farms you reclaimed to working condition, but our fields have been pushed to their limits for some time. If we want to start growing again, we\'ll need to restore some nutrients to the ground first.

And don\'t worry about the obsidian from earlier - we have some spare metal tools we can use.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian3a' => 'An old woman lives west of the central fortress all by herself. Some say she\'s a witch, but I know better - she\'s a proper, scientific alchemist!

As far as I know, she\'s been studying obsidian for the past few years. If you can fight your way to her home, she\'d probably be willing to share some of her samples with us for our gates.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian3b' => 'Laire, the old alchemist, has requested your help with an experiment. She claims to have discovered a way to artificially create obsidian!

Her concoction has been brewing for weeks now, and is almost ready for testing. But now that the whole clan finds itself locked in battle, her supply line has dried up. She\'s asking if you\'d be willing to share your personal resources.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian4' => 'Our blacksmiths have been working in shifts, day and night, every day, for years. However, it looks like the forge has finally given in to the wear and tear, and has broken down.

We must repair it soon, or we won\'t be able to keep up the fight much longer.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Obsidian5' => 'I\'ve just been informed that our well has dried up. That\'s unusual, as it\'s being fed by an underground river, and so it should actually be impossible. Sabotage is the only explanation!

The snow around here is too polluted from the constant battles the area\'s seen. Our only option is to import clean water. Will you help us out yet again?',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_ObsidianDynamiteDummy' => 'A guard on the western gate tower saw a bunch of animals sneaking around in the abandoned stronghold in our hinterland north-west of the city fortress. They\'re probably devising another of their canny plans to sabotage or destroy our defenses. If we can spare the resources, we should take care of them.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_OptionalCamp' => 'It seems there are still townspeople hiding out in our old mining district north east of the Main Hall. They lit signal fires, so they probably need our help! We\'d better hurry!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub1' => 'As much as you\'ve already proven yourself in my eyes, my clan will be hesitant to simply take my word for it.

It looks like the outpost to the east of here is under attack - a bad sign, but also an opportunity for you to show your worth.

These beasts aren\'t really sent by our clan; they are the minions of our ancestral enemy.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub2' => 'If we don\'t want the gates to break again, we\'ll have to re-establish an outpost to the north of them. The ruins of our last fortress may be foreboding, but they should make for a decent foundation.

First, we must clear the area of the jötnar\'s forces.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub3' => 'Oh no! They broke through! See how the beasts have already dug new caves behind our unreinforced gates?

We must defeat them all before we can focus on your outpost again.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub4' => 'The clan\'s builders are now safe to work on that outpost, at least for the time being. Think hard about what building would be most useful, and deliver them a Construction Kit from your home island.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub5' => 'Another wave of beasts got past the unsecured gate(s).

Take them out before they do any more damage!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub6' => 'You\'ve earned us another breather, and the clan can spare some workers for your outpost. How about we construct another building? Just make sure it\'s not the same type as before - that wouldn\'t help us much in the long run.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub7' => 'Another wave of beasts got past the unsecured gates!

Take them out before they do any more damage!',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V4_Sub8' => 'You\'ve pushed all the enemies back for now, and there\'s still room for one more building in your outpost.

Remember: If you you want to get the most out of it, you\'ll want to avoid constructing a building you already have.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Main1' => 'We have to find a way to cross the river, and reach the Lair of the Frost Giant King. The Mountain Clan call him Risi. They told us he and (as they call them) his generals launch their attacks from an area north of the river.

With the Mountain Clan\'s help, and the outpost we built here, we should be able to work out a plan to defeat this ancient evil.

I\'ll keep sending out scouts, and will let you know when we spot anything that might lead us to the Frost Giant King´s Lair.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Main2' => 'Risi gains strength when his generals are nearby. We know that much. One theory is that they carry some gear or weapons that they return to Risi when they regroup. If we manage to wipe out the generals before they have a chance to regroup with Risi, we may be able to weaken him.

On the other hand, if we just rush towards the Lair of the Frost Giant King, an alarm will be raised and the generals will have time to retreat and regroup with Risi. We want to avoid that at all costs, or we\'ll have to face their full power.

With one general down, Risi will need more time before he can attack. With two generals down, he\'ll lose some of his power, although he\'ll still be a tough foe. With three generals down, Risi will be weak, and unable to deal anywhere near as much damage. And if we defeat all his generals defeated, Risi will be left alone and vulnerable, unable to even hit a barn with a rock.

That´s all we know. It´s up to you to decide our approach.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub1' => 'The Mountain Clan demolished these bridges a long time ago to keep the giant creatures in check. But somehow, they still found a way to cross the river. 

We have to repair at least one of them if we want to get across.

The good news is that they also carry materials that could be useful to repair the bridges. We should check out camps near the bridges where they cross over to this side.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub2' => 'Our scouts will let us know when we\'re getting close to the Frost Giant King\'s Lair, before we reach the point of no return. If we continue our journey north after that, we won\'t be able to catch the remaining generals before they\'re able to regroup with their King and troops.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub3_Main' => 'This Elk is in a constant rage. Its antlers resemble huge trees, each a deadly weapon. It\'s fast, hard to hit and tramples over everything in its way.

We have to defeat it, either before or after we reach Risi´s Lair.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub4_Main' => 'Not just a regular Mammoth, this is a smarter, sturdier and deadlier foe. Speaking from personal experience, it\'s also pretty tough to evade its tusks when it´s chasing you.

We have to defeat it, either before or after we reach Risi´s Lair.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub5_Main' => 'That nasty kitty is responsible for a lot of pain. Many of us would be moved to tears if you can bring it down. But be warned. It might not be as sturdy as the other generals, but it packs a huge punch - so you\'d better not get hit!

We have to defeat it, either before or after we reach Risi´s Lair.',
        'BuffAdv_TMC_V5_Sub6_Main' => 'This beast has such impressive eyesight, it\'s able to pick you out from hundreds of miles away, even in a forest at the dead of night. Its huge wings and feathers are an impressive sight, but one only a few have been able to live to recall.

We have to defeat it, either before or after we reach Risi´s Lair.',
        'BuffQuestAThreatMain' => 'Terrible news! We have received an anonymous threatening letter that states, in scruffy handwriting, that we are going to be invaded soon! We must do something!',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub1' => 'We all need to calm down... After all, it may not be anything. But what if it is? It could be a prank... But what if it isn\'t? My lord, the uncertainty is killing me. We have to fortify the island. Let\'s put up barricades EVERYWHERE!',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub2' => 'Ahhh, I\'m still not feeling any calmer... What should I do! What can we do? I\'m not used to this kind of pressure! ...I know! We need to have more soldiers! A lot more soldiers! We need to prepare for the worst!',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub3' => 'Ok, ok - I think the nerves are starting to go away now... However, not being fully aware of our surroundings is making me a bit twitchy. Let\'s craft some spyglasses at our provision house, so we can keep an eye on things.',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub4' => 'What\'s that? A single boat!? Could it be a spy? I\'ll have him arrested immediately! My lord, our personnel are starting to grow restless and hungry. Do you think it would be possible to provide some food, so they can keep doing the great work they\'re doing in keeping us safe?',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub5' => 'A huge fleet has been sighted! One of the ships sent an emissary, who said that the boy we arrested some time ago is in fact the son of a count from another kingdom! I\'m afraid I let my paranoia get the better of me, and now we\'re paying the price. I\'m so sorry my lord! But can we perhaps offer a tribute to appease the situation? The alternative is a full-scale invasion!',
        'BuffQuestAThreat_Sub6' => 'The count offers their apologies for the misunderstanding, and proposes an alliance as compensation. However, they have a strict policy of only letting people join their alliance if they can earn their general\'s approval. Take him on an adventure to the far east with you, and let him see what we\'re made of!',
        'BuffQuestAnnoholicsMain' => 'The famous band "The Annoholics" are on tour! And from what I saw on the poster, it seems that they\'re performing nearby! Maybe we should contact them and see if we can get them to play a special gig on our island. I\'m sure that would make everyone happy!',
        'BuffQuestAnnoholics_Sub1' => 'If we are to hire The Annoholics to come to our island, we will need to prepare a contract for them, and ready an upfront payment. Please provide some paper and coins so our messengers can deliver the contract.',
        'BuffQuestAnnoholics_Sub2' => 'Now that we have a contract with them, we\'ll need to prepare a proper stage so that they can play for us. Please contact our specialist at the provision house, and bring the stage over to the mayor\'s house when it\'s ready.',
        'BuffQuestAnnoholics_Sub3' => 'Oh, what a tragedy! It seems that on their trip here, the band hit a patch of rough weather, and their instruments got broken. They won\'t be able to play like that! The only option we have right now is to create new instruments for them to use. Check the provision house and bring them over!',
        'BuffQuestAnnoholics_Sub4' => 'All the preparations are set - now we just have to spread word around and attract some fans to our island. Let\'s leave this island for a while and tell our friends about it!',
        'BuffQuestBartMain' => 'We found this leaflet from a barterer called "Bart". It says he pays well for rare materials. I thought our economy could use a little boost, so I decided to invite him over.',
        'BuffQuestBart_Sub1' => 'Bart the barterer has arrived on the island. He mentioned he hasn\'t had much interest from his leaflets, so he\'s willing to make us a good deal. He\'s offered me a small (horrible) marble statue, and has asked for a similar statue made of hardwood. Let\'s use our provision house to produce the goods he\'s asked for - just make sure you don\'t clog the production line!',
        'BuffQuestBart_Sub2' => 'Bart\'s second deal is a first edition of a rare encyclopedia that he thinks may be useful for our specialists. He\'s willing to offer it to us, in exchange for a hand-crafted replica of an ancient brass sword.',
        'BuffQuestBart_Sub3' => 'Since Bart is going to be staying with us for a few days, I think it would be a nice gesture of goodwill to offer him something to eat. Why don\'t we treat him to some really fancy food? Perhaps this way he\'ll give us a discount next time...',
        'BuffQuestBart_Sub4' => 'Bart seems to have taken a liking to us, so he offers us a new deal. He wants a table made of exotic wood and sturdy steel, and will exchange it for a really big granite doorstop. What do you think?',
        'BuffQuestBart_Sub5' => 'Bart is pleased with the business he\'s done with us, but he now has a personal request. He tries to collect coins from everywhere he goes, so he would be really happy to trade some refined weaponry for some of our coins, and a golden statue. Otherwise it wouldn\'t be bartering, would it?',
        'BuffQuestGoldsmith' => 'My, what an unusual coin. Did someone really pay with this? It looks so exotic... Maybe it\'s even worth something! I have an... acquaintance... that really knows his foreign currency. Perhaps we should get him to give it an appraisal?',
        'BuffQuestLostCompassMain' => 'Well, now this is a peculiar compass. It has quite an odd design, and doesn\'t actually seem to point north, like every other compass... I wonder if there\'s more to this little artefact?',
        'BuffQuestLostCompass_Sub1' => 'What a mysterious compass this is. It clearly does not point north, but that begs the question - where IS it pointing? One of our researchers thinks he may have an idea about how to solve this mystery, but he needs to have some specific documentation to help him figure it out.',
        'BuffQuestLostCompass_Sub2' => 'Our research indicates that the curious compass is attuned to a certain specific metal. This metal was used by pirates, in years gone by, to stash their treasure so they could easily find it again later. It seems we may have found some treasure! Let\'s follow the compass towards other islands, and see how it behaves then.',
        'BuffQuestLostCompass_Sub3' => 'No matter how often we check it, it seems that the only constant is that it\'s always pointing east. Perhaps we should try looking there?',
        'BuffQuestLostCompass_Sub4' => 'The chest is ours - but without a key, it\'s little more than a really heavy box. Fortunately, we have a locksmith waiting in our provision house that assures me that with enough materials, he can find a key that\'ll open the chest for us. He promised not to look inside if he manages to get it open.',
        'BuffQuestMirandaMain' => 'We found this message in a bottle addressed to a woman named "Miranda". The contents are about how much a man loves and misses her. It\'s all very cheesy if you ask me, but I\'d feel bad if this letter was never received.',
        'BuffQuestMiranda_Sub1' => 'Although we don\'t know who this person is, we should try and send him some sort of reply. He definitely got the wrong person! We should train a messenger pigeon at our provision house to send our message back to where it came from!',
        'BuffQuestMiranda_Sub2' => 'We have received a response from the man. His name is Jonas, and he never really expected anyone would ever get this letter! He confesses that Miranda is not the name of a woman, but the name of his cat, who has been with him his whole life. We have to go rescue him!',
        'BuffQuestMiranda_Sub3' => 'We brought the man back, but he\'s in really bad shape... He suffers from scurvy and severe dehydration. My grandma had a recipe for a vitamin-filled brew that should help him to get back into shape. Let\'s go to the provision house and prepare it!',
        'BuffQuestMysteriousCoin' => 'One of our merchants stopped by earlier, and told me he\'d been paid with a strange coin. It looks similar to ours, but it\'s definitely not from around here. It\'s a pretty looking thing, and clearly hand-crafted. Maybe we should investigate this some more?',
        'BuffQuestNewStone' => 'A young boy was playing on the beach and found a very beautiful stone. 

But what kind of stone is it? And is it valuable?',
        'BuffQuestNewStone_Sub1' => 'We\'ll need to clean the stone up a bit before we can take a better look at it. Right now, it\'s just too dirty.',
        'BuffQuestNewStone_Sub2' => 'It\'s beautiful, but without knowing anything about stones, it\'s hard to say that much more. Why not ask some experts from the smelters. Of course, they\'ll want something in exchange for their help...',
        'BuffQuestNewStone_Sub3' => 'As we\'ve got a bit of time on our hands, let\'s go to the beach. I happen to know exactly where that boy found the stone - let\'s see if we can find any more! Still, we should be careful - some settlers have already got wind of our precious stone...',
        'BuffQuestNewStone_Sub4' => 'Oh no! The rumours about your stone are spreading. We cannot defend it on our own.Please send some of your military units to protect your island.',
        'BuffQuestNewStone_Sub5' => 'The experts have been waiting for you. They\'re eager to share what they\'ve learnt.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers' => 'The deer population is shrinking! You\'ll need to figure out what\'s causing it, and find some way of restoring the natural balance.

Find the source of the problem, and help the deers to recover.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub1' => 'First of all, you\'ll need to get a feel for the size of the deer population. Ask the hunters to create a list of deer.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub2' => 'The number of deer has been falling dramatically over the past few days. But why? You should check in with the hunters again, and ask them about the wolves.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub3' => 'The wolves are behaving pretty normally. They\'re not overeating, and their population is stable. So how comes the deer population is still dwindling? Best talk with the forester.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub4' => 'You should probably try to give the woodcutters, the foresters, and the sawmills a bit of a helping hand, to thank them for their research.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub5' => 'A very excited settler reached out to me, as he\'d seen some strangers poaching our deer. That would explain a lot. We need to track down these strangers, and teach them a lesson.',
        'BuffQuestSaveTheDeers_Sub6' => 'Yes, seemingly that was the cause of our deer related issues. Let\'s give the hunter a hand, and give the deer chance to get back to normal.',
        'BuffQuestSettlersBanditsMain' => 'While I was going through my things, I found some papers of mine from back when I was a lot younger. I liked to play make believe a lot, where I\'d pretend I was someone else, and so I wrote out entire backgrounds and stories for these characters. It might be fun to share this with other people who share the same interests. What do you think?',
        'BuffQuestSettlersBandits_Sub1' => 'Here\'s what I call the "character sheet". Basically, it defines what your portrayed character will be, who he is, and what he does. In short, it\'s a player\'s "identity". In fact, if I could have some time to go through all my existing sheets, I can probably turn it into a game!',
        'BuffQuestSettlersBandits_Sub2' => 'I finished creating the rules! Boy, that was complicated. Now, I think we should make several copies of the rules at the provision house, and spread them around the island, so we can see what the public opinion is. Oh! We\'ll need some dice, too!',
        'BuffQuestSettlersBandits_Sub3' => 'I can\'t believe it! It\'s a resounding success! In fact, people are playing it so much, it\'s even created a whole new sub-culture! Very interesting. Very interesting indeed. In fact, we\'re running short on paper and coal for the game - can you provide some more?',
        'BuffQuestSharpClawMain' => 'I bring dire news, my lord! One of our wood workers just found this really sharp claw while in the forest! I have never seen anything of this nature, but one thing is for certain - it\'s come from a big beast.',
        'BuffQuestSharpClaw_Sub1' => 'If we\'re going to search for this beast, we must be very thorough. Gather your explorers for a scouting party, and send them out to search for it. If they happen to bring some treasure in the process, then all the better!',
        'BuffQuestSharpClaw_Sub2' => 'We searched the whole island, but we found nothing. Maybe we should search below the surface of the island, too? Maybe the geologists will find something underground...',
        'BuffQuestSharpClaw_Sub3' => 'Having heard the most recent testimony from our geologists, it\'s safe to say we cannot afford to take any risks. We need to prepare for the worst! If what they said is true, we\'ll need a really sturdy, and really BIG cage to put the beast in. Let\'s go to the provision house, and get to work!',
        'BuffQuestSharpClaw_Sub4' => 'With the cage finished, all we need to do now is send a squad of the bravest soldiers to take care of the beast. I\'ve already contacted the barracks, and they are willing to provide the bravest men they can out of their next batch of recruits.',
        'BuffQuestSilkCatMain' => 'Let us read the message... A member of the von Peahead court informs you that his Lord’s rare Larsian silk cat has gone missing. Gundolf von Peahead accuses his fellow nobleman Harald the Softnoggin of pilfering it. 
The two are preparing for battle over this dispute– can you believe it?',
        'BuffQuestSilkCat_Sub1' => 'We must defuse this situation. But how can we make them listen to us? These blockheads won’t even accept a flying ship as a sign of importance!

The only language they understand is their own - showy displays of wealth and power. Let\'s pitch my tent on their battlefield.  Add some showy decorations, and bring your personal guard too - that should draw their attention.',
        'BuffQuestSilkCat_Sub2' => 'Of course, von Peahead has no evidence whatsoever. He only suspects Softnoggin because he was the last person he showed the cat to before its disappearance.

They have promised to withdraw their troops, for now, in exchange for my assurance I\'ll investigate the matter. Can I count on your support? We’ll use flour to dust for foot and fingerprints!',
        'BuffQuestSilkCat_Sub3' => 'The most recent prints are from cat paws... It must have escaped on its own! All this madness over a runaway cat! 

I doubt that von Peahead will be satisfied unless we find and return his precious pet though. Where should we start looking? I wouldn\'t be surprised if it had made a beeline for the fish market.',
        'BuffQuestSilkCat_Sub4' => 'Now that we know the cat is around here somewhere, we just need some bait. Do you have any suggestions?',
        'BuffQuestStrangeIdolsMain' => 'We just found a statue of a little idol. It seems an ancient civilization may have lived on this island long ago! Our local scholars cannot wait for you to let them investigate it so we can learn more!',
        'BuffQuestStrangeIdols_Sub1' => 'Our scholars are trying to isolate what kind of material the idol is made of. They\'ve asked if they can borrow some materials fresh from our stores so they can compare consistency, weight, and a lot other words that I don\'t know what they mean.',
        'BuffQuestStrangeIdols_Sub2' => 'As it turns out, the idol isn\'t made of any material we\'ve seen before. We could always ask the scholars living on our allies\' islands, and see if they have any idea what it might be? Oh, but don\'t forget to take them some presents! We don\'t want to come across as greedy, do we?',
        'BuffQuestStrangeIdols_Sub3' => 'If what our allies said is true, and this idol is actually made of pure gold, it must be covered by a huge amount of dirt and rust... Fortunately, my grandma knows how to make a special liquid that\'ll remove any rust from gold in the space of just a few hours. Or so she says! We should be able to replicate it in our provision house.',
        'BuffQuestStrangeIdols_Sub4' => 'Let\'s try to look on the bright side. Regardless of what the idol\'s made of, I\'m sure that if it contains even a small amount of gold, we can probably sell it for a profit. It is still a very pretty decoration.',
        'BuffQuestTheJourney' => 'The surroundings of Tikki Island have been afflicted by a curse due to the missing sacred coin! We can\'t leave the Tikki like this... We must get this coin back to them! We\'ll need to craft the best ships and pack enough supplies to make it through the cursed storm.',
        'BuffQuestTheLittlePanda' => 'We just stopped some smugglers at the port, who were trying to get illegal merchandise onto our island. Hidden amongst their goods, we found a malnourished panda cub. Poor little panda... Who would do something like this? We must return him to his habitat and to his mother!',
        'BuffQuestThePandaCub' => 'Oh no, this is terrible! The smugglers took this little panda away from his mother, and now he\'s too sad to eat or drink anything. Perhaps you should try to feed him. He seems to have taken a shining to you.',
        'BuffQuestTikkiIsland' => 'This is terrible! Most of the bandits that came to steal the Tikki\'s treasure got stranded on Tikki Island due to the curse, and now they\'ve decided to settle there! They\'re oppressing the poor Tikki, and making them do their bidding by force! This deed cannot go unpunished. We must save the Tikki tribe!',
        'BuffQuestTravelCage' => 'Now the little panda\'s been nursed back to good health, it\'s time we return him to his mother. We need to create a cage that resembles the trees on his homeland so he won\'t get nervous on the trip back - and we\'ll need a sailor that can get him there safely.',
        'BuffQuestVigilanteMain' => 'When I first found this brooch, I thought that it was an ornament for clothing - but when the children around town saw me holding it, they started telling me how it belongs to a vigilante called "The Custodian", that has been fighting crime on this island. This requires more investigation!',
        'BuffQuestVigilante_Sub1' => 'The first mystery we must solve is: Does this vigilante operate only on our island, or is he some sort of travelling hero? Let\'s pay a visit to some other places. Have our generals yell "The Custodian is coming!" and see if our enemies react.',
        'BuffQuestVigilante_Sub2' => 'I\'m a bit worried that this vigilante might not fight crime "by-the-book" so to speak... So, I\'ve come up with a cunning plan. We\'ll fake a robbery in one of our houses, and make a huuuuge racket while doing so. That will certainly attract The Custodian\'s attention - and perhaps then, we can have a proper chat. Let\'s prepare some flimsy props in our provision house to make this more realistic.',
        'BuffQuestVigilante_Sub3' => 'There are two ways of dealing with this: Either she passes the tests and becomes an official member of the guard, or she will be treated like the criminals she\'s trying to stop. Having seen her two options, she\'s agreed to apply to join the guard, as long as she can keep her cool costume. The first test is a written morality test. Please provide the necessary materials to do this.',
        'BuffQuestVigilante_Sub4' => 'The second test is a physical test. Our guards must be in peak physical condition to be able to perform with the excellence required by the King. We will construct a difficult obstacle course, which you\'ll need to provide materials for. Don\'t worry, though - once the test is done, we can re-use most of the materials used.',
        'BuffQuestVigilante_Sub5' => 'She\'s more than fit for the guard - in fact, our generals are so impressed by her performance, they think she could become a general herself! They would like to perform a special leadership test, where she will join our generals in leading the troops on an adventure.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingCake' => 'I have already arranged the best bakers in our kingdom to help us create the best wedding cake of all time. They\'re all ready to start, as soon as you provide them with the required ingredients.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingInvitation' => 'The king of a neighbouring kingdom has cordially invited us to the wedding of his son, the prince, and humbly asks us to make and deliver the wedding cake. There will be a lot of people, so apparently "it better be huge"!',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory1_A' => 'These stories are hard to believe. But they are all true.
They happened to a friend of a friend\'s favorite cousin-in-law.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory1_B' => 'A groom, bright with anticipation, showed his wedding ring to his closest companion.
But the household hound mistook it for a toy, and for seven days they searched the earth, unearthing every hole the mutt had proudly dug.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory1_C' => 'They delved for many days, laboring by torch and sweat, until the mines at last gave way and fell silent beneath the weight of their striving.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory2_A' => 'These stories are hard to believe. But they are all true.
They happened to a friend of a friend\'s favorite cousin-in-law.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory2_B' => 'As the wedding drew near, the bride decreed the feast was to be held beneath veils of fine cloth, woven and hung from their branches to cast a shade worthy of the day.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory2_C' => 'Mahogany trees must be planted, for only those trees were worthy of the occasion.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory3_A' => 'These stories are hard to believe. But they are all true.
They happened to a friend of a friend\'s, the favorite cousin-in-law.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory3_B' => 'As the wedding day drew close, a florist, entrusted with all matters of order and beauty, proclaimed that bouquets must be fashioned at once.',
        'BuffQuestWeddingStory3_C' => 'Bright, towering, and wholly unsuited for any bridal grasp.
Much discussion followed, and it was agreed that no vow should be hidden behind such brazen blooms.',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy' => 'A girl was playing in the forest, and she found a small puppy. She came to us desperate for help, as the puppy is wounded, and she can\'t treat its wounds alone. Help her nurse the puppy back to health.',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy_Sub1' => 'The girl holds the little pup in her arms as it shivers, covered in wounds. Having a warm bed would make a huge difference.',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy_Sub2' => 'It seems like the puppy\'s starting to feel a little better - but until we treat his wounds, it\'s still touch and go.',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy_Sub3' => 'The puppy is finally starting to pick up. We should make sure he has enough  to eat and drink until he\'s fully recovered.',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy_Sub4' => 'Let\'s find out where it\'s coming from. Maybe the little guy came from another island and got attacked by the local wolves..',
        'BuffQuestWolfPuppy_Sub5' => 'The little pup is growing stronger - he\'s definitely going to make it through. Let\'s see if it\'d be possible to return him to the forest.',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_MainQuest' => 'An anxious villager approaches you asking for help. There was a serious storm on their island, and the villagers can\'t afford the essential repairs. The harvest was bad, and hunger is starting to haunt the people. Are you willing to help them?',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest01' => 'As you arrive on the island, you can see the destruction the storm has caused. But no matter how much you want to help rebuild the houses, the fields are more important now. Clear the fields of the dead crops, and ready them up for new ones.',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest02' => 'Until the crops grow, we should start to rebuild the town. There are so many things to do! First, the area needs to be cleared of any debris so we can start afresh on the construction.  We should count how many boulders there are, and produce just enough dynamite at the provision house to destroy them all! We don\'t want to spend valuable goods making dynamite that we won\'t use! Boulders of different sizes need different types of dynamite.',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest03' => 'After clearing the area, it\'s time to get to the buildings! But first, there are some preparations we need to take care of. Create some stinky potions and decomposers in your provision house, but don\'t use them yet! We\'re going to need them all later.

Attention: This quest will fail if you use a Stinky potion or a Decomposer.',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest04' => 'Now that everything\'s been prepared, you can start getting rid of the rats, worms and other obstacles. When presented with a choice about what to use to get rid of them, pay attention to your item availability! The stinky potions and decomposers are very limited. I recommend using them only when it is strictly necessary!

Attention: This quest will fail if you don\'t have enough stinky potions or decomposers to clear the remaining vermin.',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest05' => 'Now that we\'ve moved everything out of the way, it\'s time to get on with the reconstruction! Be careful, though. Not every building can be placed on every slot! Pay attention to which slots highlight when you choose a building kit, and then plan very carefully which buildings you can place where. Do you have some pen and paper around?

Note: If you run out of spaces to place the required buildings before you\'ve placed them, you will fail this quest!',
        'Buff_Adv_StormRecovery_SubQuest06' => 'Now that we\'ve put everything back to normal, it\'s time to make sure this won\'t happen again. Help them repair their prevention system! The tubes outside the building seem to have developed some cracks. Do you have anything that might fix them?',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Repeatable' => 'Today we gather around to share great stories to inspire future generations into pursuing great deeds.',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Timer_Loop1026' => 'This session is over.
Do not be sad, for there were will be more to come.',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Timer_Loop1080' => 'This session is over.
Do not be sad, for there were will be more to come.',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Timer_Loop864' => 'This session is over.
Do not be sad, for there were will be more to come.',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Timer_Loop918' => 'This session is over.
Do not be sad, for there were will be more to come.',
        'BuiBonus_AuroraTower_Timer_Loop972' => 'This session is over.
Do not be sad, for there were will be more to come.',
        'BuiBonus_BalloonMarket_miniStart' => 'This is so exciting! Pay a visit to the Balloon Market Tribute and say "Hi" to the balloon creator. He has a special creation, just for you!
You can find your balloon present in your Star Menu after paying a visit at the Balloon Market Tribute.',
        'BuiBonus_BalloonMarket_mini_Timer' => 'The Balloon Creator always needs some time for his new special creations. He is very careful, and only presents the best of his work.
Give him some more time and come back when he is ready. But don\'t forget to visit him again. He will not begin work on another creation until the previous one is collected.',
        'BuiBonus_BalloonMarket_mini_Timer_Loop' => 'The balloon creator always needs a bit of time to work on his new special creations. He is very careful, and only reveals the very best of his work.
Give him some time and come back when he’s ready. But don\'t forget to visit him again - he’ll not start work on another creation until the old one has been collected.',
        'BuiBonus_Depositorium_Start' => 'More than a simple storehouse, the Depositorium is a place of keeping and rediscovery. Goods are not merely stored here; they rest, waiting to be found again.
You will be able to take a tour through the endless halls and see what you will find. Just click on the building to discover hidden boxes with useful deposits. Just don\'t forget to check your Star Menu once you\'ve done it!',
        'BuiBonus_Depositorium_Timer' => 'The Depositorium, endless expanses, and a whole lot of rooms. Soon it will be time for another tour. Let\'s see what turns up next.
And don’t forget: After the tour is before the tour. Only once one tour is completed does the waiting time for the next one begin.',
        'BuiBonus_Depositorium_Timer_Loop' => 'The Depositorium, endless expanses, and a whole lot of rooms. Soon it will be time for another tour. Let\'s see what turns up next.
And don’t forget: After the tour is before the tour. Only once one tour is completed does the waiting time for the next one begin.',
        'BuiBonus_DimensionalRift_Start' => 'Go ahead. Take a peek. What\'s the worst that could happen?',
        'BuiBonus_FluffyLogistics_Loop' => 'Ah! Greetings Mayor!
There is no time to waste. We must deliver these eggs at once.',
        'BuiBonus_FlyingHouse_Start' => 'This residence is very special. Not only does it fly, but it also has a telescope attached to provide the best view of the fireworks and festivities while they last! Looking around your island, the lookout also regularly finds hidden, forgotten or lost items and can point them out to you to collect. Get to know the locations by clicking a Celebrative Lookout. 
You\'ll be able to retrieve the items by clicking on the find in your Star Menu! Now go and check out what\'s been found!',
        'BuiBonus_FlyingHouse_Timer' => 'The lookout usually finds something new every day, and you can check the time until his next find below.
But remember -  if you want to keep the lookout motivated, you should regularly pick up what he points out! The timer will only restart once you\'ve collected it.',
        'BuiBonus_FlyingHouse_Timer_Loop' => 'The Lookout usually finds something every day and you can check the time here.
But be aware that if you want to keep the lookout motivated you should regularly pick up what has been pointed out. The timer will only restart afterwards.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_Timer' => 'Here you can see how long we\'ll be at sea, whooooo! Bet you can\'t wait for us to return, huh? We are so glad to have found y-whoooo, and will try our best to reward you with nice things when we return!
Don\'t forget to come by and get your stuff - we won\'t leave for another adventure until then!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_Timer_Loop' => 'Here you can see how long we\'ll be at sea, whooooo! Bet you can\'t wait for us to return, huh? We are so glad to have found y-whoooo, and will try our best to reward you with nice things when we return!
Don\'t forget to come by and get your stuff - we won\'t leave for another adventure until then!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest1' => 'We heard a legend about mini ghosts that live on tiny islands. Doesn\'t that sound cu-whoooo-te? Help us search for them, and we\'ll have a small obolus for y-whooooo.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest10' => 'Listen lad, or gal, or, well, I can\'t see you too clearly without any eyes, so just listen, okay?
You need friends. Good friends. And you never know where you might find them. So go and tell someone that you\'re on "A Quest for Friendship", and ask for their help, OK? And maybe don\'t just keep asking the same person - that\'ll get you nowhere. Just say a friendly ghost gave you the push you needed, hee-hee, whooooo!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest11' => 'It\'s a bit embarrassing to ask, but... could you get us some ballast for our ship? The problem is, we\'re a bit too friendly, see, and so we\'re constantly being pulled upwards...We even keep stones in our pockets so we don\'t fly off before we want to. But our ship needs some additional ballast so as not to fly off. And unfortunately, every now and then a few bricks just drop straight through the ghostly hull of our ship, so we regularly have to restock our ballast. We haven\'t found any in a while, so if you stumble upon anything that might do the trick, please let me know!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest12' => 'Since we\'re all such good friends by now, could you do us a favor? We desperately need some wild horses that aren\'t afraid of ghosts! Please find us some!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest13' => 'A little while back, our ship passed a crisis-ridden island with a town near the coast. It looked like the town had been split in two by a landslide, so we got curious. But unfortunately, we couldn\'t get as near as we wanted, as wild beasts and foes with strength we\'d never seen before were roaming all about. They were wandering around just like lost ghosts.
Despite all this, we found a small family hiding out in some ruins near the coast. They told us the story of the island, and how they\'d always just about managed to keep going - somehow. But during the winters, it becomes incredibly hard to survive, especially due to the cold. If they take shelter, the beasts will leave them alone, but their stock of coal always runs out too soon, putting them in a dire situation. Would you mind gathering some flammable material?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest14' => 'Whooooo-hoo again! Ever since we settled on your island, we\'ve been able to enjoy many more adventures than before. Unfortunately, this has also made our ghostly weapons dull faster than we expected. Could you get us some iron to resharpen them?
We don\'t actually use the iron ore itself, but we learned how to extract the essence of it and instill it into our weapons, repairing and even strengthening them!
During the process, the iron ore does get destroyed nonetheless, though, so I guess you could say we are u-whoooo-sing it up.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest15' => 'Whooooo! During our travels, we\'ve encountered many settlers in p-whoo-or shape! They seem to be have been kidnapped, or got themselves trapped and forced to work for their captors and such.
We\'ve made a list of places on the islands we found so you can free them!
I wouldn\'t wait too long, though - some of them really seem close to popping their cloggs.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest16' => 'We\'ve noticed your fishing efforts are driving away the fish swarms! We can gladly help you with that by creating an artificial coral reef for our friends with fins! We love a good colorful reef ourselves, so you only need to provide us with enough material to create the reef.
Be sure to bring us the right material though - not every ordinary brick or stone will do. Here\'s a detailed description how it should look.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest17' => 'Whoooo-hooooo, wow! You should have seen that kraken! It must have been twice the size of our ship, the Flying Ghostman - and it almost managed to send us all to the end of time! I\'m still not sure how it actually managed to touch us, but it must have been around for longer than even we\'ve been roaming the seas - and it\'s clearly picked up plenty of skills along the way! We didn\'t want to hurt the majestic beastie, so we managed to slip out of its tentacles but for a prize. Unfortunately, that means part of the ship has evaporated into thin air, and a giant hole in the side of our vessel hasn\'t exactly been helping the crew\'s morale.
Could you please make us this special kind of tool? I know they\'re pretty archaic, but that\'s all we know how to use. It won\'t cost any more than your usual tools - and you can keep them afterwards.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest18' => 'Brrrr-whooooo. While travelling the abyss by foot, we managed to get caught in a ghost lake! Nothing too serious after all, but we\'re still all dripping wet and we need to dry out! I know it sounds silly, but believe me, a ghost-cold is no fun at all, as it can easily last for a decade - and a constantly sneezing ghost will eventually drive everyone nuts!
Please produce some more coal to fire up your smelters a bit more! And don\'t worry, we won\'t scare anyone! We\'ll just hang out on a clothesline nearby for a while.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest19' => 'Quick! We need your help! A band of wandering ghosts have apparently got envious of our ability to freely roam the seas, and they\'re threatening to banish us! They\'ve figured out a way to wield iron weaponry without injuring themselves, and now they\'re coming for us!
Here are the instructions for what we need you to do to give us chance to defend ourselves. Please hurry - we don\'t know when they\'ll be able to reach us!',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest2' => 'Oh my, oh my... Even 300-year-olds can sometimes bicker like little children. Unbelievab-whooooo-l. Could you show my ghostly sailors how to co-whoooooo-perate? Some don\'t get along so well only because they were born in different centuries. A small demonstration of co-whoooooo-peration might help with that.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest20' => 'Help! Help! Whoooo-heeelp! We\'ve been attacked by the most vicious, evil and cruel beings I\'ve ever seen in my entire life - and my entire death! These beasts are relentless. They\'ve been following us for days now, and they just won\'t stop pecking and quacking. Their number two even gets stuck on our railings! And no-whooooooo, I don\'t know how this is possible. But what\'s worse, I don\'t know how to remove it !
We need something to distract these enormous ducks! We can\'t simply blast, them can we?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest21' => 'This time, we\'ve come to ask a favor for someone else. It\'s for another small village, to tell the truth. Their village gets flooded almost every year, destroying what they build up and taking their dreams away with every wave. They have the materials, but what they\'re lacking is strong men to build up the flood barrier. Could you spare any?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest22' => 'A duke from the continent is arranging a battue to please the noblemen, but it seems he\'s missing the riders he needs to properly carry it out.
This would be a good chance for you to either gain some more respect with the duke - or, go with what we prefer, and sabotage the battue to spare those cute foxes and deers. It\'s up to you what you want to tell your men, though - we\'ve just come to let you know about the opportunity.
If you\'re up for it, train some riders so they know how to behave in such a no-whooooo-ble event.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest23' => 'Settlers in the north-east of your island seem to be caught in a drought and could really use some rain. We want to repay you for all you\'ve done for us, and we want to help improve the life of your people too.
Here\'s a recipe for some arrows that\'ll make it rain - but if you want the rain without creating a thunderstorm, you\'ll have to do it bit by bit, and will need quite a few specially trained bowmen to fulfill this daily task. It\'s up to you if you want to follow our suggestion thr-whooooooo-h.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest24' => 'We\'ve noticed your folk seems to be somewhat lacking in entertainment options - except for the tavern, that is! Even if that isn\'t exactly the healthiest of ways to spend their leisure time. Still, although it may not be our place to judge, we\'ve come up with a proposal. We recently saw an incredible show made up of just some simple bowmen. They were shooting flaming arrows at each other in curves, catching them in mid-air, and even playing theater while shooting arrows left and right. I think you could put something like this on too? I\'ll tell your men how to go about it.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest25' => 'Your tradesmen seem to be moaning behind your back. One of my crew overheard a discussion between them, saying that it\'s careless that your brew deliveries around the town aren\'t protected at all. Almost daily, a group of thirsty thieves comes out of the bushes and one of the deliveries vanishes! The deliverers have even stopped reporting the incidents, as it\'s just become the daily routine.
Train some soldiers to escort the deliveries to solve the conflicts peacefully, if possible. Just having troops assigned should improve the situation - and your standing with the tradesmen.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest26' => 'Even we need some time to relax every now and then. But as we seem to scare your Settlers every time we try - even though they\'ve seen us often enough by now - we\'d like to find somewhere we can get some rest, without being flustered by stuttered screams every few minutes. Could you keep an eye out for a remote location for us? Preferably it\'ll have a beach and some palm trees - but as we don\'t feel any wind or cold, any quiet and remote location would d-whoooo.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest3' => 'My personal friend, Atlas, with whom I\'ve been travelling the seas for hundreds of years now seems to be more than a little bored. It looks like he needs a change of scenery. Could you take him along on one of your adventures? I\'ll tell him his task is to watch your every move for anything suspicious - he might enjoy a bit of an espionage mission.
It doesn\'t matter much where you take him, just make sure he gets some fresh air.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest4' => 'The crew needs a challenge. Would you be able to find us a s-whooooo-itable playground to rattle our sabers?

Don\'t overdo it though - just a minor scuffle will do this time. And please, make sure the fo-whooooo-es are bad guys - you know we\'re still kind-hearted ghosts, right?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest5' => 'We stumbled upon an old notebook, written in the last days of a wintry, forsaken mother. She wished to experience some mysteries, some adventure, riddles or incredible stories after having spent her life raising a horde of children. But it should be an adventure without violence - that was noted specifically. It looks like the mother never got the chance to leave on such an adventure. Will you go in her stead and takes the notes with you, so her soul may find serenity?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest6' => 'A young man holding a baby in his arms was kneeling and sobbing at the shore. He asked the heavens if they couldn\'t return his wife and the child\'s mother. The baby had just started talking, and the first thing it apparently said was "Momma?", in a quiet and sad voice. The atmosphere on board hasn\'t been the same ever since... But now we\'ve got a new goal. We will find out what happened to the mother! If you can, please keep a look out for her too.',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest7' => 'The ship\'s company is eager for some brawls, and wants to scare some ruffians. They\'ve witnessed some cruel injustices lately, and couldn\'t do anything about it, so they want to at least hinder the other evildoers from being able to do anything similar. Can you recommend a few places?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest8' => 'One of my ghost crew found a map stuck between the walls of an old manor. Two spots are marked, and although the outlines of the island aren\'t visible anymore, it surely isn\'t the same one we found it on. Here take a lo-whooo-ok - maybe you\'ll recognize the mountains and the forest marked on the map. Maybe you\'ll find something good there. Will you share it with us?',
        'BuiBonus_GhostLantern_WeeklyQuest9' => 'I\'ve got a riddle for you! If you can\'t solve it, I\'ll have you run some errands for me as a forfeit. Deal?
OK, here goes! What has 2 wings but cannot fly? 3... 2... 1... Time\'s up!
If you still don\'t know when you return, I might tell you the answer.',
        'BuiBonus_GiftChristmasTree_Start' => 'The type of Christmas tree you just placed is really special. No-one really knows how or why it happens, but once a week, a new gift appears under each Gift Christmas Tree! Get your gift(s) by selecting a Gift Christmas Tree when the gift icon is hovering above it. The gifts will be collected, and automatically stored in your Star Menu in one big box for your convenience. Now, click your tree to get started and receive your first gift box - just be sure to check your Star Menu afterward!',
        'BuiBonus_GiftChristmasTree_Timer' => 'Wondering when you\'ll be able to find the next gift under your Gift Christmas Tree? 
Don\'t worry - I\'ve got it covered. Here you can see when the next gift will appear. 
The timer will restart after you grab your current gift.',
        'BuiBonus_GiftChristmasTree_Timer_Loop' => 'Wondering when you\'ll be able to find the next gift under your Gift Christmas Tree? 
Don\'t worry - I\'ve got it covered. Here you can see when the next gift will appear. 
The timer will restart after you grab your current gift.',
        'BuiBonus_GiftGhostShip_Start' => 'Whoo! Whoooo! Helloooooo! We are most grateful to you for placing a Ghost Lantern on your island. Most living beings are afraid of us and think we mean harm. But on the contrary! We are friendly beings, and a crew of adventurers that just cannot give up on this wonderf-whoooo-l world. There\'s just so much to disc-whooooo-ver. We will not vanish before our thirst for adventure has been quenched! Whooooo-hoo!
Our only regret is that nobody ever gave us a home to return to after our ghostly adventures, leaving us to simply wander around helplessly. So please, build as many ghost lanterns on your island as po-whoooo-ssible, so we\'ll be able to return. We will reward you for every lantern with one mo-whoooooo-re item in a ghostly reward box. We\'ll give you one box every week.
On top of that, we\'ll provide you with tidings on how you can get your hands on some extra rewards if you fulfill a certain task once a week. But only if you fulfilled the last task we gave you. We\'re not genies, you know?
Just check by our Ghost Ship that yo-whoooooo-u\'ll find on your west coast - I believe it\'s hard to overl-whoooooo-k.',
        'BuiBonus_HauntedMansion_Start' => 'Your settlers are starting to worry about that new mansion you built... They say it\'s haunted by ghosts! Let\'s investigate.',
        'BuiBonus_Offshorelighthouse_Start' => 'The old lighthouse keeper is offering his surplus catch.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Bronze_02' => 'The refinery functions well enough, Major, yet the copper it yields still bears too much waste within it.
I believe the furnace temperatures can be controlled more precisely. With proper calibration, we may yet improve the quality of our copper greatly.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Bronze_03' => 'Now that the copper runs cleaner, another flaw reveals itself.
Too much heat escapes through the exhaust channels, and the molten metal cools before the casting process is complete.
If we redesign the furnace flow, we may increase both yield and speed alike.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Gold_01' => 'Gold tests precision more than strength.
Even the slightest impurity dulls its shine and lowers its worth.
We must learn finer separation techniques if we wish our gold to rival royal minting standards.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Gold_02' => 'Several crucibles cracked during the last operation, and excessive temperatures ruined entire batches.
If we improve the heat regulators and insulate the refining chambers, we may preserve far more precious metal.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Gold_03' => 'Now that our gold refinement nears perfection, demand grows beyond our current capacity.
We must strengthen the refinery\'s upper systems and stabilize the production flow before prosperity destroys its own source.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Iron_01' => 'Iron is less forgiving than copper. The refinery can melt it, aye, but not consistently.
We must improve the furnace lining and reinforce the pressure systems if we are to tame iron properly.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Iron_02' => 'The new iron techniques have exposed another weakness.
Our bellows cannot maintain steady airflow during prolonged refinement, ruining entire batches.
Larger pressure chambers may solve the matter.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Iron_03' => 'Though the iron quality improves, waste still gathers within the slag pits.
Too much usable metal is lost during the refinement process.
If we recover these remnants and refine them anew, our efficiency may rival the greatest foundries of distant kingdoms.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Platinum_01' => 'Platinum may prove the greatest challenge yet.
Our current methods leave too many impurities trapped within the metal.
To refine platinum properly, we must achieve a level of precision beyond anything attempted before.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Platinum_02' => 'Our platinum techniques succeed, yet only barely.
Minute flaws within the furnace alignment throw entire refinement cycles into ruin.
If we improve the refinery\'s internal precision, the results may surpass all expectations.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Platinum_03' => 'We have refined copper, iron, gold, titanium, and now platinum itself.
Yet I believe the refinery still possesses untapped potential.
One final improvement may elevate this place from a mere industrial center into a wonder remembered for generations.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Titanium_01' => 'Titanium is unlike any ore we have refined before.
The heat required to shape it strains the furnace beyond safe limits, while ordinary crucibles weaken and split under the pressure.
If we are to master this metal, the refinery itself must grow stronger.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Titanium_02' => 'Titanium refinement pushes our systems dangerously close to failure.
Pipes warp, and entire chambers tremble under the furnace heat.
We require reinforced materials and advanced cooling systems if the refinery is to survive continued operation.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Titanium_03' => 'Though we can now refine titanium, the process remains painfully slow.
If we redirect the furnace flow and optimize the pressure network, production may improve dramatically.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Unlock_01' => 'My Major, the ore we haul from the earth grows poorer with each season. Yet I have heard tell of distant folk who draw greater bounty from lesser stone.
Seek out knowledge scrolls during your adventures and bring them back.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Unlock_02' => 'The plans are laid before us, yet a refinery is no humble forge. Every channel must carry molten metal without bursting apart.
See the construction finished and the mechanisms set in motion.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Unlock_03' => 'The refinery consumes fuel like a starving army consumes bread.
The old texts speak of refined charcoal and compressed fuel bricks. Strange methods...
See that these instructions reach our provisioners.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Unlock_04' => 'The new fuel will change the refinery entirely.
The furnace will burn hot enough to soften the stubborn ores that once resisted us, and the great mechanisms will finally move with the strength their makers intended.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Upgrades_01' => 'I have studied the recovered plans night after night, and I am certain now: our refinery was never meant to stand alone.

There are entire techniques missing from its design.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Upgrades_02' => 'Several portions of the design remain unfinished, almost deliberately so. Empty chambers. Unused pressure lines. Space reserved for techniques absent from the scrolls we gathered.',
        'BuiBonus_OreRefinery_Upgrades_03' => 'Rumors speak of northern engineers who harness steam pressure, desert metallurgists who separate ore with powdered salts, and distant island artisans who refine steel through repeated folding and purification.',
        'BuiBonus_Smokehouse_MiniStart' => 'The island\'s master smokers have prepared a special delicacy in your honour. Pay a visit to the Smokehouse Tribute and see what they have waiting for you.
You can find your Smoked Fish Steak in your Star Menu after visiting the Smokehouse Tribute.',
        'BuiBonus_Smokehouse_Mini_Loop' => 'Creating the perfect smoked delicacy takes time. The island\'s master smokers never rush their craft and only serve the finest results.
Come back in a day to collect your next Smoked Fish Steak. Remember: a new one won\'t be prepared until the previous one has been collected.',
        'BuiBonus_Smokehouse_Mini_Timer' => 'Creating the perfect smoked delicacy takes time. The island\'s master smokers never rush their craft and only serve the finest results.
Come back in a day to collect your next Smoked Fish Steak. Remember: a new one won\'t be prepared until the previous one has been collected.',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCovenUpgrade_Start' => 'Mayor, have you noticed the odd newcomers?

We should pay them a visit and make sure they don\'t start any trouble with the locals.',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCovenUpgrade_Upgrade1' => 'Ah, Mayor, welcome back!

Oh, 1,000 apologies for our previous behavior. I’m sure you understand how the stresses of travel can wear one down.

We see you have an interesting collection of texts with you.

If you present us with a complete set, we will make it worth your while.',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCovenUpgrade_Upgrade2' => 'Mayor! Your latest gifts have proven most useful... Most useful indeed, haha!

There are many secrets — so much knowledge yet untapped.

Why not provide us with any ancient scriptures you can find?

A person of your stature cannot be left behind in matters of wisdom...',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCoven_CancelBLoodustA' => 'It would be a shame to leave an unsatisfied customer.

Never fear. We can undo the effects... for a price...',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCoven_CancelBLoodustB' => 'We take great pride in providing only the best service money can buy.

Not happy? We can undo the effects... for a price...',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCoven_CancelRisenArmyA' => 'It would be a shame to leave an unsatisfied customer.

Never fear. We can undo the effects... for a price...',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCoven_CancelRisenArmyB' => 'We take great pride in providing only the best service money can buy.

Not happy? We can undo the effects... for a price...',
        'BuiBonus_WitchCoven_PageReward_Repeatable' => 'As you know, our sisterhood is always on the search for untold knowledge.',
        'CQ1M1_FourWinds_Tcl1' => 'Crisis! The watcher in the tower sent out several warnings over the past months but none reached us until this morning. In his letter, he says that the four winds of the world are soon to be reunited in a huge storm right above our archipelago. Apparently, this event happens every 100 years, and we do have records of the last super storm. Back then, it destroyed most of our kingdom. We cannot allow this to happen again! This is a crisis! We must prepare for the worst!',
        'CQ1M1_FourWinds_Tcl2' => 'Crisis! The watcher in the tower sent out several warnings over the past months but none reached us until this morning. In his letter, he says that the four winds of the world are soon to be reunited in a huge storm right above our archipelago. Apparently, this event happens every 100 years, and we do have records of the last super storm. Back then, it destroyed most of our kingdom. We cannot allow this to happen again! This is a crisis! We must prepare for the worst!',
        'CQ1M1_FourWinds_Tcl3' => 'Crisis! The watcher in the tower sent out several warnings over the past months but none reached us until this morning. In his letter, he says that the four winds of the world are soon to be reunited in a huge storm right above our archipelago. Apparently, this event happens every 100 years, and we do have records of the last super storm. Back then, it destroyed most of our kingdom. We cannot allow this to happen again! This is a crisis! We must prepare for the worst!',
        'CQ1M1_FourWinds_Tcl4' => 'Crisis! The watcher in the tower sent out several warnings over the past months but none reached us until this morning. In his letter, he says that the four winds of the world are soon to be reunited in a huge storm right above our archipelago. Apparently, this event happens every 100 years, and we do have records of the last super storm. Back then, it destroyed most of our kingdom. We cannot allow this to happen again! This is a crisis! We must prepare for the worst!',
        'CQ1M1_FourWinds_Tcl5' => 'Crisis! The watcher in the tower sent out several warnings over the past months but none reached us until this morning. In his letter, he says that the four winds of the world are soon to be reunited in a huge storm right above our archipelago. Apparently, this event happens every 100 years, and we do have records of the last super storm. Back then, it destroyed most of our kingdom. We cannot allow this to happen again! This is a crisis! We must prepare for the worst!',
        'CQ2M1_TheFallenArmy_Tcl2' => 'War. Such a short word for something so powerful. It’s a good thing  we have never been faced with a war - the battles we fight pale in comparison. But yes, war is raging at the outer rims of the kingdom, and, alongside his generals, our King Damien is doing his best to keep trouble from our gates. One of our kingdom\'s armies, the Ewanian Pioneers, is known to be composed of the most extraordinary soldiers this world has ever seen. It is the elite army of the King, and now they\'re at war at the rim, and a new darkness is rising. The King has ordered us all to establish an aid plan - we need to support them with all we\'ve got, and as soon as possible!',
        'CQ2M1_TheFallenArmy_Tcl3' => 'War. Such a short word for something so powerful. It’s a good thing  we have never been faced with a war - the battles we fight pale in comparison. But yes, war is raging at the outer rims of the kingdom, and, alongside his generals, our King Damien is doing his best to keep trouble from our gates. One of our kingdom\'s armies, the Ewanian Pioneers, is known to be composed of the most extraordinary soldiers this world has ever seen. It is the elite army of the King, and now they\'re at war at the rim, and a new darkness is rising. The King has ordered us all to establish an aid plan - we need to support them with all we\'ve got, and as soon as possible!',
        'CQ2M1_TheFallenArmy_Tcl4' => 'War. Such a short word for something so powerful. It’s a good thing  we have never been faced with a war - the battles we fight pale in comparison. But yes, war is raging at the outer rims of the kingdom, and, alongside his generals, our King Damien is doing his best to keep trouble from our gates. One of our kingdom\'s armies, the Ewanian Pioneers, is known to be composed of the most extraordinary soldiers this world has ever seen. It is the elite army of the King, and now they\'re at war at the rim, and a new darkness is rising. The King has ordered us all to establish an aid plan - we need to support them with all we\'ve got, and as soon as possible!',
        'CQ2M1_TheFallenArmy_Tcl5' => 'War. Such a short word for something so powerful. It’s a good thing  we have never been faced with a war - the battles we fight pale in comparison. But yes, war is raging at the outer rims of the kingdom, and, alongside his generals, our King Damien is doing his best to keep trouble from our gates. One of our kingdom\'s armies, the Ewanian Pioneers, is known to be composed of the most extraordinary soldiers this world has ever seen. It is the elite army of the King, and now they\'re at war at the rim, and a new darkness is rising. The King has ordered us all to establish an aid plan - we need to support them with all we\'ve got, and as soon as possible!',
        'CQ2S10_Revelation_Tcl2' => 'This is outrageous! We have got word from the Royal Advisor that Dust Hold is receiving support deliveries, the origin of which was tracked back to our borderland islands! It seems bandits on the borders of our Settlement are supplying the very barbarian stronghold our troops are currently battling! We must act immediately, rally troops, build the fastest ships we can, and purge those islands!',
        'CQ2S10_Revelation_Tcl3' => 'This is outrageous! We have got word from the Royal Advisor that Dust Hold is receiving support deliveries, the origin of which was tracked back to our borderland islands! It seems bandits on the borders of our Settlement are supplying the very barbarian stronghold our troops are currently battling! We must act immediately, rally troops, build the fastest ships we can, and purge those islands!',
        'CQ2S10_Revelation_Tcl4' => 'This is outrageous! We have got word from the Royal Advisor that Dust Hold is receiving support deliveries, the origin of which was tracked back to our borderland islands! It seems bandits on the borders of our Settlement are supplying the very barbarian stronghold our troops are currently battling! We must act immediately, rally troops, build the fastest ships we can, and purge those islands!',
        'CQ2S10_Revelation_Tcl5' => 'This is outrageous! We have got word from the Royal Advisor that Dust Hold is receiving support deliveries, the origin of which was tracked back to our borderland islands! It seems bandits on the borders of our Settlement are supplying the very barbarian stronghold our troops are currently battling! We must act immediately, rally troops, build the fastest ships we can, and purge those islands!',
        'CQ2S1_Reconstitution_Tcl2' => 'The liberation of Randomar has taken grave toll on the King\'s troops. Right now every bit of help is welcome to get our men back on their feet again. They are short on food, and the barren rocks of Randomar provide hardly any shelter during the freezing nights. Let\'s provide what we can to help out our Pioneers!',
        'CQ2S1_Reconstitution_Tcl3' => 'The liberation of Randomar has taken grave toll on the King\'s troops. Right now every bit of help is welcome to get our men back on their feet again. They are short on food, and the barren rocks of Randomar provide hardly any shelter during the freezing nights. Let\'s provide what we can to help out our Pioneers!',
        'CQ2S1_Reconstitution_Tcl4' => 'The liberation of Randomar has taken grave toll on the King\'s troops. Right now every bit of help is welcome to get our men back on their feet again. They are short on food, and the barren rocks of Randomar provide hardly any shelter during the freezing nights. Let\'s provide what we can to help out our Pioneers!',
        'CQ2S1_Reconstitution_Tcl5' => 'The liberation of Randomar has taken grave toll on the King\'s troops. Right now every bit of help is welcome to get our men back on their feet again. They are short on food, and the barren rocks of Randomar provide hardly any shelter during the freezing nights. Let\'s provide what we can to help out our Pioneers!',
        'CQ2S2_Recovery_Tcl2' => 'Why were our esteemed Pioneers sent to Randomar in the first place, you\'re asking? Well, those barbarians have been intercepting our trade routes for decades, and were harassing our settlements, stealing whatever they could get their hands on. It\'s time to recover the stolen goods now! Send some Specialists to see what goods can be regained, and get rid of any spoils of war we might have in stock ourselves!',
        'CQ2S2_Recovery_Tcl3' => 'Why were our esteemed Pioneers sent to Randomar in the first place, you\'re asking? Well, those barbarians have been intercepting our trade routes for decades, and were harassing our settlements, stealing whatever they could get their hands on. It\'s time to recover the stolen goods now! Send some Specialists to see what goods can be regained, and get rid of any spoils of war we might have in stock ourselves!',
        'CQ2S2_Recovery_Tcl4' => 'Why were our esteemed Pioneers sent to Randomar in the first place, you\'re asking? Well, those barbarians have been intercepting our trade routes for decades, and were harassing our settlements, stealing whatever they could get their hands on. It\'s time to recover the stolen goods now! Send some Specialists to see what goods can be regained, and get rid of any spoils of war we might have in stock ourselves!',
        'CQ2S2_Recovery_Tcl5' => 'Why were our esteemed Pioneers sent to Randomar in the first place, you\'re asking? Well, those barbarians have been intercepting our trade routes for decades, and were harassing our settlements, stealing whatever they could get their hands on. It\'s time to recover the stolen goods now! Send some Specialists to see what goods can be regained, and get rid of any spoils of war we might have in stock ourselves!',
        'CQ2S3_Sharing_Tcl2' => 'Only now have we discovered that the clan lords puppeteering the barbaric raids have taken to a desolate mountain keep - Dust Hold they dub it. And here we were thinking we had swiftly brought peace to these shaken lands... Nevertheless, before we embark on any military action again, let\'s send out our Pioneers in the spirit of peace and spread distribute to the civilians!',
        'CQ2S3_Sharing_Tcl3' => 'Only now have we discovered that the clan lords puppeteering the barbaric raids have taken to a desolate mountain keep - Dust Hold they dub it. And here we were thinking we had swiftly brought peace to these shaken lands... Nevertheless, before we embark on any military action again, let\'s send out our Pioneers in the spirit of peace and spread distribute to the civilians!',
        'CQ2S3_Sharing_Tcl4' => 'Only now have we discovered that the clan lords puppeteering the barbaric raids have taken to a desolate mountain keep - Dust Hold they dub it. And here we were thinking we had swiftly brought peace to these shaken lands... Nevertheless, before we embark on any military action again, let\'s send out our Pioneers in the spirit of peace and spread distribute to the civilians!',
        'CQ2S3_Sharing_Tcl5' => 'Only now have we discovered that the clan lords puppeteering the barbaric raids have taken to a desolate mountain keep - Dust Hold they dub it. And here we were thinking we had swiftly brought peace to these shaken lands... Nevertheless, before we embark on any military action again, let\'s send out our Pioneers in the spirit of peace and spread distribute to the civilians!',
        'CQ2S4_Elitist_Tcl2' => 'The King requests reinforcements. He wants to recruit some of our Veterans to take over Dust Hold. We will offer our most proficient men. The current bandit activities around our own settlement will give us some opportunity to survey our armies and identify the most able fighters.',
        'CQ2S4_Elitist_Tcl3' => 'The King requests reinforcements. He wants to recruit some of our Veterans to take over Dust Hold. We will offer our most proficient men. The current bandit activities around our own settlement will give us some opportunity to survey our armies and identify the most able fighters.',
        'CQ2S4_Elitist_Tcl4' => 'The King requests reinforcements. He wants to recruit some of our Veterans to take over Dust Hold. We will offer our most proficient men. The current bandit activities around our own settlement will give us some opportunity to survey our armies and identify the most able fighters.',
        'CQ2S4_Elitist_Tcl5' => 'The King requests reinforcements. He wants to recruit some of our Veterans to take over Dust Hold. We will offer our most proficient men. The current bandit activities around our own settlement will give us some opportunity to survey our armies and identify the most able fighters.',
        'CQ2S5_Equipment_Tcl2' => 'It is an honour for our troops to join the king\'s legendary Pioneers and aid in the conquest of Dust Hold. We have to make sure our men have the best equipment at their disposal. Gather our master smiths and provide the best materials. There is little time though - Dust Hold is re-arming, and marching orders have been given. No time to lose!',
        'CQ2S5_Equipment_Tcl3' => 'It is an honour for our troops to join the king\'s legendary Pioneers and aid in the conquest of Dust Hold. We have to make sure our men have the best equipment at their disposal. Gather our master smiths and provide the best materials. There is little time though - Dust Hold is re-arming, and marching orders have been given. No time to lose!',
        'CQ2S5_Equipment_Tcl4' => 'It is an honour for our troops to join the king\'s legendary Pioneers and aid in the conquest of Dust Hold. We have to make sure our men have the best equipment at their disposal. Gather our master smiths and provide the best materials. There is little time though - Dust Hold is re-arming, and marching orders have been given. No time to lose!',
        'CQ2S5_Equipment_Tcl5' => 'It is an honour for our troops to join the king\'s legendary Pioneers and aid in the conquest of Dust Hold. We have to make sure our men have the best equipment at their disposal. Gather our master smiths and provide the best materials. There is little time though - Dust Hold is re-arming, and marching orders have been given. No time to lose!',
        'CQ2S6_StandingArmy_Tcl2' => 'We need to ramp up our standing army now. We might have to extend our economy in places, so make sure we have a basic army in place, that our boys are fit for when the King arrives with his detailed requests, and we have provided any goods needed to improve the speed of our recruitment process.',
        'CQ2S6_StandingArmy_Tcl3' => 'We need to ramp up our standing army now. We might have to extend our economy in places, so make sure we have a basic army in place, that our boys are fit for when the King arrives with his detailed requests, and we have provided any goods needed to improve the speed of our recruitment process.',
        'CQ2S6_StandingArmy_Tcl4' => 'We need to ramp up our standing army now. We might have to extend our economy in places, so make sure we have a basic army in place, that our boys are fit for when the King arrives with his detailed requests, and we have provided any goods needed to improve the speed of our recruitment process.',
        'CQ2S6_StandingArmy_Tcl5' => 'We need to ramp up our standing army now. We might have to extend our economy in places, so make sure we have a basic army in place, that our boys are fit for when the King arrives with his detailed requests, and we have provided any goods needed to improve the speed of our recruitment process.',
        'CQ2S7_Scheming_Tcl2' => 'This is Dust Hold\'s doing! They are instigating riots in our vicinity to sidetrack us and weaken our support for the King\'s troops! Quickly - we must suppress the upheaval before things get out of hand! And make sure you keep our troops in good shape, so they are ready on call when the King\'s orders reach us!',
        'CQ2S7_Scheming_Tcl3' => 'This is Dust Hold\'s doing! They are instigating riots in our vicinity to sidetrack us and weaken our support for the King\'s troops! Quickly - we must suppress the upheaval before things get out of hand! And make sure you keep our troops in good shape, so they are ready on call when the King\'s orders reach us!',
        'CQ2S7_Scheming_Tcl4' => 'This is Dust Hold\'s doing! They are instigating riots in our vicinity to sidetrack us and weaken our support for the King\'s troops! Quickly - we must suppress the upheaval before things get out of hand! And make sure you keep our troops in good shape, so they are ready on call when the King\'s orders reach us!',
        'CQ2S7_Scheming_Tcl5' => 'This is Dust Hold\'s doing! They are instigating riots in our vicinity to sidetrack us and weaken our support for the King\'s troops! Quickly - we must suppress the upheaval before things get out of hand! And make sure you keep our troops in good shape, so they are ready on call when the King\'s orders reach us!',
        'CQ2S8_Aquisition_Tcl2' => 'This is it. The King\'s messenger reached us this morning. The King is inspecting troops from all Islands, and only the best are being accepted to join his elite forces. His demands are quite specific and there is not much time, so no dawdling - we must merit the King\'s trust in us!',
        'CQ2S8_Aquisition_Tcl3' => 'This is it. The King\'s messenger reached us this morning. The King is inspecting troops from all Islands, and only the best are being accepted to join his elite forces. His demands are quite specific and there is not much time, so no dawdling - we must merit the King\'s trust in us!',
        'CQ2S8_Aquisition_Tcl4' => 'This is it. The King\'s messenger reached us this morning. The King is inspecting troops from all Islands, and only the best are being accepted to join his elite forces. His demands are quite specific and there is not much time, so no dawdling - we must merit the King\'s trust in us!',
        'CQ2S8_Aquisition_Tcl5' => 'This is it. The King\'s messenger reached us this morning. The King is inspecting troops from all Islands, and only the best are being accepted to join his elite forces. His demands are quite specific and there is not much time, so no dawdling - we must merit the King\'s trust in us!',
        'CQ2S9_Perseverance_Tcl2' => 'Our scouts report great advances on the frontlines. Victory seems within reach. This is heartening news. Let\'s not fail to provide support for our troops though - repair and recovery is crucial out there. In the meantime, we must also not let control of our borderland territories slip. We should constantly have scouts patrolling our borders to keep an eye on those bandit-infested regions.',
        'CQ2S9_Perseverance_Tcl3' => 'Our scouts report great advances on the frontlines. Victory seems within reach. This is heartening news. Let\'s not fail to provide support for our troops though - repair and recovery is crucial out there. In the meantime, we must also not let control of our borderland territories slip. We should constantly have scouts patrolling our borders to keep an eye on those bandit-infested regions.',
        'CQ2S9_Perseverance_Tcl4' => 'Our scouts report great advances on the frontlines. Victory seems within reach. This is heartening news. Let\'s not fail to provide support for our troops though - repair and recovery is crucial out there. In the meantime, we must also not let control of our borderland territories slip. We should constantly have scouts patrolling our borders to keep an eye on those bandit-infested regions.',
        'CQ2S9_Perseverance_Tcl5' => 'Our scouts report great advances on the frontlines. Victory seems within reach. This is heartening news. Let\'s not fail to provide support for our troops though - repair and recovery is crucial out there. In the meantime, we must also not let control of our borderland territories slip. We should constantly have scouts patrolling our borders to keep an eye on those bandit-infested regions.',
        'CQC3M1Q1_SomethingEvil_lvl16' => 'Something isn\'t right… Our settlers feel tired and exhausted all day. Even nature itself has yet to come out of its hibernation. It is as if the whole kingdom is miserable. Maybe you can provide some refreshments to get your settlers going again?',
        'CQC3M1Q1_SomethingEvil_lvl26' => 'Something isn\'t right… Our settlers feel tired and exhausted all day. Even nature itself has yet to come out of its hibernation. It is as if the whole kingdom is miserable. Maybe you can provide some refreshments to get your settlers going again?',
