        'Easter2018plus_TutAchievementBuild_Sub02' => 'Of course, before you can start upgrading it and take full advantage of this lovely building, you\'ll need to place it somewhere on your island.

It looks a little bizarre, doesn\'t it? Where do you think would it look best?',
        'Easter2018plus_TutAchievementBuild_Sub02_University' => 'Of course, before you can start upgrading it and take advantage of this lovely building, you\'ll need to place it somewhere on your island.

A university, though? Where would you put a university? Maybe near to plenty of residencies? I can imagine people not wanting to walk a long way from their homes?',
        'Easter2018plus_TutAchievements' => 'Surprise! I\'ve brought you a little present since it\'s Easter, and, well, you know, Easter! Anyway, I need your help with some Easter related tasks. Since I know there are a lot of slackers out there, I\'ve decided to only be generous to those who really help me out.

So, here\'s the deal: I will give you a special building for your island. It\'s a special Easter building with a twist: Instead of paying for its upgrades, I want you to do stuff for me. What kind of stuff? Well, let\'s start at the beginning.',
        'Easter2018plus_TutAchievements_Sub01' => 'So, what do I need you to do? 

Check out the Achievement panel! There are specific Easter-related achievements that you can only do during this event. Each achievement gives you points specific to this event. 

I will give you the Easter Achievement building now.
Instead of spending resources on upgrades, it can be upgraded when you earn achievements and collect more achievement points from the Easter event. Every new upgrade level will require more points.

Check out what you can do in the Achievement panel!',
        'Easter_Event_2015_Buff_Adventure_MainQuest' => 'For a long time now, where Easter eggs come from has been one of life\'s biggest mysteries. Well, here\'s the truth. In a well hidden village, on a well hidden island, in a well hidden part of the world, there lies a small egg farm. But lately, there\'s been a problem. Polecats have overrun the island, and occupied the chickens\' nests so they can\'t lay any eggs!
Help the chickens to get their nests back.',
        'Easter_Event_2015_Buff_Adventure_SubQuest01' => 'A group of polecats scared away the chickens! If we want the chickens to hatch their eggs, we\'ll have to drive them away from the nests.',
        'Easter_Event_2015_Buff_Adventure_SubQuest02' => 'In order to make sure that the polecats don\'t cause any more havoc, we should try to catch them. 
The best bait to use is a special polecat gin.',
        'Easter_Event_2015_Buff_Adventure_SubQuest03' => 'Now that the predators have been safely removed from the island, all we need to do is to find the chickens. They should be hiding somewhere on the island',
        'Easter_Event_2015_Buff_Adventure_SubQuest04' => 'Now we have all the chickens - but they look a little bit scared? Perhaps even... unhinged? Maybe we can calm them down a little bit, and get them to roost?',
        'Easter_hunt1' => 'Pssst! Hey! I got a new game going on, that you can also play with your friends. 
Take this basket of eggs - at a bargain price I might add - and wait for further instructions from me. 
Trust me - it\'s going to be a blast!',
        'Easter_hunt2' => 'Hey, it\'s me again! 
Here\'s the tricky part of the deal - take the buff I gave, er... sold you earlier and apply it to one of your friend\'s Mayor\'s House. 
This will create hidden eggs on their island. 
After this, they have 12 hours to find them! Whatever they find, you both get to keep! 
Come on - give them a challenge! 

- Apply the "Easter Egg Hunt" buff to a friend\'s Mayor\'s House',
        'EconomicLong1' => 'Personally, I love scenario adventures. One of my particular favorites is “Storm Recovery” - I love the message of hope we leave to the inhabitants of the islands we help. I feel so alive every time we complete it! Do you think we could complete one this week?',
        'EconomicLong2' => 'You may think it’s pointless using valuable grout on depletable buildings like mines, but the benefits can be huge. Get some mines to level 6, and combine with refillers and buffs to see what I’m talking about!',
        'EconomicLong3' => 'This is terrible! I just received a letter from one of my cousins. He and his army are pinned down in the desert by bandits! He has sent an urgent request for elite weapons and horses. Please, I beg of you! Help my cousin!',
        'EconomicLong4' => 'Aunt Irma mentioned the other day that she hasn’t had time to breathe recently, she\'s been so busy making gift baskets for people she doesn’t even know! With this in mind, she\'s requested some holiday to recoup. This is unprecedented, but I think she may be right. How about we boost our production with potions of endless energy instead? If you’re missing some collectibles, I’m sure your friends can help, or you can find some in the market.',
        'EconomicLong5' => 'Collectibles are a great way of giving yourself a slight advantage, without putting in a whole lot of effort. If I let you in on a little secret, I actually find looking for them quite fun. Care to join me?',
        'EconomicLong6' => 'The king has requested that we provide certain materials and weapons to keep one of his most notorious prisons working at full capacity. Can we spare a few of these?',
        'EconomicLong7' => 'We\'ve received a surprise visit from an inspector that\'s come to check on your production chains. He will settle for nothing less than absolute perfection, so make sure they\'re working at full-force.',
        'EconomicLong8' => 'Some say that certain skilled geologists can actually find more than the maximum deposit size for certain minerals. I\'ve never seen one of them in action, can you show me how they work?',
        'EconomicMedium1' => 'Scenarios are very different to other adventures. Instead of sending your army in, you\'ll have to use your resources and skills to create the buffs needed to fix whatever situation you find yourself in. Oh, you say you already knew that? My apologies, I just came back from a VERY long vacation…',
        'EconomicMedium2' => 'I\'m sure you\'re already aware of the benefits of having marksmen and armoured marksmen in our elite army, so I guess it won’t come as a surprise that I have a request for extra arquebuses and additional battle horses, right?',
        'EconomicMedium3' => 'Gold is easily our most desired resource right now, but gold itself is not what we seek - instead, we want what we can manufacture with it. Make sure our production chains for gold and coins are in optimal shape. Don’t forget to use buffs!',
        'EconomicMedium4' => 'We should always maintain a steady income of platinum ore and platinum, both for our needs and theirs. Let’s make sure we have a proper production chain for platinum.',
        'EconomicMedium5' => 'We just received a report that two brothers have gotten lost on a remote island, and their family has asked for our help to find them. Can we spare some time to help these poor children?',
        'EconomicMedium6' => 'Many of our current weapons and units use gunpowder, so we need as much as we can get! Let\'s boost our gunpowder production as much as we can!',
        'EconomicMedium7' => 'Some friends of the king are on their way to pay us a visit. And by "some" I mean a family. And by "family" I mean 100 people. It\'s definitely the biggest family I\'ve ever seen. Let\'s produce a gift basket for every one of them!',
        'EconomicMedium8' => 'Our ecosystem is a very delicate one. The newfound exotic wood forests need to be taken care of carefully, otherwise they\'ll become extinct! Let\'s make sure our foresters do their job properly!',
        'EconomicShort1' => 'Now that we can finally extract granite directly from the source, we should be able to amass plenty of it in a short space of time! Let’s keep going. We can never have enough granite in our storage!',
        'EconomicShort2' => 'Along with having our production chains stable and working, it\'s equally important to boost their productivity whenever possible. By now, you know all about how important buffs are, so let’s create some extra buffs for us and our allies!',
        'EconomicShort3' => 'Despite being able to mine new, rare minerals, we mustn’t forget about essential materials like marble! Make sure to keep your geologists busy so they can find as many deposits as possible!',
        'EconomicShort4' => 'Platinum is scarce, and we\'ll need to get as much as we can to be able to complete the hardest adventures. Remember that another way of obtaining platinum is to send your explorers on prolonged treasure searches. Please get them to find some platinum ore for us!',
        'EconomicShort5' => 'One of our scientists has requested a few of the heaviest materials we have for research purposes. He\'s requested some titanium and gold ingots. Can you provide some?',
        'EconomicShort6' => 'We take pride in taking care of the less fortunate on our island. It\'s time to organize another campaign to feed the poorest souls. Prepare some bread and sausage, please.',
        'EconomicShort7' => 'Our titanium reserves are rapidly depleting, and we need to boost our mines. Let\'s invest in some tools to upgrade them - I\'m sure you won\'t regret it. It\'s even more efficient if you combine it with some buffs!',
        'EconomicShort8' => 'A prize-winning chef is visiting our island to prepare some sort of special tasting session for our nobles. She has asked if we can provide saltpetre so she can craft her own salt, and some cloth to make the meal visually appealing. Can you provide these?',
        'ExpDefeatLastBoss' => 'An island rich with resources - the perfect place for a colony! However, it looks like someone else has beaten us to it. Let\'s prepare an expedition, and see if we can chase them off! Maybe we can even convince the local bandits to help us guard this island afterwards?

But remember:
Seeing as the defenders outnumber us, we should choose our strategy wisely. Use your heavy troops to block regular camps and carry out a decisive strike against each sector\'s boss.
This way, we should be able to minimize our losses!',
        'ExpDefeatMeleeCamp' => 'In each sector, you will see two camps - a melee camp and a sector boss camp. This first melee camp does not look well defended, so we should try to defeat that first.

Use a marshal, along with some attack archers to defeat the camp. Attack units are good for defeating enemies quickly.

Also note that attack archers will do bonus damage to enemy melee units, while your own melee units won\'t. Melee units do well against cavalry instead.',
        'ExpDefeatSectorBoss' => 'Now, let\'s see what we can do against that sector leader... When you hover over the camp, you\'ll notice that there are two unit types in there, plus the leader itself. This battle will require some tactical skill. 

You\'ll need to change your units mid-battle. When attacking, note that the first enemy unit to be deployed is marked with an extra frame. You should bring a unit that\'ll be strong against it, and switch your unit type when the enemy makes a switch.',
        'ExpUseDistract' => 'Ok, now that we managed to succeed, let\'s see if we can refine our strategy. This is where our heavy units come into play.

Heavy units are excellent at taking a lot of damage, and can last a long time in combat. Attack a melee camp with your heavy units, so the camp will have its watch area deactivated. As there is only one unit type in there, you can let them fight on their own. 

Once the battle\'s begun, you can lead another marshal, along with some attack units, past the melee camp to attack the leader\'s camp.

And here\'s the best bit: When you defeat the leader, all other units in this sector will flee. That way, we can save a lot of our troops.',
        'FinalGuildFest_OpenPanel2' => 'Now the festivities are over, and the quests are all done,
Open the Guild Fest Panel, and see what you’ve won!',
        'GarrunQ1' => 'Scouts reporting: Garrun\'s hunting parties are spread all over the island. They\'re organized in small poaching sites centered around bigger Hunting Camps. 

- Destroy all the Hunting Camps',
        'GarrunQ2' => 'Only Garrun and his closest followers now stand between the bunnies and their freedom! 

- Defeat Garrun in his camp',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgument' => 'Our lords and ladies have yet again had a stupid argument and yes, we\'re going to have to clean up the mess. The latest issue is about the land they own, and the problem is that many of our buildings might be on their lands. Unfortunately, nobody knows for sure. I guess the deeds were burned in that nasty fire some years ago. Let\'s try to calm the lords down... nobody likes an angry lord.',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub1' => 'Yes, well our lords are so mad at each other that a few of them have requested you place some of the noble houses further away from each other. I don\'t think they really want that; maybe they\'re just mad. Anyway, maybe some good quality brew would calm down the spirits?',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub2' => 'There is some debate about who owns how much land. The problem is that one of the lords claims our farms were built on land belonging to him. Sadly, he is somewhat right. We have decided to pay him off by offering him some gold. I mean who can say no to gold, right?',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub3' => 'The lords claim their horses are old and dirty, so to calm them down we should give them some new ones as a gift! Ask your stable masters to provide us with the best horses they have!',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub4' => 'The lords have had a fight about the quality of food on the islands, and I fear things may start to get ugly. Luckily, I have a solution! We need to make sure we have a satisfying supply of sausages in our storehouses! And then we\'re going to need to gift the sausages... to show how much we appreciate our noblemen!',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub5' => 'The lords have had a debate about the safety of the island. Basically, they don\'t feel safe, and it\'s in our interest to make sure they do. A new stock of iron swords would do the trick!',
        'GuiDaiANobleArgumentSub6' => 'One of the lords is not sure of your trading abilities. How dare he? No... I must calm down. We must prove to him that we are outstanding traders! Prepare some fish! Fish is easy to trade!',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasure' => 'A legend exists telling of an old pirate who lost his ship and crew. He used to be spotted regularly, dragging his treasure with him, and was known for being extremely rude. However, no-one has seen him lately, and it is thought that he has passed away. Nevertheless, his treasure is out there somewhere… waiting for somebody to claim it! Let\'s have our guild work together to find it!',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub1' => 'In order to find the treasure we\'ll need to use our explorers! We can\'t ask them to become treasure hunters, but they\'ve promised to keep their eyes open. Send out your explorer, and let\'s see if he finds something! I presume he will get hungry, so some meat will help him! Prepare the meat!',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub2' => 'Our explorer has promised that next time he is out looking for whatever you send him to look for, he will also keep an eye out for the treasure. How nice. Be sure to send him out as soon as possible! He\'s taking along his family and he asked for some bread. We should make some bread for him, I guess.',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub3' => 'I\'ve talked with our explorer, and he said that next time he is out he will keep his eyes peeled for the treasure. Good man! Hope you require his services soon! While he\'s gone, we\'re going to fix his wooden hut. It\'s a way to say thank you! We\'ll need some pinewood planks for that!',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub4' => 'Listen! Our explorer has told us that he will definitely look for the treasure next time you have a task for him! I say! What a lovely man! He also asked us to take care of his mother\'s farm while he\'s gone. We talked to her, and she needs water. Time to grab you bucket…',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub5' => 'Our explorer came to me today and said he will look for any clues leading to the treasure while is he working on his task. He told us he needs to finish a statue for his brother, and I told him that we would be glad to handle it for him while he\'s looking for clues about the treasure! Anyway the statue is made of granite. You know what to do.',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub6' => 'You know what our explorer told me? He said he\'s going to look for clues when he is out there doing his task! Great! Before he left, he asked us to tend to his dogs, and it turned out he has around one hundred of them. The dogs like fish, and feeding time is approaching fast.',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub7' => 'The clues we\'ve gathered so far are vague and ambiguous, but there\'s a chance that the pirate buried his treasure on a certain adventure island. Maybe it\'s worth a check.',
        'GuiDaiATemporaryTreasureSub8' => 'Some of our knights seem to be quite interested in the swashbuckling skills of pirates. They\'ve requested some time, and a few weapons to study, so they can become an "Anti-Pirate Force", should we encounter any on our quests.',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwords' => 'The king wants to honour those who have fallen in the kingdom\'s battles over the ages by building a wall of swords, to be called (hold your breath)... The Wall of Swords. So now we must deliver a huge number of swords to the royal repository, and to top it all we haven\'t been given much time to do it.',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub1' => 'The miners union believes that they\'re protected by the Maiden, some woman that took care of them after an unfortunate accident. I hope the Maiden really is with them, because we need a lot of iron in order to start production of our share of the swords. Have your miners provide the iron ore.',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub2' => 'There was a time when there was so much steel ore that we allowed the smelters to have these steel panther statues made. Apparently, they\'re still around somewhere, but I\'ve never seen them. Anyway, we need to call upon the smelters; we need steel!',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub3' => 'We\'re about to produce a huge amount of swords, so we need to make sure our blacksmiths are ready for the task! I\'ve heard that some freshly baked bread might well motivate them!',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub4' => 'So the Wall of Swords will contain a lot of swords. Its rim will be made from steel swords, and our guild is to provide a certain amount of them, so you better have your weaponsmith ready; he will need to work day and night I\'m afraid.',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub5' => 'Oh dear. The King wants the top of the wall to be decorated with genuine Damascene swords. Does he realise how hard it is to obtain such swords? I know a man who sells them; maybe we can pay him to take some of his finest to Capital Island? Just make sure we can pay the man with our coins!',
        'GuiDaiAWallOfSwordsSub6' => 'So, the base of the wall will be made entirely of stone. I guess that\'s the part that gets dirtiest after the rains. Stone is not so easy to polish, I reckon. We\'ve received an order to provide a shipments of stone.',
        'GuiDaiAWallofSwordsSub7' => 'Most of the troops we\'ve lost were on adventures trying to make our kingdom better in every way. The best way to honour their lives would be to take our army on an adventure, and pay our respects to their memory in the process, don\'t you think?',
        'GuiDaiAWallofSwordsSub8' => 'Aside from the wall, the king would like a parade to be performed in memoriam of those who lost their lives. The general suggested that we should lead the parade with the finest battle horses, so let\'s do that.',
        'GuiDaiAWildBet' => 'The leaders of the guild of hunters have made a bet about whose island will be the most populated with animals! We mustn\'t lose this bet - make sure we have the most animals in our forests!',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub1' => 'In order to increase the island\'s wildlife, we need to have more trees so the animals can hide and feel safe. We need our foresters to come up with their best seeds! Let\'s send them some sausages as a thank you gift!',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub2' => 'I am not convinced the new animals will move into our forests fast enough, so how about we help them make a quick decision? Let\'s place stashes of wheat in random places. I\'m sure that will get their attention. Have your farms provide wheat!',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub3' => 'We\'ll be needing more wheat than we thought to lure the first animals, so we have to make sure we can provide the required amount. The best wheat comes from the best farms!',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub4' => 'Sadly, we don\'t have very many lakes in the new forest, so we need to create some watering pools. And for that we need water. Fast.',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub5' => 'We need to be sure that our animals have a good time and feel peaceful. It would be best to know exactly where the animals are going to dwell. We need to build some wooden lookouts in the woods, and for that we\'ll need planks!',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub6' => 'We need to feed the animals for the first weeks, so we\'ve decided to build a feeding garden. It\'s like a normal garden but for animals, you see? We have to keep it natural though, so we\'re going to use mostly hardwood.',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub7' => 'I\'ve been thinking... What if we just move the hunter\'s hut a little bit further away? If he doesn\'t hunt any animals, we may be closer to winning the competition, right? Do you think this would count as cheating?',
        'GuiDaiAWildBetSub8' => 'We should make a new stable. One specially designed to hold as many horses and battle horses as possible. Mahogany seems like a good choice. Its scent soothes the animals, and it\'s sturdy like... well, a horse.',
        'GuiDaiAirMail' => 'Listen to this! They want to use birds to send letters! There\'s a bird-master who arrived just this morning to set up a pigeon post on the island! Sounds interesting... I mean, imagine how fast the mail could be sent and received!',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub1' => 'The pigeons will need a specially built coop so we can breed them there. I would use pinewood planks if I were you!',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub2' => 'We\'re going to need someone with a lot of patience to train the pigeons. I think using some recruits would be the best idea!',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub3' => 'We need a special kind of bird food - one which can\'t be easily acquired. One general has mentioned that they know the seeds we\'re looking for, and will bring some back the next time they go on an adventure. We\'ve urged them to go now.',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub4' => 'The bird-master wants to set up a smaller water system for the pigeons. Yes, you\'ve guessed right - he needs some water.',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub5' => 'According to the bird-master, pigeons not only eat seeds, but bread too, believe it or not! Doh… do we look that stupid? Anyway, he needs some bread so he can feed the pigeons. A waste of good bread, if you ask me.',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub6' => 'The bird-master says that sadly, the pigeon coop will attract predators, probably eagles and other beasts. He\'s asked us for some longbows so he can protect his pigeons.',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub7' => 'The bird trainer informs me that birds are incredibly sensitive of their surroundings. They tend to be a lot more comfortable if the forests around them are blooming with wildlife. Let\'s help the birds feel at home!',
        'GuiDaiAirMailSub8' => 'The trainer suggests we build a separate, bigger cage for the fastest birds. It should be made of exotic wood and granite. Apparently, exotic wood reminds them of their homeland, so they\'re a lot more comfortable there. Let\'s make it!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoads' => 'The nobles of Capital Island have managed to convince King Damien that they need better and cleaner roads for their travels. Logically, the King has assigned us the great task of supplying the construction materials for the new road.',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub1' => 'The noble road, as it is apparently called, will be made using stone and then coated, or covered, with marble. You are to provide the stone from your rich stone deposits.',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub2' => 'The workers who are to build the road will almost certainly get very hungry. We are to provide our best bread and meat! Let them know that this guild makes the best food out there!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub3' => 'A marble paved road requires marble. The King was very specific that the marble should come from us. I guess he knows that we can provide the best! And we should be proud! They need our marble? We\'ll send them our marble!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub4' => 'Demand for marble might be higher that we expected! We need to make sure that we won\'t run out! Let us motivate our workers with some fine brew!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub5' => 'We need to make sure all our workers at the marble deposits are working as fast as they can! It might help motivate them if we sent some sausages. Everybody loves sausages!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub6' => 'Apparently Capital Island does not have enough workers, so they need us to send some over. It wouldn\'t be a bad thing for our workers; Capital Island has a lot to offer them. Prepare your men for the long voyage by ensuring there are enough horses to transport them all!',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub7' => 'The new roads will need better signs, so people know where the forks in the road lead to. They\'ll also have to be robust, so they don\'t get blown away by the wind. How about using some exotic wood planks for that?',
        'GuiDaiAllTheShinyRoadsSub8' => 'In order to keep our economy stable, the king has ordered the construction of toll booths at several points across the kingdom. These booths will give a single platinum chip to whoever pays the toll - and we have to produce said chips.',
        'GuiDaiAnobleargumentSub7' => 'I\'ve had an idea to ease the situation. A friendly competition of marksmanship. The nobles will test their skill against each other by shooting targets with a crossbow, and the winner will take a prize. Do you like it? Then let\'s get to it!',
        'GuiDaiAnobleargumentSub8' => 'It seems the situation isn\'t going to get any easier. The nobles are being louder and rowdier than usual. Perhaps it would be a good idea to subtly remind them who\'s in charge here. Have some of your elite cavalry "casually stroll" around the area.',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLife' => 'Capital Island is indeed a wonderful place to live. All the youngsters want to move there one day. The king has a dream that one day all the islands in the kingdom will be as big and flourishing as Capital Island. It\'s up to us to make the first step, so we need to build a lot of residences and have a lot of moms and dads. In order to expand, we need a lot of people!',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub1' => 'In order for us to expand we need big houses! And to build big houses we\'re going to need big tools! It\'s always good to have some new tools when you build new walls, right?',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub2' => 'We don\'t know how many new settlers to expect, so let\'s make sure we have beds for all of them. We\'re going to need some hardwood planks! I can\'t wait to live in a bigger city!',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub3' => 'I have some bad news! When we built our first residences, we made an error regarding the positioning. Don\'t ask me for more details - the cousin of one of our citizens is a architect, and he alerted us to the problem. Long story short, we need to twist and turn some of the streets. And for that we need stone!',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub4' => 'We know of course that our settlers need the water for various things. We have streets, we have houses and between them we have wells, so there\'s really nothing that can stop us from getting the required amount of water! They just need to be filled now. Have some water ready!',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub5' => 'When you have a big population, they have big expectations, and they can get a bit rowdy if they\'re left hungry. I think that if they get some extra food, they might leave us alone for a while, and just enjoy life. It would be an amazing help! Let\'s go with sausages... you can never go wrong with sausages.',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub6' => 'Though I\'m sure our lords and ladies have a comfortable enough lifestyle, that doesn\'t mean we can just forget looking after those in high society. For a start, plain noble residences are simply not good enough for them. This is why we\'ve decided to decorate some of the houses to look even more… noble, and that means we\'ll be needing some gold.',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub7' => 'Our librarian has suggested that in order to get more... "classy" scholars here, we may need to adorn our books with a bit more... finery. Let\'s provide a bunch of classy book fittings, and see if that helps.',
        'GuiDaiBigCityLifeSub8' => 'The king just mentioned that, apparently, people from high society don\'t like having to walk everywhere. For some reason, they\'d rather have someone in a carriage take them around? I don\'t get it. How will they see the beauty of our island if they don\'t walk?',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcano' => 'Up on Flintrock island, the villagers told one of our merchants that the whole island sits on top of a sleeping volcano - and they want to keep it that way. But last week there was a small eruption, and a hole appeared. A smoking one. They need our help to bury and seal that hole as soon as possible.',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub1' => 'We need to get some blocks of stone to the middle of the island and there are a lot of swamps along the way. If we use enough pinewood planks, we can build some smaller roads or bridges, if needed.',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub2' => 'We are going to use bronze cauldrons to transport the material to the hole. So guess what - in order to make bronze cauldrons, we\'re going to need some copper ore!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub3' => 'We\'re going to fill in the hole using marble! That way we can be sure to prevent any incident that might awaken the volcano!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub4' => 'We\'d like to assign a small group of guards to protect our people while they\'re on Flintrock island. Equip them with some iron swords!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub5' => 'We\'re going to need some strong people to help us with our project. The strongest I can think of are a group of soldiers! Let\'s train some!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub6' => 'We\'ve received a message that some ill-intentioned people want to intercept our shipments. I think we should make the first move!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub7' => 'The Flintrock volcano has been a bit agitated lately. One way to make sure it doesn\'t explode any time soon is by throwing some water inside. After all, we all know water puts out fires, right? We\'ll need a lot of it, though, so get to it!',
        'GuiDaiBurriedVolcanoSub8' => 'One of the locals told us that the volcano acts as the island\'s "stomach". The rumbles mean the island\'s tummy is hurting, and he suggests that we use a saline solution to calm it down a bit. Sounds like nonsense to me, but let\'s see if they\'re right!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIsland' => 'Our seafarers returned last night! And with good news! They have found the island that the bandits are coming from! It\'s called Dagger Island and is not far from here! I say we ready our men and storm the island! Let\'s teach them a lesson!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub1' => 'We don\'t know if the pirates are aware we\'ve found them, but before we can assemble an army it would be wise to ready some troops in case they surprise us! Ready the iron swords!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub2' => 'If we are to organize an assault we\'ll need to organize our army. The front line will be held by the militia, so you\'ll have to train them! I hope you\'ll use your famous trainer to look after it! We all know he tends to get hungry. Ready some fish for him!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub3' => 'The militia will hold the front line! Behind them, we need our bowmen! You are to provide the bows as fast as you can! Have them use the best weapons, and help them win the battle!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub4' => 'After our militia and bowmen are engaged in battle, we will have our cavalry flank our enemy! I need you to get your best horses for our cavalry! We better make haste!',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub5' => 'We are not sure how hard the bandits will fight back, so we had better be prepared! We need some cannons on our ships in case things get ugly. That way, we can help things to get even uglier, if you know what I mean. Deliver the cannons and mount them on the support ships, would you please?',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub6' => 'I can\'t believe it! You know that captain who was supposed to transport our units to Dagger Island? Well, he wants to be paid! The nerve! Oh well, I guess a small bag of gold ore will do the trick. Do we have any to spare?',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub7' => 'While our guild mates take care of the situation on Dagger Island, we should make sure that the bandits don\'t get reinforcements from the Nords. We should perform a pre-emptive strike on their island.',
        'GuiDaiDaggerIslandSub8' => 'If I were a bandit (which I\'m not), I would probably try to make contact with the east in search of potential allies. We cannot let that happen. To be sure, we should embark on an adventure in the desert!',
        'GuiDaiDarkLands' => 'Up there, far to the north, are some islands that never really experience proper sunshine. It\'s always dark up there. No wonder they\'re called the Dark Lands. We\'re taking part of a initiative to help the people who live there.',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub1' => 'I bet those lands have great stocks of minerals under the infinite looking snow fields, but I\'m sure they\'re having a hard time mining them out. For starters, we should send them shipments of stone.',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub2' => 'Hardwood can be used for many things, like housing, guard towers, boats, etc. I think a reasonable amount of hardwood would make a great gift!',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub3' => 'We need to find someone who can help us deliver some of the gifts to the Dark Lands. I would advise a little useful diplomacy: visit a friend and lend a helping hand!',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub4' => 'Landing on the shores of the Dark Lands will be hard, and we\'re expecting dangerous wildlife. Polar bears, white wolves, and who knows what else await us! We should train some militia and take them along for protection!',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub5' => 'We\'re going to need a lot of food for the voyage, and it seems we\'ve depleted some of our wildlife deposits. Before we leave, it would be a good idea to refill them.',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub6' => 'Ohh no! One of the transport ship has sprung a leak! We need to fix it as soon as possible! The ship was built using a lot of exotic wood planks, so fixing it will require more!',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub7' => 'There seems to be a lot of crime in the dark lands. It\'d be nice to help the local authorities restore some order. Let\'s take them out with our soldiers on an adventure, see if they learn a few tricks.',
        'GuiDaiDarkLandsSub8' => 'It\'s really hard to grow crops in the dark lands, due to... well, the lack of sun. I have this theory, however, that magic beans would grow nicely if watered correctly. Let\'s try it out.',
        'GuiDaiDesertRiders' => 'Sir! We\'ve found a storm-damaged ship near the coast! Apparently it belongs to a merchant who was supposed to bring a group of men to Capital Island. These men were born on an island covered by sand far to the south! Imagine, all that heat... The men call themselves the "Desert Riders" and seem to have a lot to trade! So, let\'s get to work!',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub1' => 'The Desert Riders can\'t get their eyes off our longbows! At first we thought it might be a sign of danger, but in fact they\'re just admiring them! They want our longbows and are ready to pay a good price, so let\'s not keep them waiting! Let\'s make them some longbows!',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub2' => 'The Desert Riders visited our stables today. I\'ve never seen men care for horses so lovingly. They sure know how to tend to these noble creatures! One of them mentioned that he would like to buy some of our herd! Let\'s make sure we provide them with all the horses they need.',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub3' => 'The Desert Riders have come to you for wheat. They\'ve heard that the horses we sold them love the wheat we make, so we\'llneed to provide them with it. I hope the horses can adapt to whatever else they get in the desert…',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub4' => 'The Desert Riders will be needing a lot of water if they\'re going to cross the ocean with so many horses! Let\'s make sure we give them the best water we have.',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub5' => 'We know that the Desert Riders will take care of the horses we sold them, but I would like to make sure they know how. We need some of our trained cavalry to teach them our ways! First lesson : how to use a carriage. Let\'s get some carriages ready for them.',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub6' => 'The ship the Desert Riders arrived on is really damaged and it\' up to us to fix it. The structure of the ship is not what we\'re used to, but I\'m sure our engineers can fix anything. In fact, they\'ve requested some hardwood planks and exotic wood planks for the starboard of the ship!',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub7' => 'It seems the damage to the ship is actually a lot worse than originally thought. The riders want to hire a few volunteers to help with the repairs, but they\'ll need a LOT of tools for that. Can we spare some?',
        'GuiDaiDesertRidersSub8' => 'They\'ve taken such a liking to our island, once they\'re all set for sailing they\'d like to grab a bunch of souvenirs to take with them. They\'ve suggested that we might want to attach some wheels to the souvenirs for easier transportation.',
        'GuiDaiEagleNest' => 'What do you know about Eagle Nest? Nothing? Let me enlighten you! Eagle Nest is a small fortress on top of that mountain there. Yes, the tallest one. The fortress has been raided by some bandits! We need to find a way to clear them out!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub1' => 'The bandits have destroyed the stone stairs that led up the mountain. I\'m still not sure if it was intentional or just an accident. We need to carry some stone with us and fix the gaps.',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub2' => 'Our general has done a count, and in his opinion our army is not big enough. We need more recruits in order to take back Eagle Nest!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub3' => 'The bandits have burned down most of the surrounding woods, and most of the wildlife has fled the area! We need to refill those deposits, fast!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub4' => 'The general leading this mission is not sure the army recruits are ready for such an encounter! He wants them to experience some combat first!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub5' => 'I know it sounds stupid, but Eagle Nest got its name because of the actual eagles living here. The eagles get agitated with all this fighting, and it’s dangerous for our troops to climb while being attacked. However, we have found a solution: fish! They love fish! Let\'s give them some!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub6' => 'The general wants to take along a Golden Brew Mug. He claims it will bring him luck in the upcoming battle at Eagle Nest.',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub7' => 'Here\'s an idea. Certain parts of that mountain are inaccessible by road. If we make some staircases and climb up to their blind spots, we may be able to surprise the bandits. Let\'s try that!',
        'GuiDaiEagleNestSub8' => 'At some point, some bandits will undoubtedly try to escape and make a break for freedom. We should provide some mounted marksmen to prevent this from happening - but we can\'t afford them to be inexperienced. Take them on an adventure first!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisiting' => 'Several ambassadors from neighbouring kingdoms and lands are coming to visit, and we have to make sure that their visit goes without any problems, so they can put in a good word for us with their leaders. Our guild has been commissioned with this task!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub1' => 'I like to think of ourselves as hospitable hosts, and so I\'d like to have a nice memory of the ambassadors being here. We should make a visitor book where we can record their signatures.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub2' => 'Our guests have to eat! I\'ve already devised a menu for them to choose from over the next few days, so the hardest part has been taken care of. What we need from you, is to provide the bread and the brew to accompany these delicacies!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub3' => 'The ambassadors\' visit is the perfect time to show how proficient our ironworks are. We should show off how our blacksmiths\' work the iron by holding a demonstration session.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub4' => 'Our carpenters work hard to always provide the finest longbows in the kingdom. Our archers have also grown accustomed to these bows, so how about impressing our guests by shooting some flying sausages with arrows?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub5' => 'One of our guests has asked about the process of manufacturing our wheels, since to the naked eye, they seem to be free of imperfections. Why don\'t we take him to one of our workshops and show him?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub6' => 'If we want to show the ambassadors that we\'re reliable as potential allies, we need to show them how important they are to us. Please arrange some visits to our allies and make sure they have all they need!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub7' => 'We\'re in charge of arranging the celebration party for their arrival. Make sure they feel welcomed with a fancy fireworks show!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_AmbassadorsAreVisitingSub8' => 'One of the ambassadors has come to us enquiring about adventures, and has shown some interest in taking part in one first-hand. Would you kindly take him to see one?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFair' => 'This year we decided to hold a "Do-it-yourself" fair to teach people be more crafty and self-sufficient. The guild has been asked to take care of all preparations, so we all have to pitch in!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub1' => 'One of our bakers has offered to host a workshop where people can learn how to make some fine bread. Or at least, the basics of making fine bread - he doesn\'t want to lose any business after all! He\'s requested that we offer some materials to help with the preparations.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub2' => 'There\'s a lot of things that can be done with wood and planks, and we\'d like to teach them to craft a few easy things. You know, the usual: a stool, a table... We\'ll need to provide a bit of hardwood, and some tools for this to be a success.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub3' => 'We invited a professional scribe to come to our island and teach a few things about calligraphy to anyone who wants to learn. He was happy to accept... As long as we provide the materials for the drill.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub4' => 'There\'s a lot more to archery than just shooting a bow. Crafting the bow itself properly requires finesse and practice, and our local bowmaker wanted to hold a workshop to explain why. He\'s requested a few examples of our longbows for this purpose.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub5' => 'Not everyone is partial to a bit of fish, bread and sausage! Some people have a bit more of an acquired taste, and we want to "treat" them to a cooking course so they can learn some delicious recipes. Let\'s provide the ingredients!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub6' => 'Our carpenters want to host a more advanced woodcraft course for those who already know their saws from their chisels. We want to teach them how to make sturdy carriages for their domestic needs.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub7' => 'Did you know that gunpowder could be used to season food? How about as a medical supply? I didn\'t! Our local gunpowder handler would like to teach the public these, and many more facts about the many uses of gunpowder, but he needs us to provide some materials first.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_DIYFairSub8' => 'Lumps of granite can be turned into beautiful works of art with the right tools and knowledge. We would like to hold a sculpting workshop for local art aficionados. We need to provide some granite and lots of tools for it, though.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetition' => 'This time our guild is in charge of the Capital Island\'s Easter egg competition! They seem to have liked ours so much they wanted it for themselves - but I say we can make it even better. Think we can pull this off?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub1' => 'Our assignment is to have enough crates to be able to store the eggs that are going to be used in the competition. We\'re going to need a bit of extra manpower for this... Can you pay a visit to our allies and ask for help?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub2' => 'Well, this is a problem... It seems that we don\'t have enough actual eggs to use in the competition. But have no fear, I have an idea - why don\'t we make some artificial eggs out of marble? It would definitely do the trick!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub3' => 'Our task is to provide the third prize for the competition. We have received a request for some raw gold ore. Also, we\'ve been instructed to deliver invitations to our close allies, so let\'s get to it.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub4' => 'The competition is going to pull in a lot of people, and the food may not be enough to go around. Let\'s make sure that we ask our allies to make sure that our food factories are on top of their game, and that we provide enough meat for the contest.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub5' => 'We\'ve been asked to provide the podium where the winners will stand at the end of the competition. We\'re going to need some exotic planks and gold for that to happen. Can you produce some?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub6' => 'We\'re running short on eggs for the competition, and the only way to meet the quota would be to head over to an adventure and obtain some more there. Grab your troops, we\'re going on an egg hunt!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub7' => 'The king wants to log the names of the competition\'s record holders on a big piece of parchment that will be displayed in the town square. We need to provide the fine paper for that, and platinum to adorn the document.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_EasterEggCompetitionSub8' => 'We\'re running a bit short on the budget for the competition, so we\'ll need to pull together some extra funds wherever we can. It\'s time to hit the markets with some rare materials - that will definitely get us what we need!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildren' => 'We\'ve been tasked today with providing the entertainment for the children. I already have some ideas, but we\'ll need the help of the whole guild to pull it off. Can I count on you all?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub1' => 'The kids are impressed with how the bowmen handle their bows, so we\'ve decided to craft some safe toy bows for them to play with, a get a feel for archery. Let\'s get to it!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub2' => 'It\'s nice and warm today, so how about we make a small pool for the kids to splash around in and have some fun? I\'m sure they\'ll love it.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub3' => 'Let\'s have some horseback riding areas spread around for the kids to enjoy. I\'ve already talked to the stables, and they\'re willing to spare enough horses. Can you take care of the rest?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub4' => 'We called upon a famed storyteller from a neighbouring kingdom to come and tell us of adventures and tales that have never been heard before. Could we get some paper so we could have a written copy of the stories for the future?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub5' => 'Kids love tree forts. We\'ve decided to make a few of them around the island in the pine trees, so there are enough for everyone. I just hope they leave the "no girls allowed" thing be. That is so last century...',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub6' => 'Our stable masters have made a small circuit where the kids can race horses. Of course, it\'s all safe and measured. I checked personally! We just need to provide the carriages and horses, and they\'ll take care of the rest.',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub7' => 'We\'ve got to make sure there are enough food stalls around so nobody gets hungry! How about we make some sausage stands to distribute food?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_FunForTheChildrenSub8' => 'Our local boy scout group needs new uniforms. The old ones are starting to get worn out and the colours are not what they used to be. Can we provide some cloth and platinum to our local tailors so they can make new, shiny uniforms?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestival' => 'We hardly ever appreciate the efforts of our workers on our island, so I thought it may be a good idea to have our own celebration in their honour. Let\'s gather the guild to make sure this festival is as good as they deserve!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub1' => 'Our local fishermen have approached me to suggest that the festival may be a good chance to improve their business, so they wanted to host a small event. Can we provide some refreshments for the attendants?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub2' => 'There\'s a new trend for having your name engraved on marble slabs and using them as decorations on your home. Our artisans have decided to take up a few requests. Can we perhaps help them out with the marble?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub3' => 'The famous writer and work counselor Jerdaint will grace us with his presence at a book-signing session at the festival! We have to make sure that he has enough paper and nibs to sign all the books he can!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub4' => 'There\'s always been a friendly rivalry between the militia and the soldiers. They\'ve requested a small space and some weapons so they can settle their differences. Can we provide?',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub5' => 'No festival would be complete without the traditional brew-chugging contest! The stomach that can hold the most brew will win a fabulous prize that... Oh, wait, there\'s no prize? We need to change that!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub6' => 'We\'re expecting a lot of attendants at this festival, so we have to make sure we have enough food for everyone. Let\'s try to get enough grub for the traditional festive barbecue!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub7' => 'Woah! With all the festival preparations we\'ve been doing, we forgot that people would still be searching and finding eggs. They\'ve almost found them all! I\'ve gathered our best horse riders to quickly hide a bunch more, but we need horses and carriages for them to use!',
        'GuiDaiEaster2016_WorkerFestivalSub8' => 'In order to keep the Easter festivities relevant, we\'d like to host an egg decorating contest for everyone who wants to participate. We\'ll need to provide some fine ornaments for people to use. Could you please gather some?',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmy' => 'There has been a terrible war in the land to the west, and the King\'s Elite Army was involved. Sadly, they were heavily wounded and must return to Capital Island to recover. Together with the other guilds, we need to lend a helping hand.',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub1' => 'The Elite Army has some very unusual rules and habits. Apparently, all they eat while they\'re on a mission is wheat and anything that can be made from it. I think we should send them some wheat!',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub2' => 'Each time the army is defeated, they like to sculpt the face of their enemy in marble. We\'re not going to ask why. Just prepare a marble block for them - we should have plenty, right?',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub3' => 'The Fallen Army has a book, and we\'ve received a copy of one of the chapters about recruit training. They want us to give them tactical feedback. We need to check it out.',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub4' => 'Some of the fallen military units have asked to join us on our adventures. We can\'t say no - they need to stay in shape! Let\'s help!',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub5' => 'The general of the Fallen Army has asked us to take some of his officers to experience an adventure. I guess he doesn\'t want them to get lazy.',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub6' => 'Sadly, there were many wounded units. The doctor from Capital Island has asked for a number of carriages - he wants to turn them into small vehicles to help some of the wounded units move around.',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub7' => 'The king\'s blacksmith has reported that there\'s a shortage of weapons! We need to provide some additional hands at the blacksmith\'s to ensure the troops have enough titanium equipment.',
        'GuiDaiFallenArmySub8' => 'The king has issued an official statement declaring that he requires reinforcements for his personal army. We\'ve been tasked with providing some mounted marksmen and knights for the war. For the kingdom!',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurniture' => 'There is a report here. A ship that was bound for Capital Island is going to stop for a quick break, and we need to welcome them. They\'re transporting some special kind of furniture for one of the lords. We should help them. For a price, of course.',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub1' => 'They\'re holding the furniture on stone blocks. We were asked what kind of stone we produce here on the island. I had to ask one of our people from the quarry to answer that. Apparently, we have the right kind of stone.',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub2' => 'It seems the ship\'s crew is bored of the food they get each day. The first mate smelled our morning bread, and now he wants to surprise the others. Let\'s give him some fresh bread.',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub3' => 'The captain came to me this morning. The ship has to be in excellent condition when it arrives at Capital Island, but right now, one of the ornaments on the eastern mast is damaged thanks to a storm they run into. He wants us to get him some marble so he can have his crew fix the ornament.',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub4' => 'Oh! I\'ve had a fisherman here complaining that the fancy ship has dropped anchor directly over his school of fish. I\'ve had the ship moved, but I think we should help the fisherman out and refill his fish deposit!',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub5' => 'The Captain is ready to pay a small fortune if we\'ll agree to take him on an adventure. I\'ve asked the commander, and he\'s said yes.',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub6' => 'While the ship is here, I\'ve decided to invite the Captain to have dinner with us. I think it would make a good impression to let him have some of our finest brew in a Gold Mug!',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub7' => 'May I suggest something? As a gesture of goodwill, perhaps we might craft some exotic wood furniture and share the plans with our new guests? I\'m sure they\'ll appreciate it - and it\'ll get us in the king\'s good books too!',
        'GuiDaiFancyFurnitureSub8' => 'Our guests have seen our mahogany reserves, and have asked for a lesson in the economy of mahogany production. I told them all they need to do is invest in some magic beans and craft the planks with adventure spoils, but they\'re insisting on a demonstration.',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnow' => 'We\'ve been contacted by the dean of the Village School regarding an urgent matter. Winter is closing in, and he wants the children to experience the same kind of fun they get in summer. Yep, he wants the children to have fun in the snow! Now there\'s an interesting guild project!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub1' => 'One of your friends owns a small workshop that can make sledges for children to use in winter. You should pay him a visit, help out, and maybe your friend will tell you the secret of how to make them!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub2' => 'There\' going to be a snowball competition, so how about we make the kids a decent target? I say we use a marble block and have our sculptors carve it into something. The children can then use the marble statue as target practice! Snowball fun to the maximum!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub3' => 'A friend of yours used to make these amazing candy canes. Children *really* love candy canes! You should visit your friend, help out a bit, and maybe get the recipe!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub4' => 'Ice skating is great fun, but we can’t trust winter to froze our lakes solid, and imagine if there are any accidents! What we can do however is dig a smaller hole and fill it with some water. The small quantity will freeze solid for sure, when the right time comes! Let\'s store some water for when the winter comes!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub5' => 'We need to assign some settlers to prepare the winter games for the children. We should replace them with some new settlers, don\'t you think?',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub6' => 'There is a tale of a very friendly breed of deer. It would heighten the mood to have some nice deer in the city when winter comes. The only problem is, we\'ve no idea where to find them. Luckily, one general does and wants to go look for them.',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub7' => 'We have to make sure that everyone stays warm when they\'re out in the snow. How about some eggnog in a golden brew mug? We\'ll hire someone to make it for us, don\'t worry!',
        'GuiDaiFunWithSnowSub8' => 'We\'d like to play a game where the kids put a magic bean inside a snowball and throw it as far as they can. Wherever it lands on the island, "their" magic beanstalk will grow. Let\'s distribute a few to the children and let them play.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalk' => 'Capital Island has many gardens but nothing that compares with the Royal Gardens. The King is really proud of this. He wants every guild to come and have their own garden inside the Royal Gardens. I guess it\'s a question of status, I don\'t know. We should load up, go to Capital Island, and make our own garden.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub1' => 'Since our friends have heard we\'re going to have our own garden, they keep sending us all kinds of gifts. In return, the logical move would be to thank them before we leave for Capital Island.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub2' => 'There should be plenty of trees in that garden, but we don’t want to harm them. If we want to build ivy hangers, tables, and benches, we\'re going to need to bring our own hardwood.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub3' => 'Our general has told us our military units could use some action before we leave. It would be a good idea to have a field drill.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub4' => 'We need to take along a lot of workers, but we don\'t want the island to lack working settlers. You should bring some new ones as soon as possible!',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub5' => 'Some of our settlers have told me they\'re going to join our trip because they want to visit Capital Island. I can\'t say no really -they\'ve never been off the island before. However, we will need to find people to replace them while they\'re away.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub6' => 'The King says that each and every guild garden should be guarded by soldiers. This means we need to bring along some soldiers, but I wouldn\'t choose the best ones. I mean, they\'ll need to stand in one place for a long time and not let people in, right?',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub7' => 'We\'d like to offer an incentive to the captains that are sent to our royal garden for peacekeeping. How about a golden brew mug? I think this should be enough to keep the captain\'s attention on the job for at least a week.',
        'GuiDaiGardenWalkSub8' => 'In order to make our share of the garden unique, we should decorate it with some ornaments that can\'t be found anywhere else. Let\'s make some using platinum and exotic wood!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDay' => 'Every now and then our geologists organize this race where they compete with each other. Now the time has come for another race! Each guild must send out their geologists to find certain deposits! In the time it takes them to get back, we must prepare a feast! Get to it! We must duly honour our geologists for their hard work!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub1' => 'Our guild\'s geologist has been tasked to find a marble deposit! In order to do that, he\'s going to need some tools! This is so much fun!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub2' => 'Our geologist has been tasked to find an iron deposit! We\'ve already prepared an escort but they will need some food too! When asked what he wants he said : Sausages!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub3' => 'Our geologist is to find a gold deposit! It\'s not the easiest of tasks, but I\'m sure he can do it! I don\'t want to worry you too much, but looking for gold is dangerous! You know, bandits, and all that. I want to send some guards to escort him. Get some horses ready!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub4' => 'Our geologist needs to find a coal mine. I hope he knows what he\'s doing; a deposit like that could be tricky to find! He also asked us to get him some water he can take along. Looking for coal can get you dirty.',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub5' => 'Our geologists are about to return from the race and we want to have the feasts ready by then! Our cooks are ready to do their magic and you are the one who can provide them with the necessary ingredients! They want to make a special fish meal! So… let\'s bring them fish!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub6' => 'We don’t usually do this, but we would like to give a prize of coins to the best geologist! You are to provide the coins! I hope you realise this is a great honour?',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub7' => 'We have been tasked with keeping our geologists in shape so they can keep up with the race. Let\'s prepare some meat for them so they\'re always on the top of their game!',
        'GuiDaiGeologyDaySub8' => 'Our geologists are the ones that have the most experience in searching for the rarest of materials. Therefore, it\'s up to us to top the rankings in this category. Let\'s try getting some saltpetre and titanium deposits working!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailors' => 'Every year we celebrate the "Day of the Sailors" event. Practically the entire island is flooded with sailors for a day, and we organize various events for them and share the fun. This year it\'s our island\'s turn to hold the event, so let\'s get to work!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub1' => 'A sailor\'s favorite food is fish, there\'s no doubt about that, so we\'ve hired Piero, the world famous cook, to prepare the perfect fish soup! He is going to use a ray-finned fish called Alosa agone. What a name!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub2' => 'One of the most beloved events is marble pulling. Basically, two teams have to pull a block of marble from one point to another, and guess what? We have to provide the marble block!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub3' => 'As funny as it might sound, sailors love to catch fish with their bare hands. They sure do look funny while they\'re doing it. We need to fill some deposits and make sure we have enough fish for them to have fun with!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub4' => 'We need to designate a gift to give to the leader of the Sailor\'s Crew. The best one would be a Golden Brew Mug!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub5' => 'The sailors want to try out some melee combat, but they\'re used to different kinds of swords. We should prepare some fine steel swords for them to parley with!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub6' => 'Some of the sailors want to tag along on an adventure. They\'re allowed to join in as soldiers.',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub7' => 'Among other things, sailors are known for their world-class quaffing competitions. We decided to host an official tournament called "All you can quaff"... with our finest brew! The prize is a granite bust of the winner. Let\'s prepare the mugs!',
        'GuiDaiHappySailorsSub8' => 'By now you\'re used to using saltpetre for making gunpowder, but did you know that it can also be used for spicing up food? And did you know that granite slabs also make for great frying pans? Let\'s produce some nice food to offer up!',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountain' => 'Our guild has received the strangest request. We are to build a mountain. Yes, you heard me correctly - Lord Edword, the king\'s nephew from the Sunset islands, is prepared to pay a fortune to have his own artificial mountain. I trust we can do it. I mean, nobody has tried such a thing yet. Who knows, it might even work.',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub1' => 'In order to build an actual mountain we will need a lot of stone. And when I say "a lot", I mean it. We would like to ask for your master masons to work double shifts.',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub2' => 'While we do need a lot more stone, we must not forget that we also need something to transport the blocks with. For this reason, I would advise you to provide carriages. Using carriages for transportation is the safest way.',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub3' => 'Though we have already sent out some stone shipments, we still need a lot of stone to build the mountain, and there\'s no time to waste. Let\'s send out our workers; those masons won\'t get the stone by themselves.',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub4' => 'We will eventually get the carriages, but we also need horses to pull them. I would advise you to visit your stables and have them prepare their best steeds. There\'s a lot of stone to be pulled.',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub5' => 'Granite is stronger than stone because its mineral composition has bound together tightly during the very slow cooling period. And the quartz and feldspar of which it is composed it are harder than steel! Than steel! So in order to build a strong mountain we\'re going to use granite. And here\'s where you come in. We need you to provide it. We\'re sure you know where to find the best! The best!',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub6' => 'We have received word that those who are to work on the mountain are on a very strict diet of fish. I guess they live healthily, right? Anyway, they just can\'t get enough fish, so we will provide them with our finest. Alert your fishermen; they have work to do!',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub7' => 'It seems that we may have underestimated the amount of granite we needed for this request. Our guild mates cannot keep up. Can you perhaps help them out with some of your reserves?',
        'GuiDaiHowToBuildAMountainSub8' => 'When you\'re laying the foundations of an artificial mountain, you need to go really deep. I heard that platinum seems to absorb sunlight for a while, making it both a great tool and a flashlight in one! Handy! Let\'s put that theory to the test.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarkness' => 'The miner\'s union on your island has decided that in order for them to operate at full potential, they will need a system of tunnels connecting all the mines around the island. We don\'t want to upset them, so let\'s start working on it. He he, if we try hard enough we might even be able to build a city down there!... I\'m sorry, that\'s nonsense.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub1' => 'Though our miners could simply use their own tools to start work on the tunnels, I believe we should provide them with new ones. It would be a good idea to start production of some brand new tools. Once they are ready, we can send them down the tunnels.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub2' => 'So, I hear that they will be needing a loot of wood and wood planks too. The tunnels need a structure, like… a supportive frame? I don\'t know how that works, but alert your settlers at the sawmill; we need pinewood planks.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub3' => 'The main shafts require stronger wood to hold fast, so we need to ask you to provide the miners with some of your famous planks made of hardwood. Please have your settlers at the sawmill prepare some good quality hardwood planks.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub4' => 'Apparently there are not enough mine entrances to fill the new tunnels with sufficient air, so the union would like to be sure the tunnel system has enough air holes. However, the holes need to be clad with iron, so we\'ll need some iron ore from the union. They\'re kind of working for themselves on this one. Air is important, right?',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub5' => 'We have a problem. The union workers are refusing to eat just any kind of vegetable; they want meat, and they want a lot of it! Let\'s give them them meat and keep them quiet.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub6' => 'You won\'t believe this. The miner\'s union wants to build a walkway inside the tunnels! Well we need to satisfy their needs, so let\'s provide them with some marble they can use. Bah… next they will ask for an underground lake or something.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub7' => 'The miners want to put our structures to the test. They\'re planning to take some cannons down there, and fire them all at the same time. Personally, I think that\'s insane, but they seem rather confident. For their sake, I hope they know what they\'re doing.',
        'GuiDaiImprovedDarknessSub8' => 'One of the miners came out as white as a sheet. He says he heard a terrifying growling down in the mine, and he thinks there\'s a monster in there! Send some swordsmen in, and see if there\'s anything to worry about.',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSea' => 'Captain Ironplank, the marshal of the King\'s navy has arrived this morning at our island. He wants our guild to help him with an important matter. Some months ago he sent out some of his men to scout the border islands, and all his ships returned except one. We are to prepare a search expedition with Captain Ironplank and find his crew! What a honourable task!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub1' => 'Though we\'re making sure they\'ll get our support for their food supply, the Captain has said that some of the men love their meat just as it is.... i.e. raw. They have some special kind of mixture of spices that they use to make their own meals. Let\'s make sure we give them some good meat.',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub2' => 'Captain Ironplank tells me that he loves seagulls and that they bring luck. His ship is filled with seagulls actually, a fact I find most disturbing. Anyway, I\'m telling you this because he has requested an unusual amount of bread, and I\'m not really sure it\'s for his crew... but who am I to ask questions? Let\'s give the man his bread!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub3' => 'The Captain is renowned as fearless, but he also knows that going into combat without proper equipment is simply foolish. To avoid defeat, he has requested we provide him with some of our finest steel swords. I think we can manage that, don\'t you?',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub4' => 'The Captain believes morale is more important than the sword, and can be lifted by giving a rousing speech, handing out rewards, etc. And then there\'s the question of brew. Not only does it raise morale, but it can also slake thirst! So, we are to provide some of our finest brew for the crew! Let\'s do it!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub5' => 'The Captain says that the sea is teeming with pirates and you never feel safe out there. He and his crew must be very brave men and women! He has asked us to provide some of the longbows we make on the island. I guess they might come in handy if they get into a skirmish at sea. Good thinking!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub6' => 'As it turns out, the Captain\'s favorite food is a good plate of fried fish with some squeezed lemon. Let\'s make sure we give the captain some fish from our stock!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub7' => 'Just in case we run into trouble, we should bring enough gunpowder to load the ship\'s cannons. Make sure you produce enough!',
        'GuiDaiLostOnTheEndlessSeaSub8' => 'I just had a thought... Maybe the captain landed on a deserted island. And by deserted I don\'t mean "without people", but an island with a desert on it. We should check the ones we know of for clues.',
        'GuiDaiPerAContribution' => 'It is widely known that with a contribution at the royal council, the guilds can gain certain advantages. Place some capital at your guild\'s disposal.',
        'GuiDaiPerADeedForADeed' => 'Our settlers have great confidence in your guild, but they would also love to be sure you have good diplomacy skills. Your settlers have asked whether your friends can visit the island and help out. I\'m sure you can handle such an easy request!',
        'GuiDaiPerAGoodFriend' => 'Last night an old friend of mine visited me, and it felt so good to see him again. It\'s really important to keep in touch with friends, you know? Especially if you\'re in a guild that holds friendship in such high regard! To celebrate friendship, we should visit a friend\'s island and lend him a helping hand!',
        'GuiDaiPerAdditionalRooms' => 'Some of our settlers have complained that every time their relatives come to visit, they don\'t have enough room! We better do something about that! We can\'t have visitors sleeping outside in the haystacks! Be sure you have enough room and food for their next visit! Our guild must not only take care of our settlers, but their kin too!',
        'GuiDaiPerAgainstVengence' => 'One of the bandit camps our soldiers wiped out during a patrol was ruled by a fearless leader. Though our soldiers have destroyed the camp, the leader managed to escape back to Dagger Island, where we believe the bandits are based. Why am I telling you this? Apparently the leader wants vengeance. We should be ready to protect ourselves from his wrath, should he decide to attack. Let\'s make sure we will be able to defend ourselves!',
        'GuiDaiPerAllTheFishInTheSea' => 'There is a new "master" fisherman who claims he can catch one hundred fish in one go. Ha! I\'ll believe it when I see it, but it would be a great spectacle for the people! Our guild will rise to the challenge! Let us show him that our fishermen are the best!',
        'GuiDaiPerArcherCamp' => 'Our best archer is about to take our youngest for some good old archer training in the forest! Our guild is always very supportive when it comes to such activities. Let\'s make sure we provide him with our finest bows!',
        'GuiDaiPerBattleReady' => 'I can\'t believe it! You remember the people who left civilization only to continue life in the midst of mother nature? Well, they\'re back, and they seem angry! I\'m not sure if we can calm them down or not… but we should be ready for a clash nevertheless! Your guild is most respected, so you have been asked to provide the guards for the meeting! Make sure you have the necessary troops!',
        'GuiDaiPerBoiledMeat' => 'You know what that old woman living in the dark woods has told me? That she boils the meat! Boiled meat! I tried it and it tastes amazing! Let\'s do a good deed for our guild and send some meat to the King! Provide the best meat you can!',
        'GuiDaiPerCleaningTheLibrary' => 'The librarians have heard about our guild and come to me with an interesting request. They want to clear out the library, and that means removing all the papers, books, and scrolls. However, high winds are to be expected, so they need us to give them some iron bars to lay on the papers and books, so the wind won\'t blow them away. Sounds like a very wise tactic. If it\'s iron they want, iron they shall get.',
        'GuiDaiPerDangerousTimes' => 'A scout has arrived this morning, reporting several unknown ships near our island. It could just be some lost fishermen... but it might also mean trouble! Our guild should be prepared for every eventuality, so let\'s make sure we have enough iron swords in our storehouse!',
        'GuiDaiPerEarlyDayMarket' => 'The Nights of the Catfish feast is right around the corner, and our guild is one of the main suppliers! It seems there\'s huge demand for fish already, so we should go to the market and sell some.',
        'GuiDaiPerEarlyMorning' => 'Good morning! Or is it? The guild has just received a letter containing information about a new task you should not leave unattended! Make sure you read the letter as soon as possible!',
        'GuiDaiPerEcologicalProblem' => 'For a long time the forests had been exploited carelessly, and now whole patches are completely bare. The king likes guilds to take care of the woods. Do something to help the ecological problem.',
        'GuiDaiPerFastPlanks' => 'You remember the house our guild built for the old hermit ages ago? It seems that a storm has damaged it, and it might collapse soon! Another storm may come at any time, and we should be ready for any damage it could do! Make sure you have a hardwood sawmill and some hardwood planks! We need to prepare fast!',
        'GuiDaiPerFavoriteIsland' => 'Queen Anita has a habit of choosing an island that she will favor for the rest for the year. Her choice is based on the island\'s workflow. A busy island is a good island! Let\'s make sure she chooses us! We need to produce some resources! This would be a great honour for our guild!',
        'GuiDaiPerFishingGrounds' => 'You have heard of shrinking fishing grounds throughout the ocean. As the king seems very concerned about this sort of thing, perhaps you can use the situation to the advantage of your guild?',
        'GuiDaiPerForBrewBreadAndHorse' => 'Our wheatfields really are a beautiful sight to see! Nevertheless, the problem remains - we need more wheat! Our farmers say they need more farms to keep up with demand! Your guild wants you to make sure you have enough farms on our island!',
        'GuiDaiPerFromForreignHands' => 'They keep saying the bread currently sold on the market is the best bread ever. In order to see if that\'s true, you need to become the guild\'s delegate, so go to the market and get some bread!',
        'GuiDaiPerGardenPets' => 'A lady from Capital Island has written a letter to our guild. She has an amazing garden and wants it filled with pets! Not live pets, no no! Marble pets! Apparently she believes that pets made from marble won\'t run away from home… well I can\'t really argue with that. Let\'s send her some of our finest marble!',
        'GuiDaiPerGoodRelations' => 'We need to be sure our friends don\'t forget how much we and our guild care for them. And we care for them a lot! Let\'s make sure we take some of our Aunt Irma\'s baskets over, and buff one of their buildings.',
        'GuiDaiPerHouseOnWheels' => 'The technician who came up with a number of good building ideas is back again! He wants to build a moveable house, and has asked our guild to help him with the resources he needs for the tests! So! Let\'s help!',
        'GuiDaiPerImportTools' => 'Our guild has hired some woodcutters, and they came to see me yesterday to complain about the quality of our tools! They claim that imported tools are much better, which I doubt very much! Let\'s prove that our tools are the best! Obtain the required amount of tools through trading!',
        'GuiDaiPerIntoTheWild' => 'Any great man or woman should eventually look for a new challenge, right? I think the time has come for you to maybe take a break and look for an adventure that would benefit not only you, but also your guild! What do you say?',
        'GuiDaiPerKeepingAnEyeOpen' => '"A guild must be built on a strong base of trust and cooperation," the book of the Guilds reads. I guess it must be true! It\'s in this extremely important-looking book, after all. It also says here that every guild must have its own stash of coins, marked with the banner, so we must start striking some coins! Make sure we own all the coins we need!',
        'GuiDaiPerMadeOfGold' => 'Have you ever heard of gold termites? No? Me neither. Apparently, all these little creatures do is eat gold ore. We need to keep them out! The only way to do that is to get a lot of water! The termites hate wate, but we will be needing a lot - the Miner\'s Union has many tunnels down there.',
        'GuiDaiPerMoreWorkMoreTools' => 'It seems that with so much to do around the island, our tools are getting worn out really fast. We need to ensure our settlers always have the required tools. Be sure to have enough tools in your storehouse!',
        'GuiDaiPerNewfangledForge' => 'I always feel nervous when the King sends his specialists to share their knowledge with us. They\'re usually really grumpy. The one that came last week wrote a note saying our forges are really old fashioned. We must not let this news reach the ears of the King! Make sure you own at least two upgraded forges!',
        'GuiDaiPerOverseaFavors' => 'Our lady of the southern coast had a dream last night! In her dream, an angel appeared from the sky and dropped stars on our buildings! She believes this to be a sign! Our guild should make her dream come true! Let\'s ask our friends to come over and gift us some buffs!',
        'GuiDaiPerSecretCargo' => 'One of the main captains of the Royal Fleet, captain Ironplank, has sent out several ships with a "secret" cargo. The ships are to dock at random islands where the cargo will be stored, and we may be among their choices. The captain wants all the islands to be able to store these goods if possible. We need to make sure we have enough brew and sausages in case our guild is chosen.',
        'GuiDaiPerSellingWater' => 'This morning we found a crate on our shores. One of our settlers opened it and found a brand new cannon inside. I\'m not sure where it came from, so it\'s probably best to get rid of it! The guild certainly doesn\'t need it. Make sure you trade it at the market!',
        'GuiDaiPerSlowTimes' => 'The Miner\'s Union believes the workers around the island have slowed down lately. Maybe they\'ve gotten tired? No, no, it can\'t be that! They\'ve asked you to make some nice sandwiches, as maybe that will raise morale! It would certainly help your guild to be more appreciated by the Miner\'s Union!',
        'GuiDaiPerSpeedMail' => 'Capital Island has sent our guild a message about a new system they want to implement regarding mail delivery. They have some people from the west who claim they are able to tame horses like no other! They are to be hired as scouts if they speak the truth! We are to provide our finest horses!',
        'GuiDaiPerStoneForTheGuild' => 'Stone is not only a basic product for building but also an effective good for trading. To be of help to your guild, you should always produce sufficient stone.',
        'GuiDaiPerSwiftness' => 'Because you are quite new to the guild, you need to expand your economy quickly. When the king has a new request, the person to react the quickest often gets the king\'s favor.',
        'GuiDaiPerTheAuntsBasket' => 'While walking through the forest, I met Aunt Irma. She was very glad to see me, and pleased to hear her special basked of goodies helped our settlers do their work! She even accompanied me to the mayor\'s house! Let\'s make five Aunt Irma\'s Baskets - she\'s promised she will attend to make sure everything is done correctly!',
        'GuiDaiPerTheHarderTheWood' => 'The guild has received a letter from the scouts. They require some shelters up in the mountains. We can\'t build them ourselves, but they assure us that if we give them the hardwood planks they will look after it themselves. And it\'s windy up there; they\'ll need strong planks indeed. Let\'s get them their hardwood planks.',
        'GuiDaiPerTheHungryMiners' => 'Did you notice that our miners are starting to look a bit tubby? I mean, one would think that working in the mines would keep them in shape! I\'ve sniffed around and found out that our miners are eating a lot of sausages! No wonder that they\'re so fat! That\'s it! The guild is cutting rations! However, we need to fill our stocks back up, so make sure we have enough sausages in our storeroom.',
        'GuiDaiPerTheIronBanners' => 'The lord of one of our lumberyards has decided to have a banner made from iron, and now every lord wants an iron banner. It\'s not like we jump every time they want something, but I think we can make an exception this time. Iron banners do look rather good, after all. Let\'s make sure we provide them with all the iron they need.',
        'GuiDaiPerTheIronWagon' => 'A wealthy merchant just arrived in the city  with the strangest of requests. Apparently, he wants to find his long lost friend - but he doesn\'t know where to look! He\'s also oddly paranoid about a potential bandit attack He wants to buy some iron ore from our guild in order to make himself an iron wagon. And who are we to question him?',
        'GuiDaiPerTheSparkInTheGrass' => 'Your explorer has told me that last time he was out in the wilderness he saw something sparkle in the grass down in the valley, near the stone deposits. It would have been a long detour for him, so at the time he decided not to check it out. Next time you send your men to look for stone, he\'ll go that way and perhaps find out exactly what was sparkling. Who knows, maybe it can benefit your guild?!',
        'GuiDaiPerTheSupervisor' => 'A guild supervisor has just arrived from Capital Island. He is to spend some time with you and oversee production. He is mostly interested in seeing how our mills work. Well, let\'s make the man happy! Have your mills produce flour!',
        'GuiDaiPerTheTimeForBread' => 'In the early morning, when our settlers and our guild members wake up, they want the air to be filled with the smell of fresh bread! I can\'t blame them; fresh bread does smell amazing! You love it too I\'m sure, but do we have enough bakeries? Perhaps not! Let\'s build at least two more bakeries!',
        'GuiDaiPerTheTraveler' => 'A traveller has arrived at your land and requests lodging for a few days. He promises to put in a good word for you and your guild with the king if you help him. Place the requested materials at the traveller\'s disposal.',
        'GuiDaiPerTheWaterUnderground' => 'One of our geologists has visited all our wells to taste the water… and he is not happy. He believes we should move our wells in the hope of finding newer, fresher water deposits. So… I suppose we should follow his advice. He knows best, and we can\'t allow this matter to shame our guild! Move at least two wells!',
        'GuiDaiPerTheWhiteTrap' => 'There have been a lot of robberies near the farms, so one of the "brighter" captains has asked our guild for help. He wants some sacks of flour! Why? So he can - listen to this - cover the perimeter with flour. When the robbers come back, this will allow him to follow their footsteps to their hideout. Given that our guild does not question the decisions of the local guard, we are to provide them with flour.',
        'GuiDaiPerTicTocSwords' => 'You know, King Damien still thinks that our guild makes the best swords in the kingdom! And every time he sends his men to our island, they want to visit the sword storeroom! Let\'s make sure our iron weaponsmiths can make the swords without any problems!',
        'GuiDaiPerTotalAnihilation' => 'Though we\'re not known as an aggressive settlement, the King wants to be sure we are capable of controlling our enemies. We should show him our guild has the bandit problem under control!',
        'GuiDaiPerVisitAtTheBarrack' => 'Many settlers have asked me what exactly goes on inside our barracks. I find it intriguing they show so much interest in our military affairs. We should hold an open day where any settler can come and see! Train some militia and let the settlers witness how our army is trained!',
        'GuiDaiPerWhenWolvesWageWar' => 'Our hunters have bad news! Apparently there\'s a new breed of wolves in the woods and they attack humans! What if they approach the main settlement? The guild must be ready for them! We need to make sure we have not only melee weapons but ranged support also!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmy' => 'I\'m sorry to bother you but it seems there is a matter to which we must attend quickly. Lord Sardin has somehow managed to persuade the King to sign a law that requires every guild to have its own army. So now we must make sure we have the required forces. Better inform the barracks!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub1' => 'Lord Sardin wants us to prove to him that we have the kind of men ready to go into battle. He didn\'t specify what kind of military he wanted to see, but he insisted the swords be made of steel. Let\'s get to work; I don\'t want him on our back. Prepare the steel swords he needs.',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub2' => 'I always thought the militia was made up of a bunch of grumpy old men, but in fact they\'re really devoted and we need them! Keeping them happy is our first priority, and what else would make them happy if not a good load of quality brew?',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub3' => 'Every army needs cavalry, right? So, if our troops are to become an army, we better prepare those horses! Send word to the stables; we need horses!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub4' => 'The front lines are often made up of well trained soldiers, and we need some! Lord Sardin does not allow undisciplined soldiers in the military, so we need to make sure we train them well! However, training must be done using copper swords. I hope you have some ready!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub5' => 'Lord Sardin believes that "every battle is fought with every weapon". I wasn\'t sure what he meant, to be honest. Eventually, I found out that he wants you to train some longbowmen at your barracks. We need new logbows!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub6' => 'Well, we might have an army soon, but we need to make sure we have the equipment too. We need to send some steel to the blacksmith!',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub7' => 'How convenient! A weapons dealer who only wants to be called "Mr. Metal" and claims to be "the best there is at what he does" wants to teach us a bit about the weapons trade. He wants us to buy some cannons.',
        'GuiDaiPersonalArmySub8' => 'The army is shaping up nicely thanks to the guild\'s efforts, but it\'s time to make things a bit trickier. Let\'s take them to a practical drill in the desert, so they know what we\'re up against.',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGold' => 'This is an awfully awkward request, but the King\'s spoiled nephew will be having his birthday soon and as a gift he has requested... golden rain. We are to supply all the gold and resources to make it happen. I can\'t find the words to describe this nonsense. What... they will shoot the gold into the air?',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub1' => 'The rain of gold will require gold. A lot of gold. We should provide the King\'s men with the necessary amount of gold ore.',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub2' => 'Listen to this! The rain of gold must contain coins! The King\'s nephew wants the coins to roll away after they land! As if the whole thing wasn\'t sufficient already! We can provide them with the gold coins they need, but we need to work fast as the coins have to fall first!',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub3' => 'They want to shoot the gold and coins from cannons, and they\'re afraid the cannons might get damaged. If that happens, the King would like to borrow some cannons from our stocks. Let us talk with the cannonmaster; we need to ready some strong cannons!',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub4' => 'I want to make sure that if the King needs more gold ore, we can provide him the best we have! For that, we not only need to work faster - we also need to ensure the right work conditions for our miners! And by right conditions, I mean food. Some freshly baked bread will do the trick!',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub5' => 'That "little" request from the King really emptied our gold resources. Some of the lords on our island have started to question our decisions, and we don\'t like that, do we? I want to throw a fancy dinner to calm them down! Our chefs should make their famous fish soup, the Golden Fin Bowl! Yes! Get some fresh fish ready!',
        'GuiDaiRainOfGoldSub6' => 'It\'s likely this event will provoke some rowdy behavior from the settlers, but even they know it\'s not a good idea to steal from the King. After the ceremony, we will need to clear the ground. Imagine all that gold… Well, to clean we\'ll need carriages to transport the gold back to the royal treasury, and for the carriages we need horses. We should visit the stables, then.',
        'GuiDaiRainOfgoldSub7' => 'You may think that this is no ordinary birthday party - and I\'d agree with you. But let\'s not forget that this is, after all, a child\'s birthday. Let\'s make an outdoors picnic for him and all of his guests.',
        'GuiDaiRainOfgoldSub8' => 'His magnanimous majesty, the king\'s nephew would like to hold an award ceremony for the settlers that worked the hardest on making his birthday party perfect. We\'ll need a prize for them. Let\'s make golden mugs for the winners!',
        'GuiDaiRainyYear' => 'The weather report we received today was not a promising one. It seems we\'re going to experience a lot of rain, and there\'s even a chance of huge storms. Just to be sure, let\'s prepare for a rainy year.',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub1' => 'Using some stone, we should start reinforcing some of our workyards and other buildings. We don\'t need to make it too official though - let\'s call it \'renovation\'.',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub2' => 'It\'s well known that fish become more active when there\'s a lot of rain. I fear that the rain will stay limited to the northern parts of the island, and the fish might migrate there. Refill the fish deposits, just to make sure we won\'t run out.',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub3' => 'In case we can\'t manage, the only way to get help is by asking Capital Island or our friends. I would stick to the second option - you know how hard it is to get anything from the King. Taking that into consideration, we should visit a friend and help out where we can.',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub4' => 'Hardwood is the only wood that is resistant to water. That\'s why it\'s a good idea to build roofs using hardwood. Some of our residences don\'t have the proper kind of roofs, and in order to replace them we\'ll need hardwood.',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub5' => 'The surrounding wilderness is particularly dangerous during heavy rain, with all the wolves and such, so we must set up an emergency guard around our villages. Prepare some fine steel swords for the guards!',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub6' => 'We need to honour the new rainy year, and the best way to do that is by celebrating. Bring out a Golden Brew Mug - let\'s do this the proper way!',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub7' => 'We should designate a relief party of elite soldiers that know how to handle a crisis, just in case the situation turns bad. Send them on some adventures so they know how to quickly respond to unexpected threats!',
        'GuiDaiRainyYearSub8' => 'I\'m worried that our wheat fields may wither away in the rainy weather. Let\'s make a barn out of mahogany wood and store our grain there until the weather clears a little bit.',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlan' => 'Sir Rogen, one of our oldest generals, is due for retirement. Given that he won so many battles for us, I think we should set up a retirement plan for him.',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub1' => 'We\'re going to need some resources we don\'t own. Luckily, our neighbour has them. Let\'s get friendly and help our allies out a bit!',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub2' => 'Sir Rogen always said that allies are the most important weapon when it comes to a battle! We\'d best keep that in mind! Let us help some of our allies with some goodies!',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub3' => 'Sir Rogen deserves the best! We want to honour him with some great events! One of them would be the fountain dance! Water isn\'t just for fish and drinks, is it? The only problem is, we\'ll need a lot of it - those fountains were never refilled.',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub4' => 'We\'re holding some goodbye events for Sir Rogen. One of them is a march of the last army he commanded. They\'re going to get in line, shoot some cannons, stuff like that. Off to the barracks - let\'s see if we can get that army on its feet!',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub5' => 'In order to honour Sir Rogen, we\'re going to take him on an adventure one last time. As a spectator, that is.',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub6' => 'As Sir Rogen leaves by ship, we\'d like to shoot flaming arrows into the air. It\'s a tradition that was introduced to us a short time ago, a great way to honour our elders... or burn a city to the ground! Either way, we need longbows.',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub7' => 'We would like to throw a surprise party for Sir Rogen. We know he has a lot of friends where our allies live, so why not invite them over to the party as well? Tell them to bring a gift basket for him, too!',
        'GuiDaiRetirementPlanSub8' => 'I think Sir Rogen deserves a fireworks show, and our chief engineer has offered to modify a few of our mortars to make the biggest and flashiest fireworks you\'ll ever see. Let\'s take him some mortars!',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhere' => 'We\'ve received a letter from some settlers that used to have a colony on this island: they want to come back. Apparently they left the island in hope of a better life, but the road they’ve chosen has lead nowhere. I guess we can lend them a small part of the island. Prepare for their arrival.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub1' => 'We need to prepare some proper shelter for these people. I guess some stone houses would do the job. We can build them inside the forest so they won\'t need any additional structure. We need stone.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub2' => 'The colonists will need food and all sorts of agricultural tools to work the land, and weapons to defend their homes. The best we can do is send them some of our swords - our farmers are very fond of their multipurpose abilities.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub3' => 'Some of our people have heard about the new colony and want to go live there for a while. Good idea - it\'ll help them get used to our ways faster.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub4' => 'We need to set up a perimeter around the forest where our new guests will be settling. We don\'t want the pirates or anyone to harm them. Prepare some cavalry!',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub5' => 'There are so many people wanting to help out that we’re going to run out of people to do any actual work. To avoid that, we need to get some more settlers up to the Mayor\'s House.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub6' => 'We considered preparing a nice feast for them, but the forest soil isn\'t great for holding a table steady. We\'ll need a lot strong exotic wood planks for this!',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub7' => 'Just because they weren\'t happy on their previous island doesn\'t mean there isn\'t a perfect place waiting for them, somewhere out there. Send a few horsemen on some adventures, and scout the terrain for other alternatives.',
        'GuiDaiRoadToNowhereSub8' => 'The first refugees have started arriving on our island. We know how hard it is to start a new life, so let\'s make things a bit easier by showing them how to process granite and titanium. This will save them a lot of time.',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSea' => 'King Damien had just returned from a foreign country he was visiting, and was astonished by the hospitality he received there. He wants your guild to prepare resources for the new royal shipyard which will build new tourist ships.',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub1' => 'The King knows that your settlement makes the best tools in the Kingdom. He has sent a special letter with his request. Better make sure those tools live up to their reputation!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub2' => 'Over time, the new royal shipyard will need a lot of wood to build ships. The guild just requires you to provide a certain amount of pinewood!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub3' => 'One of the foreign shipbuilders has told the King\'s men that a good ship must be reinforced with a lot of steel. Given this information, the royal shipyard has requested a shipment of steel to be delivered as soon as possible.',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub4' => 'The ships soon to be built at the royal shipyard will require proper decoration. We must think about first class travellers, the noble kind, if you know what I mean. What else would satisfy their needs if not iron cutlery? Be sure to prepare the iron so we can make the cutlery!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub5' => 'The cook that will serve on the main ship is a specialist and has a world famous recipe that requires quite a large quantity of sausages. We know that your settlement has some really talented butchers, so it falls to you to provide the best sausages you have!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub6' => 'All the ships should have lookout nests, right? We need to make sure we build those small nests using our strongest hardwood planks!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub7' => 'One of the things that would really help us build these ships is if we had some robust cranes to transport materials. And what metal is more robust than titanium? We should make a titanium crane!',
        'GuiDaiSeeingTheSeaSub8' => 'I\'m starting to think that our regular horses won\'t be up to this. I know it\'s not their main purpose, but it may be a good idea to use battle horses this time instead? Can you bring a few?',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoon' => 'You remember that old inventor who lives alone on that abandoned island? Gully Island? Well, somehow he\'s managed to amass a lot of coins. I guess he invented something really useful and sold it. However... he has come to us with the most disturbing request. He wants to build a cannon, a BIG cannon, big enough to shoot down the moon! Yep, you heard me. He must\'ve gone mad form loneliness. Well, as long as he pays us, we\'ll help him build his cannon, right?',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub1' => 'Though the cannon the inventor wants to build seems bigger than we could ever imagine, he still needs some additional parts. Here\'s the list - we need iron ore.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub2' => 'The inventor has told us he needs steel to coat the outer layer of the cannonball. He says that steel blocks the "cosmic radiation". I have no idea what he\'s talking about. That poor crazy old man... Let\'s just get him the steel he needs.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub3' => 'Our engineers working at the cannon forge went pale after talking to the inventor. Apparnetly, he told them how much gunpowder he needs to shoot the cannonball so it will reach the moon. There\'s no way we can provide that much gunpowder, but we\'re going to try our best, right?',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub4' => 'You know what an aiming crest is? Yes, it\'s what you use to aim with. Duh. Anyway, the inventor tells me he wants to have an aiming crest made solely out of gold. His wish is our command! Gold ore for the man.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub5' => 'The inventor says he needs some sacks of saltpetre to create a secondary explosion. Then he went into detail about exactly how it would work, but I have to admit I switched off about halfway through. Let\'s get the man some saltpetre and some more iron and hope he finds somebody else to talk to.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub6' => 'The inventor has told us he has no clue how to use a cannon, and needs us to teach him. Thankfully, we do know a cannoneer who we can hire to look after the training, and we can pay with food! How nice! He told us that he loves fish.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub7' => 'The inventor seems to be having second thoughts about shooting down the moon, so he wants a plan B. Apparently, that plan B is a giant grappling gun. He\'s asked if we can send him some crossbows to dismantle, so he can analyze their design.',
        'GuiDaiShootingDownTheMoonSub8' => 'You might want to sit down. I\'m afraid the inventor has another request - he now wants a place to securely store the moon when he manages to shoot it down. He wants the finest cloth to wrap it in, and perhaps some titanium to secure it.',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidence' => 'Listen to this! King Damien has visited the western islands once again, where he encountered a nation that lives in the trees! Yes! They\'ve actually built their homes at the top of the trees! The King is really exited to have his own little sky town, and we\'re going to help him get one!',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub1' => 'We weren\'t able to find a dense forest on Capital Island, so we\'ve decided to grow one. We\'ll be needing a lot of saplings form the foresters! I\'ve spoken to them and all they ask in return is water. I guess they\'re too lazy to just walk over to the river.',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub2' => 'I still don\'t understand how anyone can live so high up from the ground! Madness! Well if there have to be houses up there, there will also have to be roads. Plank roads, that is. You are required to provide the shipment of hardwood planks, as they are the strongest... well, almost the strongest.',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub3' => 'Though I\'m not sure how many citizens are to move up there of their own will, I\'m sure they\'re going to be hungry. Until they can actually cook their own meals, we should provide them with bread. After all, not everything grows on trees...',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub4' => 'If the workers want to do a good job building that sky town, they will need a lot of quality tools. No problem there - we have a lot of those, right? Please make sure that we have a sufficient quantity of tools for them, will you?',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub5' => 'Living in the sky town doesn\'t mean that you can feel safe all the time. You won\'t encounter a bear, that\'s for sure, but let\'s not forget about winged menaces. The King has asked me to make sure that the town gets some troops to act as guards, and who better to defend a city so high up if not a group of dedicated archers? Alert the bow makers to make us some bows!',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub6' => 'The first storehouse will be inside a small group of clouds, and we need to make sure we add some basic resources to it. They will eventually fill it, I\'m sure. What we need to bring is some meat, right?',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub7' => 'Having to carry our materials up into the trees, so high up in the air, is going to be an exhausting task. We should manufacture some sort of service lift that can hold a lot of weight. That should make our guild mates\' tasks a lot easier!',
        'GuiDaiSkyResidenceSub8' => 'Once everything\'s up there, we\'ll need to transport it across the bridges. A mahogany wheelbarrow should make things a lot easier. Why mahogany? Best weight-sturdiness ratio, of course!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasons' => 'There is a young man here called Mike, and he\'s a very talented composer. He has a wooden guitar, and many folks have heard him playing it, back in the day when he lived in the mountains. Some old women say this young man\'s music is so enchanting, it can change seasons. Imagine getting rid of this cold winter and having spring arrive the next minute? Let\'s build the man a new home and make him feel welcome. Maybe he\'ll sing for us!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub1' => 'A good house has to be built of the finest planks. I\'ve asked Mike to play for our settlers while they’re building him his new home!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub2' => 'He gave me a look at some really interesting instrument designs. I think if we can get enough hardwood, we might be able to make him some of these instruments!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub3' => 'Mike likes to play music but he also needs to eat, like everyone else. How about surprising him with a nice meal? Some sausages will do the trick!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub4' => 'Mike wants to write a song that would represent our armies, so we\'re going to need some marching cavalry to inspire him!',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub5' => 'Mike is looking for inspiration, so he\'s asked us to take him to some wild lands. The commander will take him on an adventure.',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub6' => 'Mike thinks that different emotions would trigger different rhythms in his heart. I think we should send him out on an adventure with one of your generals.',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub7' => 'The composer has had an idea. He\'s suggested that we could use our cannons as percussion in his songs, but first he needs to understand how a cannon works. Can you take him into an open area with some cannoneers?',
        'GuiDaiSongsOfSeasonsSub8' => 'Our local musician has become great friends with Mike, and they want to put on a concert at our tavern! The problem is, his lute broke, so he needs a new one fast. Can we help him?',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMines' => 'The Miner\'s Union has found an abandoned chamber with a huge gate blocking the way deeper into the cave system. They somehow managed to open it and found another, bigger chamber. It seems like an underground jungle of sorts. We need to explore it!',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub1' => 'While we\'re exploring the mine, we\'ll need somebody to take care of the island. How about a quick visit? Go see your friend, take a gift with you, and hope that while we\'re busy you\'ll receive something in return!',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub2' => 'Most of the paths inside the underground jungle are high up on rocks. Taking melee units won\'t be of any help - we need bowmen for this one!',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub3' => 'We\'ve found a circular tunnel around the underground jungle. There are a lot of cracks on the site, if you look through you can see the jungle. I say we place some longbowmen in these tunnels - if any harm comes our way, our people can protect us.',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub4' => 'It\'s true that the Miner\'s Union has managed to open the gates to the underground jungle, but we might encounter some more obstacles as we go deeper. It would probably be best to have some tools to bring along.',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub5' => 'Given that we know there\'s some kind of life deep in the underground jungle, we might even encounter humans. The best way to make new friends is to gift, and the most impressive type of gift is gold. Bring some gold ore along.',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub6' => 'The entrance to underground jungle is partially flooded by a lake. Fishermen use this lake to fish, but we need to clear the way. We\'ve made a deal with the fisherman in the area to fill up another deposit for him.',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub7' => 'Very, very deep within the mine, we reached a dead end. We believe there\'s still something behind the rocks that are in the way, but there\'s no way for us to get through. So, we\'ve decided to blow the debris away with cannons. It\'s safe, I promise!',
        'GuiDaiTheAbandonedMinesSub8' => 'We want to prepare our miners to start excavating in search of minerals. We\'ve got a batch of new recruits here, maybe we can teach them how to mine granite and saltpetre before going down there?',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekers' => 'The King has a special group of young apprentices who would one day like to become part of the royal army. The higher section, that is. Each year the King sends these young apprentices out to live real adventures. This year our guild has been given the honour of taking take care of them, so it would be best if we brought them along to observe how we complete our adventures!',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub1' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! We\'ve heard he likes his food, so we\'d better pack some extra fish for the road.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub2' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! He did bring along a lot of luggage claiming he needs all of it. And he seems to be a little bit lazy, as he has requested that he and his belongings should be carried around in carriages. Sadly, we can\'t say no.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub3' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! As it turns out, he adores drinking tea, and loves boiling loads of it. He even offered some tea to his escort, but our men looked scared and refused. The apprentice asked us to bring along a lot of water. We\'ll do as he wishes.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub4' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! Sadly, the apprentice was attacked by some pirates on his way to our island, and this has made him act all weird and scared. He will only join our adventure if we send along some military to guard him. I think this calls for some new iron swords to place in the hands of the guards - that will calm him.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub5' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! The apprentice seems to be extremely allergic to sunlight, so he must be protected at all times. We are to build him a huge umbrella, and we\'re going to need exotic planks to do so.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub6' => 'Your young apprentice has arrived and is ready to join you in your adventure! He seems to be a vegetarian, and refuses to eat anything but wheat seeds. We\'ve been asked to provide him with a lot of wheat, alright?',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub7' => 'Your young apprentice arrived, and he\'s ready to join you in your adventure! We heard he\'s very brave, so he wants to be on the frontlines with our crossbowmen. Let\'s provide some.',
        'GuiDaiTheAdventureSeekersSub8' => 'Your young apprentice arrived, and he is ready to join you in your adventure! We heard he\'s very kind and friendly, so he wants to learn and practice the art of diplomacy with your allies.',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParade' => 'I swear this world is going crazy! We have just received a letter from the King! A famous musician is about to visit Capital Island and hold a special event in the royal gardens! Apparently, he has one hundred singing chickens! Yes, you heard me correctly. Chickens. That sing. The musician requires an oversized chicken coop to be built for his precious singers... and guess who has been given the honour of providing the resources. Yes... we have.',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub1' => 'The king wants to be sure we\'re up for the task, and needs to know how efficient we are. I think the best idea would be to get some wood! Wood stacks are always a symbol picture of hard work.',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub2' => 'To build a chicken coop big enough to hold that many chickens we\'ll need hardwood planks. Let\'s have our hardwood sawmills do their best! Maybe we could even go help them?',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub3' => 'Building the coop requires not only wood but also steel to reinforce the structure. Imagine what would happen if a coop so big suddenly collapsed. Anyway, let\'s supply Capital Island with steel!',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub4' => 'You can\'t expect a chicken to sing if it\'s hungry, can you now? The musician has told us his chicken won\'t eat anything we have to offer, but I reckon they won\'t be able to resist our best quality wheat! Let’s show the musician that we can feed his chickens! Anyway, be quick about it!',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub5' => 'Do chickens get thirsty when they sing? I don\'t know. Just in case, we should prepare some kegs of our finest water to quench their thirst. Best be quick about it!',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub6' => 'Er, the musician has just requested we send over some of our settlers to take care of the… primadonnas? Do we even have any people who can attend to chickens? I sure hope we do; we don’t want to anger the king. My cousin told me he would do it for some coins. I trust my cousin.',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub7' => 'The musician has requested that we provide some materials so they can build a gorgeous stage made of marble. I\'ve never seen even the wealthiest of singers on a stage made with such a fancy material, let alone chickens! Oh well, we\'d best go along with it...',
        'GuiDaiTheChickenParadeSub8' => 'It seems that the chickens may have stage fright... Apparently, this is a common thing when performing for humans? The musician told us that the chickens would be a lot more comfortable performing before an animal audience, and asked us if we could round some up...',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogs' => 'It\'s here! Finally! The Day of the Frogs! Every four years we celebrate the great travelling frogs. When winter is nigh, they leave the northern ponds and migrate to the southern ponds. The event requires us to assure safe passage for the frogs that will cross our village!',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub1' => 'For the frogs to find the right way, we need to fry some fish and form a trail using fried fish bits. The frogs will eat and follow the trail. Don\'t give me that look - it\'s how our grandfathers did it! Bring me some fish.',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub2' => 'Birds of prey have been spotted near the frog trail - the frogs are an easy target for them on their journey. I urge you to call upon our elite Bowmen to guard the trail. We will have to compensate them though, as they\'re on their well-earned vacation at the moment.',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub3' => 'We need to take out our bronze swords and let the frogs jump over them. That way we can get the blessing of the frogs. Yes, there are some recruits who believe this brings good luck in combat. Prepare some new bronze swords.',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub4' => 'Our friend came by today and helped us prepare the frog trail. You should visit as soon as possible and return the favor!',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub5' => 'Just imagine - our esteemed neighbours seems to have acquired a taste for frogs\' legs. I suggest we send a little gift basket of sausages to satiate any appetite they might have, just so they don\'t get any ideas when seeing our frogs wandering about… Maybe we should sprinkle some units along our borders too, just to be sure.',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub6' => 'Wait a second! Our general says that some military units have left their post so they can see the frog trail! Without official leave! Have an army check this out - it can’t be true!',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub7' => 'This time, we\'d like to make a gift to the travelling frogs. We heard that there are some mushrooms that they particularly like, but, unfortunately, they don\'t grow on this island. Let\'s search for them while on an adventure.',
        'GuiDaiTheDayOfTheFrogsSub8' => 'To commemorate the day of the frogs, we decided to make some sort of monument. Well, actually it\'s more of a plaque by the pond, but it\'s the thought that counts. We\'ll need some granite to place it there.',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRose' => 'The ruler of a neighbouring island, Milady Verena, has heard about our guild and wants to hire us to organize transport of the famous Dragon Rose Seeds. What is a Dragon Rose? Well apparently, when the seed is ready, it blossoms, then burns. Don\'t ask me why, but I find this rather disturbing, although I suppose others might find it rather beautiful. In any case, we are going to help her and the escort!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub1' => 'It will do us a lot of good to help milady! First we must provide the necessary number of horses so all her guards and servants have a comfortable trip. Be sure to prepare the best horses your stable master can provide!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub2' => 'The road will be long and we can\'t have milady starve! She would love some sandwiches. We need to use our best sausages! Make some!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub3' => 'We know that even guards need to have a good time when they\'re off duty. To help milady\'s guards relax, we should provide them with some of our finest brew, right? I\'m sure they would love it!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub4' => 'It is well knows that milady Verena owns the Steel Guards. They are called this because they use steel swords! I\'m sure they would love some brand new steel swords for the trip, so let us talk with our weaponsmiths!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub5' => 'The servants mending the supply wagons have requested we aid them with some spare wheels. You can never be too careful on a long trip like this, can you now? I was thinking it would be a nice deed to gift the escort some good quality wheels.',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub6' => 'Though I am sure the Steel Guard can protect milady, if there is an ambush, their armour might get broken. The Guard\'s blacksmith has asked for some steel so he can fix the armour if necessary. Let\'s give the man some steel.',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub7' => 'Our local inventor has had an idea. He wants to make a comfortable parasol out of... hardwood. I know it sounds ridiculous, but hear me out! What other object offers great protection from the sun - AND from enemy arrows. Let\'s make one for the steel guard!',
        'GuiDaiTheDragonRoseSub8' => 'It\'s not that I don\'t trust the steel guard to get the job done, but you can never take too many precautions with these things. How about sending a few of our elite units to support them on their journey?',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepository' => 'The King has a new friend, a man from Tagalia, a mysterious island to the south. Apparently, the man, who also walks around with a cat on his shoulder, will be moving to Capital Island to build a genuine Tagalian repository. The building will be able to hold a lot of goods. They will call it The Eternal Repository. We are to help them with our share of supplies.',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub1' => 'We need to provide the brew for the repository. They\'ve heard our brew is really good, which is good news! Let\'s send them some!',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub2' => 'The repository has an area that will be filled with food. We have been given the task of delivering the fish. I would alert the fishermen if I were you; we need to deliver the fish quickly!',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub3' => 'The repository has a special area where all kinds of ore will be stored. We have been asked to provide the iron ore, so we should tell the miner\'s union to get to work.',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub4' => 'I thought that maybe we would have to deliver the bread too, but they only need our flour. We have to provide them with several sacks. Our millers will be happy to hear about this!',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub5' => 'I\'ve heard that there will be a lot of shelves inside the repository and they need the strongest wood available to construct them. We have the "honour" of delivering the shipment of hardwood planks. To the sawmills!',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub6' => 'We are not yet sure whether the repository will hold weapons, but I\'ve heard a rumour they might want us to make some steel swords. It would be a good idea to be prepared. Let\'s make some steel swords!',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub7' => 'We need to make some containers that are sturdy enough to transport fragile materials. A set of exotic planks reinforced with titanium should do it. Can you carry them to the workshop?',
        'GuiDaiTheEternalRepositorySub8' => 'Once everything here is done, there\'s a high chance that we may have some problems with thieves. We\'ll need to install some kind of anti-theft system. I had mortars in mind. They make noise and scare the thieves away!',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCentury' => 'The year of the Fat Pork is upon us, and as you know, a huge feast is being held in his honour! We call it: The Feast of the Century! We have to do our part in preparing the feast, so let\'s get to work. We don’t want to disappoint King Damien!',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub1' => 'One of the dishes will be fish. They plan to bring in a cook from the east whose specialty is a meal of raw fish. Who would eat raw fish? He calls it "sushi". Sounds like something you would call your cat! Anyway, what we need to do now is provide the feast with fish.',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub2' => 'The feast organizer has told me that they\'re going to bake a lot of food, and he would be most grateful if he could have some of our fine flour. Let\'s hope the wind continues to blow so our millers can do their best!',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub3' => 'Some of our settlers have decided to take part in the feast, and told one of the cooks our grain is \'gold\'. I guess they mean it\'s really good. We\'ve received a request to provide the feast with our golden grain, so let\'s do it.',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub4' => 'This food artist who will be part of the feast is famous for his boiled eggs, but apparently he is very picky when it comes to water. He has heard that we can provide crystal clear water from our wells, and now he wants some. Let\'s send them some water, then. Weird people...',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub5' => 'We have just received news that a storm has destroyed one of the ships that was delivering the meat for the feast! They have asked if we can help them. Our hunters have reported a lot of game in the surrounding woods, so it shouldn\'t be a problem to provide the required meat, right?',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub6' => 'The feast is going be so big, they\'ll need to close down the Capital\'s harbors. They\'ve started crafting these really long tables for the people and are using some kind of new technique where they piece together the tables, resulting in a lot of space for the food. However, they need our hardwood planks, so let\'s send them some!',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub7' => 'As the old saying goes - it\'s not a "feast" without a BBQ zone! We\'ve finished the preparations, all we need now is to put the coal on the grill, and light up the sausages... Or is it the other way around?',
        'GuiDaiTheFeastOfTheCenturySub8' => 'Our local gourmet chef wants to share his latest invention with us. He says that all you have to do is to cook some toast on a fire made of mahogany. He calls it the best invention since... well, toast.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIsland' => 'A man has landed on our island in a very weird flying basket attached to a huge balloon. He claims to have come from the Floating Island! Have you ever heard anything so absurd? He has asked us to help him repair his flying machine. Let\'s do it.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub1' => 'He needs some stones to use as weights. Apparently, to float higher, he\'ll release a few bags holding the stones, but what if they hit anyone?',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub2' => 'While helping the balloon guy, we noticed the basket landed right on a fish school. The local fisherman is really angry. We should refill his fish school.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub3' => 'The balloon guy has asked us for a partial escort. When his balloon is repaired, he will leave our island and head south. He wants us to escort him for a while by ship. We should take along some longbowmen in case we run into pirates.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub4' => 'While gathering the tools to fix his balloon, our guest would like to take a look around some other islands as well. This is great because we can ask our general to take him along an adventure.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub5' => 'While fixing a thing he calls an \'engine\', something happened and there was a huge explosion. Not big enough to hurt anyone, but it was so loud it scared away most of the wildlife. We need to refill our wildlife in the area!',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub6' => 'The balloon guy is about to finish his repairs, but he needs some strong men to help push the balloon toward the creek. I think we should designate some soldiers from the barracks to help - they\'re the strongest units after all.',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub7' => 'The more we help the traveller fix his machine, the faster we get! The guild is already big enough as it is, but maybe we could ask some of our allies to help? Let\'s take them a gift basket. They can\'t say no to that!',
        'GuiDaiTheFloatingIslandSub8' => 'The traveller\'s asked if we have some gum he could use to patch up his balloon, but the closest thing we have is grout. He\'s also looking to decorate his chronicles with a few nice bookfittings. Can we spare some?',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGenerals' => 'King Damien wants to hold a ceremony in honour of the generals of his armies. As you might imagine, this means our generals must be present too! Let us prepare the generals and their troops for the ceremony!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub1' => 'Your general will be represented by a group of selected bowmen! They will also need some new bows!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub2' => 'Your selected general will represent the proud and swift cavalry! Though usually horses are not allowed to enter the main square, King Damien will make an exception this time, to honour the celebration. Ready your best horses!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub3' => 'Recruits are an important part of an army, as is any other brave men or woman who fights for peace or justice. Your general is to be escorted by recruits, but we need to fix their swords. Provide a load of copper ore so we can fix their swords!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub4' => 'Your general has insisted on being represented by the cannonneers. We can\'t take too many cannons to the ship, so we need to limit his request a little. I hope he\'ll accept that. Bring out the cannons!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub5' => 'The crossbowmen are known to be a grumpy bunch of people, but they do know how to win a battle. This is why your general wanted them to represent him. We need new crossbows, though, so let\'s make some.',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub6' => 'Your general wants to be represented by soldiers. We all know that soldiers require a lot of armour and weaponry, so it didn\'t surprise us when the blacksmith asked for more water, to finish all the requested equipment. We need to supply him with water!',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub7' => 'Your army needs to have a powerful artillery if it wants to be taken seriously. Can you provide the necessary gunpowder for this request?',
        'GuiDaiTheGoodGeneralsSub8' => 'As you know by now, the most powerful armies are equipped with the finest platinum swords. The blacksmith has taken a bet that he can produce platinum swords quicker than anyone else, so let\'s help him win this bet!',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothers' => 'Today we\'ve received two guests from an island called Booth, sent by King Damien himself. They seem to be brothers, and are trying out a new way of building a sort of underground tunnel system called \'sewers\'. I\'ve no idea why is that a good thing. Help them with their first experiment.',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub1' => 'Before they started digging, they asked us about the famous Fish Platter we eat around here. They would love to try some of the fish we have. The smaller brother seems slightly overweight, and looks hungry, so we had better get a decent amount of fish.',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub2' => 'There\'s a feeling these tests might end up being a little messy. We should check our troop count to make sure we have enough units if something happens and we have to deal with it.',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub3' => 'The brothers managed to dig some tunnels, but apparently they also want to clean them. That\'s going to require quite a lot of water…',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub4' => 'While the brothers are doing their digging, we should focus on our troops, especially recruits. How about sending them for a fight or two?',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub5' => 'The brothers will need some strong tools so they can dig properly. I suggest you provide them with some iron, and let them make their own weird tools.',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub6' => 'The brothers\' digging seems to be a little bit too loud. Many animals have been seen fleeing the sector. We should check our deposits and maybe fill them up!',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub7' => 'The brothers said they\'ll need some adhesive to make some "pipes", in order to test how they affect the sea wildlife. I have no idea what these are for, but whatever. Let\'s give them some grout.',
        'GuiDaiTheHammerBrothersSub8' => 'The brothers heard that we had some magic beans with us, and they\'re a bit concerned in case any mutations happen due to water pollution. Let\'s build a mahogany fence and show them how we grow them so they can rest easy.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIsland' => 'You remember the island of Countess Zavora? A scout returned today with the news that the island is surrounded by a thick layer of mist. The scout ventured deeper and it appears the whole island is dead. Then, when he reached the Countess\' manor, he saw her. Problem is, as everyone knows, she\'s been dead for years. It would be wise to investigate.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub1' => 'Some weird things have been happening since the scout came back. There was a huge fire out on the farms, and we lost some wheat. It would be good to help the farmers get their stocks back before we leave.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub2' => 'The scout\'s first stop was one of your friends\' islands! There are reports of unusual lights inside many residences - the people are scared. How about we pay your friend a visit, and try and calm down the "spirits"?',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub3' => 'The weirdest thing - Samuel the Deerstalker told me that last night he arrived at the fields where he usually hunts, and saw hundreds of animals gathering around a person standing in the middle. Unfortunately, he then stepped on a twig, the sound scared all the animals away, and the person was nowhere to be seen. We need to refill the field with wildlife before we leave.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub4' => 'Hey! The merchant told me that last night he had a weird customer, and as the guy was leaving, all the iron swords started dancing out after him. His wife confirms the story\'s true too. Hmm, I think they must have been tired or something. Anyway, let\'s help the merchant out with some iron swords before we leave.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub5' => 'Some settlers have reported a silvery wave of flame burning through the woods. The huge... well I suppose you\'d call it a fire, has scared away most of the wildlife, and the hunters who work around here aren\'t happy. We should refill the wildlife before we leave to check out that island.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub6' => 'Our general claims he found a message carved on the side of an adventuring ship this morning. He insists we tag along before we go investigate the island!',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub7' => 'A little creature, who looks like an imp, came to us while we were visiting and knew exactly what we were after. He\'s offered to share all he knows about the legend of the countess... for a price.',
        'GuiDaiTheHauntedIslandSub8' => 'If we are to explore the haunted island, we\'ll need to assemble a force of the bravest soldiers we can muster. It\'ll be better for them if they have some horses, so train a few mounted units.',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssue' => 'There\'s nothing better than waking up in the morning and having a good old piece of honey bread! Sadly, our supplier from Pollon has stopped his shipments because he has a problem with his bees! We should try and help!',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub1' => 'The honey supplier says he wants to build a stone wall around the field where he keeps the beehives. He\'s asked for some stone.',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub2' => 'I decided to loan the supplier some of our recruits, you know, to guard the area and all that. Check the barracks!',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub3' => 'Did you know that bees prefer meat? No? Me neither. The honey supplier claims meat can be used to lure the bees to a certain spot, where the most flowers are. We need to send him some meat, but be sure to refill our deposits first!',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub4' => 'One of our allies appears to be an expert when it comes to bees, and he has given us some great tips about how to deal with them. I think we should thank our ally for the help!',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub5' => 'If it turns out the origin of the problem is the wildlife living in the surrounding woods, we might need to send over some army units. Please check our troop count!',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub6' => 'We should send out a General and some troops to scout the surrounding islands. Maybe they\'ll be able to find the origin of the problem.',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub7' => 'It seems that the bees in one of our beehives have gone a bit wild! I once heard from my grandpa that one of the best ways to get the bees to calm down again is to use smoke. Unfortunately, all I could find is this gunpowder. Oh well, close enough - let\'s give it a try.',
        'GuiDaiTheHoneyIssueSub8' => 'The Queen is in danger! Some bandits have appeared and want to kidnap her! Quick, bring some arquebuses and let\'s defend her!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlords' => 'We have received news that the King is to be visited by one of his friends, some prince. The prince wants to know which of the King\'s followers has the safest island. Sound like a challenge! Let us prove that we have the safest island in the Kingdom!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub1' => 'To ensure our victory we must be sure our island is safe! Maybe have your scout commander can take care of the problem? Cleaning some land… is always a good idea, right? In any case, he has requested iron so he can equip his people with some nice armour.',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub2' => 'We need to prove to the prince that we own the safest island, but I fear there may still be some bandits lurking around! We need to make sure there are no more bandits in the sector in question. I\'ve assembled a group of soldiers to check ebery bush, look behind every tree. Ahh, and they will need some horses!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub3' => 'You know what makes a place look safe? Weapons. I think that if we install some cannons here and there, the place will feel safer already. Let\'s get some cannons!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub4' => 'The bandits from the forest know we won\'t be able to catch them, no matter what, so I\'ve dediced to make a deal with them. We give them some bread and they will leave our settlers alone… for a while. It\'s the best way, trust me!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub5' => 'I fear we have detected some pirate ships near your island. To make sure we\'re not invaded by bandits, we should prepare ourselves! We don\'t want problems now, while the prince is watching! I think our coast patrol could use some new steel swords… just to scare away any pirates that might decide to land on our island.',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub6' => 'Our scouts have informed us they have run out of the coal they use for campfires while patrolling the island. Let\'s get them some coal!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub7' => 'If we want to show how safe our island is, we\'ll need to prove we have the best of the best when it comes to weaponry. Make enough titanium swords to equip a small squad of soldiers!',
        'GuiDaiTheLandlordsSub8' => 'We may have the edge in the technology stakes, so we should make sure we show it off to the judges. Let\'s give them a live demonstration of how our mortars work when operated by capable besiegers.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueen' => 'One of my scouts has brought me a strange report. Apparently, an abandoned ship has been found, and some of the farmers have reported a group of people passing through the land. Finally, it was discovered that the queen of the Summer Island has come to visit us. Why we were not aware of this visit, I do not know. We should find her at once!',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub1' => 'We\'re not sure where the queen and her escort might be heading, so next time we send a scout out to look for treasure, let\'s ask him to keep his eyes open for clues… I want you to send out some scouts, but we need to give them horses first!',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub2' => 'The queen sure knows how to hide her tracks. Lord Saradin thinks they may be spies… but I don\'t think so. She can\'t just have become invisible… or can she? We need to send some scouts! They have requested some bread for the mission, let\'s make them some.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub3' => 'We could track down the queen by sending out some of our scouts, but they\'ll need lookout towers. The leader of the scouts has asked me to tell you that he can set the towers up, but they need hardwood planks for that.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub4' => 'Even if we don\'t know where the queen is right now, we better make sure she is safe. I have organized a group of guards to patrol the island. They lack quality weapons, so I want to ask you to give them some of our finest steel swords.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub5' => 'I think it would be a good idea to organize a search party to look for the lost queen. We\'ll need some cavalry, as they travel fast on horseback. I\'ve already talked with the stablemaster - he needs copper ore to coat the horseshoes. Send the man some copper ore, will you?',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub6' => 'We need all the eyes we can get to look for the queen. I\'ve already convinced our hunters to help out! However, they\'ve said they\'ll be needing longbows. Fair enough, I mean weapons are kind of important out there, in the wilderness.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub7' => 'If the queen is around here, but nobody\'s seen her for a while, she may be in trouble. I\'d like to think that\'s not the case, but it\'s better if we make a few extra crossbows, just to be on the safe side.',
        'GuiDaiTheLostQueenSub8' => 'The scouts aren\'t being very effective, so I\'d like to create a separate party of your knights to become an official Search Task Force. Perhaps if the queen notices their shiny armour, she may come to the knights herself.',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmaker' => 'Good news! The famous mapmaker, Coron Franz is visiting us in order to map our island and the surroundings! Great! Let\'s do all we can to help him, shall we?',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub1' => 'We must make sure no harm is done to Coron as he travels across our island! Training some new military units would be a good idea! We need strong men with strong weapons, so what we must do now is make some shiny iron swords!',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub2' => 'Though Coron was not very eager to ride a horse, we encouraged him to. It will make the mapping of the island go much faster, and you get a clearer view from horseback. Let\'s admit it, Coron is not a very tall man. Just don’t tell him I said that!',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub3' => 'Coron will have a long journey, so we had better pack him some good food from our kitchens! We need some sausages! The best meal out there!',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub4' => 'Coron will need to draw his maps and he can\'t just do it on the ground, can he now? He has told us he will need map tables. At every stop. Given that we won\'t be carrying a table from place to place each time, we had better assemble new ones at each stop. Make sure we have the necessary hardwood planks and tools!',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub5' => 'Coron seems to be a clean man. And when I say that, I mean it. He actually washes his clothes every time he gets the chance, and has asked us to make sure we have enough clean water available. Prepare seom water for the trip!',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub6' => 'Working with paper, there is always a chance the wind will become a cartographer\'s second worst enemy, fire being the first. Anyway, we\'re going to get some steel weights to hold down the maps while Coron works. Provide the necessary steel.',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub7' => 'Coron wants to have printed versions of his maps at some point, including detailed explanations of each area. He needs us to provide the means for him to write these annotations.',
        'GuiDaiTheMapmakerSub8' => 'Coron mentioned that when his work is done, he\'d like to sell his maps in a "collector\'s edition". I guess there are collectors for everything! He\'s requested the finest paper, and an example of a really nice-looking book.',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridge' => 'Yet again our most beloved King Damien has requested our aid! Queen Anita believes that Capital Island should have all its bridges made of pure marble, so the King wants to surprise her when she get back from visiting another Kingdom. Let\'s prepare our best settlers for this task!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub1' => 'Marble is not an easy material to chisel or even to cut. We will need new, strong tools! Given that your toolmakers are the best of the best, I would like to you to provide the workers with new, marble-shattering tools!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub2' => 'So… all the bridges on Capital Island will be made of pure marble eh? Well then… I guess they will need a lot of marble, won\'t they? I hope you have got your settlers ready! We need marble!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub3' => 'In order to provide the best marble, we need to ensure we have the best marble masons! We spoke with one of the masons, and he told us he wants to experiment with a new kind of wooden structure that would hasten the production of marble. He needs some pinewood planks for that!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub4' => 'Given that this is a request from the King himself, we can\'t risk running out of marble. I mean, imagine the shame! No no, don\'t imagine it, it\'s terrible! But let\'s focus! I need you to make sure we send a stock of marble to Capital Island! Will you look after that please?',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub5' => 'The King wants our very own settlers to work on the bridges, so let\'s send them to Capital Island! As far as I know, most of the settlers are really eager to work there! All we need is todo is ensure they have enough food for the voyage! They want sausages!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub6' => 'Our men will leave for Capital Island to help with the bridge building! We are all really excited, but what if they go hungry? Well, we\'ll just have to make sure they have enough food for the trip, right? Let\'s pack them some bread!',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub7' => 'It\'s no surprise that we\'ll need a huge amount of marble to make this bridge, but our architect believes that the foundations of the bridge should be made of a more robust material. She suggests granite for that.',
        'GuiDaiTheMarbleBridgeSub8' => 'Marble is beautiful, but it\'s also a very heavy material for a bridge. We need to make sure that the links are not going to give in, so they have to be made from the toughest of metals: titanium. Please produce some!',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPonds' => 'Lady Amidale from the neighbouring Kingdom wishes to hire your guild in order to build her a replica of the world famous Mirror Ponds. This work definitely requires a lot of preparation, but your guild can be sure that she will be most grateful when admiring her face in the ponds.',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub1' => 'In order to prepare for digging, you must first produce the required amount of tools. You can\'t expect your settlers to use their hands, can you now?',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub2' => 'Those ponds will need water to become actual ponds, and water does not travel by itself. You\'ll need to produce enough wood to make buckets to transport the water. We need to make sure you can produce the wood!',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub3' => 'Well, we\'re going to need a lot of manpower if we want to provide all those resources for lady Amidale\'s ponds. I\'ve heard your settlement has some really strong men in it, but they\'re kind of picky when it comes to carrying goods around. Maybe if we give them some planks so they can make their own carts to carry the goods around, hmm?',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub4' => 'There are a lot of settlers working on this operation, and even though they are devoted, they are also hungry. We would like to ask you to be the one to provide the rations. We\'ve heard your bakers make the best bread around these parts, and we\'ll be needing a lot.',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub5' => 'Water may give a perfect reflection if still, but we\'ve just found out that the bottom of the ponds need to be covered with polished marble. As your island has many marble deposits, we would like you to provide the amount of marble needed.',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub6' => 'Apparently you can\'t use any old kind of water to fill the ponds. We know that the underground rivers that run through your lands are the clearest around, so we require you to provide us with the water. These ponds need to be crystal clear, you know, like a mirror.',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub7' => 'The legend says that anyone who looks into the mirror ponds will see a beautiful reflection. I\'d like to put that to the test. Send our ugliest men there to see if it\'s true. How about the cannoneers?',
        'GuiDaiTheMirrorPondsSub8' => 'In order to make this pond truly special, I thought it would be nice if we made some platinum decorations for it. Lady Amidale will love it, for sure!',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectors' => 'A group of people arrived on a magnificent ship today. They claim to be ore collectors from a land far away. They are fascinated with the ore we have here and would love to buy some. What a good opportunity to make a little profit! Let\'s get to work, shall we?',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub1' => 'We want to make sure the newcomers feel comfortable while we fill their ships with our ore, so I\'ve invited them to a feast! We have everything we need except sausages. We\'ll be needing more of those, I\'m afraid.',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub2' => 'They seem to love the copper ore more than any of the other types we have, so make sure you can supply the quantity they require!',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub3' => 'One of the men took a look at one of the iron bars, licked it, and smiled. I have no idea what to think of that. I guess he likes the… taste of iron? Anyway, you need to provide them with iron ore, and make sure it\'s tasty. Ha ha!',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub4' => 'Listen to this! Gold ore is practically the most precious type we have, and you know what they said when we gave them some? "We don\'t like it!" They don\'t like gold! Hah! They\'re going to take some of it regardless, so best make sure we have enough.',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub5' => 'We showed them a titanium ore sample, and some of them got sick! Can you imagine that? What\'s wrong with them? Anyway, their supposed leader said he would take only a small load of titanium ore, so let\'s do this.',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub6' => 'We asked them if they\'re hungry, but they kept looking at the ore. I swear one of them started to chew on a piece of copper. We have to feed them! Be sure to bring some bread as soon as possible!',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub7' => 'Despite being a bunch of "expert" collectors, they\'ve never seen any platinum ore. Now they\'ve seen some of ours, they\'ve asked if we can provide them with some of it so they can investigate where it comes from.',
        'GuiDaiTheOreCollectorsSub8' => 'The ore collectors have been from island to island, but they haven\'t seen how titanium is collected yet. Can you perhaps take them to one of our mines, and see that they learn the trade?',
        'GuiDaiThePainter' => 'A painter has arrived from a far away island. He claims to be the best wall painter in the kingdom, but I\'ve never heard of him. However, we might be able to use him to our advantage. He can paint walls, you see? We could have him decorate some of the interiors of our residences. Imagine how grateful our settlers will be! Make sure you provide the painter with everything he needs!',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub1' => 'It seems that this wall painting business requires a lot of weird things. For example, one of the painter\'s projects requires coins and marble. Can you believe that? He\'s going to use coins to decorate the walls! Heavens… Let\'s get him some coins then.',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub2' => 'The painter says that some of the houses need bigger walls so he can work his magic. We won\'t start building any new walls ourselves, but we\'ve promised him some stones. Maybe he can… build something himself?',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub3' => 'One of the noble lords from our island has requested the painter paint his walls using gold. Yes, you heard me. I mean the whole island knows how rich he is, so why does he need gold on his walls? Anyway, we promised we\'d do everything we could, so make sure you bring some gold ore for the painter!',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub4' => 'The painter has asked us to loan him some of our men to help him carry around his cans of paint, and he has quite a few... We\'d better make sure we have enough settlers ready to help him any time he wishes to move his work station to another house. They also need to be equipped with our best tools! Let\'s prepare the tools!',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub5' => 'The painter tells me he uses a special kind of brush made from copper, and even makes paint from copper. Don\'t ask me how he does it. All you need to know is that he wants us to provide him with some copper ore, and we\'re going to do just that.',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub6' => 'The painter claims that he can paint on marble. I\'ll believe it when I see it. One of the lords from our island owns a house completely built from marble, but the painting still requires some modifications. He\'s asked us to provide him with some good quality marble that he can use in case there are any... unfortunate accidents.',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub7' => 'The painter claims he\'s had an epiphany, and needs someone to write his memoirs. This could go on for a while... Do we have enough nibs?',
        'GuiDaiThePainterSub8' => 'The painter has heard some of our soldiers talking about their adventures in the desert, and he\'s asked if he can go along too. Could you take him on our next one? I just hope he doesn\'t get lost...',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShip' => 'Great news! King Damien is ordering a new royal ship and has invited us to participate in the project! I can\'t imagine a greater honour right now! We need to do our best!',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub1' => 'Delivering all the required resources might turn out to be a tad too hard, and we may end up requesting help from our allies. I\'m not sure how things will go yet, but it\'s probably best to strengthen our relations in any case. You\'d better get on it.',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub2' => 'A royal ship should contain all the goods a king and his guests may require. The King has asked us personally to fill the ship\'s hold with our quality brew!',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub3' => 'Some of our recruits want to become sailors on the royal ship! They will be representing our guild, so I guess we should give them some proper training before we send them over to Capital Island.',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub4' => 'One of our ships ran into a storm but was saved by one of our allies. We should thank them immediately! The ship is already on its way to Capital Island, and I\'m glad to report the cargo is intact!',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub5' => 'I\'ve made a small miscalculation here! It seems we\'ve delivered a little too much meat to Capital Island, and now we\'re running low ourselves. Just to avoid any problems, we should refill some meat deposits!',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub6' => 'The ships even set sail at night, and we can\'t risk losing them! I\'ve decided to place some longbowmen aboard to signal the ships using flaming arrows so they don\'t get lost. Train some longbowmen.',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub7' => 'Hardwood planks are fine. Exotic planks are better. But nothing beats mahogany planks for building a ship. Let\'s provide some for our engineers!',
        'GuiDaiTheRoyalShipSub8' => 'Grout is an excellent adhesive, as you know. What you probably didn\'t know is that once it dries out, it\'s completely waterproof! The king\'s engineers are scratching their heads about this. Can you obtain some grout so we can show them?',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShores' => 'The Merchants\' Guild needs our urgent help. Their island is filled with repositories, but there was a huge hurricane some weeks ago and it destroyed most of the buildings. They want to rebuild them using a special blueprint obtained through a merchant from a far away land. Let us help them as much as we can. They are usually really grateful!',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub1' => 'Before we start sending the traders our resources, it would be wise to make sure we have enough space to store them! We need new rooms! It would be a good idea prepare the stones!',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub2' => 'Apparently, one of the traders knows a way of using flour to fortify the walls. I know it sounds absurd… but as long as they pay, I don\'t really care what they do with it. We have to provide them with the flour.',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub3' => 'We could really do with some strong planks to reinforce the storm damaged buildings. I think we need some strong hardwood planks!',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub4' => 'They have asked us if they can store their wares inside our storehouses until their storage buildings are repaired, and that\'s fine. The only problem is that the wares are really heavy, so we need to build some steel racks. And for those, we need steel.',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub5' => 'The traders have told us the wood they used to build the old storehouses was of very poor quality. Thanks to our foresters, our trees are really strong. Let\'s send the traders some of our finest hardwood! I\'m sure they\'ll be amazed!',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub6' => 'The traders will receive a lot of resources that will help them reinforce or repair their repositories. They are missing just one resource - some hardwood planks. Given that your sawmills are in top shape, you are to provide the hardwood planks for the traders!',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub7' => 'If we are to prevent another hurricane from tearing down the buildings here, we need to reinforce them with really strong materials. This sounds like a job for granite. Let\'s get some.',
        'GuiDaiTheStormyShoresSub8' => 'The reason why grout is so valuable is because it\'s so very good at fixing materials together. It is extremely valuable, but in this time of emergency, I say we should give some of our own to those affected by the hurricane.',
        'GuiDaiTheVault' => 'The King has sent us a letter. Again. He says Warden Tatral is to build one of the biggest prisons ever built. The King has given Warden Tatral an island where he is to build the prison he intends to call "The Vault". Apparently, this prison will only hold really dangerous people. We\'ve been asked to play a part in the planning and building of The Vault.',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub1' => 'Warden Tatral wants to build a very interesting prison. One of the levels will be made mostly from wood. Don\'t ask me why. We need to prepare a shipment of pinewood planks!',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub2' => 'There\'s going to be a patrol drill around the prison island, and we’ve been asked to provide some recruits for it. I think the guys will be happy to get out the barracks and just patrol.',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub3' => 'Warden Tatral doesn\'t like walking. He prefers to be on horseback, and demands his guard should be mounted as well. The King has told him our horses are the best, so we\'re to bring over some horses!',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub4' => 'Warden Tatrak is considering hiring some of our units, but first he wants to see them in real combat. The general agreed to take Warden Tatral along. Let\'s see a battle with recruits!',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub5' => 'Warden Tatral needs to learn about military tactics before he can make plans for his prison guards. The general has offered to take the Warden on an adventure.',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub6' => 'Warden Tatral tells us his island has no wildlife, and has asked us if he can take one or two hundred animals. Yes, well, of course he can, but we\'ll need to refill as soon as possible, or our hunters will have problems hunting.',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub7' => 'In order to keep the prisoners fed, but minimize their chance of hijacking one of the king\'s ships to escape, the warden suggests planting some magic beans, so we have virtually endless food to feed the prisoners with.',
        'GuiDaiTheVaultSub8' => 'The warden has seen our ranged elite units in action, and suggested they be just what we need to defend the prison. Let\'s send some marksmen to patrol the prison for a while. They\'ll be back soon.',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWilds' => 'One of our explorers has found a yet unexplored valley! He claims to have seen lions there, and some ancient looking ruins too! This all sounds too exciting! The King wants us to find some time and prepare an expedition!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub1' => 'If there are lions we had better make some quality lure to capture some! Just imagine: our own lion! Please prepare some sausages - I bet they love sausages!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub2' => 'We\'re not aware of the quality of terrain inside the valley, so we should send some horsemen too. It\'s never bad to have some horses around. Train some cavalry!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub3' => 'We have no idea what awaits us inside the valley, so we should make sure our explorers and guards are prepared. Get some nice bronze swords ready for them!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub4' => 'The expedition to the valley needs to be well equipped. We can\'t expect our explorers and guards to carry around those huge bags, so we should loan them some horses!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub5' => 'Our explorers will eventually get hungry, and I believe one of them is a really good cook. Pack them some meat - let them have a feast or two!',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub6' => 'The head of the exploration, our Master Explorer, has asked us for a Golden Brew Mug. Every time he leaves on a big exploration mission, he drinks his brew from a Golden Mug. I think we have one somewhere, right?',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub7' => 'We can cover more ground if we split up. Let\'s call some of our friends and see if they can help us map out the area.',
        'GuiDaiTheVeiledWildsSub8' => 'I noticed some mountains in the distance. We should probably check to see if they might be a source of the rare materials we need, but our geologist doesn\'t know exactly what he\'s looking for. Show him some platinum ore!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiver' => 'One of the neighbouring islands has a serious problem with a group of bandits who are hiding in their forest. These bandits have even gone so far as to burn down all bridges that could provide safe passage over the large river dividing the island, and are thus occupying one half of the island. The lord of the island wants to get rid of the bandits, and is ready to use his most talented archers to counter them with a rain of arrows! Let us be sure we provide the necessary resources.',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub1' => 'It\'s obvious our friends will require a lot of bows to win that battle at the river. Though we\'ve already ordered the arrows, we might need to make more. Our stock of bows might not be sufficient to satisfy demand! Make some bows for them!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub2' => 'As I said, to win such a combat, they will need to use the best longbows we can offer. Have your bowmakers produce the required amount of longbows!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub3' => 'Many of their archers are trained to use longbows, and yes their supplies are limited. No worries though - we\'re here to help! Provide our friends with longbows!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub4' => 'Our friends are about to be supplied with the weapons they need, but it seems we need more wood to make the bows. Make sure you have a decent supply of wood!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub5' => 'Our friends have told us that one of their squads intends to attack from the water! They\'re going to storm the front lines on the other side of the beach, and for that they\'ll need strong swords, so let\'s send them some of our iron swords!',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub6' => 'One of the alchemists has told us about a small globe that can explode and do serious damage. They want to use it in battle, and the globes seem to be filled with gunpowder, so we\'ve asked how we can help and they have told us they would welcome some gunpowder. Hard to find, for sure, but essential I guess.',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub7' => 'The general has had the idea of setting up some watchtowers, so the archers will have a clear view of their surroundings, as well as some protection from the bandits. He suggested said protection be made of granite, so let\'s provide him with some.',
        'GuiDaiTheWarAboveTheRiverSub8' => 'Archers are great, but you know what can\'t be beaten in terms of ranged weapons? Arquebuses. I\'m sure that none of their troops has ever seen one, so let\'s make a few and show them what it\'s all about.',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHome' => 'Fantastic news! Do you remember Sir Arminus, the long lost general? Apparently he has been found on a small island and would like to come home! We need to prepare a proper welcome!',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub1' => 'One thing is sure: Sir Arminus loves his Saturday fish meal! Yes, it was some kind of a tradition at his house. Send his family some fish so they can prepare the meal!',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub2' => 'His family\'s old home has been abandoned ever since he left. It\'s a cold and sad place these days. Let\'s heat the old place up, light a fire in the chimney, prepare a nice hot bath, that kind of stuff. You\'ll need to provide the coal.',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub3' => 'Sir Arminus will arrive on the other side of the island, so we had better send over some horses. He loved horse riding - imagine how excited he will be.',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub4' => 'Oh! While preparing for the welcome party, the family has found a sinkhole in the backyard! We should fix it as soon as possible using hardwood planks!',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub5' => 'Sir Arminus was in charge of a brave army made of soldiers back in his golden days. Let\'s honour him for that! Prepare soldiers at the barracks!',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub6' => 'The moment Sir Arminus arrives at the Mayor\'s Office, he will be awarded a medal! We want him to get the most out of the ceremony, and enjoy the whole experience, so prepare a Golden Brew Mug!',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub7' => 'Sir Arminus will undoubtedly have a lot of interesting stories to tell about his experience. It\'s important that we document his adventures, so I\'ve hired a professional writer to jot his tales down. Only problem is, I haven\'t paid him yet. Can you do that?',
        'GuiDaiTheWayHomeSub8' => 'The military changed a lot while Sir Arminus was away. We should show him our new technology. Let\'s forge some platinum swords so he can get a good feel for our new "toys"!',
        'GuiDaiTheWizards' => 'A very particular group of five people arrived at the local inn last night. They call themselves "The Wizards" and they\'re looking for somebody on our island. They\'ve asked for our assistance. Want to hear what\'s weirder? They didn\'t come by ship, they just appeared. Let\'s help them quickly, so they will leave as soon as possible.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub1' => 'One of them came to me and asked for some fish. He looked really hairy and was somewhat scared of my every move. I was scared of him too to be honest. I think we should just give him some fish and be done with it.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub2' => 'One of them walks and talks funny. His skin is really silvery, unnatural if you ask me! Anyway, he was interested in seeing our military force. I walked him around the barracks, but he wants to see the actual training process. Invite him to see how we train our recruits.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub3' => 'The thin guy wants bread. He reminded me of a scarecrow - thin as a rake. I told him to come back later. Prepare some bread for him please.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub4' => 'There is a girl with them, but she looks really sad. She kept telling me she wants to go home, and how she misses her friends. Then she asked me if I have any friends. I told her that I do - plenty. She wants me to take her to one of my friends. Want to join us? Please?',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub5' => 'The tallest of them seems to be their leader. He has glasses and looks like he won\'t take no for an answer. He wants to borrow some of our cavalry to help him move around the island.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub6' => 'They\'ve started to look for whatever they came for. I think we should keep on good terms with them, so let\'s honour them with our Gold Brew Mug.',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub7' => 'The man with the long beard has asked if we could show him our books, to see if he can learn anything from our culture. He seems to have seen a lot of world and met some interesting people. Take him to the bookbinder!',
        'GuiDaiTheWizardsSub8' => 'The wizards have gathered in the tavern, and have started talking about using new materials to create new spells and concoctions. Maybe we can help them out by offering them some of our rarest materials?',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzel' => 'A very rich and famous cook wants to surprise the King for his birthday by baking the world\'s biggest pretzel. We all know that King Damien loves pretzels, don\'t we? The cook has asked our guild to help him, and we\'re most eager to do so.',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub1' => 'The cook has requested we provide him with our clearest water. I guess we\'re going to be lowering a lot of buckets into those crystal clear wells of ours, right?',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub2' => 'We all know that you can\'t make a good pretzel without the right flour. We promised the cook that we were going to provide the best flour our mills can yield, but we need to do it fast; baking has to start soon, so let\'s get to it!',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub3' => 'Demand for flour is high right now, thanks to the cook and his idea, so we better make sure we have our mills running. Build at least two mills so we\'ll be prepared if the demand for flour increases.',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub4' => 'Although we have a lot of good quality wheat, the cook wants to use *new* wheat. I wasn\'t sure what he meant by that, but he was kind enough to explain. So, we need to get him the best wheat we have. I told him that all of our wheat is good quality, but who am I to argue with the master cook?',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub5' => 'The cook wants to apply a new kind of salted glaze to the pretzel, so he\'ll be needing a lot of salt. One of our neighbours has a salt mine and is willing provide the salt, but it needs to be mined. We can send our man, but he\'ll need the necessary tools. Let\'s make some good quality tools, shall we?',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestPretzelSub6' => 'We\'ve received a report that demand for water is very high at the moment. It must be because we\'ve allocated most of the water to the cook. The best move now would be to build some more wells, but we\'ll need stone for that.',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestpretzelSub7' => 'The pretzel is obviously going to be eaten, but while we\'re supplying the coal for the massive oven, it would be a good idea to start telling our friends about it so they can try a bit. What better way to spread the word than by giving them a gift basket?',
        'GuiDaiTheWorldsBiggestpretzelSub8' => 'We have a problem. The world\'s biggest pretzel has attracted the attention of some of the world\'s biggest pigeons that want to eat it! But don\'t worry, I have a cunning plan! Spread as much bread as you can, as far away from it as possible, and the pigeons will go there instead!',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravan' => 'Far to the south are the desert islands. Every now and then, a caravan comes visiting our island, opens the bazaar, and trades with our settlers. It\'s called "The Yellow Caravan" because… well, because it\'s yellow. We need to ensure that all the trading goes peacefully, and our guests feel welcomed.',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub1' => 'Our friend is very sad the Caravan couldn\'t visit, so why don\'t we visit them instead? And let\'s take some gifts!',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub2' => 'Our travelling friends have asked if they can restock provisions for their next big journey. They know of our baker\'s excellent reputation and would like to buy some bread. Also, they plan on venturing into some dangerous regions, and ask if we have any spare military they can hire.',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub3' => 'The leader of the Caravan has told me their archers couldn\'t make it this year, and has asked whether we can lend him some of our longbowmen. Let\'s train some at the barracks!',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub4' => 'The Caravan leader would appreciate some decent conversation, and wants to meet some of your friends! Why not visit and bring along the leader?',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub5' => 'The Caravan contains a lot of birds, and they seem to be running out of seeds to feed them. I\'ve offered the leader some of our wheat seeds, but he would rather feed them our bread. Alright - bread it is.',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub6' => 'The Caravan leader has asked us if there\'s any way to get cannons at the market. We told him that it is indeed possible, but for some reason he doesn\'t want to go there. Let\'s go and buy him some cannons.',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub7' => 'The merchants from the yellow caravan want to perform a market study of the effect of including crossbows amongst their wares. To do that, they\'ve asked if they could borrow a few of ours for a bit. Can we spare some?',
        'GuiDaiTheYellowCaravanSub8' => 'The merchants want to make the ultimate luxurious item - the platinum brew mug. In order to do that, they want to get a couple of golden brew mugs, fuse them together, and then melt some platinum to coat both of them up. I\'m curious to see how this turns out! Can we help?',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSun' => 'We\'ve just heard from your cousin, Theodor. He\'s moved to a desert island and formed a community. I\'ve no idea how he managed it. He has written to say he\'s in trouble though - surprise surprise - and needs your help. Again. His little settlement is in the middle of the desert and the sun is their biggest enemy. He needs help to save his community.',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub1' => 'We\'re going to need help transporting the goods to Theodor\'s island, so it would be a good idea to pay a visit to our friends and take a gift!',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub2' => 'We need to take some recruits with us. They will serve well as basic defence - I mean who\'s going to attack a deserted island with a small, poor town in the middle?',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub3' => 'Theodor loves sausages, and so does the whole community, apparently. We have to bring him some - remember the last time we forgot? Ugh.',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub4' => 'Theodor\'s first defence general has asked us to bring along some fine longbows so he can set up a guard on the outer walls. Sure, why not.',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub5' => 'We\'ve heard the town has some broken walls. I know, Theodor is family and all that, but are you sure you want to fix those walls using exotic wood planks? Really? Alright…',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub6' => 'Theodor has asked us to take his field general to experience an adventure. For training.',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub7' => 'Theodor\'s soldiers are only equipped with regular iron swords, which may not be the best idea if you want to appear strong. Let\'s show him how we produce titanium swords.',
        'GuiDaiUnderTheSunSub8' => 'When we asked Theodor about his diplomatic plans, he just shrugged. Inconceivable! We should definitely explore this route. Let\'s prepare a peace offering and take it to their representative.',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrison' => 'Count Hackett from Capital island wants to build a prison on a small, star-shaped tropical island. It\'s not a bad idea, but to use a whole island for that… I don\'t think it\'s efficient. Anyway, we need to help them because we\'re going to encounter more bad guys, and it\'s better for the Count to take care of them!',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub1' => 'Prisons have strong walls, so how about sending them some good quality stone?',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub2' => 'The Count wants a repository of food sealed off from the prisoners, and we\'ve been asked to provide the bread!',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub3' => 'The builders hired to build the outposts have asked us for some fish. I say, let\'s send them some!',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub4' => 'There is some heavy cargo that needs to be moved up and then down the ships. I think we we\'ll need some horses for that!',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub5' => 'Since there are wild animals roaming the area, the guards will need weapons to save the prisoners from animal attacks. Deliver the guards some crossbows.',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub6' => 'Each watchtower will need to have at least one cannon on top to defend against wild animals. Some of them will be installed in the mountains. Better safe than sorry!',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub7' => 'If we ever had to deal with an escaped prisoner, we\'d need someone who could put a stop to him in the blink of an eye. In this regard, an archer won\'t cut it. We\'ll need to deploy a few crossbowmen to watch the perimeter.',
        'GuiDaiUniquePrisonSub8' => 'We should also prepare for the possibility of any of the prisoners\' allies trying to stage a breakout. We need to make sure that we have the appropriate long-range defences to deal with enemy ships. Prepare some mortars.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContract' => 'There\'s a man in the lobby. He said his name is Will Fixit. That\'s a rather weird name if you ask me. He\'s a contractor, and for a small fee he can improve a number of things around our village, some of which I never even thought needed changing. His reasoning is quite convincing, so I suggest we give him a shot!',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub1' => 'Will Fixit has told me the most important thing is to have good relations with thy neighbour. We do, I told him, but he insisted I take him along for a visit. Come with us.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub2' => 'Will Fixit believes our village defence isn\'t faulty, but he did have one comment. Although we have plenty of recruits walking around, he didn\'t see any bowmen on the top of any houses or towers. And he\'s right - there aren\'t. Let\'s train some bowmen and get them in place.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub3' => 'Will Fixit says we need a statue in the middle of the village that represents somebody powerful. Can\'t think of anyone yet, but let\'s provide the marble block for it.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub4' => 'The fish we\'ve been using to cook our meals, like the Fish Platters, aren\'t the proper breed. I didn\'t even know there were several different breed around here. Will Fixit has done something to the fish school, and now he wants us to get some fish.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub5' => 'Will Fixit has observed our villagers\' diet and tells us he\'s a little concerned with our meat consumption. He suggests we eat more Fish. Also he\'s kind of worried about the way we treat our horses.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub6' => 'Will Fixit wants to tag along on an adventure so he can evaluate our military forces. Our general has some negative feelings about this, but he\'s finally given in.',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub7' => 'Will says that a renowned artisan once taught him how to craft some nice ornaments from granite and exotic wood. He\'d like to make one for us as a memento of his visit. What a nice guy he is!',
        'GuiDaiVillageContractSub8' => 'Will is a big detractor of weapons. But even he admits that arquebuses are a wonder of engineering. He thinks that by modifying some, he may be able to make them useful for some non-war related purposes too.',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelers' => 'We\'ve just received a letter from the King! He is worried! Somebody has told him that our kingdom is not being friendly enough with the travellers who cross our realms, and now he wants to make sure we are! So let\'s make sure we show those travellers how welcoming we are! Let\'s give them a taste of our hospitality, right?',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub1' => 'Most of our travellers are hunters, so let\'s prepare some good quality bows for them. They might even use them to take care of our critter problem! How perfect would that be! Have your bow makers prove their worth!',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub2' => 'Travellers often arrive on horseback, but some arrive by sea! Let\'s make sure we have some horses ready for when they arrive, shall we?',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub3' => 'Every traveller enjoys a good cup of fresh water, especially if it comes from our underground crystal lakes! Let\'s make sure we have fresh water ready for them!',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub4' => 'Travellers do tend to make campfires and spend a lot of time around them. There are many things one can do near a campfire, but eating is one of the most delicious! Let\'s make sure we have some bread in our storehouses!',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub5' => 'We do know that travellers are not usually rich. I mean why would you travel by yourself if you were rich, right? Let\'s prepare a game of bones for them, with gold as a reward! I\'m sure we can spare some gold ore pieces to make them happy!',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub6' => 'We have heard that travellers are often looking for trouble, and we want to avoid that. I\'d like you to make new iron swords for your troops! We need to keep those troublemakers at bay!',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub7' => 'You know what we should do? We should throw a party for the travellers that come in. Some music, a few brews and our finest meat sausages. I can even do stand-up comedy if you want? No? Oh, ok...',
        'GuiDaiWelcomeTheTravelersSub8' => 'When I was young, my momma took me to the town fair, and there was this nice booth where people could shoot some targets and get fluffy prizes. How about we modify some arquebuses and re-create the stall?',
        'GuiDaiWhitePets' => 'Do you know Lord Addam? Yes, Addam, with two d\'s. He was sailing past our island when a small storm hit his ship, the Pink Karotten. Eventually he was able to recover his crew, but he lost his most precious belongings: his white pets - a cat, a parrot, and monkey. He\'s asked us to help him find them.',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub1' => 'First, we have to fix Lord Addam\'s ship, so we need to get some pinewood planks for his crew to start the repairs!',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub2' => 'Lord Addam fears his pets may have been stolen by one of the pirate ships that have been stalking him for a while. If that\'s true, and there are indeed pirates in the vicinity of the island, we should make sure we\'re prepared!',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub3' => 'In order to find the pets, we\'ve sent out some messages to our neighbours! Some of them have already started to look for the pets! We should visit their island and thank them for the help! Bring a gift!',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub4' => 'If we want to find the pets fast, we\'ll need more manpower. I would advise you to call upon some of our recruits - they move fast on land and have good knowledge of the surroundings.',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub5' => 'We\'ve assigned a lot of settlers to the search team. So many, that we\'re almost out of working settlers, and we can\'t afford to stop all work! I would like to ask you to get a new workforce for the island!',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub6' => 'Lord Addam says that his pets are not really the kind you can… pet. They might get aggressive when they\'re away from him. Looks like we should train some soldiers and take them along, just in case…',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub7' => 'So, remember those missing pets? Yeah, the cat. Yeah... Turns out that may have been an understatement. It\'s actually much bigger and more fearsome than a cat. We need to set a trap for her.',
        'GuiDaiWhitePetsSub8' => 'We\'ll need to be able to store the pets in a proper cage as the rest of the guild finds them. Let\'s make the most robust cages we can, using mahogany planks and titanium.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControl' => 'There\'s a group of people here from Capital Island. They\'re the Wildlife Control Group, and surprisingly enough, they\'re here to check out our wildlife. After two days of research, they\'ve come back with a long list. We need to fix the issues they\'ve noted as soon as possible, or our guild may receive a fine!',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub1' => 'They saw we\'re big on fishing and want to know how we treat our fish. I wanted to tell them what we kill them and eat them, but decided not to overshare. They\'ve asked for some fish they can check. Bring them the fish, carefully.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub2' => 'We have been recommended to build shelter for our deer population in order to contain it a little better. Our hunters might also be grateful for that, actually. I hear some of them have been visiting our neighbour\'s islands lately in order to fulfill their quota...',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub3' => 'They want to check our horses, so we have to bring them out to the field near the stables. It\'ll look like some kind of a horse show. I don’t want to mislead the settlers into thinking we’re holding an event and they weren\'t invited.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub4' => 'The Wildlife Control Group has reached the barracks and they want to know how many military units we have. When I asked them why they want to know, they said it\'s part of their routine. Please have an army check.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub5' => 'The Wildlife Control Group has noticed there are way too many predatory birds around our island. I don\'t see that as a problem, but they want us to form a longbowman unit to protect animals from the predators, if it becomes necessary. Let\'s train some longbowmen then.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub6' => 'The Wildlife Control Group has found a lake, although they say there isn\'t the required amount of fish in it. Did they count them, or what? How do they know that? Anyway, what\'s the point of arguing. Just refill the fish school and make them happy.',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub7' => 'Wildlife Control is a bit worried about our deer population. They\'ve suggested that we give them time to breed and replenish their numbers by declaring this rabbit season for our hunters. We\'ll need a few signs to make this clear in the forest!',
        'GuiDaiWildlifeControlSub8' => 'Wildlife Control mainly deal with animals, but they also care about our forests. They want to make sure that our exotic wood forests are not in danger, and so they\'re encouraging our foresters to do their bit!',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightCome' => 'Bad news, I\'m afraid! Our very own weather prophet woke up this morning with a pain in his stomach. He believes that winter is upon us. He keeps talking of snow and all that! I don\'t believe him, but we need to be prepared, just in case!',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub1' => 'The hunters need game so they can hunt. We can lure more animals by using bread and a special mixture of spices a lady sold me not so long back. I still have the spices, so all we need is the bread!',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub2' => 'We need more fish! But it\'s hard to get them lately, so we\'re going to use a new trick, and it requires steel. What\'s the trick, you ask? Well, we melt the steel and form it into little cubes. Then we drop the cubes into the water and wait for the sun to shine on them and create a show of lights. Then we wait for the fish to gather around! It\'s that simple! Now let\'s get the steel!',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub3' => 'It\'s very good that we\'re taking care of our island but let\'s not forget our friends! I\'m not sure they\'re preparing for the cold that\'s coming, so let\'s be a good neighbour and prepare some hardwood for them! That way, if they ever run out, we\'ll be the first to send them some! Cold can only be fought with fire. Or brew, or course.',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub4' => 'As you know, wheat won\'t grow during the cold weather, so we\'d better fill our storehouse with as much flour as we can! Why flour? Well, because even our mills might freeze, you see?',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub5' => 'Snow snow snow! People always want it, until it actually arrives - then everything freezes up solid. We need to get some blankets to keep the kids warm. There\'s a merchant on the island who has a surprising number of blankets for sale. He\'s asking for sausages in return, would you believe... Sounds like the perfect food for this weather...',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub6' => 'With the news of the snow and cold weather, many people agree we\'re going to need soup and tea, and both require water, so let\'s fill up as many barrels we can.',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub7' => 'Some of our settlers are concerned that they\'ll be freezing their pants off when winter comes. They could use some extra coal, if we can spare it.',
        'GuiDaiWinterMightComeSub8' => 'Our local tailor thinks he can develop a new kind of blanket that will keep everyone warm - even if they leave their home... He says he\'s going to need a bunch of cloth to create a sample, though. Can you give him what he needs?',
        'GuildFest_Adventures_Turnin' => 'With every trail and every quest, embark with heart and zeal.
Who will conquer adventures untold, in this challenge real?',
        'GuildFest_Day10_Turnin' => 'The pages wait, the words are yours, for you to craft with grace.
Join the contest, write your book, and let your talents race.',
        'GuildFest_Day1_Turnin' => 'With every swing, uncover wealth, and make the mountains groan.
Join the contest, strike it rich, let your mining prowess be known!',
        'GuildFest_Day2_Turnin' => 'With each chop, the timber falls, creating quite the sound.
Join the contest, cut the lumber, let your skills astound.',
        'GuildFest_Day3_Turnin' => 'To all who seek the gleam of gold, the challenge now is set.
Mine the metals, claim your prize, it’s a contest you won’t forget.',
        'GuildFest_Day4_Turnin' => 'The stove is hot, the pans are ready, your talent will be shown.
Compete to make the finest food, and claim the kitchen throne.',
        'GuildFest_Day5_Turnin' => 'To all the smiths and artisans, the challenge now draws near.
Forge the swords with skill and care, and show your talents here.',
        'GuildFest_Day6_Turnin' => 'To all the crafters, skilled and keen, the challenge now begins.
Forge ranged weaponry with glee, and see who truly wins.',
        'GuildFest_Day7_Turnin' => 'Sharpen your quills and ready your minds, it\'s time to write with flair.
In this contest of text craftmanship, let’s see how your words compare.',
        'GuildFest_Day8_Turnin' => 'To the artisans, all skilled and keen, the challenge now begins.
Create the most exquisite works, and see whose talent wins.',
        'GuildFest_Day9_Turnin' => 'The ingredients wait, your skills are key, for you to craft with pride.
Join the contest, create your goods, your talents be your guide.',
        'GuildFest_ExtraBuilding' => 'Temporary accommodation, with an extra queue to gain; Guild Fest brings guilds together, where victory is the aim!',
        'GuildFest_ExtraBuilding2' => 'On adventures we go, to win the fight,
Extra accommodations will speed up the night.
Gather the tokens, let’s make them soar,
Guild Fest success is knocking at the door.',
        'GuildFest_GuildSize2' => 'Join a guild, don’t be shy,
It only needs two members to fly.
One is too lonely, don’t go it alone,
With a guild, you\'ll soon find a place to call home!',
        'GuildFest_OpenPanel' => 'Check the Guild Fest Panel, where the stakes are high; watch as the best players reach for the sky.',
        'GuildFest_Tutorial_Main' => 'Welcome to Guild Fest! Join us at the grounds, where fun knows no bounds - a place of pure joy, where laughter resounds.',
        'HQ1_ThePumpkinMaster' => 'Hey! Don\'t be scared! It\'s me, Eliot, the Pumpkin Master! I bet you\'re wondering why it\'s so dark outside, aren\'t you? Well, it\'s a bit... CREEPY! A dark presence called the Hollow Man has stolen the sun! I need  your help to find the children of the night and scare the Hollow Man away! And that, is a job for my magical pumpkins! First, we\'ll need to own at least one pumpkin Cemetery and make some pumpkins!',
        'HQ1h_TendingTheSpookyCrops' => 'I know that my little pumpkins are growing slowly, but I just might have the solution! I\'ve heard you know of a way to speed up things using the goodies that you can produce at your Provision House! Show me!',
        'HQ2_TricksAndTreats' => 'The Hollow Man was born from pure darkness and mystery, that\'s why we can\'t see him in the dark! In order to scare him away, we need to make sure we\'re wise to his little tricks! Let\'s make some darkness at your provision house and test it… no, not on your island, but I\'m sure you have some friends who wouldn\'t mind being... test subjects... he he he.',
        'HQ3_ShinyLights' => 'The Hollow Man uses pure darkness to do wrong, so we need to use pure light to repel his deeds! I found the recipe for pure light during my travels to another land. Let me show you how to make a very powerful light at your Provision house, and if any of your buildings become affected by darkness, we could even try it out!',
        'HQ4_SixFeetUnder' => 'The next step might scare you a little! BOO! Ha ha ha, I\'m just kidding. In order to fight the Hollow Man we\'re going to need the help of the children of the night. We should start with our good friend, the Zombie. We need to summon him… or perhaps we should rather say: we need to dig him out. Sadly, he is buried very deep underground and we\'re going to need a lot of tools to dig him free! Bring your settler and make sure he\'s equipped with the best tools!',
        'HQ5_LordlyCall' => 'Do you know Mr. Myers? He was a great general in the olden days, but hasn\'t been feeling so well recently. He lives somewhere in a hidden crypt, but we have to find him as we need his help. The only way to summon him is to give him back his most beloved armour chestplate. We don\'t have one right now, but we can make one. We\'re going to need copper and iron ore for that!',
        'HQ6_MarbleMoon' => 'The last of the children of the night is doctor Frank and Stein. He is an expert on marble. They say he owns a castle made solely from marble, can you believe that? Anyway, it would be a good idea to call on him to help us because to scare away the Hollow Man we\'re going to need a lot of marble! Either you produce it yourself, or ask for the doctor\'s help - it\'s your choice.',
        'HQ7_SunBuff' => 'Hello, it\'s me Eliot! I need your help again to bring the sun back. You\'ll find the recipe for the Sun Buff in your provision house! It\'s a magical powder. Produce some and use it! If all goes well we\'ll have the sun back in no time!',
        'HQ8_WildGrowingPumpkins' => 'While our pumpkins are still growing, we can always try to find some ready-grown ones on your island. If you spot one, just click on it to collect it.

Keep in mind that they need some time to grow too. If you\'re unlucky today, why not try your luck again tomorrow.

- Collect 1 pumpkin on your island',
        'HQ9_ImportedPumpkins' => 'Another way to get pumpkins is to go on an adventure. Perhaps you want to give it a try?

- Complete an Adventure',
        'HW2013_EventMonster1' => 'It works! The pure water\'s weakened him! Just imagine what a few more canisters would do!

Quick - let\'s produce enough pure water to bring him down!

- Defeat the golem by using enough pure water.',
        'HW2013_EventMonster2' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it',
        'HW2013_EventMonster3' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it',
        'HW2013_EventMonster4' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it',
        'HW2013_EventMonster_Global' => 'You know that awkward feeling you get when you\'re carving your pumpkins, doing some magic potion brewing and are absentmindedly chanting some old spells you learned during your apprenticeship, when suddenly you invoke a giant golem in your garden and don’t know what to do with it?

No? Oh…
Well, nevertheless, do you think you could help me to get rid of this golem before he eats or tramples me... Er... I mean your settlers?

There is just one teensy, tiny detail you should know before you begin, though... I’m afraid I may have summoned more than just one golem…
In fact, I think I\'ve summoned so many your neighbours and friends will probably have to join in the fight too.

I need some time to prepare a banishing spell, and will need to seek out ingredients from all over the world.
Each golem your neighbours defeat will buy me some time. If we all pull together, we should be able to clean up this mess!

In fact, I think I already have an idea on how to beat the golem on your island.',
        'HW2013_EventMonster_Looped' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it',
        'HW2013_EventMonster_Reach19' => 'Before we can overcome the golem, we have to get you to a certain level. There\'s no way you\'ll be able to take him on as you are! Keep on leveling as you were, and I\'ll come back to you when you\'re ready.',
        'HW2013_EventMonster_Tut1' => 'Listen closely my friend, because I have a cunning plan.
Things aren\'t looking great as they stand. Our weapons cannot harm its stony-skin. Even our cannons are shrugged off like mosquito-bites.
But there is another way to defeat him.

What animates this golem is its inner fire. If we could extinguish it, it should freeze and turn into stone. We tried regular water, but it had no effect. 
Perhaps now we should take the concentrated approach, and try purified water instead!

It\'s worth a try.  Tell your settlers to drop what they\'re doing, and start producing purified water as soon as they can!',
        'HW2013_EventMonster_Tut2' => 'Alright, now let’s test those canisters of purified water! Simply click on the golem and a new window will appear. You can use your purified water there.',
        'HW2013_ThePumpkinMasterMain' => 'Have we met before? Your face looks... familiar. But where are my manners! My name is Eliot and you look like you\'re confused about what\'s happening on your island. Don\'t worry - I\'ll talk you through everything you need to know. So, where shall we begin?!',
        'HW2013_ThePumpkinMasterSub1' => 'First of all, you should try to get as many pumpkins as you can! Why? Because you can buy cool stuff with them, of course! Even buildings! One way of getting them is through buying pumpkin cemeteries. You find them at the merchant. There are different kinds, sizes and speeds available, so why not take a look and buy some?',
        'HW2013_ThePumpkinMasterSub2' => 'Of course, you can also collect pumpkins in other ways. Besides pumpkin cemeteries, you can earn them as rewards for quests, by taking part in several adventures, as collectibles in your home zone, by buying them at the merchant, or as a reward for defeating a golem! Trading with other players is also possible too! So happy collecting!',
        'HW2014_EventMonster1' => 'It works! The pure water\'s weakened him! Just imagine what a few more canisters would do!

Quick - let\'s produce enough pure water to bring him down!

- Defeat the golem by using enough pure water.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster2' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster3' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster4' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the golem by using enough purified water on it.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Ancient1' => 'Wow, yet another type of golem!! This one\'s even bigger - and it\'s on fire!
Looks like the enriched water isn\'t working now either. In fact, it almost looks like this thing\'s protected by a curse of some kind. 

For this, I think we\'ll need to call in the big guns - it\'s time to break out the holy water, to douse this golem\'s inner fire!

Produce enough holy water to bring the ancient golem down.

- Defeat the ancient golem by using enough holy water.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Ancient2' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the ancient golem by using enough holy water on it',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Ancient3' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the ancient golem by using enough holy water on it',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Ancient4' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the ancient golem by using enough holy water on it',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Ancient_Looped' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

- Defeat the ancient golem by using enough holy water on it',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Greater1' => 'What?! That golem looks somehow... different? And bigger!?
Looks like the purified water we were using is no longer effective. But what else can we try?

Ah - our settlers do have another technique for making enriched water! Perhaps that could put out the golem\'s inner fire!

Come on - let\'s make some enriched water, and bring the greater golem down.

- Defeat the greater golem by using enough enriched water.',
        'HW2014_EventMonster_Greater2' => 'I\'m afraid another golem has gone astray on your island. I\'ve already gathered everything I need from him, but I\'d expect your settlers would be grateful if you could defeat this one too.

