        'RedNose_DonateStuff' => 'In order to reach the donation goal we need to collect and donate as many red noses as possible. If you work together with your friends, this should be a cakewalk!',
        'RedNose_Main' => 'Have you heard? Red Nose Day is coming on December 5th. This is a great chance to help out a good cause!

To show our support, we\'ll be starting a server event in which you can contribute by collecting and donating red noses.

When the total amount of noses collected reaches a set level,, we\'ll donate a certain amount of money  to the Red Nose Day Initiative.',
        'RedNose_Reach16' => 'There are various ways to get noses, but you\'ll need more experience if you want to take advantage of them. Just keep on leveling, and I\'ll come back to you when you\'re ready.',
        'RedNose_Sub1' => 'The easiest way to find red noses is to send your explorers on a treasure search.

The longer the search lasts, the more noses your explorer can find.
Why not try it out now, and send one of your explorers on a short treasure search?',
        'RedNose_Sub2' => 'You\'ve collected quite a few red noses, so why not donate them to the cause?
To do so, simply visit your storehouse or mayor’s house, and choose the ‘Event’ tab. You\'ll find your red noses in inside, and can donate them by clicking on them.',
        'RedNose_Sub3' => 'If you want more noses, you can always produce some from your collectible items.
Let’s try to collect the items we need to produce a small basket of red noses.',
        'RedNose_Sub4' => 'Now that you\'ve collected the necessary items, you can start producing your own red noses.
To do so, simply visit your Mayor\'s House, select the ‘Collections’ tab and click to produce a basket of red noses.
When the basket is finished, simply use it on your Mayor’s House to collect your red noses.',
        'SSBookbinder' => 'I can produce different sorts of documents that will allow you to share the knowledge of your brightest minds. Let us build a Bookbinder workshop, and I will show what your Settlers are really capable of!',
        'SSCodex' => 'It is done - the manufacturing pipeline for the Codex is complete! Visit me in my workshop at any time and let\'s talk about producing some of these most precious volumes! This will provide you with the most advanced and secret skills and knowledge.',
        'SSExplorerBronzeComplete' => 'I propose we go on and teach this restless fellow the basics of navigation and travel planning first. After that, we should be able to tell what really he has a knack for.',
        'SSExplorerCompleteTree' => 'These explorers, eh? Here today, gone tomorrow! All these treasure searches and expeditions! A little groundedness wouldn\'t hurt, would it? Some commitment and dedication. Give them an area of expertise to specialise in - make them stand for something in life!',
        'SSExplorerFirstSkill' => 'I\'m not even sure he can actually read. He can\'t read a map, that much is sure! Just how can someone take so much time for every journey?',
        'SSExplorerGoldComplete' => 'Well, he has proven that he knows his metier, much to my astonishement, I have to admit, so it would be a good idea to provide him with our finest works now, and truly make him a specialist.',
        'SSExplorerSilverComplete' => 'It can\'t hurt to send a few of our more advanced books his way. I was thinking material sciences or a bit of history, so he can actually tell what he is bringing us.',
        'SSFinesmith' => 'I\'m telling you, give people the right tools and they will willingly share their knowledge with the world. Let us get a Finesmith to produce some Nibs!',
        'SSGeneralBronzeComplete' => 'Your generals enjoyed the most excellent training, but military tactics have advanced a lot since then. It would be a good idea to read up on recent developments.',
        'SSGeneralCompleteTree' => 'Most of your generals have years of experience on the battlefield, but they are woefully out of date when it comes to modern military science. I\'m sure at least one of them would appreciate some further education.',
        'SSGeneralFirstSkill' => 'The first step to leading an army is a good understanding of communication. Luckily, I know just the book to get you started.',
        'SSGeneralGoldComplete' => 'This final discipline might also be the most important one. A perfect strategy can sometimes turn even overwhelming odds around in your favor. These books might be expensive to produce, but I\'m sure they\'ll be worth it.',
        'SSGeneralSilverComplete' => 'Our student is doing well. Next, we will focus on the often overlooked matter of logistics. How do you optimize supply routes? How do you ensure that medical personnel are where they\'re most needed?',
        'SSGeologistBronzeComplete' => 'Basic training will help our friend to commit and somewhat predetermine his specialisation later on, so be careful what you teach in this phase!',
        'SSGeologistCompleteTree' => 'Did you notice that the Geologists often seem to settle for quite mediocre results? There\'s got to be more to get from these deposits! I say we give the first Manuscript to a Geologist and broaden his horizons a bit!',
        'SSGeologistFirstSkill' => 'Every journey begins with a first step, and the plan to educate this young fellow properly might turn out be a truly epic journey!',
        'SSGeologistGoldComplete' => 'It is about time to introduce our man to the greatest teachings of geology, one might say the secrets of the earth. Choose with great care - the abilities at stake are what make a truly exceptional Geologist.',
        'SSGeologistSilverComplete' => 'Our friend has ascended to the higher reaches of geology, if one can say that about a mole like him. Now we carefully have to assess his disposition and the potential uses.',
        'SSLettersmith' => 'I have been struck by an idea that might just change the way we share writing. It\'s this concept for reusing printing stencils, but it will require all-new production methods. Provide a Lettersmith to produce the printing press letters!',
        'SSMain1' => 'In order to spread writing, we will need the help of a few specialists. Get these workshops for your settlement and we shall get going.',
        'SSMain2' => 'The Manuscripts were a great starting point for the education of your Settlers. Now we should build upon this and take it one step further.',
        'SSMain3' => 'Truly secret knowledge and particularly valuable skills require a special type of book. I suggest you build workshops dedicated to the refinement of our Tomes.',
        'SSManuscript' => 'I\'m thrilled to tell you we are now able to produce the first manuscripts. Visit me in my workshop and we\'ll discuss the first edition! Remember to put that knowledge to use immediately afterwards. For example, your Geologists would benefit greatly from this.',
        'SSOrnamentalsmith' => 'To allow for the noblest and finest type of documents we will need an Ornamentalsmith. Creating a Codex requires much experience and skill. However, the result is the most amazing piece of bookbindery I am able to deliver.',
        'SSPapermillAdvanced' => 'By using the best materials we will be able to live up to the highest bibliophiliac standards. Let us use the experience we have gathered to build an Advanced Papermill, and create the finest paper of our era has ever known!',
        'SSPapermillIntermediate' => 'Our new printing approach requires a more robust type of paper, so we will be needing some new workshops. Build an Intermediate Papermill so we can work with our new technology.',
        'SSPapermillSimple' => 'To enable our Settlers to archive their knowledge for future generations we still lack something essential: paper! Build a Papermill and we shall have all we need to make documents.',
        'SSProductivityCL2' => 'Greetings! I am Master Gotenberg, bookbinder by profession. Have you ever considered  how much we could increase our workshop\'s efficiency if everyone had access to all their craft\'s knowledge? Such an endeavor requires quite an infrastructure though. Can you provide that?',
        'SSProductivityCL3' => 'With Manuscripts, we won\'t be able to cover all the aspects of our more complex crafts. It is about time we expanded our capacities to accommodate better document production.',
        'SSProductivityCL4' => 'The Master craftsmen are asking for more distinguished volumes to share their exquisite knowledge with. We shall need more sophisticated manufacturing methods to meet this requirement. Let\'s make sure our economy is up to it.',
        'SSTome' => 'The new formats look quite impressive. I can\'t even imagine what knowledge they might be able to carry. I recommend producing and distributing some Tomes as soon as possible.',
        'Soccer2016_Main' => 'Did you hear? The Settlers Football Championship is coming up again! Counties and Kingdoms from all over the continent will be taking part - and we should too, to gain glory and honour for our kingdom. There are prizes to be won, too! By trading the footballs we gather through quests and activities, we could win some amazing stuff! Let me explain how it all works!

Finish all the introduction quests in order to participate in the tournament.',
        'Soccer2016_Main02' => 'The tournament has started. To win the Settlers‘ Football Championship we have to win 4 matches in a row. Just remember to regularly check the Football Championship fixture list. You can find your next opponents by opening the green doors.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub01' => 'All parties must be at least level 16 to be able to participate in the Football Championship.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub02' => 'Now the first step. To access information about the Football Championship, open the event window. You can reach it via the options panel, which is right beneath your avatar picture.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub03' => 'Did you notice the football button next to your avatar picture? Using it opens the Football Championship fixture list. This is the most important part of the tournament. Green doors contain your next tournament opponent, brown doors hold a nice present for you, and trophy doors contain a special thank you. However, you can only open a trophy door if you\'ve managed to open every door that came before it. By the way, you can open green doors at any time during the event.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub04' => 'Well, now that\'s sorted, we should probably take part in our first match! Open your Star Menu, start the adventure “The First Match” and visit the adventure zone.

Hint: You\'ll find the adventure in the first green door in the fixture list.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub05a' => 'At the moment, our Settlers are all going totally crazy about football. As they aren\'t the tidiest bunch, it\'s actually possible to find some items by simply collecting the things these football maniacs have left behind.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub05b' => 'To find some more exotic items, you can send out your explorers. They\'ll observe the other teams, and return with interesting items, so we can improve our own tactics.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub06' => 'Once we\'ve collected enough utensils, we should start to transform those into tactics we can use on the playing pitch. Go to your provision house and order a foul. We\'re going to need it to defeat their midfielder.

Hint: If you have a rarity provision house, you can produce the same items there much faster.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub07' => 'The practice match you found in the fixture list will help us to prepare for the tournament proper. The Knight of Crowrock has agreed to let us practice against his team. Start the match and defeat your opponent!',
        'Soccer2016_Sub08' => 'So, this will be our first real match. Our opponent is the barony of Tepidwater. Much like us, they haven\'t played many matches yet. Folks say the barony is playing a very offensive 4-3-3 system. We should be especially aware of their midfielders, but at the same time watch out for their three strikers. The baron of Tepidwater has some strong players in his team.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub09' => 'Here comes the next match of the group stage. Today our opponent will be the Barony of Emberstream. The guys from Emberstream are a very defensive team with a strong defensive squad. If we want to make it to their goal, we\'ll need a plan.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub10' => 'Now it\'s getting serious. Our first knock-out match, against the Shire of Oxwater. During the group stage they showed skill in attacking, while maintaining a stabile defence. They play in a 4-2-4 system – that means with four set strikers.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub11' => 'In the quarter finals, we will play the Electorate of Sunflower Grove. They\'ve certainly earned their place amongst the last eight teams in the tournament. Similar to our former opponent they play with a strong attacking squad, although their midfield is a little more balanced. This will be a tough enemy.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub12' => 'Semi-finals… what a wonderful day. If you\'d have told me at the beginning of the tournament that we would make it this far, I wouldn’t have believed you. But here we are, up against the grand Duchy of Darkwood. What do you need to know about this opponent? They stand closely staggered in a 1-4-1-4 system and have many strong players.',
        'Soccer2016_Sub13' => 'Can you feel it? The air is filled with a mixture of tension, anticipation, and energy… it’s the day of the finals. Our opponent is the Kingdom of Dragonhead. They were always one of the best teams in the tournament, but they\'ll soon be second best! All players in this team are strong, and they are confident to boot. But they\'ve never played us. Go out on the field and show them what we\'re made of!',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Main' => 'You are going to host some of this year\'s tournament games on your island! That\'s certainly exciting, but it\'ll also be a lot of work. 

Will you be able to handle all the daily responsibilities? Don\'t worry if you fall behind, though - even if you finish a quest late, the next one will be waiting for you until the end of the tournament.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub1' => 'If your island is to host official matches, you\'ll need a professional playing field first.
It doesn\'t have to be expensive, but the measurements and markings must be precise.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub10' => 'For many, traveling to this tournament is a once-in-a-lifetime luxury, and they\'d love to take something home to remember it by.

As it so happens, I\'ve already had a few ideas. You could sell dolls in the players\' likenesses, soccer balls, or shirts like the players wear on the field.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub11' => 'There have been some reports of a few brawls among the audience during past few games. Some people are saying they don\'t feel safe, and I think they may have a point.
Can you post a few guards to keep an eye on things?',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub12' => 'The fans are swarming your snack stands! We didn\'t anticipate this kind of demand! We need to establish a stable supply line quickly, or we\'ll have a lot of grumpy tourists on our hands!

Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub13' => 'Fans have been asking for autographs, and the players are happy to oblige! Or at least, they would be - but they don\'t have any pens or paper on them!',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub14' => 'Your last formal responsibility as an organizer is to sponsor a set of medals, to be awarded to the winning team and runner ups.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub15' => 'The tournament is as good as over, but the tourists like your island a lot and are hesitant to leave. They are feeling a little bored though. How about telling them some stories of your travels?

Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub2' => 'You\'ll need plenty of personnel to handle all the jobs that come with organizing and conducting games - not to mention catering for the tourists! Let\'s find some eager settlers, and prepare some training literature for them.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub3' => 'Have you had a think about how you\'re going to house the players and the fans? They\'ll all need places to stay!
You may want to build more residences. 

Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub4' => 'With the games proper starting in only a few days, we\'re going to need to provide plenty of tickets for the fans - and that\'s going to take some work. You should get started soon!',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub5' => 'Soccer games are long, and the spectators might get hungry. Seems like a good opportunity to make some coin. But if you want to sell food, you\'ll need some stands to sell them from first.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub6' => 'The weather\'s really hot at the moment. Maybe we should prioritize stocking those snack stands with drinks before we take on any food. After all, we don\'t want our tourists fainting now, do we?

Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub7' => 'I have found the perfect dish to sell on your food stands! It\'s called a "hot dog", and they\'ve been selling it during matches on other islands.
No idea what that name\'s about though - it\'s just a sausage in a bun. Both ingredients have to be fresh!',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub8' => 'We\'ve received so many visitors, many are having to stay in the far corners of the island. As such, they end up having to walk long distances to the games, and some of them are getting completely lost.
Can you organize some wagons to get people to the playing field on time?',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_22-27_Sub9' => 'The hot dogs are a great success! Maybe you can expand the menu? Aunt Irma always has good ideas. Why not prepare some gift baskets?

Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
