Note: Completing this quest will increase your population growth during the event.',
        'Soccer2018plus_Infrastructure_ReachMinLevel' => 'You applied as an organizer and host for this year\'s tournament, but the other organizers think you\'re still a little too green behind the ears.
Maybe come back when you\'ve gathered more experience?',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Hub' => 'We have discovered a huge challenge for our archipelago. Along with its shipment of goods, a trade partner’s cargo vessel recently  brought with it a few unwanted passengers: a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which pose a real threat to our ecosystem! The good news is our experts have already provided us with a list of appropriate counter measures to deal with the intruders, one after another.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Boophis Maleficii - a yellow, frog-like amphibian that poisons our swamp lands with its secretions, endangering all plant and animal life in our swamps.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main1_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
We found out that Boophis Maleficii will be paralyzed if it touches some specially prepared paper. Please provide the material!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main1_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
Some business travelers on transit through our lands have shown an interest in helping us out. If we pay enough, they\'ll take all our amphibians with them in their traps when they leave our archipelago. Please provide the gold coins we need!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main1_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on an adventure.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
One of the intruding species we need to deal with is Constrictor Ignotus, a rather small but powerful constrictor snake, which is a threat to our settler’s pets. We need to protect them from this dangerous new predator.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main2_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
We found out that Constrictor Ignotus spits oil when it\'s exposed to clouds of flour. Before we get rid of it, we should try extracting some oil first! Please provide the flour!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main2_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
It appears these snakes are no match for our mighty island-bred horses. We could easily chase every last Constrictor Ignotus away, if we only had enough horses to do so. Please produce the horses we need!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main2_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on an adventure.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main3' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
One of the intruding species we need to deal with is a giant caterpillar that has no natural predator on our islands. It is also highly toxic, and emits a strange neon glow that is intensely unpleasant to look at. We can’t allow them to pupate and evolve - it\'d be way too dangerous. This species is so weird, biologists still can\'t agree on a fitting name for the creature - that\'s why we\'ve gone with “Unknown Larva”.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main3_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
Exposing “Unknown Larvae” to copper stops them emitting that unpleasant neon glow. That’s the first thing we should do. Please provide the copper we need!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main3_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
Once the “Unknown Larva” has been prevented from glowing, it turns out exposing it to gold powder will render it completely harmless. Please produce some gold!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main3_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on an adventure.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main4' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Calliphora Gilva, a yellow fly that loves our sausages. Unfortunately, it contaminates any meat it touches with its saliva, making our sweet sausages instantaneously inedible.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main4_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
That yellow fly\'s already wasted so many of our sausages, it’s a total disaster! Now we need to get rid of the rotten food...',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main4_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
We\'ve discovered that these yellow flies react to coal. If we produce enough coal, we can drive them back, and ultimately chase them off our islands. Please produce some coal!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main4_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on any adventure.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main5' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Coccinella Putrefactiona. At first sight it looks like an ordinary ladybug, but if you get close enough, you\'ll discover it has a rather noxious smell. You\'ll have to do something soon, as this little bug is causing a dangerous disturbance in our biome!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main5_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
We need a huge amount of wood to manufacture lots of little traps for Coccinella Putrefactiona. Please provide the necessary material!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main5_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
We\'ve discovered that marble powder acts as a highly effective repellent for Coccinella Putrefactiona. Please produce some marble!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main5_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on two mini-missions.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main6' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Mustela Furialis - an insanely aggressive weasel species that is preying on small livestock. You need to do something!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main6_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
Using wheat and fish, we can make an effective bait for these little weasels, which are preying on our livestock. Firstly, please provide the wheat!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main6_Sub2' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
Using wheat and fish, we can make an effective bait for these little weasels, which are preying on our livestock. We\'ve already got enough wheat - please produce the fish!',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main6_Sub3' => 'Now we should check whether all the specimens are finally gone. Go out and check on any adventure.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main7' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Vespula Doloris Magni, a tiny little wasp whose sting is excruciating - much more so than the sting or bite of any known insect on our archipelago! We need to stop it from spreading.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main7_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders.
We found out that Vespula Doloris Magni is highly susceptible to our archipelago’s brew. We can lure them in using brew traps.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main7_Sub2' => 'If we feed Vespula Doloris Magni with enough of our fresh-baked bread, it seems to lose its poisonous potency - and ultimately its invasive potential.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_26-46_Main7_Sub3' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders.
If we feed Vespula Doloris Magni with enough of our freshly-baked bread, it seems to lose its poisonous potency, and ultimately, its invasive potential.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_47-61_Hub' => 'We have discovered a huge challenge for our archipelago. Along with its shipment of goods, a trade partner’s cargo vessel recently  brought with it a few unwanted passengers: a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which pose a real threat to our ecosystem! The good news is our experts have already provided us with a list of appropriate counter measures to deal with the intruders, one after another.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_47-61_Main1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it some highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a real threat to our ecosystem! Luckily, our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate counter-measures to deal with the intruders.
One of the invading species we need to deal with is Boophis Maleficii - a yellow, frog-like amphibian that poisons our swamp lands with its secretions. Any water that touches it becomes inedible.',
        'Soccer2018plus_InvasiveSpecies_47-61_Main1_Sub1' => 'A trade partner’s cargo vessel brought with it a number of highly invasive species from abroad, which now pose a danger to our ecosystem. Our experts have provided us with a list of appropriate measures to deal with the intruders, one by one.
