We are just awaiting your approval.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part8_lvl40' => 'Let us wait until these beauties complete their purpose...',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part8_lvl52' => 'Let us wait until these beauties complete their purpose...',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part8_lvl64' => 'Let us wait until these beauties complete their purpose...',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part8_lvl70' => 'Let us wait until these beauties complete their purpose...',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part8_lvl80' => 'Let us wait until these beauties complete their purpose...',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl40' => 'As mentioned before, we’ll store the bulk of the Star Shards on board. Nevertheless, it is only fair that you have some to use at your leisure, in exchange for all the support you’ve provided.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl52' => 'As mentioned before, we’ll store the bulk of the Star Shards on board. Nevertheless, it is only fair that you have some to use at your leisure, in exchange for all the support you’ve provided.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl64' => 'As mentioned before, we’ll store the bulk of the Star Shards on board. Nevertheless, it is only fair that you have some to use at your leisure, in exchange for all the support you’ve provided.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl70' => 'As mentioned before, we’ll store the bulk of the Star Shards on board. Nevertheless, it is only fair that you have some to use at your leisure, in exchange for all the support you’ve provided.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_Part9_lvl80' => 'As mentioned before, we’ll store the bulk of the Star Shards on board. Nevertheless, it is only fair that you have some to use at your leisure, in exchange for all the support you’ve provided.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl40' => 'Hello again, Mayor.

As I predicted, it seems the star showers we experienced previously are part of an ongoing phenomena.

We’d better get the Forerunner ready.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl52' => 'Hello again, Mayor.

As I predicted, it seems the star showers we experienced previously are part of an ongoing phenomena.

We’d better get the Forerunner ready.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl64' => 'Hello again, Mayor.

As I predicted, it seems the star showers we experienced previously are part of an ongoing phenomena.

We’d better get the Forerunner ready.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl70' => 'Hello again, Mayor.

As I predicted, it seems the star showers we experienced previously are part of an ongoing phenomena.

We’d better get the Forerunner ready.',
        'Starfall_Repeatable_Variation4_Main_lvl80' => 'Hello again, Mayor.

As I predicted, it seems the star showers we experienced previously are part of an ongoing phenomena.

We’d better get the Forerunner ready.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Main' => 'A massive flash of light in the sky signals that times might be changing for the unsuspecting settlers of this island.

Everyone’s feeling unsettled, but Explorer Rina is leading the efforts to uncover this mystery.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1' => 'Well hello there, Mayor! I\'m Rina, one of the explorers. As you might be aware, we\'ve got ourselves a bit of a situation...

I’ve taken the the liberty of organizing an expedition to find out what we’re facing - and I have a feeling we need to find out fast!',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part10' => 'As I mentioned before, we need to prepare the tools we need to extract the fallen stars from our land.

The Forerunner is equipped with the facilities to construct such tools, but not a lot of storage space... Trade offs.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part11' => 'With the materials in place, we can now construct the mechanical wonders we need to tear through hard structure of the fallen stars.

We’ll need one tool for each fallen star we detect.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part12' => 'The S.C.R.A.P.P.E.R.s are ready and waiting. Remember, these are single use tools, but I designed them to have minimal waste material after they’ve done their job.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part13' => 'Well, I\'ll be! The crystalline structure of the fallen star is proving to be a challenge even for our S.C.R.A.P.P.E.R.s.

They’ll take some time to finish their work.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part14' => 'Even though they cannot be allowed to come into contact with the land, these shards have interesting properties. 

We’ll keep this one aboard the Forerunner for safekeeping.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part15' => 'We would like to carry out some experiments in the Forerunner’s onboard laboratory. 

Each research task requires a large amount of star shards, but I assure you, the discoveries we could make are well worth the effort.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1_A' => 'Regarding the expedition I mentioned earlier, we\'ve got two things we need to tackle. First, we’ll need to recruit explorers - good ones.

I need the finest explorers we have to join me.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part1_B' => 'Secondly, I’ll need you to send these fine recruits out on treasure searches.

Their findings will give me a better idea of what we’re dealing with.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2' => 'Our initial search has discovered some fragments - dust motes, if you will - which are part of something much more larger which has fallen from the sky.

We should do as follows.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_A' => 'I don\'t like the look of these motes.

Mayor, I’ll need the resources from the following list to create the equipment we need to safely retrieve the foreign objects.

I’ll also need some brave volunteers.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_B' => 'Here\'s a sketch I made of what we\'ll need to provide in terms of the necessary safety equipment. 

I know it looks sketchy, but that’s exactly what a sketch means, and it is the best I was able to devise at such short notice.

You’ll be able to find what we need at the Provision House.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part2_C' => 'Now that everybody’s properly outfitted for the task ahead, we should head out and collect the motes.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3' => 'So the dust motes have been safely retrieved?

Perfect!

There’s something both mesmerizing and terrifying about their otherworldly glow.

We need to take them somewhere we can properly study them and find out more about their nature.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3_A' => 'To be honest, Mayor. I\'m not entirely comfortable about carrying out the research in such a populated area.

These dust motes could be dangerous.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part3_B' => 'And now, we wait...

I trust the investigations are in the most capable hands you could find.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4' => 'We cannot allow these "Fallen Stars" to taint the environment  they came into contact with, let alone the people.

We need a new kind of facility that could properly store these stars, and allow us to study them as far from everything we hold dear as possible.

I believe I have just the thing...',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_A' => 'This project needs copious amounts of wood for it to fly.

Here’s a list with the specifications, varieties, cut sizes, and last but not least, quantities we need.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_A2' => 'We need to turn this, quite frankly, impressive stock of wood into hull parts.

The plans have been already delivered to your Provision House.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_B' => 'I know that cloth isn’t the first thing that comes to mind when you hear "high security facility".

Things are a bit up the air right now, but trust me - it’ll all make sense in time.

If we’re not able to keep up with the production demands for this project, maybe we can trade for the materials we need?',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_B2' => 'These patterns show how to properly cut and stitch together all this cloth into the shapes we need.

You can find them at the Provision House.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_C' => 'As unorthodox as it sounds, we’ll need copious amounts of highly fermentable products.

These are of the utmost importance if we want this project to lift off.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part4_C2' => 'Here’s the recipe and formulations for how to ferment these raw materials into a gas with the necessary properties for our little project.

Everything is ready to go at the Provision House.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part5' => 'The pieces of the puzzle are all in place, Mayor. Allow me to present you with the schematics for the Airship.

I’ve taken the liberty of delivering them to the Provision House, because I cannot wait to see her fly.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part6' => 'The ship is ready to make her maiden voyage, Mayor!

All she needs now is a proper name.

…How about the Forerunner?

Please, do the honors at your house.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7' => 'Now that she’s up and running, we have work to do!

Please, join me on the bridge. We have much to discuss.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7_A' => 'With a floating headquarters and science facility, we can fly all over the island and retrieve any dust motes quickly.

Unlike last time, we’re now well prepared to produce the right equipment to procure said motes safely.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part7_B' => 'The captain has pinpointed the location of the dust motes.

We should put those collection kits we made earlier to good use.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part8' => 'I have... not so great news, Mayor.

These fallen stars are emanating an energy that is harmful to the land and all who dwell upon it. 

With the dust motes we collected earlier, we can track down the larger Fallen Star fragments.',
        'Starfall_Unlock_Part9' => 'We’ll need to find remove any fragments as soon as we can, before they cause irreversible damage.

Deliver the survey to the captain so we can make our way to the fragments.',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_Granite' => 'Your Explorer\'s "Streetwise Negotiator" skill has activated a Bonus Quest.

Find Granite on a Treasure Search to receive additional rewards!',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_Salpeter' => 'Your Explorer\'s "Streetwise Negotiator" skill has activated a Bonus Quest.

Find Saltpetre on a Treasure Search to receive additional rewards!',
        'StreetwiseNegotiator_TitaniumOre' => 'Your Explorer\'s "Streetwise Negotiator" skill has activated a Bonus Quest.

Find Titanium Ore on a Treasure Search to receive additional rewards!',
        'TheSiegeQ1' => 'We need to move quickly and decisively. The siege vanguard is almost at the mansion\'s entrance!

First, you\'ll need to free the occupied sectors as you advance towards the mansion.

Then, in one swift action, you must simultaneously strike at both the besieging party and their command camps to dispatch the military leaders. 
A good execution of this manoeuvre will break the bandits\' grip on the trader\'s mansion.',
        'TombRaidersQ1' => 'A great evil is on the verge of being awoken on this land. 

Make haste and disrupt the ritual. Destroying the Unholy Altars that can be seen near the tomb should do the trick.
Go forth and purge the taint from this island!',
        'TombRaidersQ2' => 'The tomb lies quiet now that the ritual has been broken. The tremors have stopped and the sun shines again on the ancient stones. 

Time to take whatever precious, non-cursed artefacts we might find inside and seal this place for good.',
        'TutAddSector' => 'My scouts report there are more bandits than expected. Send your explorer out to explore more sectors so that we can be completely sure.',
        'TutAdditionalForester' => 'The economy overview shows that you do not have enough foresters to provide a constant wood supply. Build another forester to provide more wood.',
        'TutAdditionalSawmill' => 'Additional sawmills mean more planks, and that makes construction go faster, which is exactly what we need right now. Keep an eye on your pinewood production.',
        'TutAdvanced1001NightsRaid' => 'You have an impressive army, my lord, but I\'d like to see just how good they are. I want to put their capabilities to the test with a very difficult task. Your generals are excited, but are you up to the challenge?',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsChain' => 'We have an army, and we have a strong, productive settlement! All we need is now to take back the archipelago that belongs to me! Let us prepare the final steps!',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsExploration' => 'My lord! May I have your undivided attention? Your people are ready to take back the islands. Prepare the resources for your men and ready your generals! It is time to clear out all the sectors!',
        'TutAdvancedAllSectorsUnlock' => 'My lord, it is time for me to reveal my true identity! I am not a lord! In truth, I am a Sultan! In disguise! But... do you think you could keep it to yourself? Please, don\'t tell a soul! I love travelling the world in disguise. No man has ever been so kind and helpful to me as you were, my good lord. I just have one last request, and then I shall leave you be! Conquer all the sectors and reclaim them!',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicine01' => 'The first thing the practitioner needs is some obsidian ore.',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicine02' => 'The next thing the practitioner needs is some fresh, home grown oilseed to produce oil for his massage therapy, which he claims helps defend against cold hands and cold feet.',
        'TutAdvancedAlternativeMedicineChain' => 'An alternative practitioner has risen to fame on your archipelago. Many of your settlers claim he\'s healed them from various illnesses and nuisances. Unfortunately though, he\'s now run out of the materials he uses for his therapies.',
        'TutAdvancedArmouredMarksmanTraining' => 'One of your archers found me the other day, and expressed his concerns regarding their armour. Apparently the boiled leather we\'re giving them is not enough - they want more. I believe it would be best to train some armoured marksmen who could protect the others in need.',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsFirst' => 'My lord, we need to expand, and we need to do it quickly. Several scouts were sent out, and most of them returned with the news that the surrounding areas are all occupied by bandits! Gather your men and defeat the bandits!',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsSecond' => 'Curses! These bandits are causing trouble around our borders! Last night some of them snuck inside the settlement and stole several apple pies and sweets! Scoundrels! Dogs! I will not tolerate this! My lord, please, send your general and clear out the bandit camps in the area!',
        'TutAdvancedBanditsThird' => 'Ugh! One of the merchants coming from the east was attacked by bandits! It seems that these rats will not stop interfering in our dealings! The merchant was kind enough to share the location of the bandit camp. I say we wake up your general and have him take care of this problem. Defeat the bandit camps!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerChain' => 'Every good army needs siege weapons. You never know where the enemy may hole themselves up. Even if they hide behind their precious walls, if we bring siege weapons with us, we can crush their defences!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerFoundry' => 'I was told about the mortars your people can build. My lord, if you don\'t mind me saying, you seem a dangerous sort. Yet I want my islands back, and I will not back out. Build a foundry so we can continue our preparations!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerMortar' => 'Mortars! This is exciting, my lord! When we reconquer my islands, I will make sure King Schahri learns about this new breed of warfare! What? You\'ve never met King Schahri? Well then - I\'d best introduce you as soon as time allows! But let us not get lost in details, make me... err... make us some mortars!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerTraining' => 'My lord! While browsing your library, I found a book that mentioned a machine called "the besieger"! We absolutely need to build some of these! We could even adapt the mortar we made! These machines can destroy even the most fortified walls if used correctly! Build some besiegers!',
        'TutAdvancedBesiegerWagonMaker' => 'My lord, our enemies often hide behind solid walls. Instead of climbing those walls, we could destroy them. But for that we need big explosives! And to move big things, we\'ll need wagons. I think it\'s time to build a wagon maker.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_CompleteSnowWhite' => 'This was just one expansion - there are a lot more where that came from! I\'m sure you\'ll discover more blueprints once you start travelling to exotic places. Help the people solve their issues, and earn more blueprints for your epic farmyard.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_Main' => 'Ahh, you placed your shiny new epic farmyard! Let me tell you a little more about this incredible building. You can expand it with new production chains going forward - but for now, let\'s start from the beginning.',
        'TutAdvancedEWCorn_UnlockChain' => 'Let\'s expand your epic farmyard with a new production chain. Each expansion and upgrade of a production chain requires a blueprint.',
        'TutAdvancedEpicTreasureHuntUse' => 'My world is filled with tales about lost treasures, mystical places and curious people. One of them is a boy I know called Ali Baba. The boy has this peculiar ability to find maps that usually lead to treasures. I told one of your explorers to go look for Ali Baba, perhaps he can spare a coin for the boy to share his knowledge? Send your explorer on an epic treasure search.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksChain' => 'Oh no! The wood\'s causing problems again! It seems we have another shortage. Most of the buildings we built require wood. I think we should consider filling up our storehouses again.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksExoticWood' => 'My lord, I\'m sorry to bother you with my problems again. After you crush my enemy, I\'ll need help to rebuild the cities of my empi-, er, I mean islands. For that I will need the best resources we can find, and I was hoping it might be possible for you to prepare some exotic wood for me?',
        'TutAdvancedExoticPlanksProduce' => 'I truly appreciate the exotic wood you gave me my lord. But as you know, the wood has to be worked in order to be useful. I\'m planning on building several ships to aid in transporting resources around the islands. Can you have your settlers produce some exotic wood planks please?',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodChain' => 'Mahogany wood is hard to get around these islands. It is a privilege, you see? But fear not! We have plenty of exotic wood!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodCutter' => 'We cannot waste the rare wood! I will… I mean, we, will need wood in order to rebuild my empire… I, er, I mean my settlement - what is wrong with me today…? All in all, you should build an exotic woodcutter. That would be a good start.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodForester' => 'Hold it! Your men are cutting down the wood like there\'s no tomorrow! I don\'t want to rule over a land that has no trees! Here, I\'ve managed to save a bag of exotic wood seeds. Give this bag to your settlers and build an exotic wood forester\'s hut to take care of the problem.',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodOptimize' => 'I have here a report from your storehouse master. He tells me that the production of exotic wood is currently not optimal, as the settlers in charge have found a small lamp that allegedly makes their wishes come true. I\'m sure they\'re really just looking for an excuse to go slacking off. Talk with your storehouse master and have him optimize your exotic wood production!',
        'TutAdvancedExoticWoodProduce' => 'Now that we have everything we need to produce wood, I think the next step should be to fill up the storehouse. Let\'s produce some exotic wood - it\'s always good to have some on hand.',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonaberti01' => 'The Bonabertis are used to an insanely luxurious lifestyle. You should be prepared to accommodate for that, as it will certainly be advantageous to be on good terms with the Bonaberti family.',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonaberti02' => 'Now we need some high-quality interiors. It\'s rumored that the Bonabertis have a soft spot for mahogany.',
        'TutAdvancedFamilyBonabertiChain' => 'The Bonabertis, a very wealthy and highly influential family dynasty from a neighboring island, have notified you of an upcoming visit.',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteChain' => 'It seems that while we were focusing on restocking our wood supplies, we ran out of other resources, such as granite. We should let the miners know!',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteDeposit' => 'People that perform great deeds should be immortalized. And what better way to preserve someone\'s visage than by building a statue! My islands had many great men and my cities were filled with the most unique statues you have ever seen! But to construct more, I will need granite. Build a granite mason.',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteMason' => 'My lord, it seems that we might be in the need of more granite. While this island may not be rich in resources, granite can be found almost anywhere a solid patch lays. Send out your scouts to find granite deposits.',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteOptimize' => 'My lord? I was visiting the granite mines the other day, and something caught my eye - they have no proper equipment! I talked to the artisans around the settlement, and ordered them to use the proper clothing and tools. But this small distraction has also caused a small delay, so it would be wise if you could optimize our granite production.',
        'TutAdvancedGraniteProduce' => 'All a good mason needs is a good pickaxe to be ready for work! Now that we know where the granite is, we can start producing it. The more the better, that\'s what I say! Produce granite.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightBattleHorses' => 'We have the best horses and the best saddles! The only thing we need to do now is to add those two together! Have your stable master produce some battle horses for us.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightChain' => 'Berim Khalar has a talent for finding and hiring the most dangerous mischief makers out there. In order to defeat him, we\'re going to need some horsemen!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightEliteStable' => 'Right! Now we\'ll need a special stable to filter the purest of breeds, and the bravest of steeds to become true, elite horses. The trainers are already waiting for you - you just need to give them the appropriate facility!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightMountedSwordsman' => 'The best way to engage the enemy is by doing it on horseback. I know this, because I have a diploma in battle-tactics. The enemy should be surprised when they see your mounted regiment! Order your trainers to train some mounted swordsmen!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightSaddleMaker' => 'My future plans include horses, and soldiers that can ride them. We need to provide them with comfortable saddles, for comfort should not be an issue when they run into battle. Build a saddlecloth weaver!',
        'TutAdvancedKnightShepard' => 'As I\'ve mentioned before, in order to defeat Berim Khalar and his armies, we\'ll need some troops of our own. Plain soldiers will simply not suffice - we need to aim for the best. Let us prepare! What we need first is a homestead for the wool.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightTraining' => 'I once owned a book that originated from your lands! It tells a story of a knight that battled countless enemies to save a damsel in distress! I believe we need knights like that in our army! Have some knights trained at the barracks.',
        'TutAdvancedKnightWeaver' => 'The pack of wool the shepherd sent over needs to be taken care of! I\'m not too fond of wool myself, as it often… produces a very unpleasant smell, if you know what I mean. We need to build a clothier\'s hut.',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyChain' => 'My lord, it has caught my attention that your settlers are not taking advantage of the resources that grow on the Enhar islands! Have you ever heard of the amazing mahogany wood? No? Well then, prepare to be astonished!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyGather' => 'My love for wood is endless, but sadly, mahogany wood is very rare. There are certain merchants who\'ll pay off gangs of woodcutters to locate this rare wood. They pay a good coin for it. Send your armies to explore the new adventures, so they can bring back some of that mahogany wood!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganyPlanks' => 'I want to see with my own eyes how these sawmills work. Can you please indulge me, my lord, and produce a number of planks for me? I, well, I mean, not for me - for the people, of course… of course. Produce some mahogany planks!',
        'TutAdvancedMahoganySawmill' => 'Mahogany wood, when it comes in its natural form, can be used to build all kinds of structures or vehicles. But I gather you know best what you will use it for! I heard one of your woodcutters talking, and apparently your people know a way to shape wood! The "sawmill", I believe they called it. So why not build one mahogany sawmill!',
        'TutAdvancedManorBuild' => 'I saw a picture of a manor! I think a building like that would be much more appropriate for a lord! I\'ve asked around the settlement, but the only man who can build a manor is old Pa Custeau! Though he\'s a very old man, his blueprints are certainly impressive! What are you waiting for? Let\'s build a manor!',
        'TutAdvancedManorChain' => 'My lord, where I come from I was kind of a lord as well. Now, I\'m not being impolite here, no, I just... I just think that maybe the time has come for us to move to a… bigger house?',
        'TutAdvancedManorPopulation' => 'We may have a manor now, but we shouldn\'t forget about our settlers! They are also on foreign land, and scared of the unknown! I think we should build new houses for them! Raise your population by building more houses.',
        'TutAdvancedMarksmanTraining' => 'We need arrows, to rain DEADLY HELL FIRE down on our hated enemies!! Ahhh ha ha haaaaa! Oh, er, I... I\'m sorry, I got carried away. We have our horsemen and our knights. Now, we need some ranged support. For this, we need people who can man the ranged weapons. Our best bet would be to train a number of marksmen.',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanArchebuse' => 'Your artisan seems to lack patience. He\'s sent me countless letters describing what he needs to make those weapons, even though I\'m sure you\'ve already prepared everything for him! Please, have him produce us some arquebuses.',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanArchebuseMaker' => 'My lord, do you know what an arquebus is? Well of course you do! A beautiful ranged weapon like this cannot remain unnoticed. I would like to advise you summon your artisan, and see if they can make you one. Build an arquebus maker.',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanChain' => 'We have the frontline ready! Now we need to create the ranged division of the army! Let us ready the archers!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanEpicTutentureSearch' => 'While we\'re spending most of our time preparing for the battle, your army is getting… how should I put it… sloppy? Maybe not the best word to use. Anyway, I\'ve spoken with one of your explorers, and he told me he\'s more than eager to go exploring. Have your explorer search for an epic adventure!',
        'TutAdvancedMountedMarksmanTraining' => 'Now this… ahh! This is unexpected! Some of your marksmen requested to be transferred to the frontline! Can you imagine? A frontline that contains ranged soldiers? I have never heard of such… wait a second, that\'s actually not such a bad idea after all! Train some mounted marksmen, and let\'s see what comes out of this.',
        'TutAdvancedNewCoatOfPaint' => 'The last visitors you received at the mayor’s house didn\'t seem overly impressed with the building’s condition. A particularly fastidious guest even said it appeared rather old-fashioned to him. Let’s give it a new coat of paint.',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorBandits' => 'Quick! Wake up! Berim Khalar\'s men were spotted by your scouts! They have a small camp not far from here. I don\'t think they know we\'re here yet, though, so we must strike as soon as possible! Call on your general to gather his men and clear out the enemy\'s camp!',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorChain' => 'Ahh! What a surprise! Welcome to the islands of Enhar, the most exotic place you will ever see! My name is Noble Ludwig, but my friends call me Master Ludwig. Judging from your garments, I see that you are a noble yourself! Please, follow me to my abode. I have a proposition for you.',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorDeed' => 'Wait, what? Has that island always been there? I\'ve just noticed it! No matter, we can always use the extra space. We need a Sector Deed to be able to claim the land.',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorExploration' => 'You might ask why I would choose to live alone here. Unfortunately, I have the perfect answer: I didn\'t. I was robbed. A warlord known as Berim Khalar raided my islands and took everything from me! I was the only one who escaped! Help me recover my fortune, and I promise you will be well rewarded! Explore the region and find a place where we can start a new settlement.',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorPrepare' => 'These islands look nice and cozy, but it\'s better if we don\'t get our guard down. Who knows what might be waiting under that thick fog?',
        'TutAdvancedNewSectorWarehouse' => 'The smell of a new beginning! It\'s in your mouth, in your eyes and in your hair. But there is no time to waste! The next step is to build a storehouse on the newly explored sector! Don\'t worry, I have a diploma in engineering, so I can help you draw up the plans! Go now, and order your settlers to build a storehouse.',
        'TutAdvancedOptions' => 'My lord, I cannot understate how important it is for you to fully understand the options menu. This time I would like to tell you about the advanced options. These ones are particularly valuable when it comes to increasing your performance. Why not give them a look?',
        'TutAdvancedPlatinumOptimize' => 'My lord. As you may have heard, my islands are filled with a thousand (and one) stories. Some of us spend their whole lives travelling along the sand dunes telling stories to those who are willing to hear them. One of these storytellers, a young woman, has arrived at one of the platinum deposits. Unfortunately, she\'s spent so long telling stories that the men forgot their tasks. Optimize the platinum production.',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffChain' => 'I joined your people last night at the camp fire. We shared stories about our lives, and somehow we ended up talking about food. It was then that one of your soldiers mentioned you have an amazing cook. I think it would be a good idea to send a small gift to your provision houses. Some barazek maybe?',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffOwn' => 'My lord, have you never heard of barazek? It\'s only one of the most delicious cookies ever created!! While I don\'t know the exact recipe, I\'m sure if you went on an adventure to the new lands you\'d find some! Embark on a new adventure!',
        'TutAdvancedProvisionBuffUse' => 'My lord, I know the barazek looks delicious, but you must put your workers first! Imagine how happy they\'d be when they saw our gift! Please, use the barazek on your provision houses.',
        'TutAdvancedReadyArmy' => 'My Lord, I know it\'s been a long time since you explored a sector, but it\'s best we don\'t forget that it took a lot of fighting to claim our initial island! If we are to claim new islands, it\'s best we prepare ourselves for anything.',
        'TutAdvancedRecruitArmy' => 'With the weapons ready, we\'re only missing manpower now. We need to make sure we have enough room to hold a big army and our workers. You know what they say: "better safe than sorry".',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterChain' => 'According to one of your alchemists, saltpetre is the main ingredient in gunpowder! Now, as you know, gunpowder can be the difference maker in any battle - so let\'s get as much saltpetre as possible!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterDeposit' => 'My lord, would you happen to know how to mine saltpetre? You do? Marvelous! This is the perfect chance for us to plan for the time when arrows will not suffice to fight back against our enemies. We need gunpowder, but for that we need saltpetre! Build a saltpetre mine!',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterMine' => 'It\'s not an easy task to look for a saltpetre deposit! One wrong hit with the pickaxe and you can send yourself flying in an explosion! I\'d send only the most experienced scouts to find them, just to be on the safe side! Choose your scouts and send them out to find the saltpetre deposits.',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterOptimize' => 'I\'m afraid I bring bad news! Last night, while the moon was shining bright, there was a small accident at one of the saltpetre deposits. One of the miners decided to cook a duck, but forgot to put out the fire! The fire burned its way towards the hut, but thankfully they were able to stop it in time. However, this small incident has caused some delay so it would be a good idea to quickly optimize our saltpetre production.',
        'TutAdvancedSalpeterProduce' => 'Have you ever heard of a man called "Wild Peter"? He was a great gunslinger! Every time you saw him, he was carrying several guns, and he could fire them all off in less than five seconds flat! I saved his life once, and he offered to share his secrets with me. He taught me how to make proper gunpowder. Produce some saltpetre, and I might share my knowledge!',
        'TutAdvancedStockMaterials' => 'If we\'re going to start a new settlement on these islands, it\'s best if we stockpile as many construction materials as possible, just in case. How are the exotic wood and granite reserves looking?',
        'TutAdvancedStory01' => 'Oh my. A bird just flew into the room - an exotic one! It came bearing a message. Let me read it to you: "Ahem! Help! I am being held as a prisoner in the Watery Woods! Please send help!" The Watery Woods... That\'s where all those bandits come from! The prisoner seems to be a member of the royal family, as he was using a special kind of writing. Prepare an expedition to save him! We will need horses, wagons and arquebuses!',
        'TutAdvancedStory02' => 'Remember the prisoner we rescued? It turns out his name is Captain Mapparan! He\'s a man of... curious habits. He\'s traveled the world far and wide, and knows every single place there is. But that was many years ago, and now his age has caught up with him and he\'s no longer able to travel. So, he\'s decided to build himself the world\'s biggest library. Of course, if you want a library, you\'ll need plenty of books, scrolls and relics to fill it - and it\'s with this he\'d like our help. He promises great treasures in return! Let\'s start by taking care of the military part.',
        'TutAdvancedStory03' => 'Captain Mapparan speaks of a pirate who stole some of his maps. These maps contain directions to islands of an unknown distance, holding secrets that anyone would love to explore. It seems to me that this Captain is an adventurous one? Good - let us prepare our platinum smelters and complete all that the Captain requests from us!',
        'TutAdvancedStory04' => 'Come closer my  lord, and listen to this. The Captain wants his home to not only resemble a ship, but to actually be a ship! I was under the impression he was joking, but no - he actually wants us to build him a ship for a home! And not a small one, I might add! My lord, we\'ll need a lot of wood for this - and the means to carry the heavy logs. See to it!',
        'TutAdvancedStory05' => 'The blueprints suggest that Captain Mapparan wants the ship\'s inner floors to be laden with granite! Now, I can understand the good captain wanting some elegance, but granite is not easy to find... Here\'s hoping the rewards are worth it, considering all he\'s asking of us. Let\'s tend to the Granite.',
        'TutAdvancedStory06' => 'Cannons? Now he wants his home... ship... whatever it is to have cannons!? He claims that he just knows that pirates will try to take over his ship, and thus he needs protection! Very well! The good news is that he actually has the cannons and the cannon balls, but he\'s lacking gunpowder. On to the saltpetre mines we go!',
        'TutAdvancedStory07' => 'As I mentioned before, a library needs books! When Captain Mapparan brings his books to his ship, he\'ll need to have some proper fittings for them. Now, I know that proper fittings require titanium, as it is the strongest ore out there... But I\'ve also heard that titanium can protect the reader from evil curses! Seeing as this could be a problem, I say that we make the captain some good book fittings from titanium.',
        'TutAdvancedStory08' => 'My lord! Captain Mapparan approached me looking for a considerable loan. He claims he needs to pay several mercenaries to do the dirty work for him. However, I\'m not sure your current treasury would allow you to give him the loan… What? You want to know how much he asked for? No my lord, I cannot say, I fear you might faint! I have been keeping an eye on the market and it seems that the price of platinum ore is fluctuating. How about you buy some, and then sell it on for profit?',
        'TutAdvancedStory09' => 'My lord, I have good news! Captain Mapparan wants to thank you for all the help! He\'s called upon his friends from far off lands to come together for the feast of the century! I heard that my good friend, King Schahri will be attending as well! We need to prepare our best foods and drinks. Send the captain some meat, fish, bread and of course, a lot of brew!',
        'TutAdvancedStory10' => 'It\'s all about treasure. Everything is all about treasure. Captain Mapparan still keeps us up every night with his amazing stories! He keeps claiming that nobody knows as much about this world as he does! I want to prove him wrong! My lord, we should complete more treasure hunts, and learn all that we can!',
        'TutAdvancedStory11' => 'Captain Mapparan is about to make a decision! I really hope he\'ll choose to settle on your island! 
I had a look at our stocks, and it seems we could use some more gold and platinum ore to really help seal the deal. Once we fill our stocks, I\'m going to personally offer Captain Mapparan citizenship. Er, with your permission, of course. 
Send your generals on adventures, and bring back some gold and platinum ore!',
        'TutAdvancedStoryChain' => 'Captain Mapparan\'s presence on our island is very important, and we should do everything in our power to keep him here! I think we need to prove to him how adventurous we are!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanChain' => 'Platinum is an amazing ore. I love how it shines - and how you can craft so many valuable things using it. The next step is to make sure we\'re ready to produce it!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanEliteBarracks' => 'In my kingdo- er, I mean, on my island, we equip our best soldiers with weapons forged from platinum. I\'m sure you do the same for your own elite guard? The enemy should never be underestimated, we need the best! Build an elite barrack.',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPaltinumSmelter' => 'Platinum is a rare ore to find, but not the rarest! If you have an educated smelter, he can work magic with it! But before he can do that, you\'ll need to smelt it and make those shiny bars. Build a platinum smelter!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumOre' => 'My lord, I\'ve been doing some mathematics and crunching the numbers, and I\'m pleased to say I\'ve reached my conclusion. We need more ore! Yes, you see here? If we want to have a proper army we\'ll need all the weapons we can produce. Wake up your settlers and have them look for some platinum ore!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumSwords' => 'You can make the most exquisite swords out of platinum! The strongest warrior I ever encountered fought using only swords crafted from the finest platinum. I\'m sure your weaponsmith is familiar with the crafting technique! Have him make us some platinum swords!',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanPlatinumWeaponsmith' => 'I see your settlers have some talent when it comes to weapon crafting! The best way for us to make use of that platinum is to turn it into weapons! We\'ll need weapons if we\'re to take on the armies of Berim Khalar after all! Build a platinum weaponsmith.',
        'TutAdvancedSwordmanTraining' => 'We need to show the people that they\'re always safe! I would suggest a small ceremony where soldiers can mingle amongst the people, and talk to the folk! Train a swordsman at the barracks!',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingBuild' => 'The blueprints are ready, the resources are ready and the men are eager to start. Captain Mapparan will arrive soon, along with his company of men to supervise the construction. My lord, order your settlers to build Captain Mapparan\'s ship!',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingChain' => 'The day has come! We have all the resources we need to build Captain Mapparan\'s ship!',
        'TutAdvancedTaskBuildingUse' => 'Ah, how about paying a visit to Captain Mapparan? I\'m sure he has several tasks for us, and I\'ve heard that the rewards he\'s giving out are also noteworthy! Let\'s complete some of the tasks he\'s offering!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumChain' => 'Granite is indeed a very strong ore! But you know what\'s even better? That\'s right - titanium! Our next task is a given!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumDeposit' => 'Titanium is another ore that\'s hard to find and mine. My people at Wall Maria were never able to manage it, thus they left me with no option but to trade for it. It didn\'t come cheap, though... even the kings charge a lot for a pile. Your miners build much stronger mines than mine, so why not have them build a titanium mine and get us prepared!',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumMine' => 'Have your scouts ever attempted to find titanium ore? It\'s tricky, isn\'t it? But I know a secret! You see, there\'s this curious little bird breed called an "eren". These birds usually nest near titanium ore deposits, as they\'re partial to its smell. I smelled the ore once, but to be honest, it\'s foul! Why not pass this information on to your scouts and have them look for titanium ore deposits.',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumOptimize' => 'Something\'s not right! Since your men found that lamp, we\'ve been flooded with problems. Several chunks of titanium were left unattended, and one of them fell on the next, creating a chain reaction! Eventually the last chunk crashed into one of the outhouses, but luckily nobody was inside. The miners spent most of the day cleaning up the mess. You should help them optimize their titanium production.',
        'TutAdvancedTitaniumProduce' => 'Because titanium is hard to work with, people started breaking it apart in huge chunks. When the night fell, the lonely chunks looked like giants ready to eat the miners. Ha ha! Imagine that. We should call upon your miners to produce some titanium ore.',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperity01' => 'Take a look at the trade market and sell some goods for gold coins!',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperity02' => 'You showed great skill with your trades, but your treasurer still isn\'t happy. He asks you to produce some shiny gold coins.',
        'TutAdvancedWealthAndProsperityChain' => 'Now the whole archipelago is fully in our hands, it’s time for your settlers to prosper and begin to accumulate wealth.',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorses01' => 'The first thing we need to do is to tame the horses, and get them used to having a rider.',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorses02' => 'Now that the wild horses have been successfully tamed, we need to train them to become battle horses.',
        'TutAdvancedWildHorsesChain' => 'Incredible! Wild horses have been seen on the main island. What a great opportunity to tame and train them for your military.',
        'TutAdventure' => 'It seems the coast is clear. I promised to tell you more and I am always true to my word. Here I have a map of a small island. Click on the map in your star menu and start the adventure. Afterwards, you can travel there. Take some units with you and I\'ll meet with you there.
Note: The adventure can also be bought a limited number of times in the shop, in exchange for fish.',
        'TutAdventureMaster' => 'My father has written me a letter requesting we talk. Instead of joining you on your journey, I will comply with his request and meet with him. I wish you luck. We will see each other again when you have become the greatest explorer of all time.',
        'TutArmies' => 'You can now assign your recruits to this garrison. This will create an actual army that can attack the pesky bandits.

- Assign your recruits to the garrison',
        'TutArmiesNew' => 'Now it is time to assign units to the general. Click on the garrison and move the slider below the recruits to the right. Normal generals can command 200 units maximum.',
        'TutBakery' => 'The time has come. I can build the bakery. Ever since I\'ve lived on this island, I\'ve dreamed of being able to eat fresh bread. I am so excited!',
        'TutBanditLeader' => 'So, boy, things are getting serious now! My scouts have located a bandit leader. If we defeat him, it will disperse the enemy\'s units and free the sector.',
        'TutBandits' => 'Check your nearby sectors. There are bandit camps there. In order to clear this sector you have to attack them.

- Defeat 1 bandit camp',
        'TutBanditsNew' => 'So, the battle begins! Try to position your garrison as effectively as possible, and cross at the least watched areas. To check whether your troop composition is effective, you can use the pre-battle feedback. Show the bandits it was a bad idea to settle on your island.',
        'TutBarracks' => 'You might have noticed that some sectors are infested with bandits. 
In order to clear out these vermin you\'ll need troops.

- Build 1 barracks

TIP:
Barracks require a fair amount of building materials. If you are short on materials, check the store for some attractive deals!',
        'TutBarracksNew' => 'Hey Kid! I am Lord Sardin. The fat guy… what\'s he called… anyway, you know who I mean... he told me you need help with your military. Wait a second, you don\'t even have any barracks! That\'s not much I can do until you get some.',
        'TutBattleReport' => 'To see exactly what went well (or not so well), you can check the battle report to be found in your message inbox.',
        'TutBeer' => 'In order to train recruits and keep them happy, you will need to produce brew.
You can now create all the necessary buildings to do that.

- Build 1 farm
- Build 1 wheatfield
- Build 1 well
- Build 1 brewery

NOTE:
A farm always needs at least one wheatfield to produce wheat.
Two or more farms can harvest wheat from the same wheatfield.',
        'TutBigArmy' => 'This is getting serious. You already have a glorious city and an effective economy. Now, we should concentrate on the military, since they are not only supposed to fight well but also represent your kingdom\'s strength. This means we still need to increase the number of units.',
        'TutBigArmy2' => 'I don\'t want to tell you which units to choose for your army. You\'re probably able to decide that on your own. Just make sure you mix them up a little bit - not only is it more flexible, it also looks better.',
        'TutBigArmy3' => 'Great challenges await you. If you want to succeed, you\'ll need a big army with a good mixture of melee and ranged damage units. Prepare yourself well before leaving for the adventures.',
        'TutBonusAddFriend' => 'I see that a lot of other settlers have settled very close to you. Maybe you should become friends with some of them? Having allies is never a bad thing…',
        'TutBonusAdventuresBought' => 'Say, you have these map fragments, don\'t you? I was just at the merchant\'s and saw that he offers adventures in exchange for map fragments. You should pay him a visit. It\'s worth looking into if your explorer isn\'t having much luck.',
        'TutBonusAdventuresOwned' => 'Ha ha, look how many adventures I have. Isn\'t that fantastic? I think you should always have some. I always feel uneasy when I don\'t have any available. How about you?',
        'TutBonusAdventuresPlayed' => 'Pssst… It is me. I\'ve discovered there are a lot of different adventures with differing enemy types and islands. In any case, you should try out multiple ones.',
        'TutBonusAuntIrmasGiftBasket' => 'Nice to see you again. As expected, my relatives liked the bread very much, but there is still some left. Maybe you should process the bread into gift baskets?',
        'TutBonusBattle' => 'I hope you do not become too cocky. You definitely mastered the first adventure, but have you also managed to complete the other ones? To earn my respect, you first have to complete the more difficult adventures with fewer losses.',
        'TutBonusBattle2' => 'However, as always, you should not be satisfied with simply completing them - they consume your resources, so try to use as few units as possible.',
        'TutBonusBattle3' => 'Pssst… I\'ve brought you something. In your star menu you can find two adventures I found during my journey. If you manage to complete them without incurring great losses, I have something cool for you.',
        'TutBonusBattle4' => 'Hmm… I was just thrown out of my own office by Lord Sardin. He had a young woman in tow. Now I am not sure what to do with myself. Could you take me with you on one of your adventures? I\'ve always wanted to see what it\'s like.',
        'TutBonusBattle5' => 'Bah, my father… He doesn\'t have much confidence in you, so I\'ve made a bet with him. We bet that you will incur fewer losses during your adventures than he thinks. Now, you just have to prove me right.',
        'TutBonusBattle6' => 'I don\'t know what to do. I have so many help requests from other islands, but most of my soldiers have requested vacation, and if they don\'t get back to their families there will be a lot of awkward questions. Can you answer with the requests by sparing just a few units?',
        'TutBonusBattle7' => 'Well, I\'m back. I\'ve already heard how you managed to organize cannoneer training yourself. Looks like I was unnecessarily worried. However, now I\'m curious to see how our cannoneers will prove themselves in battle.',
        'TutBonusBow' => 'We agreed on 100 bows. I wonder what he wants to do with them. You could almost win a war with that many. Whatever, it\'s worth it, believe me.',
        'TutBonusBread' => 'The bread our bakery produces tastes really good. I have a favor to ask of you. In a few days\' time, some of my relatives will be coming to visit me. Could you please provide us some bread?',
        'TutBonusBuffCoalMines' => 'I\'ve just noticed that you\'ve overworked your coal production a little bit. Just remember that buffed production buildings can make a difference. When the buff runs out, the production rate decreases again. Try it out.',
        'TutBonusBuffFarm' => 'I\'ve heard talk of a group of raiders approaching. Should they decide to rest here, we will need more wheat to secure the supply of horses.',
        'TutBonusBuffFriend' => 'So, do you get on with Sardin? He might seem a bit rude but he is a brilliant tactician. But let\'s get back on topic; the king attaches great importance to neighbourly help at the moment. I think it would be good to join forces with one of your neighbours and help them.',
        'TutBonusBuffGoldmine' => 'And how is the goldmine going? You should always try to buff your goldmine as effectively as possible. The more expensive the production of a resource, the more it pays off to buff a building.',
        'TutBonusBuffLvl1' => 'A kind of fortuneteller has just arrived in your city and has asked for a solid sandwich. If you help him, he says he will tell your future. Generally, I am not superstitious, but maybe we should grant his request.',
        'TutBonusBuffRealwoodCutter' => 'Do not get distracted by this... What was his name? Klaus? The little fat man, you know who I mean. Do not get too distracted by him. We need hard wood for longbows. Maybe you could increase the production outcome for a short time.',
        'TutBonusBuffSteelforge' => 'I see you\'ve become interested in adventures lately. I am not sure where your interest comes from, but I like it. Military experience is never a bad thing, and I would advise you to boost your weapon production.',
        'TutBonusBuffWellFarm' => 'We have a lot to harvest on our farm. If you were willing to support us with food, we could multiply our yield. And that would be fantastic, wouldn\'t it?
If you\'re feeling extra kind, you could give some food to the workers at your small wells as well!',
        'TutBonusBuffs' => 'Remember buffs? Producing buffs takes some time, but you usually need them on short notice. That\'s why I recommend you always have some in stock.',
        'TutBonusBuildingQueue' => 'I noticed that there have been a lot of buildings in your building construction queue lately. I should remind you firstly that it is possible to buy temporary or permanent construction slots, and secondly, that you can change the order of the buildings with the arrows. Try it out!',
        'TutBonusCannoneers' => 'Lummy! Lord Sardin asked me to help you oversee the training of the cannoneers, but I don\'t have a clue how to go about it! I don\'t know what to say. I think you might be able to do better than me on your own.',
        'TutBonusCannonsStock' => 'Since we now have a cannon forge, we should increase our stock of cannons a little bit. Cannoneers are priceless in battle, believe me.',
        'TutBonusCoal' => 'Good to see you. I just received a message from the king. He has heard about you producing coal already. Right now he needs some, and asks whether you can accord him some.',
        'TutBonusCoalDeposit' => 'Lord Sardin has come to me with an unusual request. I think he was a bit too embarrassed to tell you directly. He says he needs coal for the training of his units, but he didn\'t want to tell me exactly how he was going to use it. Just send your explorer to find a coal deposit.',
        'TutBonusCoalDepositsFound' => 'My greetings. Sir Oliver rendezvoused with me a few minutes ago to plan the construction of a gold smelter. You should remember that a gold smelter needs coal to produce gold bars, so you should acquire enough coal mines beforehand.',
        'TutBonusCoalmine' => 'Now the only thing left to do is commission the construction of the mine. Meanwhile, I will try to find out why exactly Lord Sardin wants coal. I\'d really like to know.',
        'TutBonusCoinTrade' => 'Hmm… constructing coin production should be handled very carefully, but I have to admit I don\'t have enough experience to give out advice. What do you think about trading a little with coins to get a feeling for their value?',
        'TutBonusCoinage' => 'Well, the time has come to construct the building that produces coins: the coinage. As you may imagine, the coinage processes gold bars into gold coins, so let\'s get started!',
        'TutBonusCoins' => 'Now it\'s time to give your coin production the acid test. Let\'s see how long you need to produce a certain amount of coins yourself. I am really curious.',
        'TutBonusCopperDeposit' => 'By the way, have you been sending your geologist out regularly to find new deposits? Remember, you can always have more than one deposit at a time. How about searching for copper?',
        'TutBonusCopperMine' => 'In contrast to workyards like masons, mines have to be placed directly upon the deposits. As I told you a while ago, you have to keep production times short. Of course, you cannot reposition buildings - but what you can do is to build a storehouse near your mines. That keeps production times short, too.',
        'TutBonusCrossbows' => 'I know I said I wanted to let you do it on your own, but you mustn\'t forget that crossbows are made out of titanium and exotic wood. This means you\'ll need a stock of both these resources to produce crossbows without difficulty.',
        'TutBonusDekorationBuildings' => 'Hmm… Recently, during an adventure, I found the plans for a flower bed. If I understand correctly, it\'s a kind of decoration building to beautify your home island, although it doesn\'t have any other function. Could you please test that theory out?',
        'TutBonusEpicDecorationBuilding' => 'Well, I have to admit your island looks really fantastic, but one thing is still missing - an epic decoration building, a castle or something like that. I\'m sure you can find something suitable during one of the adventures.',
        'TutBonusExoticWoodStock' => 'Since we are currently working on increasing our stocks, we should continue doing so with exotic wood too. After all, you\'ve been consuming a lot of it lately. Just go about it the same way as with granite.',
        'TutBonusExoticwoodPlanksStock' => 'My greetings. I really appreciate you refilling the stocks of granite and exotic wood, but I would recommend you process some of the exotic wood into planks, especially as our plank consumption has increased a lot recently.',
        'TutBonusFarmUpgraded' => 'Greetings. I wanted to give you a status report for your farms. Production itself is running well, but some farms would work a bit more effectively if you provided them with some resources for upgrading.',
        'TutBonusFarmfield' => 'Please excuse the interruption, but I have a small favor to ask of you. A farmer from a neighbouring country has made a bet that his farm has more wheat and water, and I want to prove him wrong. So, we\'ll be needing more wheat fields!',
        'TutBonusFarms' => 'Please excuse me. I know you are very busy, but I won\'t disturb you for long. I just wanted to say that as soon as we begin producing bread, we\'ll be needing a lot of wheat. Maybe it would be best to build farms now so you don\'t have to deal with it later on?',
        'TutBonusFishProduction' => 'Since we have produced enough buffs, it\'s time to reproduce the fish, because when the basic resource of the buffs is exhausted, no more buffs can be produced.',
        'TutBonusFollowUpAdventure' => 'Oh man… Why am I looking so tired, you say? I\'ve just returned from a follow-up adventure. I found it on a regular mission, and it didn\'t look that difficult, but man was it tricky. On the plus side, I was rewarded with a plethora of resources and buffs, and even blueprints for a building. Not such a bad deal after all!',
        'TutBonusGainCoins' => 'You can produce coins yourself, trade them, buy them from the merchant or find them on your adventures. Sometimes, even your explorer will take some coins back. Try out all the possible ways and when you are feeling confident, we\'ll start organizing your own coin production.',
        'TutBonusGenerals' => 'A general (also a friend of mine) is resting at our tavern at the moment. Have you already hired multiple generals? If not, now would be a good time to start. He\'s a really good man.',
        'TutBonusGoldDeposit' => 'One of our geologists just came and told me he thinks we have gold on our island, although he wasn\'t sure. He needs more time to find out. Send your geologist out to find a gold deposit. Maybe we\'ll get lucky.',
        'TutBonusGoldbar' => 'Similarly to the other buildings, I would recommend you produce some bars in preparation for building the coinage. While you are taking care of production, I will create my monthly report for the king.',
        'TutBonusGoldmine' => 'So, did you sleep on it? Coin production, I mean. If you want your own production, you\'ll need a goldmine first, and they don\'t come cheap, so try to keep the mine running as long as possible.',
        'TutBonusGoldore' => 'Soon we\'ll be able to begin the second stage of coin production. First though, I would recommend creating a small stock of gold ore, because the gold smelter needs quite a lot of it.',
        'TutBonusGoldsmelter' => 'Well, now it\'s time to construct the gold smelter. I see you have already stocked up on coal in preparation for coin production. Very commendable. If you continue like that, soon you will no longer need my help.',
        'TutBonusGraniteStock' => 'While you are producing titanium, we should still keep an eye on our granite problem. I know it\'s an exasperating topic but it has to be dealt with. We should increase our stocks. Whether you trade or find granite yourself is up to you.',
        'TutBonusGraniteThroughAdventures' => 'Now we know where to purchase it from, it is time to do so and get some. As I already said, we\'ll be needing a lot, so go get! The more you find the better.',
        'TutBonusHugeCapital' => 'I\'ve just received a letter from the king. He writes that the king of another kingdom has accused us of having a useless trade network, because you cannot earn gold with it. Because he thinks a great deal of you, the king requests you prove the other king wrong.',
        'TutBonusHugeCapital2' => 'You will not believe what I just heard. Do you remember the king who badmouthed our trade network? He\'s sticking to his opinion and affirms that no one is capable of gathering a certain quantity of riches. I am sure you can prove him wrong again.',
        'TutBonusIronDeposit' => 'Something terrible has happened. One of the children has gone into a mine and the mine collapsed after them. Can you help us find the kid? It was an iron mine.',
        'TutBonusIronOre' => 'As soon as you build a mine on the deposit, we can start searching. Your mine workers can help search while they are digging.',
        'TutBonusMarbleDeposit' => 'How do you like the new resources? You can make a lot out of them. Remember that marble deposits deplete quite fast. When you have several, the stonecutter will always choose the nearest one.',
        'TutBonusMarbleStock' => 'I hope I\'m not disturbing you. I have a favor to ask of you. There is an ancient tradition among the stone cutters that requires them to participate in a competition to see who produces marble most effectively. Could you be the adjudicator? We\'ll produce up to a certain stock capacity and see who has contributed the most.',
        'TutBonusMoreAdventures' => 'Wow, did you also receive a letter? I\'ve been invited to participate in the competition too. Of course, I\'m going to win, but I wish you luck nonetheless. May the best man win.',
        'TutBonusMoreMasons' => 'If you have a little time, I would like to share two things with you: First, you can track quests by clicking the small box next to the quests in the quest book, and secondly, you can pin the building menu if you want to prevent it from closing, when you are building streets, for example. Take a look.',
        'TutBonusMoreMines' => 'Did you already notice that the trade prices for selling ore are really advantageous at the moment? Maybe we should make use of this opportunity, construct a few mines, and see if it really pays off.',
        'TutBonusMoreWood' => 'A former comrade from the military academy has asked me to help him. He has received orders to defend a village and doesn\'t have enough bows. I really want to help him. First of all, we\'ll need a large amount of wood.',
        'TutBonusMultiplayerAdventure' => 'Well, now it is getting serious. The final round of the competition has come. I just received the letter. Phew, take deep breaths... I\'m really excited, I have to admit. Now it will be decided who is the best explorer. Let\'s go!',
        'TutBonusOptimizeCoalChain' => 'Wow, your economy really consumes a lot of coal. Do you still have enough of it? Could you please check if your coal production line is still working properly? I just need to reassure my craftspeople that there will be enough coal at their disposal.',
        'TutBonusPlanks' => 'Ah, plank production is already working effectively as far as I can see. You should also raise your stock of planks a bit.',
        'TutBonusPlayAdventures' => 'Hmm… One of our geologists has just told me that we do not have any granite deposits on this island. That\'s a shame, as we\'ll need a lot in the future. Could you check whether you can find granite on the adventure islands?',
        'TutBonusPopulation1' => 'When did you last have a look at the settlers overview? I am just asking because you are running out of settlers again. I don\'t mean to bother you, I just want to make sure that you have enough of them when you need them. If you have enough space for settlers, you can hire some for bread in the provision house.',
        'TutBonusProductionTime' => 'It\'s important always to keep production paths as short as possible. The shorter they are, the faster certain workyards will produce. You can see the path lengths in the details tab for your workyards, or directly when you are about to construct a building. Moving buildings can help you make production as effective as possible.',
        'TutBonusPurchaseGeologist' => 'Specialists always need a certain amount of time to fulfill their tasks. As you progress, your times will become longer and longer. However, if you do not like to wait, you can shorten them with just one click. Try it!',
        'TutBonusRaiseStockBread' => 'Wow, producing units really takes a lot of time, especially when you have to wait for settlers to move to your city. If you need settlers faster, you can attract them with bread. For example, you can hire Retired Bandits in exchange for bread at your provisions house.',
        'TutBonusRaiseStockCoal' => 'Greetings. I see that you are going to begin your own steel production. A good decision - Steel is a fantastic material. Just remember that it will require more coal, so you had better raise your stocks.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodPlanks' => 'Greetings. I have a small problem. The consumption of hardwood planks has increased a lot lately, especially since your orders for building new residences. I would be very grateful if you could raise stocks a little bit.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodStock' => 'My greetings. I\'ve noticed your woodworm problem. I am aware that it mainly concerns exotic wood, but I think the hardwood may also be infected. We should destroy our stock and start afresh.',
        'TutBonusRealwoodforester' => 'Yesterday we received a newsletter which went to all nearby lands. It is an invitation to the so-called green initiative, which encourages a more responsible attitude to nature. We should take part and build a forester or two.',
        'TutBonusResourceBuff' => 'Looks like the letter is from your brother Theodor, and there\'s a package of resources accompanying it. I took the liberty of adding the resources to your star menu, and you can read the letter in your mailbox. I am curious to know what your brother wants to tell you.',
        'TutBonusSawmill' => 'Before I forget, with a click on a building you can see further details about it. Try it on the sawmill and see for yourself.',
        'TutBonusSpecialAdventures' => 'I\'ve just received the next letter for the adventure competition. I\'m so excited. This time it\'s a bit more difficult, but I love a challenge. I\'ll start work on it immediately. You too should work hard on it!',
        'TutBonusSteel' => 'You\'ve really been quite busy with your adventures. Did you lose a lot of units? Producing more always takes some time. How about steel production? Do you already have enough steel in stock to train a solid amount of soldiers?',
        'TutBonusSteelswords' => 'Wow, steel swords. They really look strong. Could you allocate some of them to me? I will give you something really useful in return. You had better produce some more to cover those you give me, and make sure no-one gets suspicious.',
        'TutBonusStone' => 'With the added resources from Theodor, we should have enough of nearly everything except stone. Produce some, because we\'ll be needing a lot of it during our upcoming challenges.',
        'TutBonusStoneDeposit' => 'Did I mention that it is possible to have several deposits at the same time? Just send your geologist out more often. An additional stone deposit always comes in handy.',
        'TutBonusTavern' => 'Phew! Building a tavern can take quite a while. Did you know that it\'s possible to finish construction more quickly? As soon as something is in your building queue, you can finish it instantly by clicking the blue diamond. It just costs a few gems.',
        'TutBonusToolStock' => 'Have you remembered to keep an eye on some of your older production chains? For example, check tool production. You need tools for many different buildings, so take a quick look to make sure tool production is still optimum.',
        'TutBonusTools' => 'I know Lord Sardin is a bit severe and has you really busy, but despite all that, don\'t forget your economy, especially your tool production. Is it going well?',
        'TutBonusTradeStone' => 'My greetings. How is your military planning going? I just saw that you have a trade office now. That\'s fantastic news! I know the mayor of a neighbouring town who also has one. He needs stone. Maybe you can trade some?',
        'TutBonusTradeWater' => 'Oh, you\'ve expanded your water production a little bit. I assume that was upon the advice of Lord Sardin. Either way, it\'s a good move, because I took a look at trading, and it seems water is a fine good to trade with.',
        'TutBonusTradeWeapons' => 'Did you remember to involve trade in your planning? You have a great task ahead of you, and you should not hesitate to use your military. The king will be very happy if you do!',
        'TutBonusVisitFriend' => 'I\'ve just returned from visiting one of your neighbours. A really nice island with interesting building structures. Why don\'t you visit your neighbour\'s islands yourself?',
        'TutBonusWater' => 'Finally we can train cavalry ourselves. How is water production going? We need water for brew as well as the horses, but I don\'t think there\'s any chance we will run short of it.',
        'TutBonusWell' => 'All we need now is some additional wells, and I will win the bet. Would you be so kind and help me once more?',
        'TutBonusWell2' => 'Greetings. I\'ve just seen the assignment for the construction of stables. Have you taken into account that horses also need water? You should think about building additional wells.',
        'TutBonusWheat' => 'I see you have built multiple farms. That\'s good, because soon we\'ll be needing horses, and they consume a lot of wheat. It would be best to anticipate and start production now.',
        'TutBonusWood' => 'As you already know, we will need a lot of wood to have enough building materials. You should always have some in stock so you don\'t run short.',
        'TutBowmaker' => 'Have you already taken a look at your recruits? They are quite robust when attacked, but not quite so good at fighting back. We need a unit that\'s able to deal out more damage. Bowmen would be the best. Build a bowmaker so we can train bowmen.',
        'TutBowman' => 'Besides melee fighters, you are now able to create your first ranged troops, the bowmen.

- Create 1 bowman unit',
        'TutBowmanNew' => 'So, let us begin with training the bowmen. I think 10 will be enough to start with, but be sure always to have some more in reserve, just in case.',
        'TutBranchOffice' => 'You won\'t believe the news I\'ve got! The king is trying to establish a trading network. As soon as you build a trade office, you\'ll be able to trade with anyone else who has a similar office. We shouldn\'t let this chance pass!',
        'TutBread' => 'Wheat is not only used to brew. You can also use flour to produce bread which your workers will like much more than eating fish all the time. 

Create all the necessary buildings and produce one bread.',
        'TutBrewery' => 'Bread? Don\'t make me laugh. Bread can wait. What we really need is brew! After all, we want to create an army. Luckily, wheat and water are also the two ingredients needed to produce brew, so it wasn\'t all in vain. All that is left to do is to build a brewery.',
        'TutBronzeDeposit' => 'Your geologist can now search for copper.

- Find 1 copper deposit',
        'TutBronzeDepositNew' => 'Did you already take a look at the new sector? I heard that it might contain copper deposits. Why not send a geologist to look for them? Maybe the rumours are true.',
        'TutBronzeMine' => 'Now you can build a copper mine.

- Build 1 copper mine

NOTE:
Contrary to masons, mines have to be placed directly on top of the found deposit.',
        'TutBronzeMineNew' => 'We should definitely build a copper mine. I will write the king immediately and secure your tenure for the deposit. You look after construction.',
        'TutBronzeSmelter' => 'Hmm… I have heard some troubling rumours. The settlers tell of bandits making trouble. I cannot confirm this yet, but we should be cautious. It might be best to process the copper into bars.',
        'TutBronzeSword' => 'Bronze swords are needed to train recruits.
You can now create all the necessary buildings to produce bronze swords.

- Produce 1 bronze sword',
        'TutBronzeSwordNew' => 'Do not get distracted too much by the fat man! We have to concentrate on the military. That is the most important thing! I hope weapon production is running well?',
        'TutBronzeWeaponChainOptimize' => 'An emissary of your brother Theodor has just arrived, completely hysterical, and told me your brother fears he will soon be attacked. He beseeches your help. Before we send him troops, we should check our weapon productions, starting with the bronze swords.',
        'TutBronzeWeaponsmith' => 'My scouts have discovered the first bandit camp. Now is the time to start weapon production! Build a weaponsmith for bronze swords as soon as possible!',
        'TutBuildingLicenze' => 'The fat man… What is he called? Holger? Whatever, you know who I mean. Anyway, he really wanted me to tell you that the way to obtain building licences is by freeing sectors. You can find them in your star menu, and have to use them on your Mayor\'s house.',
        'TutButcher' => 'After that business with the bear, we still have a lot of meat left. I\'m sure there\'s something useful we can do with it. How about building a butcher? He could process the meat into sausage.',
        'TutBuyGoodsViaTrade' => 'Psssst… It\'s me again. How is the adventure search going? Could you get me some exotic wood by trading? I cannot trade myself… for a number of reasons I don\'t want to go into.',
        'TutCannonforge' => 'I have finished preparations for the construction of the cannon forge. As soon as you give the signal, we can start. It will become a gorgeous building, just wait and see. I am convinced that Lord Sardin will have the same opinion too.',
        'TutCapital' => 'We should improve your trading skills at any cost. We will need lots of coins to upgrade buildings. In general, coins are always useful for trade, which is why we should set ourselves a certain coin income as a goal.',
        'TutCarpenter' => 'Ah, I found them! The plans for building a carpenter. He can produce the carriages with the help of the wheels. Just inform us when we should begin construction, and remember that the plans are quite complicated, so we will need some time.',
        'TutCavalry' => 'We have stables and nobody tells me? That is splendid! Now, we can begin to train the cavalry. There are a lot of qualified settlers we can train as cavalrymen. The more the better.',
        'TutCavalryFight' => 'The little… What? Oh, I just got a letter from the former comrade I was telling you about earlier. He says that I\'m incapable of defeating a bandit camp using just 50 cavalry or more.',
        'TutClaimAnotherSector' => 'Don\'t you think that it is becoming rather cramped here? I think it is time to expand your holdings. I know Lord Sardin is not here at the moment, but I am sure you will make it on your own.',
        'TutCoin' => 'Your final quest is at hand!
Gold, precious gold!
Defeat all the bandits and get access to the gold deposits in the northeastern mountains.

- Build 1 gold mine
- Build 1 gold smelter
- Build 1 coinage',
        'TutCokingPlant' => 'In order to process your copper ore you will need coal.
A coking plant can produce coal out of wood.
Keep in mind that you might need another woodcutter to cope with the increased wood usage.

- Build 1 coking plant',
        'TutCokingPlantNew' => 'There are different ways to obtain coal. One of them is a coking plant. That\'s where coal is made out of pinewood. Remember that your pinewood consumption will increase.',
        'TutCollectionAdvItem' => 'Collect a Bronze Cauldron from an adventure map. It can only be found on adventure maps you visit and will not reappear on that adventure once you have collected it. Best of luck!',
        'TutCollectionComplete' => 'Complete the "Country Saying" collection by gathering all the required ingredients! Why are you still reading this? Get going!',
        'TutCollectionGather' => 'Collecting the items on the map is no easy task! You\'ll need to look closely, as they\'re so easy to miss.
To start off, gather 10 Scarecrows and 12 Herbs. If you don\'t see them all on the map at once, don\'t worry - they\'ll re-appear during the day.',
        'TutCollectionTab' => 'To check your available collections, open the Collections tab in the mayor\'s house. They will become available progressively as your level increases.',
        'TutCollectionsChain' => 'You subjects are reporting increased sightings of useful trinkets lying around the countryside. Perhaps if they were gathered, we could make something useful out of them. Every little bit counts you know.
Long term quest chain: to complete this main quest, finish all sub-quests.',
        'TutContentGeneratorCompleteDailyQuest' => 'We have to reveal mor... no, ALL of them! Please help me gather more crystals, and I will take you with me on my journey!',
        'TutContentGeneratorCompleteQuestBuff' => 'The world has so much to offer, we just have to reach out and take it. I\'ve collected a huge amount of letters on my travels. All the love stories, the drama, the humour... Every letter has its own unique story. Let us reveal the truth behind this short letter here.',
        'TutContentGeneratorMain' => 'Good day! Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Sonya Graham - you might have heard of me before? I am travelling through our world, exploring exotic places and cultures.',
        'TutContentGeneratorRollShortLetter' => 'This is The Excelsior. It might look messy, but I assure you this airship is the peak of our industrial prowess. Please, come on board, and let me show you around.',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_EpicForge' => 'Finally, the Mountain Clan can live in peace. For the first time in ages, they can dare to leave their home in the mountains without having to fear the dreadful consequences. As a way of showing their gratitude for everything we´ve done, they\'ve sent their best workers to help us solve our mountain crisis.

But that\'s not all. They promised that not only will they help stop any further earthquakes, but they can also put the vulcanic might to good use, and power an Epic Forge with it!

Go and build this fiery masterpiece.',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Expedition' => 'An expedition crew has to be sent into the mountain. As this is the first time we\'ve encountered a situation like this, I will lead the expedition personally. We\'ll have to dig deep if we\'re going to get any conclusive information about this volcano\'s activity.',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Main' => 'Rumbling... Shaking... Aunt Irma´s Gift Basket falling off the table... Something awful is happening on our home island! It seems the big mountain near the archipelago has lost its temper - and its head! Seemingly the volcano wasn´t as dormant as everyone thought... We need take care of this crisis before anyone gets seriously hurt!',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_MountainClan' => 'There are legends of a tribe of Nords living high in the mountains. They are experts in mining, smithing, and the construction of huge strongholds. If the legends are true, perhaps you can meet the Nords yourself - and maybe you\'ll be able to convince them to help you out during this crisis.',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Prediction' => 'It doesn´t look like the volcano\'s going to erupt any time soon - but that doesn´t mean it´s harmless, either. Tremors are being felt on a regular basis, and each is enough to put our residents into a flurry. Not to mention all those broken coffee cups!

I found some old diagrams that detail how to build a seismoscope. It may not solve the crisis, but it\'ll definitely give the residents some peace of mind.',
        'TutContentGenerator_MCC_Sector' => 'We should start by taking a closer look at this newborn volcano. However, in order to get close enough, we\'ll first have to explore the land surrounding the former mountain, and dispatch any foes blocking our path. This has to be done, for the sake of all Settlers!',
        'TutCreateBuff' => 'Now create your first fish platter in the provision house.
Make sure you have the required resources in your storehouse.

- Create 1 fish platter',
        'TutCreateBuffNew' => 'In your provisions house you can create processed food, also known as buffs, for your workyards, refillers for some of your deposits, plus a few other things. However for now, let\'s concentrate on buffs.',
        'TutCrossbowsmith' => 'Please excuse my absence. I had to deal with some private matters… Anyway, I\'ve taught you nearly everything I know. Of course, there are a few better weapons and units you can still build, but I think you\'ll manage it alone. For example, we could use crossbowmen.',
        'TutDetailsTab' => 'Oh, something comes to my mind. Have you already looked into upgrading a building? In the detail tab you can see how many resources will be produced and how many are needed.',
        'TutEconomyOverview' => 'This economy overview is the newest invention of the king\'s treasurer. I took the liberty of integrating it here as well. With it, you can check whether there are any problems in your production chains and whether you can do something more effectively. For example, it seems your tree deposits are decreasing. You should check them.',
        'TutEliteSoldiers' => 'I just saw Seraphina. Was she here? Hmm… adventure. Well, maybe these adventures would be a good way to try out your new units. Since your home islands don\'t seem to have any new challenges to offer any more, produce some units and use them in an adventure.',
        'TutEpicAdventures' => 'Hello, how are you? How\'s the adventure search going? Found any treasure yet? I just happen to know that those bad guys on the far off islands have robbed one of the king\'s coin transports and stolen all the gold. How do feel about trying to get it back?',
        'TutEpicWorkyards1' => 'A historic moment, Milord!
Today we start our first production at our Epic Workyard. It\'s an event of great significance which proclaims Your great foresight and penchant for new things, as well as the undeniable greatness of our island!

Start a seed to pinewood production chain at your Epic Workyard.',
        'TutEpicWorkyards2' => 'We\'ve got our Epic Workyard is up and running, but it can do so much more! 
Use the remaining two slots to start additional Tree Planting production chains.',
        'TutEpicWorkyards3' => 'Can you hear the machines? They purr like a kitten - now let\'s make them roar like a lion! 
Use the "Magic Bean Soup" buff to double the Epic Workyard\'s production, and then select the building to see it in action.',
        'TutEpicWorkyards4' => 'It\'s time we set-up our first Epic Workyard. It will bring both glory to our island, and a much-needed boost to our economy. 
Great journeys start with but a single step, remember!

Purchase an Epic Woodyard from the Shop (Epic items) and place it on the island.',
        'TutExoticWood' => 'Have you already found some exotic wood? It is the very best wood that exists. Unfortunately, we don\'t have any exotic trees to cut down here. You can only get the wood from your explorer or through your adventures. Build up a supply of it, because we will be needing it very soon.',
        'TutExoticWoodPlanks' => 'Good, production is going fine as far as I can see. While the wood is being processed, I will check how to get rid of these worms. After all, we want to be able to store this wood again in the future.',
        'TutExoticWoodSawmill' => 'Uh oh… with the last delivery we imported a special kind of woodworm. It particularly likes chomping on the exotic wood we organized recently. We should process it immediately, but first we need a sawmill for this kind of wood.',
        'TutExploreClaim' => 'Your next task will be to explore this zone a little more.
For this you have received an explorer.

- Open star menu
- Send your explorer to map a new sector',
        'TutExploreClaimNew' => 'I have just returned from the king\'s library. It seems that this island has not been mapped yet. It\'s very likely that there\'s a lot we can use here, it\'s just that we don\'t know where the resources are to be found. Send an explorer to discover the hidden areas one by one. Similarly to the geologist, you can hire an explorer at the tavern.',
        'TutExplorer' => 'As you may remember, the first four sectors were discovered automatically. All following sectors have to be discovered manually by another Specialist: The Explorer.
You can hire Explorers in your Tavern...',
        'TutFarm' => 'Hello and greetings. Some days ago we made some tests on the earth on the island, and found that it is perfect for growing wheat. We could use that to bake bread. What do you think about building some farms for cultivating wheat?',
        'TutFarmfield' => 'Ah, I see you\'ve already built a wheat field. Every farm harvests only from the nearest wheat field. However, it\'s wise to have multiple wheat fields, as they deplete after a while. If there\'s no other wheat field left, the farm will stop production.',
        'TutFishRefill' => 'Have you already noticed that your deposits deplete when you destroy them? There are deposits you have to refill manually, like fish. Therefore, you have to produce a refill in your provision house and use it on the depleted deposit.',
        'TutFisher' => 'Providing your workyards with food packages will increase their productivity.
To create your first food packages you will need fish.

- Build 1 fisherman',
        'TutFisherNew' => 'Your settlers already have a place to work and live. They are working well, but would do better if given a buff. Consequently, we need fish.',
        'TutForester' => 'Wood is a limited resource. Make sure your woods are reforested regularly.

- Build 1 pinewood forester',
        'TutForesterNew' => 'Maybe you\'ve already asked yourself whether all the trees will disappear if we keep on clearing the forest like that. You\'re right, and that is why we have to do something to prevent such a situation: we will build a forester.',
        'TutForum' => 'You are learning very fast. I know, I expect a lot from you. Settling isn’t easy. In case you need any further help, or are unsure of how to handle certain things, there are buttons just below your avatar that will take you to the forum, support, or the tutorial.',
        'TutFreeHomezone' => 'I\'m getting near daily reports of settlers being robbed by bandits. It is time to strike back! We should completely decimate the bandits and make an example of them.',
        'TutFreeHomezone2' => 'Now that we have longbowmen, the time has come to push the bandits back further. It is also a good opportunity to test their abilities. Have fun.',
        'TutFreeHomezone3' => 'Almost! I almost caught her. It was really close, but even during the chase we must not forget your home island is still threatened by bandits. I think it is time to end this once and for all. Banish them from your island forever!',
        'TutGarrison' => 'The general can be placed in your sectors. He will create a garrison after arriving at his destination.

- Open the Star menu
- Select the general and place him in one of your sectors',
        'TutGarrisonNew' => 'To assign units to your general, you need him to make a garrison. Just go to your star menu, click on the general and then on a green field on your map. He will hit the road immediately and build his garrison.',
        'TutGeneral' => 'Military units can\'t go to battle on their own. They need a general to lead them.
Specialists, like the general, can be hired in the tavern.

- Build 1 tavern
- Hire 1 general',
        'TutGeneralLost' => 'I heard your general was defeated? Don\'t worry, it\'s not a disaster. I have put something into your star menu that you can use to heal him in no time. You should analyze why he lost, but first heal your general so he is ready for duty again.',
        'TutGeneralNew' => 'The situation is getting serious. Units alone are not enough to fight with - you need someone to lead them. Me? No, I cannot guide them, I have more important things to do, but if I\'m not mistaken, you own a tavern! You can hire a general there for a few coins.',
        'TutGeologist' => 'You have received your first specialist, the geologist.
He will help you find the next building material: Stone.

- Open the star menu
- Send the geologist to find a stone deposit

TIP:
You can always see the active quest by clicking the quest button.',
        'TutGeologistNew' => 'If you open your star menu, you\'ll see the new geologist you hired at the tavern. He will help us find special deposits on our island. First, we need stone. Go to the star menu and send him out to search for stone by clicking on him.',
        'TutGraniteTrade' => 'Hey hey. It\'s me. I\'ve been travelling a lot, and visited the nicest islands, but the bandits there are very well equipped. If you want to go there too, you really should rearm, and for that you will need granite as soon as possible.',
        'TutGreatCapital' => 'A generous offer has arrived from the king. At the moment you are subordinated to him, but he offers you your independence if you manage to gather a certain amount of coins, by any means you soo fit. You should take him up on this offer!',
        'TutGuildBank' => 'Together, we are stronger - and potentially richer, too. To take advantage of your extra buying power, you should build a guild bank to support your guild with resources. Perhaps the guild already has some resources stored, which you might be able to use?',
        'TutGuildBankUI' => 'The guild bank gives you a lot of options for sharing and trading resources and items. To see what\'s stored in the bank, click on the building. Because there are so many possibilities, the architects left a manual in the building, which explains how the bank works. You can find the manual by clicking on the question mark.',
        'TutGuildMarketVote' => 'Did you hear about the guild market? I heard they\'re introducing a new system for their votes. Let\'s get over there and see what\'s new.',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteParticipation' => 'The guild market is a collection of delicate items - and you get to decide which ones. The guild market vote is your opportunity to influence what the guild market stocks. Try it out and submit your vote. I\'ve submitted mine already.',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteReset' => 'Made the wrong choice? That\'s sad, but don\'t worry. You can withdraw your vote submission and vote again! Why not try it out?',
        'TutGuildMarketVoteResults' => 'Let\'s take a look at the results from past votes. This will show you how the current selection for the guild market was chosen. I can\'t wait to see the results!',
        'TutHarbour_Building' => 'The blueprints are ready. Now, we need only a few more resources, and we\'ll be able to build the key that will unlock many new new domains. With our brand-new harbor, we\'ll be able to send as many settlers as are willing on their journey to new lands.',
        'TutHarbour_Emigration' => 'With this beauty of a harbor, we\'ll be able to travel huge distances, and our explorers should be able to find new places to conduct treasure hunts.
On top of that, we may even be able to amass riches by supporting our fellow settlers overseas.',
        'TutHarbour_Main' => 'People from the continent were left with no choice but to flee, and are now heading for the far away islands of Tavos. Without offering much in the way of specifics, a request went out for Settlers willing to go on adventures to find a new life - and hopefully, a new home. The expenses incurred in shipping settlers over will be covered - and will even be rewarded in gold. But first, some preparations will have to be made.',
        'TutHarbour_Population' => 'Now, let us delegate some settlers to head up this most important of endeavors.
A few will have to manage the construction of a suitable site here on our island to keep the process running. Others will need to pave the way and travel ahead to plot a course and eliminate any obstacles. We\'ll need to wait and see what else has to be taken care of.',
        'TutHarbour_Reach13' => 'First, we have to ensure we are able to sustain the growth of our own island and economy. Achieve stability, and we\'ll be able to continue our endeavor.',
        'TutHorse' => 'You can now create all buildings needed to train cavalry units.

- Create 1 cavalry unit',
        'TutHunter' => 'Oh no! Once again a deer has gnawed at my documents. I\'ve had enough! These wild animals are becoming a plague. We have to find someone to get rid of the animals!',
        'TutIronChainOptimize' => 'Your military has grown really fast, and I\'ve just checked out your new militia. Tough men. They need iron swords, am I right? Have you optimized your iron production already?',
        'TutIronmine' => 'Hmm… I can see a lot happened while I was away… Fancy-schmancy trade office. However, reports have reached me that this island holds iron deposits. If true, that would be splendid, because we could use them to produce better weapons.',
        'TutIronsmelter' => 'But first we have to smelt the iron. Basically, you should proceed in the same way as with copper ore, so build an iron smelter and smelt away.',
        'TutIronweaponsmith' => 'Correct! We still need an iron weaponsmith. Just remember that the production of iron weapons uses more resources than for bronze ones.',
        'TutLongAdventureSearch' => 'Hmm… You\'ve upgraded your military quite a lot. Let me guess, that was my father\'s idea. He has always believed that more is more. Anyway, the real reason I\'m here is because I\'ve found a new route for your explorer.',
        'TutLongTreasureSearch' => 'Pssst… I\'ve explored a new route containing many treasures. It takes a little time, because the paths are often very steep, but you can find the nicest things there. I\'ll give you the information, but you\'ll owe me a favor…',
        'TutLongbowmaker' => 'I was en route today with my scouts and saw something rather worrying. Some bandit camps have very strong units. Most have just one, but that\'s already sufficient to cause problems. To counter these units we will need more damage than our bowmen can offer.',
        'TutLongbowmen' => 'Psssst… Come here! I have to be careful because I do not want to be detected. Have you heard about other islands already? There are lots of treasures to be found and mischief that needs to be dealt with. I would gladly tell you more if you give me some longbowmen.',
        'TutLongbows' => 'It still weighs heavy on my mind that I didn\'t manage to catch that person. Should she try to enter the city a second time, I will arrest her immediately. Anyway, we should continue according to plan and produce the longbows.',
        'TutMainAdventure' => 'Bandits are not just present on your home zone. By the time we complete this chain of quests, you will know everything important about adventures and how to experience them.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainAdventureMaster' => 'There is still a lot to tell you about adventures. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will know absolutely everything about adventures.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainBattle' => 'Battle is a complex and important topic. By the time we complete this chain of quests, you will know the basics of battle and have your first small army.
Short quest chain: To complete this main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainBattleMaster' => 'All that\'s left to do is to make sure your army is perfect. By the time we complete this chain of quests, you will have a well balanced weapon economy and a large army.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainBeerProductionChain' => 'For stable brew production you will need lots of new buildings. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have efficient brew production.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainBetterProductionBuff' => 'You are already able to use buffs. By the time we complete this quest chain, a new buff will be available to you.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainEpicWorkyards' => 'Good day, Milord!
Our scientists have come up with a new contraption: they call it an Epic Workyard. 
It\'s a huge, imposing structure that houses complex mechanisms which can transform and produce resources at incredible speed. Truly a magnificent achievement and a wonder of technology!
Much time and effort has been involved in its creation, so the Scientists Guild is demanding Magic Beans in compensation for the structure - but I say it\'s well worth it!',
        'TutMainFirstStrikeUnits' => 'Not all units attack at the same time. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will know what first strike means, and what cavalry is.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainFishAndMeat' => 'You already know the possibilities for using fish, but there are still some things you could learn. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will know everything about fish and meat.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainFreeHomezone' => 'You have probably already recognized the bandits on your home zone. By the time we complete this quest chain, these bandits will no longer be a problem.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainLastUnits' => 'It seems you are ready for the strongest unit types. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have all the remaining unit types and productions.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainLuxuryMaterials' => 'New buildings will become available which will need new building materials. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will know all the necessary facts about these materials.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainMoreUnits' => 'Recruits will not suffice as units for all types of battle. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have militia as a new unit possibility.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainNewBuildingMaterials' => 'New buildings will become available which will need new building materials. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have all necessary buildings for these materials.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainNewLands' => 'Claiming new lands is a complex task. By the time we complete this chain of quests, you will know everything important about conquering other areas on your home zone.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainParanoid' => 'It seems your brother has problems. By completing this quest chain, you have helped your brother.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainPlankProductionChain' => 'For stable pinewood plank production, a lot of steps are necessary. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have efficient plank production.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainPopulationCap' => 'Population is always an issue, as you already know. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have a large population capacity.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainPopulationCapPreparations' => 'Population is always a big issue. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will be able to handle your population issues.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainProvisionerBuffs' => 'To be able to use buffs, you will have to take certain steps. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will be able to produce and use one simple buff.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01' => 'Our explorers report that beyond the known regions lies an undiscovered land. Many islands, rich with resources, are waiting to be explored and colonised. But we are not alone in this knowledge. Other kingdoms are preparing to compete for the resources, and bandits and other shady folk are said to have colonised these islands.

In order to participate in the race for glory and resources, we should build up an expedition force. I shall show you what we need to do, in order to prepare for this great enterprise.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Generals' => 'When sending out troops on an expedition, they\'ll require an expert leader. Luckily, our nearest tavern contains plenty of expert marshals. These battle-hardened strategists know how to deal with the unknown dangers of unexplored worlds.

Remember: You can\'t use your standard generals on expeditions, so you\'ll need to use marshals instead.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Help' => 'In order to learn about the Colony mode and PvP, please check out the PvP section in our archive.

You will also find some important information on maintenance that\'s well worth a read.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Production' => 'Exploring unknown islands and sectors is dangerous. Thus, we need to prepare our expedition carefully. For that we should first set up some new buildings to hire specialised troops and provide them with the necessary equipment.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Recovery' => 'These expeditions can be very dangerous. We need to be sure that not only are we taking enough troops with us, but that we have enough medical supplies too. 
Our provisioner now can produce expedition medipacks. With these, we can instantly revive our marshals, should they be defeated in battle. You should probably produce some - just in case, of course.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Troops' => 'Our new troops can be trained in the Combat Academy. For our first expedition, I would recommend training some Heavy infantry units, alongside attack archers and attack infantry.

Keep in mind that you cannot use regular troops- those that have been recruited in the barracks - on an expedition island. You need troops from the combat academy.',
        'TutMainPvPStage01_Weapons' => 'In the Combat Armoury you can produce new weapons for our expedition forces. The armoury works like a provision house, letting you produce weapons just like you would a regular buff. To begin with, we\'ll need some heavy maces, attack pikes, and attack bows.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02' => 'Now that we\'re all set, it\'s starting to get serious. Our explorers have made it to an island at the edge of the uncharted territories. We should send expedition troops there to find out what dangers we will be dealing with. You can find the expedition map in your Star Menu. 

Note: If you want to play the expedition again for more practice, you can get it in the Shop for a low price.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_Exp' => 'Defeat all the bandits on this small island and come home safely!',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_Progression' => 'Congratulations! By completing the training expedition, you have reached PvP level 2. Check out the PvP progression window beneath your avatar to collect your rewards. Your rewards will be saved for you, until you collect them.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_SendArmy' => 'Once you\'ve selected the expedition island, choose the option "Send Army" from the quest tracker, and send off your three marshals with your trained troops.',
        'TutMainPvPStage02_WaterCastle' => 'As the great leader of the expedition forces, you have been awarded a water castle. This water castle shall be a symbol of your experience. Place it in the lake in the middle of your island. Right now, it may only look like a small tower, but with every 2 PvP levels you gain, it will increase its size - and our kingdom\'s glory.',
        'TutMainPvPStage03_Troops' => 'Before actually looking for a new island to explore, we should recruit some more troops. 

Remember: A colony island is only available for a short amount of time, so you should always have troops prepared before starting the expedition.',
        'TutMainPvPstage03' => 'That small island we just cleared was only the beginning. It\'s time to continue towards the core of the uncharted territories. Set up an expedition force and send your explorers out to find an island to claim. But beware - you will encounter bandit forces, and might even meet troops from other kingdoms!',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_Conquer' => 'Engage and conquer your first small colony. Utilize all troops and marshals you have, but don\'t forget to produce more troops while fighting. You might need them!',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_Explorers' => 'To find a suitable island to colonise, we need to make use of our explorer\'s expertise. Go to your Star Menu, select any explorer and then chose the option "Find Expedition". Then fight for a small colony.

Good luck!',
        'TutMainPvPstage03_SendArmy' => 'Now that we\'ve gathered our forces, and found an island we\'d like to explore, we should send our army to the expedition.

Do so by clicking on the Quest Tracker and then choosing "Send Army".',
        'TutMainPvPstage04' => 'We\'ve freed our first potential colony from its adversaries! Now, we should build up our defences and claim it so it\'ll produce resources for us.

You can build defence buildings by opening the build menu in your colony zone. There you can spend the defence points you acquired by conquering the colony to construct defensive buildings.',
        'TutMainPvPstage04_ClaimColony' => 'Now that we\'ve put our defences in place, we should make this island officially ours:

Claim the island by pressing the "Claim Colony" button in the Colony Management menu. It will then start producing your resources.',
        'TutMainPvPstage04_Defence_Mode' => 'Once a colony island has been conquered, you can build additional defences on it to protect it. Handily, our show of force and determination has convinced the local bandit leaders to fight on our side. We should improve their defence, cover its weak points, and do all we can to prevent other conquerors from taking the island from us.',
        'TutMainRangedUnits' => 'Ranged units are an important unit variant. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have access to two different kinds of bowmen.
Medium duration quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainSoldiers' => 'Maybe you have already figured out that there will be more types of units. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have soldiers as a new unit possibility.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainStoneProduction' => 'For stable stone production, you will need some preparation. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have efficient stone production.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainStorage' => 'Storage capacity is always very important. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have a large storage capacity and the knowledge necessary to increase it further.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainSupport' => 'To know the possibilities the game gives you for more comfortable playing you should know some functions. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will know the most important comfort features.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainToolProductionChain' => 'For stable tool production, you will require fresh knowledge on several topics. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will have efficient tool production.
Short quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainTrade' => 'Trading is an important feature. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will be able to trade and have your first trading experiences.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainTreasureSearch' => 'Treasure search is a good way to get rare or valuable resources. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will be able to make use of all the possible treasure searches.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainUpdateOldChains' => 'While building new production chains, older ones will get become unbalanced. By the time we complete this quest chain, you will be able to handle this problem.
Long quest chain: To complete the main quest, finish all its subquests.',
        'TutMainWealthy' => 'Now it\'s up to you to become the richest person and best merchant on the planet! When you complete this quest chain, there will be nothing more to say - and you\'ll have stacks of money to keep you busy.
Long term quest chain: To complete this main quest, finish all sub quests.',
        'TutMapparts' => 'Pssst… I have returned. I\'ve found a lot of these map fragments. Since I have no real use for them, I thought it would be best to give them to you. After all, you can buy interesting adventures with them.',
        'TutMarble' => 'The outer sectors also provide a new type of stone: Marble.
Check your geologists, claim sectors and search for marble deposits.

- Produce 1 marble',
        'TutMarbleNew' => 'Producing marble is a lot easier than hardwood. Basically, you just need a marble mason who cuts the marble directly from the deposit.',
        'TutMason' => 'It\'s time to harvest some stones.

- Build 1 mason

NOTE:
Stone deposits are not bound to one mason, so you can place several masons next to the deposit.',
        'TutMasonNew' => 'Of course, stone does not cut itself. For that we need a specialist: a mason. Place him as near as possible to the deposit and the storehouse to keep the journey short.',
        'TutMeat' => 'Have you heard? A kind of grizzly bear has been seen in the woods, and it\'s highly aggressive. A number of settlers have been attacked. We have to act. It might be a good idea to let the hunter produce some meat and mix it up with a sleeping potion so we can relocate the bear.',
        'TutMeatFishOptimize' => 'The sausages our butcher produces are really good, but I\'ve talked to him and he says he doesn\'t have sufficient meat to produce as many sausages as he should. Have you already had a look at meat and fish in your economic overview? Maybe an adjustment is needed.',
        'TutMediumAdventureSearch' => 'Hello, I am back again. At least I don\'t need to hide anymore. Yes, I am Sardin\'s daughter. My pigheaded father won\'t allow me to join the army, which is why I keep searching for adventures. By the way, I have the coordinates for your explorer\'s new search.',
        'TutMediumTreasureSearch' => 'A settler has come to me and said that during one of his journeys he found coins - quite a lot of them. Maybe your explorers will also find some when they go searching for treasures?',
        'TutMilitia' => 'Your Recruits are good fighters, but later on you will need more powerful units.
You can now create all buildings needed to train a new type of military unit.

- Create 1 militia unit',
        'TutMilitiaFight' => 'Training finished. Now things can begin. Let your militia fight for you and see for yourself what they are capable of. You can also mix up different unit types in one army.',
        'TutMilitiaNew' => 'You might be able to guess what comes next: militia training. Compared to weapons, the militia need more time and resources to be built, but in return they can do more.',
        'TutMiller' => 'Greetings. I hear that your wheat production is working well. With your permission, I would like to get your bread production organized, starting with the construction of a mill.',
        'TutMoreCapital' => 'Greetings. Don\'t worry, I do not have something to ask of you, just an idea. Yesterday I found a coin lying on the floor, and I got very excited about it. I was so happy that I worked way more effectively the following day. How about spreading some coins across the city and making your settlers happy with them? I\'m sure they\'ll work better that way!',
        'TutMoreEconomyOverview' => 'Anyway... The economy overview can show you more detailed information about what exactly improved in your wood production. Take a look.',
        'TutMoreEconomyOverviewAgain' => 'Now that you have built another building that requires pinewood, the balance of your economy has changed. It would be best to check exactly how it\'s been affected.',
        'TutMoreExplorer' => 'I heard what Henry told you about the granite. He is absolutely right; we will be needing large amounts of granite. Trading is always a possibility of course, but to find more adventures and granite we really should recruit more explorers.',
        'TutMoreMasons' => 'Hmm… Take a look at your economy overview. Your stone production is quite low. You should think about building another mason. We will need a lot of stone for upcoming buildings.',
        'TutMoreNobleResidences' => 'Your efforts to expand your military are obvious, but remember that you will need lots of settlers for the military and all the new buildings. And they in turn need a lot of space. Build some residences so that you have enough capacity',
        'TutMorePopulation' => 'Do you see how the settlers are already floating into your country? Feel free to take some time to enjoy it. By the way, I have heard about a mysterious potion that has the power to speed the growth up.',
        'TutMoreRealwood' => 'A suspicious looking person has been sneaking around your city. I will take care of him and find out who he is. Meanwhile, you should concentrate on hardwood production so we can produce enough longbows quickly.',
        'TutMoreResidences' => 'Have you heard about the latest trend in the kingdom? Newly-built residences built in a kind of residential community. We should think about taking the idea onboard. The king likes his ideas to be adopted.',
        'TutMoreTrades' => 'We\'ve been so busy we\'ve neglected trade a little bit, don\'t you think? Remember that the king places a lot of importance on supporting trade. Maybe we should concentrate on that again for a while.',
        'TutMoreWoodCutter' => 'Do you like the economic overview? By looking at production time and the quantities of resources produced, you can get the best out of each work yard. For example, for wood it would be two woodcutters for three foresters. The best thing would be to build another woodcutter.',
        'TutMoveBuilding' => 'I have some more information for you, so please listen. A master builder has settled on your island. He has the ability to reposition your buildings. Fantastic, isn\'t it?',
        'TutNewMaterialChainsOptimize' => 'As you no doubt remember, we introduced new building materials some time ago. However, we did not check whether we had a positive balance and had even constructed new buildings, which also produce some of these materials. So it is now time to balance these resource chains. Take a look at your economic overview and raise production of these new materials to a decent value.',
        'TutNobleResidence' => 'Did you know that an architect is currently in your town? He has brought the latest plans from the kingdom for new residences. Not only do they look better, but they also have room for more settlers.',
        'TutOpenShop' => 'Did you see already? The king sent a merchant some time ago, offering a large variety of different items. If you find something to your fancy, do not hesitate to buy it.',
        'TutOptimizeWeaponChains' => 'The amount of settlers you can train to become units looks alright, but remember you also need weapons. I hope you have continued to keep an eye on the efficiency of your weapon production chains, because you\'ll be needing a lot of weapons very shortly.',
        'TutPlayAdventures' => 'I knew you would be here. I\'ve chased you so often in this direction. It was just a matter of time before I caught up with you. Now, reveal who you are!... Oh my god! This cannot be. Seraphina! Could you please leave us alone for a while?',
        'TutPopulation1' => 'Oh, it looks like you are running out of available settlers. If you mouse over the settler icon in the resource bar at the top of the screen, you can see information about your settlers, like, for example, when you will get a new one and how much space is left. Check what you have to improve to get new settlers, and buy new ones from the merchant when there is enough space.',
        'TutPopulationCap' => 'Remember the king\'s last task? I\'ve received a message. He has a new task for you, offering support as long as you accommodate a certain number of settlers.',
        'TutPopulationCap2' => 'A new letter from the king has arrived, but it is meant for your eyes only, which is why I have placed the letter in your mail box. I wonder what it says…',
        'TutPopulationCap3' => 'Pssst… During my last journey, I came upon a messenger who had been robbed. He gave me this letter and asked me to bring it to you. It has no sender details. I thought it had to be important, so I decided to do you this favor.',
        'TutPopulationCap4' => 'Hey, what happened to Lord Sardin? I\'ve never seen him so excited. I leave for just a few short hours, and the strangest things happen. Oh by the way, I have a new letter for you with no details of who sent it.',
        'TutPopulationCap5' => 'Wow, you\'ll never guess what I found! There are some islands quite far away, with epic treasures like coins and special building plans. However, you\'ll need a huge army for the voyage, and that will require new, unemployed settlers.',
        'TutPopulationCap6' => 'I can see you are diligently working on making your city perfect and polished. I think we should do the same with your military. After all, the military reflects the image of its owner, so let\'s increase the amount of unemployed settlers to attract more potential soldiers.',
        'TutPopulationCap7' => 'I see my father has left, but I won\'t until you have become the greatest explorer of any time. However, you\'ll need far more than the army you have at the moment, including more units for example.',
        'TutPopulationCap8' => 'I can see my father has left. I will not go until you have become the greatest explorer of any time. However, you\'ll need a far greater army than you have at the moment - more units, for example.',
        'TutPowderhut' => 'I found it! I found it! The construction plans to upgrade carriages to cannons. We\'ll be needing two different buildings - a powderhut and a cannon forge. If you\'re interested, you should start with the powderhut.',
        'TutProduceFishRefill' => 'I offer you my compliments. My name is Henry. I am one of your craftsmen. My colleague the fisherman told me that the fish stocks are decreasing. You should know that you can refill these kinds of deposits. Would you be so kind as to produce some refillers?',
        'TutProduceRecruits' => 'Your brother is becoming more and more impatient. We should send him some units soon to stop him going insane with fear. Train a few recruits and I will send them to him as soon as they are done.',
        'TutProduceSoldiers' => 'Well, the swords didn\'t calm your brother down for very long it seems. He has become very agitated again. It is time to send him the soldiers. After that, hopefully, he will finally calm down.',
        'TutProduceSteelswords' => 'I must talk to you once again about the fears of your brother Theodor. He has sent a message saying he prefers not to wait so long for the soldiers, and hence would like us to send steel swords to start off with.',
        'TutProduceTools' => 'Greetings. Good to see you again. I have heard of some trouble around here, but it does not concern me. I am just here to tell you that the construction of the buildings, whose plans we have now, will consume a lot of tools. You should think about expanding your tool production.',
        'TutProvisionHouse' => 'In order to process your fish into food packages you will need a provision house.

- Build 1 provision house',
        'TutProvisionHouseNew' => 'But first you have to build a provisions house where your groceries can be processed. After all, freshly caught fish cannot be eaten immediately.',
        'TutPurchaseGeologist' => 'Now that the tavern is finished, we should think about the next step. Do you remember that you can hire specialists there? With a click on the tavern, you can see which specialists are available. Go and purchase a geologist!',
        'TutQualityFoodBuff' => 'You have produced enough bread to create a better Food Buff.
Go to your Provision House and create it.',
        'TutRaiseGranite' => 'Greetings. How are you doing? I\'ve checked the new plans, and they are really fascinating, but we will need granite for most of the buildings. It\'s a rare stone we cannot find on this island, but maybe you can obtain some during your adventures?',
        'TutRealWood' => 'In the outer sectors you will find a new type of wood: Hardwood.
Advanced buildings will need planks of this material to be created.

- Produce 1 hardwood plank',
        'TutRealWoodNew' => 'I just arrived. I was on a voyage and have seen lots of new and different things. The latest trend is for buildings made out of hardwood and marble. In any case, we should upgrade to keep being competitive.',
        'TutRecruit' => 'Now it\'s time to prepare your first army.

- Train 5 recruits in the barracks',
        'TutRecruitNew' => 'Before you can assign units to your general, you need to produce them in your barracks. 10 recruits should be enough to start off with.',
        'TutSausage' => 'There is a countrywide competition among the settlers to see who is able to build the highest and most stable sausage pyramid. Actually, I didn\'t want to bother you with it, but Sir Oliver said I should ask anyway. So, would you sponsor us and provide the sausages? Of course, we would be happy to share the reward with you.',
        'TutSawmill' => 'To construct more buildings, you will need different building materials. The first building material is planks. The sawmill produces pinewood planks out of pinewood.

- Build 1 pinewood sawmill',
        'TutSawmillNew' => 'The wood is of no great use to you in itself. However, in order to build additional buildings, you\'ll need planks. You should build a wood sawmill.',
        'TutSelectBarracks' => 'In the barracks you can choose from various troop types

- Select the barracks and check how much resources are required to train a recruit.',
        'TutSelectBarracksNew' => 'Don\'t tell me you don\'t know how the barracks work?! Oh man, I really have to start from the very beginning. The barracks is where you can train your troops. Take a look at it.',
        'TutSelectMayorhouse' => 'The Mayor\'s house is your first storehouse. All goods are stored here. A click on a storehouse gives you an overview of your current stock level.

- Select the Mayor\'s house and take a look at your current stock level',
        'TutSelectMayorhouseNew' => 'In the Mayor\'s house and your storehouses you can see the resources you have in stock, spread over several tabs. Just like the sawmill, the Mayor\'s house can be clicked on to show the detail window. Try it out.',
        'TutSellGoodsViaTrade' => 'It seems your economy is working quite well. Have you already noticed that we do not need a lot of stones and planks anymore? In case you have a large amount of any specific resource left, you can trade it in and get more useful resources.',
        'TutShortAdventureSearch' => 'If you want to find more maps, you\'ll have to do it by yourself. Just send your explorer on an adventure search, and if you are lucky, he\'ll find one. However, the strength of enemy units varies, so always take enough units with you.',
        'TutSimpleResidence' => 'Your population needs living space.
Since your mayor\'s house only supports a limited number of people, you\'ll need more space.

- Build 1 residence',
        'TutSimpleResidenceNew' => 'Your storehouses are well stocked and your settlement is expanding, but your settlers want somewhere to live. You should build them suitable houses to live in. The more residences you have, the more settlers will move to your settlement.',
        'TutSolidSandwich' => 'You really should concentrate more on your soldiers and not waste your time with bagatelles. Wait a minute... I think the bread may actually be of use here. Maybe we can improve our military capabilities with it somehow?',
        'TutStable' => 'The group of riders arrived a short while ago. They would like to rest but we have no place for their horses. Maybe we can build them a little stable?',
        'TutSteelWeaponChainOptimize' => 'Tell me this is not true. Now Theodor wants soldiers from us because he is afraid that recruits might not suffice. Whatever. After all, he is your brother. Just check whether your steel production is well balanced first.',
        'TutSteelWeaponsmith' => 'But first, to more important matters - we need a steel weaponsmith to process steel into steel swords. I am so looking forward to commanding the first soldiers.',
        'TutSteelforge' => 'My scouts report of enemy activities on other islands. My instinct tells me we should keep on expanding the military, so it would be a good idea to have a steel smelter.',
        'TutStorage' => 'I\'ve just received a message from the king. He has decided to assign you a task. He wants you to have the biggest storage capacity in all the land. Before that though, he\'d like to test whether you are up to the task, so he\'ll start with a smaller goal.',
        'TutStorage2' => 'Eek! We have rats in our storehouses! We should renovate as soon as possible and chase the rats away. The best thing would be to combine renovation with an increase in storage capacity. The king is sure to ask for this soon anyway.',
        'TutStorage3' => 'Strange... It\'s been a while since we were tasked with expanding our storage capacity. Don\'t you think that\'s a little curious too? Do you believe we should just keep on expanding? Maybe the king expect us to show some initiative.',
        'TutStorage4' => 'So, how are things? Ready for a new task from the king? It seems you never fail to satisfy him. I\'ve never known him to support someone that willingly. Well then, on to dealing with the storage capacity!',
        'TutStorage5' => 'Greetings. It\'s always a pleasure to see you. I just wanted to let you know that the amount of resources suffice, and that everything technical is working fine. However, we could do with better isolation for the storehouses here and there. Would it be possible to upgrade one or two?',
        'TutStorage6' => 'Ah, it\'s good to be home again. I am sorry for not contacting you for so long, but I had a lot of things to discuss with the king. He has also given me a new task for you. It\'s the last one, so he has promised a substantial reward.',
        'TutStorage7' => 'Your city has become really glorious. Now we can slowly begin finishing it off. I\'m thinking particularly of the storehouses - we should align them with the cityscape. The upgrade takes a lot of time and resources, so you\'d better start as soon as possible.',
        'TutStorage8' => 'You\'ve nearly done everything a man can do. The time has come to make your city perfect, and upgrade your mayor\'s house to level 5. It\'s almost unbelievable to see you come this far. I never imagined you would do so well. I am proud of you.',
        'TutSurveyQuest' => 'You should now start your first production. Produce your first resources so they can serve as a base for further production chains.',
        'TutTavern' => 'Military units aren\'t able to go into battle on their own. They need a General to lead them. The General is the second Specialist that you can hire. All Specialists can be hired in the Tavern.
- Create a Tavern.',
        'TutTavernNew' => 'Have you ever been to a tavern? You can meet the most interesting people there. It is also a good place to find people with particular skills, so-called specialists. We should build one so we can hire some.',
        'TutTitanium' => 'Before we can begin manufacturing swords, we need have some titanium in stock. To produce titanium takes quite some time, so you had best begin with soon.',
        'TutTitaniumForge' => 'Oh, has my daughter vanished again? Typical! She\'s never very comfortable when she stays too long in one place, and becomes unreliable. That\'s one reason why I did not want her to join the army. Whatever... Next, we should construct a Titanium smelter.',
        'TutTitaniumWeapon' => 'Best start production immediately. You will be thrilled, because these are the best weapons you can get. With them, we will easily drive all our enemies back.',
        'TutTitaniumWeaponSmith' => 'A carpenter producing carriages? Useless! We need weapon production, not these bits and pieces. For example, we need a Damascene weaponsmith. By now we should have enough titanium ready.',
        'TutToolProductionChainOptimize' => 'So, how is your military establishment going? I have been following your economic growth with much interest. Since you produce swords, did you check your tool production in your economy overview? Maybe some changes are necessary?',
        'TutToolResourceBuff' => 'If you buy something from the merchant, he transfers it to your star menu free of charge. As soon as you have transferred it to your stock we can begin to build.',
        'TutTools' => 'With all the copper and coal available you are now able to produce tools.

- Build 1 copper smelter
- Build 1 toolmaker',
        'TutToolsNew' => 'To produce tools, we need a toolmaker to process copper bars. It would be best to have it built and ready to go as fast as possible.',
        'TutTrade' => 'Have you taken a look at your trades already? You\'ll find them by clicking the scales in the menu list. There, you can offer items or accept offers from other traders. Knock yourself out.',
        'TutTradeWeapons' => 'As you have no doubt already noticed, the production of goods takes a lot of time in the beginning. If you do not have time to wait, you can use trade to acquire the needed items. Either you take an already existing offer, or you make one yourself. Try it out.',
        'TutTreasure' => 'Your explorer reports a friend has told him about a treasure. He would be glad to retrieve it for you, but needs the time to do it. Once you agree, simply check your star menu and send him on short treasure search.',
        'TutUpgrade' => 'You can upgrade your buildings to increase their productivity. 

- Select one of your buildings and click the upgrade button.',
        'TutUpgradeNew' => 'I know you are very busy right now creating an army… Sardin didn\'t even want to let me through to see you… but I have to tell you something about your buildings. You can upgrade them. Try it out.',
        'TutUpgradedBuildings' => 'I have just returned from a visit of the king\'s court. I have to admit, his city looks really beautiful. I think this is mainly because of its harmonious cityscape. You too should try to keep your building upgrades on the same level. It just looks better.',
        'TutUpgradedNobleResidences' => 'Pssst… It\'s me again. I\'m just about to go on a journey to find new adventures. Since I\'m going quite far this time, I might find a new route for your explorer, and more challenging adventures. If I do, you will need more units for them. Maybe you should upgrade your noble residences to claim more settlers?',
        'TutUseBuff' => 'The fish platter can be used to increase the productivity of a workyard temporarily.

- Open star menu
- Use 1 fish platter on a workyard',
        'TutUseBuffNew' => 'Once a buff has finished being produced, it is transferred to your star menu. From there, you can use it on whichever workyard you want. Try it out.',
        'TutUseControls' => 'I have a little suggestion. It is possible to make settling more comfortable using different options. In the top left, below your avatar, you can find certain options, including some to tweak the camera or the sound. You should take a look.',
        'TutUseFishRefill' => 'Excuse me… It\'s me again. You most likely know already, but I just wanted to make sure: you have multiple fish deposits and can refill them, even beyond their original maximum.',
        'TutUseShop' => 'Oh, it looks like your tool stock is decreasing rapidly. For constructing buildings you need a lot of tools. Since we are not yet able to produce them on our own, we should buy some from the merchant.',
        'TutUseSolidSandwich' => 'Ah, I think I know what you\'re up to. You plan to buff all relevant production facilities to get more military resources out of them at the same time. Very clever, I have to admit.',
        'TutVeryLongTreasureSearch' => 'Hey hey! Going on a journey is always so exciting. Remember when I told you about the difficult adventures, and how you can get valuable things from them? I\'ve finally discovered a good route your explorer can use to find them.',
        'TutWarehouse' => 'A new sector has been discovered in the north.
It seems that nobody owns this sector, so you can claim it.

- Build 1 storehouse in a new sector',
        'TutWarehouseNew' => 'It is time to expand your property. Since the explorer has already mapped a new area, all that is left for you to do is claim your new property by building a storehouse in the new sector. After that, you can build in the new sector as you wish.',
        'TutWell' => 'The farmer has already got busy and started harvesting wheat. But to produce bread, we still need water. It can be gathered from wells, but there\'s no need to build them near the farms, as we can get the water from the storehouse.',
        'TutWheatProductionOptimize' => 'The settler in charge of the stables came to see me a while ago and told me the farmers refuse to give him wheat unless they have official confirmation that enough wheat is being produced. Could you please check if there is any way to improve wheat production, and inform the farmers?',
        'TutWheelmaker' => 'Greetings. I have found something very interesting. A friend of mine forgot to take it with him. I thought a carriage like this might be useful, and who knows what use can be made of it. Maybe you should think about producing one yourself. In which case, we\'ll be needing a wheelmaker.',
        'TutWoodChainOptimize' => 'Because you have already made great progress, I will not tell you exactly what to do. I am sure you will make work it out. However, I would advise optimizing your pinewood production.',
        'TutWoodCutter' => 'Welcome, friend!

I will teach you all there is to know about managing your town.
Start your settlement by building a woodcutter to gather some wood.

- Build 1 pinewood cutter',
        'TutWoodCutterNew' => 'I welcome you. My name is Sir Oliver. As you may know, the king has sent me to help you. Accordingly, we should not waste any more time and begin making building material for your settlement. It would be best to start with wood.',
        'TutZoneWideBuffs1' => 'Not all buffs are applied to buildings; some are applied to a whole island!
You can check which of these are currently active by clicking on the golden sparkles in the resource bar at the top of the screen.',
        'TutZoneWideBuffs2' => 'Let\'s try using a zone-wide buff! You can easily identify them in the star menu thanks to their green border. 
Buff your home island with the fairy fire I gave you earlier and observe its effects in the zone-wide buffs window.',
        'TwinTown_AdvDefeatAllCaves' => 'Explore the cave and defeat all the enemies!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_0' => 'Oh my, that really was a long journey! I don\'t think I\'ve ever traveled so far by ship! Maybe not even with the Excelsior... Good thing we have a proper harbor now, though, else this would all have been a lot more troublesome...

Hmm. This land looks somehow familiar, but it feels very different... Like there\'s some kind of dread in the air... Oh well, it\'s probably just my imagination. Let\'s climb this big tree here and use it as a lookout post to check our bearings.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_1' => 'OK! First, we need to rid the village of the immediate threat, and then fight our way through to the Mayor\'s House. If this really is Laeylorn, the people here should be able to help us find out what happened to Kaedric. Defeat the bandits in the town area!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_10' => 'Another pirate attack! Defeat them and protect the village! We\'re at least kind of your brothers and sisters by now, aren\'t we?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_11' => 'To bring the constant pirate attacks to a halt, I think we\'ll need to rebuild the barricades around our village. Being so unprotected seems to make us too easy a target for those pirates. With a proper blockade, we should be able to fend them off for good.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_2' => 'Let\'s take a look around town and see who lives here - or perhaps, who lived here, rather? It does seem awfully quiet.

Visiting the Mayor\'s House would seem to be the most promising approach, seeing as everyone else just slams their doors or runs away as soon as they see us...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_20' => 'You\'ve already helped us a lot, and I am personally going to see that you get any information we have about that missing person you\'re looking for. But on top of that, I have an even better proposal I was hoping to put to you...

Even though we don\'t have much in the way of riches right now, decades ago, when I was a still a small child, Laeylorn was a prosperous city, and one that was famous the world over. Laeylorn was originally just the name of the city, and only later became the name of the island too. That\'s how big Laeylorn once was. It\'s a bit confusing, I know, but there is a good reason for it. Only after the town started to shrink, and people began fleeing the island... Oh, I\'m getting ahead of myself. 

So, my proposal is about twinning our villages, and fraternizing our islands. Your big city, and our tiny village. If we were to do this, I\'m sure that Laeylorn, over time, can become as big and as beautiful as it was a century ago. We\'ll share knowledge and resources. We can also provide you with some of the lost knowledge and wisdom we dig up from Laeylorn, and reward you greatly for all your help. We do still have some treasures left hidden away in our secret caves... I\'m getting ahead of myself again, aren\'t I? So, will you partner up with us?

Excellent! I think a partnering gift would be in order! I\'ll do my best to provide one from the things we still have, and hope to be able to compensate you further in future. But, as you can probably see, we don\'t exactly have all that much at the moment... In return, it would be nice if you could provide us with some basic defense troops, so we aren\'t constantly being hindered in our reconstruction plans. It\'d need to be a pretty sizeable force, though, as I\'m afraid a small one would only suffice to fend off wildlife and uncoordinated bandits... For the bigger attacks, I- ahem, I think I\'m getting ahead of myself. Come visit me when the troops have arrived.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_21' => 'I cannot express how deeply thankful I- no, we ALL are - for you sending across these reinforcements. Now we have these troops protecting us, the pirates will have a much harder job should they attempt to ransack our reconstruction efforts again. However, overall, our defenses are still lacking. Still, first things first. Our food stocks are almost empty, and the people are starving!

Our food reserves have been shrinking faster than we can restock them, but relying on supplies being sent in all the time is too risky, especially in the long-term. Please, help us rebuild a few fields at the edge of the village. This should be far more practical.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_22' => 'It\'s time to clean this place up! Having those ruins everywhere is getting a bit depressing. Please, get rid of them. That should improve the mood of the people, and will also give us more space to expand the town.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_23' => 'It\'s time to bare our teeth to any pirate bandits out there! Lets erect some cannon towers to defend ourselves, and hopefully scare them away! They should know that their strength isn\'t enough to deal with such power!

I hope they give up soon... I guess we\'ll just have to show them that their efforts are futile, and banish them from Laeylorn!

Don\'t forget - I\'ll call for you when another attack is imminent, so you don\'t have to spend all your time here.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_25' => 'Let\'s ask around - maybe the villagers know something? Someone ought to have seen Kaedric... He\'s not a person you could easily forget or overlook. He may have gotten a bit older, but he still has quite the outrageous personality. There\'s a reason why we haven\'t become the best of friends...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_26' => 'Look around the village, and see if you can find any hints about Kaedric\'s visit here.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_27' => 'I guess I\'ll have to confront Ferri now. I don\'t know why he\'s so reluctant to help us, but with the clues we\'ve gathered, it\'s quite clear which direction Kaedric went in. Lets see what Ferri has to say. Could you wait outside the Mayor\'s House this time? I want to clear the air my way. I\'ll be back in a jiffy, I promise.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_28' => 'It seems Ferri wasn\'t underestimating the wilderness out here... Before we can continue our search, we must shoo away those... ahem... beasts?!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_29' => 'Ah, over there! Do you see it? And those! What was he looking at? Oh... I think I see a pattern. Can we collect the tracks and see where he went next?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_3' => 'Welcome to our beautiful country! At least, what\'s left of it. I am the acting mayor of what remains of our once prosperous town. You can call me Ferri. You didn\'t beat those thieves and thugs just to steal what precious few riches we have left, did you?

So, what can I do you for? Ah, I see. So you\'re looking for a specific person? Though I\'m thankful for your help just now, I\'m afraid we do have other priorities to take care of at the minute, so I\'m afraid we can\'t be of much use.

Although, if you could help me with some, er... tasks, perhaps we could come to some sort of agreement? Come with me, and I\'ll explain all.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_30' => 'How curious... This building doesn\'t look abandoned at all? Perhaps the people living here have met Kaedric?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_31' => 'I\'m getting good at this... See these branches? And there - I think those are footprints! These must be some of the ruins Ferri was talking about! But this can\'t be what Kaedric was interested in... It\'s just a ruin? Hmm... Maybe I\'ll check it out. Do you want to do the same? Oh wow, look at these! Such a strong crimson color... I wonder what Kaedric was looking for?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_32' => 'We\'ll have to ask our specialists to craft some very precise dynamite... Else we\'ll not only be getitng rid of the rock, but we\'ll be turning everything nearby into rubble too. Also, I fear we\'ll have to build some kind of special casing to ensure the dynamite doesn\'t get wet on the long journey - or even worse, explode due to the lightning storms. I shudder just thinking about this.

Hopefully Kaedric\'s not just lying behind the mountain in some sort of ditch... Actually, it\'s worth a try. KAAAAAEEEEDRIIIIIC!!!... Nothing. OK, let\'s blow this thing up!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_33' => 'You see the spots in the south eastern part of the village? Those are natural deposits of saltpeter and titanium ore. I\'m happy to leave the decision about which resource to mine up to you, as you probably have a better understanding of the market value and what would be more useful to us in the long run. We\'ll send you your cut weekly. But please, be aware - you cannot change your decision afterwards, and we cannot mine both, as this would destroy the mine. The ground in Laeylorn is a bit, ahem... fragile.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_34' => 'It\'s been a pleasure to see you work - although it is unfortunate you couldn\'t find Kaedric. I hope you find him soon. If we hear anything, I\'ll be sure to contact you and Sonya personally. 

For now, though, we\'ll get to rebuilding our beatiful town as promised. If you find the time before you leave, be sure you stop by for a good meal and a chat, eh?',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_35' => 'Somehow, I\'ve come to enjoy these puzzles and riddles. We should send some specialists to take a closer look at this weird house and its surroundings. These apples are a bit shinier than usual, if I\'m not mistaken. But somehow, there\'s also something a bit... dreadful about them. I\'d love to do the investigation myself, but I\'m afraid I have neither the time nor the expertise. Do you know anyone who\'d be willing to do the job? Oh no... please don\'t tell me you\'re thinking about HIM?! Oh, what have I done... I hope he doesn\'t blow up the whole area.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_4' => 'We desperately need to rebuild the essential buildings on this island. But before we can do that... well, while there\'s all the residence ruins around the village, no-one will be able to focus on their work. That\'s because... I almost don\'t dare to say it... but let\'s just say, there may have to be some burials performed in parallel... Would you please take this burden upon yourself, to remove the ruins and rebuild the residences? Please! I can\'t bear asking the other villagers to do so. They\'ve been through enough.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_5' => 'Do you think you could build us some cemeteries, too, please? Our lost friends deserve a fitting final place of rest. Although the years have strengthened my heart, even I would have a hard time burying our friends... The last attacks were particularly devastating. The invaders were simply trying to blow the town up, it seems. Well, you can see the results for yourself. Not to mention, someone very special to me was among the victims... I simply cannot bring myself to do it.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_6' => 'There\'s still a lot that\'s left to be done, but for now... could I ask you to leave, and give us some space to mourn? We should be safe for some time, but we really need a bit of time to ourselves. Without invaders... or visitors.

But don\'t wait too long to come back - we don\'t know how long it might take for the next enemies to find their way to our island! I\'ll tell you more later.',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_7' => 'Thanks for staying true to your word. As you can see, we are in dire need of your help. Had I anticipated this, I wouldn\'t have sent you home in the first place... Turns out some bandits had been hiding in the forest south of the village all along.

A group of children were playing in the woods when they saw a handful of them scouting the village. They were talking in such a way that we believe they will ambush the village later tonight. Please, help us! Quick!',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_8' => 'A villager just ran into the Main Hall screaming something about a bunch of wild animals marching towards the town from the north. They must have come from the nearby forest. Most likely they\'re looking for food, as the winter isn\'t too far away...',
        'TwinTown_Adv_Chapter1_Sub_9' => 'That damned pirate... We met a few years back, and he swore he\'d get his revenge. It seems now is the time. I guess his pland is to send wave after wave of pirates - and any other creatures they\'ve gathered along the way - at us, just to deal as much damage as possible, before he even dares set foot on the island. Please, I beg you, protect us! If it were just some random bandits we could stand our ground, but we don\'t stand a chance against trained pirates with such bloodlust in their eyes!',
        'TwinTown_El_Chupacabra_Tracks' => 'Now, here Kaedric definitely wouldn\'t have been able to disguise himself... Not sure if some of his skills from his years as a young thief helped him out here, or if he\'s found some other way to pass through such a dangerous place unharmed.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main1' => 'I have some big favors to ask... But they will bring us new quests and adventures!

I have a feeling this might become the most difficult endeavor we have ever embarked upon...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2' => 'I haven\'t heard anything from Kaedric for quite some time... I fear the worst. He would have given us a sign of life if he had the chance. He\'s not the kind to unnecessarily worry others... We must continue our search!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_1' => 'Let us send out more explorers, and task them with performing an undercover search for my mentor, Kaedric. I hope we can learn more soon... But this time, we have to broaden our search radius, and ask even on the farthest outskirts of our reach.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_10' => 'Now he\'s gone off in a completely different direction... Kaedric sure has travelled a lot these past few months. I wonder if he\'s still on the move, or if he was able to draw some conclusions....',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_11' => 'OK. For now, this is the last item on Kaedric\'s list. But I doubt this was actually his last stop.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_2' => 'Kaedric always loved to visit the different mines and excavations on our island, to see if anything unexpected had been dug up. Maybe we don\'t have to look that far? Perhaps there\'s something useful a bit closer than we thought!

Ask your specialists to take a look at the deposits Kaedric visited last. Maybe they could find a hint as to where we should continue our search.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_3' => 'Let us travel to Laeylorn again. We have to find a clue as to where to look next. If Ferri cannot help us, we\'ll have to take matters into our own hands. I cannot wait any longer!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_4' => 'It\'s strange. Some people looked like they might know something, but then they all send us to the mayor, who just says he\'s still investigating and doesn\'t have the time to look into it right now. Something\'s not right. But after this - let us call it "success" - on Laeylorn, I wonder what we can find if we start asking around right here?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_5' => 'With yours and Ferris\' permission, I would like to take a closer look around Laeylorn myself. I know it\'s risky, but I promise, I\'ll be careful. Oh yeah, sure - you can come with me! Let\'s see what we can find!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_6' => 'Whatever\'s below Laeylorn, it is most definitely scary. We should send resources, weapons and troops to Laeylorn so we can explore this cave. Did Ferri know about this? I\'d assume he\'d have told us about it if he did? Not sure why he\'d want to keep something like this a secret...

At some point, we\'ll have to build a proper outpost on Laeylorn to decrease the cost of these endeavors. For now, let\'s stash some equipment over there, so we can restock our troops after battles.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_7' => 'Now that we\'re fully prepared for this huge endeavor, let\'s head out. I can\'t wait to explore that huge cave! What are we going to find there? Is Kaedric down there, waiting for help?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_8' => 'This is the first item on our list, and we shouldn\'t wait too long to tick it off. Still, it\'s not too far away, so it shouldn\'t pose too big a problem. Hopefully, we\'ll start to better understand what Kaedric was doing, as we follow his steps through this adventure.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main2_Sub_9' => 'It\'s getting darker and more dangerous with every step we tread following Kaedric\'s footprints. What did he want here? Maybe he was following someone. That would make sense. Maybe someone from Laeylorn was here?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3' => 'It\'s time to show we\'re serious about twinning our town with Laeylorn for the prosperity of both our islands. It won\'t be long till our help is direly needed.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_1' => 'The pirates are attacking again! Please send troops to defeat them, and chase them off the island.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_1_Starter2' => 'I knew they\'d come sooner rather than later. That damned pirate leader! If I ever get my hand on him, he will pay for all the misfortune he\'s brought us!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_2' => 'Some of those mischievous pirates have stolen our most treasured secrets! Please, help us reclaim what\'s rightfully ours! As partners, you\'ll give me your word you won\'t steal them either, right? Those sealed texts will stay sealed?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_3' => 'Send a bigger army to ensure the safety of Laeylorn, and reinforce your bond with us as your partner town. The people of Laeylorn are still under constant threat. Our children haven\'t slept a night through for months. Put an end to this. It won\'t keep the island safe forever, but at least it\'ll provide the village with a breather, and a good foundation for further endeavors.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main3_Sub_4' => 'With all the adventuring and fighting that\'s been going on recently, you should be sure to help your twin town too! After all, an investment in Laeylorn is an investment in your future too!
You should decide between a Saltpeter Mine or a Titanium Mine!

Let me explain. Since we\'re now able to take care of most of our own basic needs, it feels like it\'s time to see if we can bring Laeylorn\'s economy back to its feet. But as space is limited, you\'ll have to choose what you want to build on Laeylorn carefully, as in turn, it\'ll determine your payoffs! I can only ship things over to you that you helped us to produce in the first place.
So, to get started, you should decide if you\'d rather mine for saltpeter, or titanium. You cannot mine both! Once you\'ve prepared the materials, come on over to Laeylorn, find the construction site, and get building! It\'ll pay off soon!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Main4' => 'Bid your farewell to Laeylorn for now and give your regards to Ferri Felder.

Finishing this quest concludes the first chapter of the Twin Town Quests.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Start_1' => 'An old acquaintance of mine asked us to come see him in the tavern, which is very unusual. Normally, he\'d just visit me at the Excelsior. This time, he even sent the invite using a stranger as a messenger, instead of just posting a letter or dropping by himself. Of course, I\'m curious to hear what he has to say. Let me know when you\'re ready, and we\'ll head over.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_1' => 'OK... This isn\'t funny. Where is he? And why did he leave such a strange message with the barman?

"Need help. Laeylorn. Don\'t tell anyone. Life and Death!"

Do you know any Laeylorn? Is it a person, or something? Hmm... I guess it might be a place, but if it is, I\'ve never heard of it... This time, I have to ask a personal favor. The acquaintance I talked about is Kaedric, my former mentor in the Explorers\' Guild. Although we don\'t like each other personally, we\'ve always respected each other for our skills, and tried to keep in contact. He helped me out during several adventures with the Excelsior, and I returned the favor. I wonder what kind of mess that old grumbler\'s got himself into this time?

I guess we\'ll have to cast the net wide if we want to find out more about this "Laaeeyyloorrnn".',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_10' => 'Our advisers have insisted on some more stuff. On the plus side, they did promise that this would be their final set of recommendations.

If we pack what they\'ve suggested to keep the crews healthy and well entertained, it can\'t hurt, can it? We do want to avoid a mutiny midway through, after all... Oh, and just in case - to ensure we don\'t get destroyed by a thunderstorm, your specialists want to install some earthing wires. Although I don\'t understand how that\'ll work if we\'re on water...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_11' => 'Let\'s prepare a few support points on the way towards Laeylorn. You can choose where to set them up. It can\'t hurt to have a few extra provisions and some additional troops prepared in case we need reinforcements, get chased by foes, or suffer a shipwreck and get washed ashore!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_12' => 'For today, let us take counsel with our pillows and then head out no later then tomorrow. I don\'t really want to delay things for another night either, but in the end, I agree with our advisers. It\'s better not to rush into anything just now. Have a good night\'s rest, and see you tomorrow at the harbor as early as the birds!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_13' => 'Without further ado, let\'s get started! Oh, wait! I almost forgot! I had a dream last night about running away from some unidentifiable beast - but no matter how hard I tried, I just couldn\'t get away. So, it got me thinking... Let\'s produce some horseshoes for our trip, just in case it was a vision, and we find ourselves having to make haste. I also have the feeling we may need to upgrade some of our military equipment. Just trust me on this - I almost never ask favors based on my gut, but this one isn\'t going to let me rest...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_14' => 'OK, this is important! Ferri asked us to grant his people some time to mourn their lost ones. But we should be doing this more in general. Taking a break, I mean. Let\'s be sure we take a little time off every now and then, OK? 

I just want to be sure you\'re aware, we can return any time we want . Our progress on Laeylorn will be kept, as long as we fully complete any tasks before we leave. If we abort a mission part-way through, any efforts we made will probably be for naught. 
After aborting, or in other words, deferring the adventure, you\'ll be sent a mail. This way you can always go back to Laeylorn, almost like magic.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_15' => 'We need to send some basic defense troops over to Laeylorn, so they aren\'t wiped while we\'re not there. But first, we need some volunteers!

This will be the first act of twinning our two towns, bringing some hope to the people of Laeylorn... at the cost of some resources of ours.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_16' => 'OK! Now that we\'ve trained the volunteers, we just need to wait for them to arrive on Laeylorn. Ugh, how I hate all this waiting. Be sure to return to Laeylorn afterwards, and check everything\'s all in order over there. Are you getting used to all these voyages over seas now?
It seems every time we go, something new happens. Remember the time that big thing attacked us? Oh wow, that was something, hahaha...',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_17' => 'We received notice that someone snuck into the food reserves on Laeylorn and stole more than half of it. The people on Laeylorn didn\'t have many supplies left anyway... And we need to provide our troops over there with sufficient supplies too!

We should send some guides to teach the people how to build temporary shelters, so those who are still hiding outside the village at least don\'t freeze to death or catch and spread diseases. With everything that gets consumed, lost or rots on the long journey to Laeylorn, there are always huge amounts we have to send. And then you\'ve got to plan for the return trip - or do you want to leave the crews stranded over there?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_2' => 'We\'re going to need a huge amount of materials and provisions if we\'re going to make it to Laeylorn. There\'s a chance we might need slightly less once we\'ve finalized the route and all, but for now, let\'s be better safe than sorry.

Let\'s start by building several ships to take us there. I don\'t want place an unnecessary toll on our settlers, so please be sure to not take any resources from our reserves, OK?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_3' => 'Please prepare some additional defenses to guard the island. We want to be sure we avoid any... unpleasant issues while we\'re travelling. A mixed group of units should improve the island\'s security sufficiently. We\'ll order them to patrol the island.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_4' => 'I know I\'m asking a lot of you, but this journey might end up being longer than we anticipate - and I really don\'t want to see any starving sailors. Just don\'t forget to cure the meat!

Good thing we finally have a proper harbor. Without it, this whole undertaking would be impossible. We\'d never manage to load all these ships!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_5' => 'Let\'s check that everything is in order here before we travel. Give the logistics and appearance of our beloved home a quick once-over. There might be a few things we should improve before we set out!',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_6' => 'Here\'s a short list of extra resources this endeavor will require. Tools, obviously, to repair anything that breaks once we\'re under way.

Coins, in case we have to trade for more provisions. Horses, to make travel on land much easier in case we have to go cross-country. Hmm... Are we forgetting anything?',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_7' => 'OK! Let\'s put ourselves to the test, and see if we\'ve remembered everything we need. Treat it as a final rehearsal.',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_8' => 'I talked to several of our specialists, and made them our official advisers for this adventure. They came up with a whole list of other items they thought we\'d require. Well, needless to say, I declined our generals\' request to bring along a bunch of spare weapons - we\'re not setting out to fight a war! But, well, some requests seem reasonable enough.

Coal to keep us warm; water in case we can\'t find sufficient freshwater springs along the way; sausages, as they take a while to go off; and paper, which apparently has tons of uses I\'d never thought of, from taking notes to drawing maps, up to handing out information to anyone we meet, or even sending messages. I hope that\'s the last of the preparations though - I just want to head out! Right now! *sigh*',
        'TwinTown_Home_Chapter1_Sub_9' => 'We should make sure our production chains are all in optimal condition, just in case we need to replenish our supplies in a hurry. It wouldn\'t hurt to pay our friends a visit, too. We might need to ask for their help.

Oh, and make sure our miners don\'t run out of work until we return!',
        'TwinTown_Outlaws_Tracks' => 'Oh, this looks dangerous... The air almost reeks of thievery and death up ahead. Kaedric was only able to investigate all these places thanks to his special abilities. He could be really sneaky if he wanted to... Us, on the other hand? We\'re just going to have to fight our way through, even if we do scout the area before we head in. It\'s the only way we\'ll get to take a closer look at the tracks Kaedric left for us.',
        'TwinTown_RoaringBull_Tracks' => 'Seriously, how did Kaedric actually manage to move amongst these cultists without being found out and torn to shreds? His skills must have come a long way since the last time I saw him - which is saying something, considering his age.',
        'TwinTown_TheHeroicLittleTailor_Tracks' => 'I\'d say it\'s business as usual. Let\'s follow Kaedric\'s tracks, and see what we can find.',
        'Unity_Final' => 'Mr. Foozler left a note behind. It reads

"Dear Mayor... Apologies for any trouble I may or may not have caused you.
Go ahead and try the Zone Refresher. You won\'t regret it.

Yours truly, DF"',
        'Unity_Main' => 'An emissary of the King is coming.

He states that his mission is to audit the inner workings of your island, to help you make the necessary changes to survive these troubling times - and every other challenge the world can throw at you.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1' => 'Greetings! My name is Dunning Foozler. I\'m an envoy of the King, and have been sent here to oversee your settlement and make sure everything is in agreement with our regulations - and that you have everything you need to succeed in future.

But first things first, I need you to find me a proper place to stay and set up my equipment.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub1' => 'I have been told that your hospitality is legendary. If you please, I\'d like to stay at your very best.',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub2' => 'Ah! I know what\'s wrong. The location you chose is not conducive to a properly productive environment.

Let\'s find a better spot, shall we?',
        'Unity_Main_Part1_Sub3' => 'My luggage hasn\'t been taken to my lodgings. I need my equipment so I can set up my office before I can start working. Would you kindly...?',
        'Unity_Main_Part2' => 'First in the docket, I have this new formula for a... um... "fauna performance enhancer". Yes, that\'s what it says here.

In theory, this beauty should dramatically increase game meat available for settlers.

But first, we need to gather the resources needed to develop it. These need to be fresh - stored goods lack the necessary potency.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub1' => 'To begin with, we need to study the nature of the local fauna. 

Let\'s start with learning about the piscine variety.

For this task, I\'ll need you to bring me some recently captured aquatic wildlife.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub2' => 'That\'s the fish dealt with - now we need to focus our efforts on understanding land-based creatures.

We\'ll need to examine your own livestock, as well as the wild creatures that dwell in the woods.',
        'Unity_Main_Part2_Sub3' => 'Here - my concoction for improving the yield of your livestock is ready.

I guarantee it is completely safe to use, and the results will more than make up for your troubles.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3' => 'After the last... um... "incident", I\'ve come to the conclusion that it\'d be safer if we conducted our tests somewhere a bit more out of the way. At least, until my formulas are stable.

WHICH THEY SHOULD BE! 

My calculations are well known for their precision. So I\'ve been told.

Happily, I happened to stumble upon the coordinates for this nearby deserted island, which will serve as a perfectly safe test site.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub1' => 'To get to the island, we\'ll need to build a ship. And to build a ship, we need wood. And lots of it.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub2' => 'Now, we\'ll need some nails to... Er... nail all those planks together into something that resembles a ship.

Iron is the best material for the task ahead.

Again, it needs to be freshly mined iron. Rusty old stock just won\'t make the cut.',
        'Unity_Main_Part3_Sub3' => 'Now we just need to deliver all the produced materials to the nearest shipyard, so we can start building your first ship.',
        'Unity_Main_Part4' => 'Use the ticket I gave you earlier. Onward, to the island!

I\'m quivering with anxiety just thinking about the discoveries we\'ll be able to make once we get there.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5' => 'Like I said before - I\'ve had an epiphany.

I believe I\'ve devised a formula for a buff that will dramatically increase your production output.

This time, it\'s also completely free of unwanted side effects.

The numbers don\'t lie!',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub1' => 'Minerals are essential for proper nutrition. And nutrition is an important part of my elixirs.

Please, could you provide me with the minerals in this list?',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub2' => 'The second most important ingredient is a type of vegetable protein, easily extractable from the grain you produce locally.

I don\'t want to frighten you with big words. The key point is that we need copious amounts of grain.',
        'Unity_Main_Part5_Sub3' => 'I will now provide you with clear instructions on how to properly administer the elixir.

Would you kindly provide me with a pen and paper?',
        'Unity_Main_Part6' => 'The moment of truth is upon us! Go forth and use your new buff to usher in a new era of unprecedented productivity.

We should be proud of what we are about to achieve.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7' => 'These documents contain the final formula. I took the liberty of adding a little extra to put off the fires and make up for what has been lost.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub1' => 'Unsurprisingly, the key ingredient for the formula is water. Lots and lots of fresh water.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub2' => 'Let us not take any chances this time. We will proceed by doing controlled tests.

First up is livestock.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub3' => 'The initial tests went very well. No side effects, and the animals look even more lively than before.

For the next step, I\'ll need the exact goods listed here in this paper.',
        'Unity_Main_Part7_Sub4' => 'I\'m done with dinner, so now I will proceed to test the elixir with some human testing.

For that, I will need some desperate souls... I mean, brave volunteers.

If all goes according to plan, I will return to you with a final batch of elixir shortly.',
        'Unity_Main_Reach20' => 'Get your island ready for the arrival of the auditor.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1' => 'Exotic Wood\'s resilience may be legendary, but it has met its match in the amazing durability of titanium-built blades. Using titanium as a material for tools has allowed us to use hardwood processing equipment to manufacture exotic wood planks.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p1' => 'The incredibly complex manufacturing process for exotic wood planks is only made possible by the skill and dedication of the men working the logs.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p2' => 'While we prepare the tools, the schematics will have to be guarded. Employing a bunch of soldiers and making sure they\'re paid enough to keep them bribe-free sounds like a plan.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank1_p3' => 'These tools are the embodiment of the most cutting-edge technology we have achieved so far. Built from the finest materials, used by our finest workmen they will deliver the coveted exotic planks at tremendous speed.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2' => 'The titanium blades are excellent for cutting exotic wood into planks, but the process was throttled by the exhausting task of polishing the planks to create a usable surface. Using Magic Beans, yet again, has allowed us to power automated polishers to amazing speeds and thus, enhance an already great production line even further.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p1' => 'The science guild will not start researching this incredible innovation until they know you\'re completely committed to Exotic Wood processing.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p2' => 'The building schematics for these tools are so complex that the Science Guild has actually requested additional paper and nibs so that they can finally complete them.',
        'UnlockEW_ExWoodToExPlankRank2_p3' => 'The sacrifices we made were well worth it - the final stage of constructing these incredible machines is to gather the materials required to build and power them.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1' => 'Granite has the best heat resistance of all the known materials we have. This has led our scientists to come up with the idea of using it to build coking ovens that can stand the constant heat of the near-automated coking process in the Epic Woodyard, while processing coal out of hardwood.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1_p1' => 'The granite ovens will have to be built on-site as they are too heavy to carry around. Their extremely thick walls have to be built up high, which will require some elaborate scaffolding.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank1_p2' => 'Stone, dust and water - basic building mortar - when pressed between extremely heavy granite blocks, becomes a part of the structure, holding everything in place.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2' => 'Using Magic Beans as a power source is nothing new - but using this power directly as heat is an innovation. The heat resulting from channeling a Magic Bean mixture\'s blast is enough to transform hardwood into coal at incredible speed.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2_p1' => 'Carefully mixing ground Magic Beans and common flour has yielded a mixture which, when exposed to flame, unleashes a powerful high-temperature blast.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToCoalRank2_p2' => 'The Coking Ovens, even when built from granite, are severely weakened by the blast waves of this coking process. Titanium bracing has been deemed necessary if we are to keep them working.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2' => 'A new generation of jointers is required to handle the intensity of the automated hardwood processing system. Steel blades are much more effective than the Iron ones that were previously used on manual processing.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2_p1' => 'Assembling a team of crack professionals will be the key to our success. We won\'t be able to get this done without the right people.
Unfortunately, that means spending some coin to attract the finest in the land.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank2_p2' => 'Building the actual joiners will require high quality materials that can stand the stress of the process.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3' => 'By imbuing Magic Bean extract into the metal, our scientists have been able to manufacture sawblades that require no additional power source and just keep spinning in place, powered by their own momentum. 
This will greatly reduce the space requirements for the sawmill and will allow many more sawblades to be installed, multiplying its already impressive output.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p1' => 'The energy produced by the magic beans reaction will need to be contained. We have to build an enclosure strong enough to withstand their heat, but light enough that men can carry it. Any beans that are left over will be returned to us.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p2' => 'The beans have to be mixed with 100 parts water, and carefully grinded with a granite mortar and pestle - the only thing that can safely contain the mixture.',
        'UnlockEW_HardwoodToHWPlanksRank3_p3' => 'Steel core sawblades with titanium tips - a splendid target for our scientist\'s "Animation Mixture".',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2' => 'Hardwood is a demanding plant to grow. However, within the Epic Woodyard, a system of circulating steam, raised beds and automatic tillers allow for great amounts of Hardwood saplings to be grown in a single batch, equaling and surpassing all but the best hardwood foresters we have to-date.',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p1' => 'We\'ll need to establish a good seed base first, if we are to proceed with this research. We need our supplies to be of the absolute top quality and can settle for nothing less.',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p2' => 'A complex set of steam pipes, that can deliver the necessary amount of heat and water to the seedlings, will need to be set-up before we move on with the construction.',
        'UnlockEW_SeedToHardwoodRank2_p3' => 'The final step is to build the raised beds and the complex mechanism that will automatically till the earth and plant the seeds. It\'s going to take a lot of skill to get this done - and all while the pipes are leaking all over the place!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2' => 'Besides being an excellent material for ornaments and fancy buildings, marble has some interesting properties that allow for some superior furnaces to be built from it. These furnaces are able to withstand the temperatures needed to coke Pinewood logs at incredible speed.
Our scientists are eager to implement them in our Epic Woodyard, should you provide resources for the prototypes.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2_p1' => 'To start the production for these ovens, one must first gather the necessary items and knowledge. While the tools we need may be found locally, the marble masonry work will require the finest masons on the island.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank2_p2' => 'The furnaces will be both a marvel of technology and a work of art, each and every one of them.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3' => 'Magic Beans, Water and Pinewood Planks are the ingredients used in a very complex reaction that, once started, will provide an inextinguishable, high-temperature fire that will coke entire Pinewood logs almost instantly.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3_p1' => 'The reaction needed to power this new type of coking will need to take place in a well contained area. The only design we\'ve found that\'s capable of withstanding such a reaction is made of granite, with steel reinforcements. As usual, anything we have left over after construction will be delivered to the storehouse.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToCoalRank3_p2' => 'Time to fuel that furnace and strike the first spark. Let\'s keep our fingers crossed!',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2' => 'Using a special type of saw blades, made with a heavy, compact bronze core and replaceable iron cutting edges, the Epic Woodyard can produce Pinewood Planks at a remarkable pace.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2_p1' => 'The operators of this particular shop can only be recruited from the most technologically advanced Sawmills we have.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank2_p2' => 'Here are the materials we\'ll need to complete the prototype, together with the first batch of blades.  If there\'s any excess material, it will be returned to our storehouse.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3' => 'Magic Beans have been successfully tested as a power source, amongst their other amazing properties. 
The Science Guild believes that, with the proper resources, they will be able to produce a saw blade that can spin in perpetuity. The application of this invention in pinewood processing will provide huge improvements over any current method.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3_p1' => 'Transporting the Magic Beans to the Woodyard will require some special equipment. For such a small batch, a secure steel case should suffice.',
        'UnlockEW_WoodToPlankRank3_p2' => 'The construction of the actual sawblades will require a large batch of pure Iron. Accelerating the blades to the point where they\'ll never stop will require us to feed them some planks.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialArchive' => 'First, let\'s take a look at how you might be able to help me get my beloved back. Have a flick through the archive, I´ve added some lovely notes there.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialEnding' => 'Please, don\'t give up! Carry on spreading the love as much as you can, so that my love can come back to me! I believe in you! And of course, your effort will be rewarded...

I can just see it now. When my love comes back, I will jump into their arms, kiss and cuddle them, and never let go.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerBouquet' => 'All these beautiful blossoms can be used to produce a wide range of things - but perhaps none as romantic as flower bouquets. Feel free to charm your friends and loved ones with the fruits of your wares, and make your friends\' islands overflow with joy and love. As a happy side effect, it\'ll also help the scent of my flowers spread across thousands of islands, and hopefully, reach my darling´s button nose.

Still, I have yet to hear anything from my love -  and none of my darling\'s comrades or friends could tell me anything, either. Truth be told, I\'m really starting to worry now. I know it\'s still early days, but I just can´t help it. Please, hurry. And let your friends know we need their help too!',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerFarm' => 'To ensure that at least a few flowers reach my love, and their scent can guide my sweet back to me, we need to produce an immense amount of flowers, and send them throughout the world.

If you can, please plant three flower farms on your island, so that the flowers can blossom en masse.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialFlowerSeed' => 'Oh, my dear friend... I´m afraid it won\'t be enough to only produce one batch of flowers.

The unique scent of my blossoms comes from the manifold mixture of flower seeds, which have been gathered from many different islands and regions around the world. Please, help me gather them, and sow them on your flower farms. I´ll oversee the process, and make sure we create a bloom you can smell for miles.

To help you get started, I\'ve put a pack of flower seeds in your Star Menu. Just apply these on a Flower Farm.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialMain' => 'Oh, hey cutie! I\'ve been on this island for years now, but I don\'t think we\'ve met? My name\'s Flora. I\'m the one who\'s been growing, cutting and arranging those lovely flowerbeds all over town. I\'ve actually got a pretty big request for you - hope you\'re not the type to immediately roll your eyes when you hear stories about love and romance!

I\'m here to open my heart to you. My sweetheart fights in your army. They have yet to return from their last mission, but I have no reason to believe they didn\'t make it. Truth is, my love tends to have a bit of a hazy memory. Sometimes, they even forget how to get back home. I love them very much... but now, just before Valentine´s Day, I fear they might not find their way back in time. Usually, my precious carries a love letter doused with the scent of my flowers, which usually jump-starts their memory... However, I fear it might have been destroyed during battle.

So, would you be willing to be my savior, and help bring my beloved back for Valentine´s Day? My idea is to send flowers across the ocean, so my baby-cakes can smell my flowers again. I´ll talk you through my idea, step by step.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialReach16' => 'Hey, you! I\'m sorry, my dear - I\'m afraid I don´t have much time. First, we need to make sure you have enough influence to be able to help me. 

Please, come visit me as soon as possible, when you\'ve been able to expand your reach.',
        'Valentines2019plus_TutorialValentineCard' => 'It might be far-fetched, but I´d like to ask you another favor - even if it is slightly clutching at straws... If a flower´s fragrance can\'t cross the oceans intact, perhaps my words of love will. I have a few old love letters my sweetheart and I sent each other. Perhaps sending parts of these oaths of love around will get through to my dearest.

Even if it doesn\'t, sharing the love should boost the growth of flowers on your friends islands as well, as my flowers are fertilized by love. Don´t laugh!',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Main' => 'Oh… this is exciting!  A practice match against the Knight of Crowrock and his entourage. Here we can figure out how to play this match. Luckily for us, they are also new to this sport. While most of their players are rookies, people say the team has some decent midfielders. So let’s see what we can do here.

Remember, to win the match, you\'ll need to use different tactical tools, which you can produce in the Provision House.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Main1' => 'Let’s begin! Your goal is to defeat all your opponents. To achieve this, you should first make yourself aware of each opposing player’s skills. Only then you will know what you\'ll have to do to defeat them. Each opponent has his own weak spot. To see which skills the player has, simply click on him. Once you have figured out their skills, you can apply the tactical items that counter them.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Main1_old' => 'Let\'s try and figure out how to defeat the enemy team. This set of tasks should help us get on the right tracks.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub1' => 'Let’s begin! Your goal is to defeat all your opponents. To achieve this, you should first make yourself aware of each opposing player’s skills. Only then you will know what you\'ll have to do to defeat them. Each opponent has his own weak spot. To see which skills the player has, simply click on him.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub2' => 'Now that you know how to stop the opposing team, we should try winning that match. Defeat each remaining opponent individually. But be aware that you will need to use different means to defeat each of them.',
        'WMEventAdvQ1Sub3' => 'Midfielders are either especially skillful at dribbling, with impressive speed, or are more defensive oriented players. It\'s a versatile role, to say the least. Here we have a player who\'s a really good dribbler. To separate him from the ball, use the Tackle. Your opponent will lose his balance, and before he knows what happened, you\'re off with the ball!',
        'WMEventAdvQ2' => 'So, this will be our first real match. Our opponent is the barony of Tepidwater. Similar to us, they haven\'t played many matches yet. Folks say the barony is playing a very offensive 4-3-3 system. We should be especially aware of their midfielders, but at the same time watch out for their three strikers. The baron of Tepidwater has some strong players in his team.',
        'WMEventAdvQ2Sub1' => 'Sometimes you can eliminate an opponent using only a single tactic item. If you take a look at the Tepidwater goalkeeper, you will see that he has both the “High Jumper” and “Fast Reflexes” skills. Both can be countered with a Penalty Kick.

If a tactic item can be used against several skills, it will always affect them in a certain order, as shown in the tactic item’s tooltip. Watch how the skill “High Jumper” gets removed first, followed by “Fast Reflexes”.',
        'WMEventAdvQ3' => 'Here comes the next match of the group stage. Today our opponent will be the Barony of Emberstream. The guys from Emberstream are a very defensive team with a strong defensive squad. If we want to make it to their goal, we\'ll need a plan.',
        'WMEventAdvQ4' => 'Now it\'s getting serious. Our first knock-out match, against the Shire of Oxwater. During the group stage they showed skill in attacking, while maintaining a stabile defence. They play in a 4-2-4 system – that means with four set strikers.',
        'WMEventAdvQ4Sub1' => 'Sometimes you can deal with an opponent while using only a single tactic item. If you take a look at the Tepidwater goalkeeper, you will see that he has both the “High Jumper” and “Fast Reflexes” skills. Both can be countered with a penalty kick.

If a tactic item can be used against several skills, it will always affect them in a certain order, as shown in the tactic item’s tooltip. Watch how the skill “High Jumper” gets removed first, followed by “Fast Reflexes”.',
        'WMEventAdvQ5' => 'In the quarter finals, we will play the Electorate of Sunflower Grove. They\'ve certainly earned their place amongst the last eight teams in the tournament. Similar to our former opponent they play with a strong attacking squad, although their midfield is a little more balanced. This will be a tough enemy.',
        'WMEventAdvQ6' => 'The semi-finals… what a wonderful day. If you\'d have told me at the beginning of the tournament that we would make it this far, I wouldn’t have believed you. But here we are, up against the grand Duchy of Darkwood. What do you need to know about this opponent? They stand closely staggered in a 1-4-1-4 system and have many strong players.',
        'WMEventAdvQ7' => 'Can you feel it? The air is filled with a mixture of tension, anticipation, and energy… it’s the day of the finals. Our opponent is the Kingdom of Dragonhead. They were always one of the best teams in the tournament, but they\'ll soon be second best! All players in this team are strong, and they are confident to boot. But they\'ve never played us. Go out on the field and show them what we\'re made of!',
        'WM_Main' => 'Did you hear? The Settlers Football Championship is coming up again! Counties and kingdoms from all over the continent will be taking part - and we should too, to gain glory and honour for our kingdom. There are prizes to be won, too! By trading the footballs we gather through quests and activities, we could win some amazing stuff! Let me explain how it all works!

Finish all introduction quests in order to participate in the tournament.',
        'WM_Main02' => 'The tournament has started. To win the Settlers‘ World championship we have to win 6 matches in a row. Just remember to regularly check the World Championship fixture list. There you can find your next opponents by opening the green doors.',
        'WM_Sub01' => 'To be allowed to participate in the World Championship, all parties need to be at least level 16.',
        'WM_Sub02' => 'Now the first step. To get information about the World Championship, open the Event Window. You can reach it via the options panel, which is right beneath your avatar picture',
        'WM_Sub03' => 'Did you notice the football-button next to your avatar picture? Using it opens the championship fixture list. This is the main port of call for you during the tournament. Every day, you can open a new door and get a reward.
Green doors contain your next tournament opponent, brown doors hold a nice present for you, and trophy doors contain a special thank you. However, you can only open a trophy door if you managed to open every door that came before it. By the way, you can open green doors at any time after the day they unlock.',
        'WM_Sub04' => 'Green doors contain your next tournament opponent, brown doors hold a nice present for you, and trophy doors contain a special thank you. However, you can only open a trophy door if you managed to open every door that came before it. By the way, you can open green doors at any time after the day they unlock.',
        'WM_Sub05' => 'In order to produce tactic items, for example, the Red Card in the Provision House, you\'ll need to use different resources. There are several different ways to get these.  For example, we can find some items on our home island, we can get them by doing daily quests, or we can send our Explorers to search for them. Let\'s try the different methods.',
        'WM_Sub05a' => 'At the moment, all our Settlers are literally crazy about football. As they aren\'t the tidiest bunch, it\'s actually possible to find some items by simply collecting the things these football maniacs have left behind.',
        'WM_Sub05b' => 'To find some more exotic items, you can send your Scout to, er, scout. He\'ll observe the other teams, and return with interesting items, so we can improve our own tactics.',
        'WM_Sub06' => 'Now that we have collected enough resources, we should start to transform those into tactics we can use on the playing field. Go to your Provision House and order a Foul. We are going to need it to defeat their midfielder.

Hint: If you have a Rarity Provision House, you can produce the same items there much faster.',
        'WM_Sub07' => 'Finish the practice match against the Knight of Crowrock.',
        'WM_Sub08' => 'So, this will be our first real match. Our opponent is the barony of Tepidwater. Similar to us, they haven\'t played many matches yet. Folks say the barony is playing a very offensive 4-3-3 system. We should be especially aware of their midfielders, but at the same time watch out for their three strikers. The baron of Tepidwater has some strong players in his team.',
        'WM_Sub09' => 'Here comes the next match of the group stage. Today our opponent will be the Barony of Emberstream. The guys from Emberstream are a very defensive team with a strong defensive squad. If we want to make it to their goal, we\'ll need a plan.',
        'WM_Sub10' => 'Now it\'s getting serious. Our first knock-out match, against the Shire of Oxwater. During the group stage they showed skill in attacking, while maintaining a stabile defence. They play in a 4-2-4 system – that means with four set strikers.',
        'WM_Sub11' => 'In the quarter finals, we will play the Electorate of Sunflower Grove. They\'ve certainly earnt their place amongst the last eight teams in the tournament. Similar to our former opponent they play with a strong attacking squad, although their midfield is a little more balanced. This will be a tough enemy.',
        'WM_Sub12' => 'Semi-finals… what a wonderful day. If you\'d have told me at the beginning of the tournament that we would make it this far, I wouldn’t have believed you. But here we are, up against the grand Duchy of Darkwood. What do you need to know about this opponent? They stand closely staggered in a 1-4-1-4 system and have many strong players.',
        'WM_Sub13' => 'Can you feel it? The air is filled with a mixture of tension, anticipation, and energy… it’s the day of the finals. Our opponent is the Kingdom of Dragonhead. They were always one of the best teams in the tournament, but they\'ll soon be second best! All players in this team are strong, and they are confident to boot. But they\'ve never played us. Go out on the field and show them what we\'re made of!',
