        'ChangeSkin_christmas_mayorhouse_long' => 'Changes your Mayor\'s House into a playful Christmas variant.',
        'ChangeSkin_default_market_long' => 'Changes a Christmas Market to a normal market.',
        'ChangeSkin_evil_mayourhouse_long' => 'Changes your Mayor\'s House into a sinister looking variant. Only for true villains!',
        'ChangeSkin_lvl1_mayourhouse_long' => 'Gives your Mayor\'s House the nostalgic look of a level 1 Mayor\'s House.',
        'ChangeSkin_lvl2_mayourhouse_long' => 'Gives your Mayor\'s House the nostalgic look of a level 2 Mayor\'s House.',
        'ChangeSkin_mediterranean_mayourhouse_blue_long' => 'Changes your Mayor\'s House into a noble blue variant.',
        'ChangeSkin_mediterranean_mayourhouse_red_long' => 'Changes your Mayor\'s House into a noble red variant.',
        'ChimneysweepsBag' => 'The Union of Left-handed Chimneysweepers has gathered noteworthy amounts of heating remnants from their clients\' chimneys. Despite seeming somewhat dubious, the Union assures that this is common practice and in the client\'s best interest. They are now offering people the opportunity to buy coal in neatly pre-packed portions.',
        'ChocolateDepot' => 'A storehouse commissioned by the same person who owns the Chocolatier. He seems to have quite a sweet tooth.',
        'ChristmasAThousandSnowflakes' => 'Opening this magical little bag from Santa Claus will summon a snowstorm that will cover your island with a blanket of snow!',
        'ChristmasBreweryBuff' => 'One of your settlers, calling himself a deviser, has developed a machine which can heat liquids swiftly and accelerate the process of fermentation. Unfortunately, he has not been able to test it, yet. Perhaps you could give it a try?',
        'ChristmasBuffKrampus' => 'Oh dear... It seems there were a lot of naughty children this year... St. Nicholas takes these things very seriously, and his companion, Krampus, has taken it upon himself to optimize coal production, to meet the season\'s demand for punishment gifts.',
        'ChristmasBuildingBox' => 'A nice small Christmas surprise package that contains one of a range of various buildings, including valuable ones like improved silos or the frozen manor.',
        'ChristmasLargePresentPackage' => 'A huge package filled with presents. Could you imagine anything better?',
        'ChristmasMysteryBoxDeco' => 'A mysterious box, with unknown contents. A dark power seems to be floating around it. The people say that it could even be strong enough to create castles.',
        'ChristmasMysteryBoxResourcesBuffs' => 'A mysterious box, with unknown contents. It smells like many different tasty things. The people say that it could enchant both people and animals.',
        'ChristmasProductivityBuff' => 'These very sweet cookies are made with a lot of sugar. If your workers eat some of them, they will have bags of energy and work much more effectively.',
        'ChristmasSchoolBuff' => 'Tea revives the mind! Give this to your pupils and they will be fit for the hard life of a settler in no time.',
        'ChristmasSmallPresentPackage' => 'A package including some presents. The perfect thing to bring joy to your beloved ones at Christmas.',
        'ChristmasSolarFlare' => 'Tired of the cold, snowy winter and long, dark nights? By using the exceptional Solar Flare, you can instantly melt all the snow away from your island, and bring back daylight!',
        'ChristmasSpeedUpPopulation' => 'This Christmas feast can be served very quickly in your Mayor\'s house and includes a lot of different dishes. You will see that many settlers will visit your city when they hear about the feast.',
        'Christmas_Bench' => 'A beautiful bench, perfect for winter. Sit down and cuddle on it with a cocoa or a hot lemon tea.',
        'Christmas_Hut' => 'Bring Christmas to every corner of your island with this tranquil Christmas Hut.',
        'Christmas_Lantern' => 'This sweet little lantern will let the Christmas Spirit shine across your island.',
        'Christmas_Nutcracker' => 'A must have for all Christmas Fans, and a tribute to nut enthusiasts everywhere.',
        'Christmas_Presents' => 'Nothing says Christmas more than a big bunch of neatly packed Christmas presents.',
        'Christmas_Pyramid' => 'A traditional Christmas decoration, with its roots in the folklore of the Ore Mountains.',
        'ChummyExplorer' => 'Chummy Geologist\'s sibling. Always in a good mood. Always quiet. Will return with chocolatey goodness after a search.',
        'ChummyGeologist' => 'There is nothing in life the Chummy Geologist wants more than to be your friend. To befriend you, he\'ll either find deposits really quickly, or return with sweet chocolate from his longer searches once every couple of searches.',
        'ClassyHotel' => 'A very pompous, very expensive, very sought-after vacation accommodation. Well worth its price tag.',
        'CoalLvl1' => 'Because of its usefulness, some people even call it "Black gold". Nearly every weapon needs this resource for production. With this pile of coal your weaponsmiths will never, ever stand still...',
        'CoalLvl2' => 'While working in one of your woods, a woodcutter has fallen into a hole and found a lot of coal in there. Now he\'s selling the coal for a small finder\'s reward and enough to offset his pain and suffering.',
        'CoalMineEndless' => 'Tired of rebuilding coal mines? Get the "Endless Coal Mine"!',
        'CoalRefillGuild' => 'This chunk of black rock is more valuable than it looks.',
        'CoffeeShop' => 'The place to get a sip or two of that bittersweet, productivity-boosting burnt bean juice.',
        'CoinsLvl1' => 'The dream of every explorer, peasant or king. A big chest of shiny gold coins. What more can you ask for?',
        'CollectibleFoodCartGuildShop' => 'Need loads of food? Then these food carts are for you!',
        'CollectibleMysteryBox' => 'A beautiful collection of all the collectibles you could ever wish for, including Adamantium Ore and Food Carts.',
        'CommandCenter' => 'Before every campaign, military leaders across the lands gather within these halls to devise clever strategies.',
        'CommandCenterAid' => 'A decoration building that increases the Command Centre\'s production speed.',
        'ConcertHall' => 'Grant yourself some high culture and build the wonderful Concert Hall. This building lets you change your background music, while at the same time benefiting from some very powerful zone buffs.
Cooldown: 24 hours, can be reduced by additional buildings of the same type.',
        'ConscientiousGeologist' => 'Young geologists are always looking for that big find, and sometimes miss the forest for the trees. Diligent experts know that checking twice often yields twice the gains.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffBomb_random_units' => 'These strong units with long range can be hired to fire once at an enemy camp. Indeed, you can not determine the exact unit type to shoot at, but in general the lesser units you have to fight against, the better, right?',
        'ConversionBattleBuffBomb_random_units_limited' => 'Fire a volley of arrows at the enemy camp before attacking it. A number of random units in the camp will be defeated and removed.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffBomb_random_units_limited_2' => 'Fire a volley of flaming arrows at the enemy camp before attacking it. A defined amount of random units in the camp will be defeated and removed.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffDestroy_small_camps' => 'You are close to the enemy boss  but one camp is still standing in your way? Your units are defeated and your time is running out? Buy yourself a Small Catapult and simply destroy the camp holding you from winning the adventure.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffDestroy_small_medium_camps' => 'You are close to the enemy boss  but one camp is still standing in your way? Your units are defeated and your time is running out? The camp is too heavy for a Small Catapult? Try out the Big Catapult. With this improved version, even medium camps are no problem.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffKill_random_unit_type' => 'You are facing a camp which would be easy for you to defeat, if there wasn\'t for this particular unit standing in the way? No problem! With the Weak Point Potion you can easily move these types of obstacles out of your way.',
        'ConversionBattleBuffKill_random_unit_type_limited' => 'Hire this assassin to remove a randomly chosen unit type from the camp completely.',
        'ConversionExoticWoodPackage' => 'You are in need of additional exotic wood? This is your chance! Get some precious exotic wood just today!',
        'ConversionGemPackage' => 'A nice package full with sparkling Gems. Surely, you can make good use of them.',
        'ConversionGeneral2' => 'Are you sick of the general stereotype? Do you prefer generals who own a certain energy? The Master of Martial Arts is not only a master in fighting, he also has his own visual style.',
        'ConversionGeneral3' => 'This Veteran is a legend among the generals. Not only is he able to command 220 units, but he can also fight! If you want a shiny hero for the battlefield, a soldier who can make a difference, this is your man!',
        'ConversionGranitePackage' => 'You are in desperate need of granite to upgrade buildings? No problem! Here is an attractive granite package to fill your gaps.',
        'ConversionHiredMilitary_Soldiers50' => 'You do not have enough left units to complete the adventure in time? You want to have some units on stock for an emergency case but you have no free settlers left? These stalwart soldiers would love to enter your service. Against a certain payment, of course!',
        'ConversionSalpeterPackage' => 'A package holding a good amount of saltpetre. But handle it with caution as there are chemical fluids inside!',
        'ConversionTitaniumOrePackage' => 'You must recruit new units but you also have to produce new weapons? This package holds enough titan ore to produce some new weapons.',
        'ConvertBMtoTools' => 'A suspicious looking figure in a hooded cloak is offering a big crate of tools. Where do they come from, you ask? Well, sometimes it\'s better not to know...',
        'ConvertCopperToIron' => 'For the last few days, a strange foreigner with a huge covered wagon has been roaming through your lands, snapping up every bronze bar he can get. Curiously enough he pays the owners with precious iron. Sounds like a good deal for both parties.',
        'ConvertPlanksToHPlanks' => 'This hulk has been damaged in the latest pirate encounter. Still, most of the planks it is made of can be disassembled. Just remove the blood stains and they are as good as new.',
        'ConvertStoneToMarble' => 'A man with an extraordinarily big belly is offering marble in exchange for huge amounts of stones. When asked, he rants about his menhir production, his little dog and his lovesickness.',
        'CopperOreLvl1' => 'This copper is sold as a heap of tiny pellets. It looks like the seller painstakingly picked it out of our mines\' waste.',
        'CorageousExplorer' => 'A very thorough explorer, devoted to searching every corner of the world for treasure. She is faster than regular explorers, and will bring twice as many rewards when sent on any kind of treasure search.',
        'CornLvl1' => 'Carts full of wheat, waiting to be made into the best brew and bread. They glisten golden in the sun.',
        'CozyCabin' => 'A rustic hunting lodge, your latest kill roasting on the fire, and your little partner massaging your feet, while the little ones play on the floor with the dogs.',
        'CrossbowsLvl1' => 'Crossbows are both powerful and easy to use compared to traditional bows. Being slow to reload however, crossbowmen still need to bring a lot of expertise with them, because every shot counts.',
        'CrystalGeode' => 'An inert fragment of a fallen star. Its energies are long gone, but it’s still mesmerizing to look at.',
        'CrystalLighthouse' => 'A Lighthouse powered by the energies of a fallen star. Can light the night like its noon.',
        'CrystalShardPit' => 'A star has fallen from the sky. It\'s made of pure crystal.',
        'CrystalShardPit_deco' => 'Another star that fell from the sky. Too bad the red crystals are impossible to mine. But they sure are pretty to look at...',
        'CrystallanternSingle' => 'A street light powered by a tiny piece of a fallen star.',
        'CultistBundle1' => '3 amazing explorers in one neat bundle! Includes books to get them ready ASAP!',
        'CultistBundle2' => 'With this amazing bundle, you\'ll never run out of storage space.',
        'CultistBundle3' => 'With these mighty powerful generals, you won\'t have to fear even the strongest of cultists.',
        'CultistBundle4' => 'Are your military endeavors lacking a little something? This is it!',
        'CultistBundle5' => 'Looking for something more extravagant? Check out this utility bundle!',
        'CultistBundle6' => 'Three endless mines in one bundle. And apparently with a geologist still stuck in the mine!',
        'CultistBundle7' => 'Fancy some improvements?',
        'CultistBundle8' => 'What\'s not to like about a full week of premium time? For only 20,000 iron, this is a real bargain.',
        'CultistBundle9' => 'Oh, what\'s this? Someone\'s willing to provide 3 building deeds in exchange for water?',
        'CultistBundleCrazy' => 'In between haunting all those adventure islands, the Cultists somehow managed to summon a skeleton. As it turns out, that thing came with a crazy bundle of various items from past events - and some extras!',
        'CultistBundleSecret' => 'So, you finally found me, eh? Now bring me some fish, or else I\'ll…',
        'CupreousGeologist' => 'A geologist who specializes in finding copper.',
        'CursedCastle' => 'A terrifying sight. Only the bravest dare to venture within its halls.',
        'CursedTower' => 'Abandoned ages ago because of the stories surrounding it. It is said that plentiful riches await those brave enough to dare it.',
        'DamasceneHammer' => 'A clever blacksmith has realised that what is good for hitting people could also be used for hammering iron. Surprisingly, he was not completely wrong! He has invented a hammer made of 1,000 Damascene swords, and this tool - despite being ridiculously heavy - is alleviating his work miraculously!',
        'DarkRoofedWarehouse' => 'All goods are stored, delivered and taken from here. Has the capacity to store 40,000 resources.',
        'Deco_Ofrenda' => 'Place an Ofrenda at home and use it as an altar to never forget the settlers you lost in battles.',
        'Deco_RabbitBush' => 'Here\'s a nice decoration - a topiary shaped by a master gardener to resemble the Easter Bunny. Or at least, how he imagines the Easter Bunny would look (since nobody has ever seen him).',
        'Deco_SkeletonScarecrow' => 'A scarecrow was once used to scare away birds and protect fields - but this one is special. It looks alive, and many people are afraid. If you want to protect your village from strangers, this skeleton scarecrow can help you.',
        'Deco_Tombstone' => 'Nobody knows exactly who was laid to rest here. But everyone’s very sure that he or she must have been a very popular person.',
        'Depositorium' => 'More than a simple storehouse, the Depositorium is a place of keeping and rediscovery. Goods are not merely stored here; they rest, waiting to be found again.',
        'DiligentGeologist' => 'Carefully looking in every nook and cranny, the Diligent Geologist can find even the best-hidden treasures. Her passion began as a child when she accompanied her father on treasure hunts at the beach. She sure takes her time though, and enjoys the search more than her findings. She still remembers her father saying "If you\'re lucky once, you\'re always lucky twice".',
        'DimensionalRift' => 'A tiny storage shack that uses dark rituals to be able to store more goods that seems physically possible.',
        'EMBuildingTrophy' => 'A magnificent, twinkling goblet with cryptic inscriptions on it, telling of triumphal victories and staggering defeats in the year of 2012. The mysterious monument exudes an aura of infectious euphoria and confidence. You find yourself wondering whether you\'ll get to keep it longer than four years.',
        'EMBuildingflowerbed_flag_01' => 'Dress your island in the colours of the team you support. This flowerbed let\'s you nail your colours to the mast. Or ground. At the very worst you might still be able to make a nice wreath from it.',
