        'EMIncreaseMaxBuildings' => 'The hordes of supporters that you have acquired throughout the championship require housing. Therefore, it might make sense to provide some quarters. Best inform the neighbours that it might get noisy these next few days.',
        'EMProductionBoost' => 'Not only do they promise high spirits and cheerfulness, they also raise the spirit of your settler\'s workday. This culinary Mexican wave ensures more hat-tricks in the workplace.',
        'EMResourceBoxLvl1' => 'Buy a sack of useful training materials in order to prepare your boys properly for this major event.',
        'EMResourceBoxLvl2' => 'Buy a sack of useful training materials in order to prepare your boys properly for this major event.',
        'EMSpeedUpPopulationGrowth' => 'The festive mood seems to have a peculiar effect on the reproductive behavior of your community. The frenzy of competition and victory seems to bring people closer together.',
        'Easter2015MysteryBox' => 'A very mysterious egg containing a random item. From adventures to resources, anything is possible.',
        'Easter2016MysteryBox' => 'A colourful box containing a random buff or deposit refiller. A faint golden shimmer shines through the cracks.',
        'Easter2017TreePack' => 'Because there can never be enough greenery on your island, here\'s a pack of three trees to decorate it. Why not try out some different combinations, and see where they look best!',
        'Easter2021BuildingsBundle' => 'Benefit from a huge discount on these 3 buildings – with a Prestigious Friend Buff on top. This bundle is event-exclusive!',
        'Easter2021SpecialistsBundle' => 'This is our springtime specialist bundle. Get it now and take advantage of some sweet premium time, along with 4 great specialists to make spring really special. This bundle is event-exclusive!',
        'Easter2021SuperBundle' => 'There is simply no better deal than the event-exclusive Easter Super Bundle. Spend eggs to get everything listed below.',
        'Easter2026_LargeBundle' => 'A large bundle that strikes the right balance of fluffiness and sweetness',
        'Easter2026_MediumBundle' => 'A medium bundle that strikes the right balance of fluffiness and sweetness',
        'Easter2026_SmallBundle' => 'A small bundle that strikes the right balance of fluffiness and sweetness',
        'EasterAreaBuff' => 'A well voiced speech that can make even the laziest of workers put his back into it.',
        'EasterEggPraline' => 'These pralines are delicious, and filled with all different kinds of chocolate. Almost anyone would work faster with these.',
        'EasterGeneral2015' => 'An experienced general, whose body is well and truly ready, after his experience in numerous battles.',
        'EasterMarshal2015' => 'A gutsy young man with high hopes. Travels faster than a regular marshal.',
        'EasterMineralRabbit' => 'Just because you\'re looking for Easter eggs doesn\'t mean you can\'t find coal.',
        'EasterMysteryBox' => 'A mysterious crate, which holds great treasures inside. However, you won\'t know what you\'ve got until you open it!',
        'EasternBigEggPackage' => 'A big basket of stripy eggs, for those who\'d rather not search for themselves.

Please be aware that your remaining eggs will be transformed to gold coins at the end of the Easter event.',
        'EasternHugeEggPackage' => 'A cartful of the most beautiful Easter Eggs. A whole school class helped search to find them - and the helpful little Settlers were even allowed to keep the superfluous ones.',
        'EasternProvisionerBuffLvl1' => 'Since the settlers in the provision house cannot be sustained with fish platters or sandwiches, what is left? Correct! Chocolate! Give this chocolate rabbit to a settler in the provision house and you will increase motivation.',
        'EasternSmallEggPackage' => 'A small basket of stripy eggs, for those who\'d rather not search for themselves.

Please be aware that your remaining eggs will be transformed to gold coins at the end of the Easter event.',
        'EffectBuff_BuffFX_Fireworks' => 'Bored by golden sparkles everywhere? This will make your home island shine in all sorts of colours!
While this zone-wide buff is active, buffed buildings shoot fireworks instead of sparkling.',
        'EffectBuff_BuffFX_Hearts' => 'Fill your town with love! While this buff is active, any buffs will create lovely hearts instead of sparkles.',
        'EffectBuff_FlowerFarm_Resurrector' => 'A fertilizer for your flower farms, if they need to be revived.',
        'EffectBuff_RainFX_FlowerPetals' => 'Proper mood for celebration.',
        'EffectBuff_pumpkinfield_01_resurrector' => 'Did your pumpkin cemetery run out? Don\'t worry! This fertilizer will bring it back to full health with 10 pumpkins, so it can continue its production. Just make sure it doesn\'t run out again!
NOTE: This item only works on the ruins of a small pumpkin cemetery.',
        'EffectBuff_pumpkinfield_02_resurrector' => 'Did your pumpkin cemetery run out? Don\'t worry! This fertilizer will bring it back to full health with 10 pumpkins, so it can continue its production. Just make sure it doesn\'t run out again!
NOTE: This item only works on the ruins of a common pumpkin cemetery.',
        'EffectBuff_pumpkinfield_03_resurrector' => 'Did your pumpkin cemetery run out? Don\'t worry! This fertilizer will bring it back to full health with 10 pumpkins, so it can continue its production. Just make sure it doesn\'t run out again!
NOTE: This item only works on the ruins of a noble pumpkin cemetery.',
        'EfficientAdvancedToolmaker' => 'An alternative engineering of the Advanced tool maker. Trades off a little bit of speed in exchange for resource economy.',
        'EfficientCrossbowsmith' => 'An alternative engineering of the Crossbowsmith. Trades off a little bit of speed for a better resource economy.',
        'EfficientPlatinumSmelter' => 'An alternative engineering of the Platinum Smelter. Trades off a little bit of speed for resource economy.',
        'EggLvl1' => 'A mysterious rabbit in a dark alley is secretly selling Easter eggs. If you say the password "Easter" to him, you\'ll be able to buy some.',
        'ElderTreeLH' => 'A very old tree that teems with magic. Legends say that it is as old as time itself and has the ability to find hidden treasures.',
        'EliteGuildBanner_Deco' => 'A piece of memorabilia from the festivities to keep around on your island.',
        'EmphaticExplorer' => 'Friendly, brave and very decisive, she doesn\'t waste time, and is eager to make every treasure search worth every second.',
        'EnchantedCastle' => 'Its walls are built with an ancient stone that teems with magic. Settlers who dwell in it are filled with an overwhelming feeling joy and love.',
        'EowEventAdventure' => 'The old astrologist has convinced our venerable King Damien that we\'re doomed! The whole world is doomed! The world will end because of a terrible curse, cast by an old and mysterious clan of witch-doctors over a thousand years ago!',
        'EpicWorkyardWood' => 'Both undisputable evidence of your prowess and a greatly improved production building, this truly magnificent structure is every player\'s desire.',
        'EspionageBuilding' => 'This building comes with a cadre of scouts. They\'ll evaluate the situation on any adventures you start, to ensure you get the most out of them.',
        'ExoticPlanksLvl1' => 'A merchant from a far away country wants to sell you exotic wood planks. They are very rare and will allow you to construct high-quality buildings.',
        'ExoticWoodLvl1' => 'This rare and exotic wood puts the cat among the pigeons at the weekly farmer\'s market. All visitors want to sneak a peak at this strange looking building material. Fortunately, you are the only one amongst the masses who has the necessary wealth for this rare resource...',
        'Expedition Island (lvl29-31, difficulty 10)' => 'A small island where you can learn the basics of how to fight for and gain a colony!',
        'ExpertAdmiral' => 'A Veteran Marshal has led armies to many victories. He can recover twice as quickly from defeat than a normal general, and can also bring more troops in to combat.',
        'ExpertTransporterAdmiral' => 'The expedition quartermaster can transport a lot of troops to an expedition island. As he\'s a specialist in these kinds of risky trips to unknown islands, he cannot be used on normal adventures.',
        'FillUpAny' => 'Mysteriously sparkling seeds, fallen from the moon. These can miraculously enrich any deposit to which they are applied. How is this possible, you ask? Well, even Alchemy can\'t explain everything.',
        'FillUpAnyLv2' => 'We got lucky and secured a huge haul of omniseeds! 
It is said that these rare, magical seeds have fallen from the moon. You\'d think with the amount we\'ve found we could figure out why they work on all kinds of deposits, but it still remains a mystery.',
        'FillUpCopperLvl1' => 'Equipped with a confidence-inspiring wooden rod, this specialist will find new reserves in your copper deposits. Trust him. He\'s really good.',
        'FillUpFishLvl1' => 'A huge barrel filled with charming female fish. This will solve the spawning problems in your shoals of fish for a long time...',
        'FillUpGoldLvl1' => 'This parrot has been trained by pirates to find gold. If you feed it enough crackers it will lead your workers to new gold reserves deep in the mountains.',
        'FillUpGoldLvl2' => 'With this pickaxe your settlers can mine gold ore more effectively than ever. Simply use it on the mine and be amazed how much gold ore one mine can have.',
        'FillUpGraniteLvl1' => 'Your settlers can expose more granite using this hammer.',
        'FillUpIronLvl1' => 'Originally he specialised as a water diviner, but the only thing he ever found was iron. So he decided to become an iron diviner!',
        'FillUpIronLvl2' => 'Your iron ore mines are nearly empty and you need backup? With this pickaxe, your settlers can mine from a huge iron ore deposit.',
        'FillUpMarbleLvl1' => 'The potential of a marble deposit is measured by the quality of workforce organization. An intelligent overseer can increase this potential significantly. Really!',
        'FillUpMarbleLvl2' => 'A professor named Frank and Stein, famous for his creepy experiments, has found a way to refill almost empty marble deposits. Do you want to hire him?',
        'FillUpSalpeterLvl1' => 'Your settlers have found a way to enrich the saltpetre deposits in the mountains. This technology is now available to you.',
        'FillUpStoneLvl1' => 'With these improved chisels, your workers can cut even more stones from a single deposit. It is astounding what a difference good tools can make.',
        'FillUpTitaniumLvl1' => 'This pickaxe allows your settlers to access more rich titanium deposits.',
        'FirwoodLvl1' => 'The last whirlwind that swept over the land destroyed nearly all the woodcutter huts in your land, but this smart salesman has made a virtue of necessity and now sells the ruined huts as high quality pinewood for low budgets.',
        'FirwoodLvl2' => 'Do you need a lot of pinewood quickly? This large stash was intended as firewood for next winter, but the sheer quantity of it will allow you to use it for any purpose.',
        'FishCaretaker' => 'Only real fish lovers can become a fish caretaker. They spend their whole life breeding fish, so that no fish species will ever become extinct!',
        'FishEggs' => 'A brand-new fish egg breeding ground: the eggs hatch when they come in contact with water.',
        'FishFarm' => 'The home of a passionate and nature loving fisherman who loves to fish, but does not want to endanger wild fish species. He\'s known for his boundless knowledge of how to breed fish in great numbers.',
        'FishLvl1' => 'Finest fish from Lutetia. You can smell them a mile away. Which doesn\'t mean the fish is stale, seriously! Just keep in mind that you cannot return the fish once you have bought them.',
        'FishLvl2' => 'Today\'s complete haul from a large fishing vessel. Who cares about fancy Lutetia when regional fish tastes twice as good - and only smells half as strong?',
        'FishStatue_deco' => 'This gigantic fish has been cursed to remain immobile until the end of time.',
        'FloatingStorehouse' => 'Overcrowded at home? No more room to hoard stuff you never use? We’ve got you covered.
Build your new storage offshore! Cannot be used to transport goods or conquer new lands, but it sure has enough room to hoard stuff away!',
        'FlourLvl1' => 'A good dozen sacks of wheat flour. As fine and pure as it seems to be, you cannot wait to try whatever amazing bread your bakers will make from it!',
        'FlowerBlossomsResidence' => 'Get a home that blooms year-round with this charming floral-inspired residence. Petals not included, but guaranteed to brighten your day!',
        'FlowerBlossomsStorehouse' => 'Keep your resources in full bloom with our floral-inspired Storehouse. Store with style and add a touch of whimsy to your storage solution.',
        'FlowerPackageLarge' => 'A package of beautiful flowers, which can be traded in for unique items during the Valentine\'s Event.',
        'FlowerPackageSmall' => 'A package of beautiful flowers, which can be traded in for unique items during the Valentine\'s Event.',
        'FluffyButteExplorer' => 'With strong legs, he hops his way in and out of tasks 3 times faster than a standard explorer. His magical bag allows him to store copious amounts of magical goods.',
        'FluffyLogistics' => 'Fluffy Butte works diligently and tirelessly to deliver Easter Eggs in a timely manner.
No child should miss the opportunity to waste a whole day looking for hidden eggs.',
        'ForgottenCemetery_Residence' => 'This cemetery got forgotten about decades ago, but with space being limited, some inhabitants decided that this could be the perfect place to live. Now they have shelter, and are close to the loved ones they lost.',
        'FrankenHouse' => 'The home and workplace of a "differently minded" man of science, who is obsessed with curing death.',
        'FrostyGeneral' => 'Don’t let yourself be fooled by his pale blue skin colour. Deep down inside burns the will to conquer. He strikes hard, and will improve your army’s defensive units.',
        'GFF' => 'You are one of the most generous people in the settlers\' universe, but your friends don\'t believe you are. Prove yourself with the Gems for friends!',
        'GemPit' => 'Deep within the bowels of the earth, subjected to incredibly severe conditions, your men have amazingly discovered a gem lode. Only your most adept diggers are capable of unearthing these precious gems while risking their very lives.',
        'GeneralAnslem' => 'An auspicious champion from the Lands of Anteria. Former member of the Frostbeard Tribes.',
        'GeneralJuan' => 'Juan has always been known as a very friendly person. He decided to become a general to show his team that even fighting can be fun. His two small cats are always by his side. Never underestimate this amazing trio!',
        'GeneralLoudmouth' => 'General Loudmouth is loud, bold and always full of energy. In battle, she has this striking expression on her face, always showing determination and a strong will to win. She is hard but fair to all the soldiers in her army, and very caring toward her battle horse.',
        'GeneralMary' => 'Mary, Santa\'s wife, has grown bored of sitting around at the North Pole all year. She promises to bake you some cookies if you let her beat up some bad guys.',
        'GeneralNusala' => 'An astute champion from the Lands of Anteria. Former member of the Dune Tribe.',
        'GeneralSpeedBuff_Mystical' => 'These horseshoes are forged out of star dust, and improve the walking speed of your generals.',
        'GeneralSpeedBuff_Obsidian' => 'These horseshoes are made of dark glass, but they\'re at least as hard as steel somehow! Have you ever seen anything like it? 
I got these crates from a Nord merchant, but even she couldn\'t explain where it came from.',
        'GeneralTrembleBeard' => 'As wise as his beard is long. He\'s never been the bravest or strongest among the ranks of the generals, but makes up for it with his extraordinary sageness.',
        'GeneralVargus' => 'A fierce champion from the Lands of Anteria. Former Sergeant-at-Arms of the Crown Legion.',
        'GenerousBundle1' => 'A must-have for every settler. Worth 3 times its gem value! 
Check out the glorious content!',
        'GenerousBundle11' => 'A crucial pack for every settler. Worth 3 times its resource value, get your buffs now! Only one purchase per player.',
        'GenerousBundle13_Halloween2020' => 'A scarily magnificient bundle. An elite troop of generals with some equally elite housing. 
Event limited bundle with an insane 50% discount! Get it now or fear the consequences! Muahahaha!',
        'GenerousBundle14_Halloween2020' => 'Not zombies, but still creepy! Get your hands on a bunch of halloween generals at a sweet discount!
Don\'t trick yourself, treat yourself!',
        'GenerousBundle15_Halloween2020' => 'Brilliant beautification for any settlement with lots of building space. It\'s also the perfect bundle for brilliant scientists who want to get their own laboratory!',
        'GenerousBundle16' => 'A small but impressive bundle for everyone preparing to become a famous adventurer.',
        'GenerousBundle17' => 'This is the package for experienced adventurers that want to mentor others about to embark upon a great journey. After all this time, it might be nice just to listen to others who\'ve explored unknown lands.',
        'GenerousBundle18' => 'On a far away venture, a trader companion came across this incredible deal and knew you wouldn\'t be able to resist.',
        'GenerousBundle2_Anniversary2019' => 'A bundle to celebrate the jubilee! 
3x buildings, 3x specialists and over 50 buffs! 
Worth more than 3 times its gem value! 
Don\'t miss out on this amazing time-limited offer!',
        'GenerousBundle3_Anniversary2019' => 'A small but powerful time-limited bundle with a great discount, only available during the anniversary. Check out the cool content below!',
        'GenerousBundle4' => 'Treat yourself with this delicious little package to make your settling life a bit easier. It won\'t hurt if you spoil yourself a little bit with this tasty, time-limited delicacy.
Where else do you get a delicacy that costs 3x less than the ingredients normally would? Yum!',
        'GenerousBundle5_Halloween2019' => 'An eerily awesome package for new starters, or those who want to boost their effectiveness during the event.',
        'GenerousBundle6' => 'A supernatural general accompanied by two cunning explorers? What more could you want! And don\'t forget the 30 days premium time.',
        'GenerousBundle_Halloween2021' => 'A frighteningly helpful bundle for everyone, with useful buildings, specialists, and buffs.',
        'GeologistOnVacation' => 'A geologist that takes twice as long for tasks - he is on vacation after all. The upside is that he\'s very thoughtful, and will bring gifts and souvenirs back with him.',
        'GhostExplorer' => 'An explorer from a bygone age who keeps diligently working on his tasks.',
        'GhostGeneral' => 'This noble ghost seeks retribution, and believes you to be the perfect partner to accomplish it.',
        'GiantBarrel' => 'A warehouse made from a gigantic barrel. Nobody has a clue who or what made it, or what was once stored in it. A bit over-the-top if you ask me...',
        'GingerbreadGeologist' => 'Being made of bread, what he lacks in mobility he makes up for in luck, as he always seem to find a few extra resources - and sometimes even items.',
        'GloryExploriExplorer' => 'A horse-loving explorer who is still tied to a troubled past. She is always seeking the thrill of the special adventure.',
        'GoldMineEndless' => 'By finding a vein of gold that runs so deep it\'ll last for several generations, the mine will appear all but endless. Just don´t let the gold fever get a grip on you!',
        'GoldOreKnowledge1' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the secrets of working gold.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a manuscript.',
        'GoldOreKnowledge2' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the closely guarded secrets of working gold.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a tome.',
        'GoldOreLvl1' => 'A pirate crew wants to sell you a "treasure of gold". When you open one of the chests to reveal gold ore instead of the expected coins, they just shrug.',
        'GoldheartedGeologist' => 'A geologist with a heart of gold. It seems as if the gods want to reward her kindness and hard-working nature.',
        'GrandFieldHospital' => 'Produce zone buffs that allow you to recover troops after battles.',
        'GraniteLvl1' => 'The stone of the upper class has made its way onto your market stalls. Hard, precious and very rare. But this blank-faced companion seems not to know about the real worth of this resource.',
        'GranitePit_Mini' => 'Like your favorite granite pit, but endless, though slower. You can\'t have it all.',
        'GroutFactory' => 'Are your old buildings looking a bit hard on the eyes?
Why not give them a fresh coat of grout with a brand-new Grout Factory!',
        'Groutlvl1' => 'Grout is our masons\' latest invention. It helps make our buildings\' structure more solid, and allows us to upgrade them to higher levels.',
        'GuildAdventure1' => 'The pirates\' island might be just a legend, but recently some wayfarers disappeared north of here, near Skull Cove. We\'re more than positive there are some nasty pirates hiding there! And we don\'t like pirates, no sir!',
        'GuildBanner_Deco' => 'A piece of memorabilia from the festivities to keep around on your island.',
        'GuildFestBundle1' => 'A bundle worth its weight in Gold',
        'GuildFestBundle2' => 'A bundle worth its weight in Silver',
        'GuildFestBundle3' => 'A bundle worth its weight in Bronze',
        'GuildFestTentI' => 'A temporary lodging for our esteemed guest. It is equipped with all the amenities they would expect for such a joyous occasion.',
        'GuildFestTentII' => 'A temporary lodging for our esteemed guest. It is equipped with all the amenities they would expect for such a joyous occasion.',
        'GuildFestTentIII' => 'A temporary lodging for our esteemed guest. It is equipped with all the amenities they would expect for such a joyous occasion.',
        'GuildFillMarble' => 'Some stones may contain chunks of marble, but only professional masons can spot them. And of course, they won\'t do it for free!',
        'GuildHouse_Mini' => 'A tiny version of the Guild Office building that passively produces Guild Coins for your convenience.',
        'GuildMasterGeologistLvl1' => 'Good news! The guild was able to strike a deal with the Miner\'s Union! We can now hire a Jolly Geologist with our guild coins!',
        'Halloween2019General' => 'Never look down on the baby of the family. Despite looking much like his brother, the Younger Gemini General doesn\'t draw his strength from a huge army. Instead, he relies mostly on himself, and only takes a handful of units with him to guard his back. One can only speculate as to where his strength comes from, but his reddish skin suggests something supernatural.',
        'Halloween2021Bundle1' => 'Treat yourself with this horrifyingly useful set of buildings, specialists and buffs.',
        'Halloween2021Bundle2' => 'Get the Halloween Spirit going with this convenient bundle.',
        'HalloweenGeneral' => 'It is Halloween and the Grim Reaper is visiting you. He wants to make an offer: he will lead your army, and in turn only wants a few pumpkins... and your soul.',
        'HalloweenGeneralDracul' => 'The sinister nobleman introduces himself as Lord Dracul. Thirsty for... battle, he is willing to lead your troops. It seems he does not care for which side he fights; some pumpkins will be all it takes to bring him to you.',
        'HalloweenRefill' => 'Mysteriously sparkling seeds, fallen from the moon. These can miraculously enrich any deposit to which they are applied. How is this possible, you ask? Well, even Alchemy can\'t explain everything.',
        'HalloweenResourceLvl1' => 'This orange vegetable with a cheeky grin can only be harvested once a year. Get it now before they all sell out!',
        'HalloweenResourceLvl2' => 'A woman farmer has collected a basket of pumpkins, but when one of them started to talk and said that the basket was uncomfortable, the woman decided she\'d rather sell the lot as soon as possible! Do you want to buy them?',
        'HalloweenResourceLvl3' => 'A cart of pumpkins seemingly started to move on its own. Only when looking closely could you see that the pumpkins themselves were pushing the cart. At least, until a farmer caught them and made them available for sale. A small fence around the cart suffices to keep them in place.',
        'HarborTowerWarehouse' => 'All goods are stored, delivered and taken from here.',
        'HardCurrencyLvl1' => 'Some gems to help you make smoother progress while testing on the test environment.',
        'HardPlanksLvl1' => 'Higher class building materials in one convenient package. Weighs nearly nothing and can be transported to a storehouse near you immediately.',
        'HardPlanksLvl2' => 'A settler has overestimated the building materials needed for his residence and has a lot of hardwood planks left over. He\'d like to sell them as quickly as possible.',
        'HardWoodLvl1' => 'A storm has hit your island and demolished some trees. The forester has collected the branches and given them to the local merchant.',
        'HardWoodLvl2' => 'On an island next to yours a new settlement is going to be built. The settlers have to deforest the area and you can buy the resulting wood now.',
        'HauntedMansion_pop' => 'Ah, I see you\'re looking at these mansion blueprints. You\'ve got a fine eye! 
But I must warn you - there may be something otherworldly in those angles and lines! Every time someone follows these plans, the house appears to draw in dozens of ghosts in an instant.',
        'HiredMilitary_ArmoredMarksmen50' => 'These bold mercenaries brag about being adept both at taking out weak targets, and focusing down tough enemies. Will you contract them to see if they can back up their claims?',
        'HiredMilitary_ArmoredMarksmen5000' => 'These bold mercenaries brag about being adept both at taking out weak targets, and focusing down tough enemies. Will you contract them to see if they can back up their claims?',
        'HiredMilitary_Besiegers50' => 'Does your army need more offensive power? These besiegers\' mortars can demolish large targets or groups of enemies equally well. They are a little slow, however, so make sure to protect them until they are ready to fire.',
        'HiredMilitary_Besiegers5000' => 'Does your army need more offensive power? These besiegers\' mortars can demolish large targets or groups of enemies equally well. They are a little slow, however, so make sure to protect them until they are ready to fire.',
        'HiredMilitary_Bowman100' => 'Agile and cheap is good but do you need ranged support? No problem! These bowmen are ready for battle and would be happy to fight for your cause.',
        'HiredMilitary_Bowmen50' => 'Is your army lacking in the archery department? These bowmen will agree to help you out for a little while - for a little pay, of course.',
        'HiredMilitary_Bowmen5000' => 'Is your army lacking in the archery department? These bowmen will agree to help you out for a little while - for a little pay, of course.',
        'HiredMilitary_Cannoneers50' => 'Trained cannoneer crews for hire. Their cannons are easily the most destructive weapons among standard troops.',
        'HiredMilitary_Cannoneers5000' => 'Trained cannoneer crews for hire. Their cannons are easily the most destructive weapons among standard troops.',
        'HiredMilitary_Cavalry100' => 'If you are searching for agile, immediate support look no more! These cavalry units are fast, cheap and immediately usable.',
        'HiredMilitary_Cavalry50' => 'This band of mercenary cavalry is well known for their swift attacks on unsuspecting targets. Hiring them may help you take down key opponents before they can retaliate.',
        'HiredMilitary_Cavalry5000' => 'This band of mercenary cavalry is well known for their swift attacks on unsuspecting targets. Hiring them may help you take down key opponents before they can retaliate.',
        'HiredMilitary_Crossbowmen50' => 'A rowdy bunch of mercenaries shares a hearty chuckle at the bows and longbows your troops are equipped with. They offer you a good deal on contracting some crossbowmen to demonstrate their power.',
        'HiredMilitary_Crossbowmen5000' => 'A rowdy bunch of mercenaries shares a hearty chuckle at the bows and longbows your troops are equipped with. They offer you a good deal on contracting some crossbowmen to demonstrate their power.',
        'HiredMilitary_EliteSoldiers50' => 'These guys sure look tough! Better yet, despite being mercenaries, they will loyally protect your personal troops with their lives.',
        'HiredMilitary_EliteSoldiers5000' => 'These guys sure look tough! Better yet, despite being mercenaries, they will loyally protect your personal troops with their lives.',
        'HiredMilitary_Knights50' => 'These mercenaries already impress you by staying in the saddles of their ferocious looking horses. After watching them spar, you feel even more compelled to contract them for a while.',
        'HiredMilitary_Knights5000' => 'These mercenaries already impress you by staying in the saddles of their ferocious looking horses. After watching them spar, you feel even more compelled to contract them for a while.',
        'HiredMilitary_Longbowmen50' => 'Mercenary longbowmen available for hire! Consider contracting them if you want to dish out more damage in combat.',
        'HiredMilitary_Longbowmen5000' => 'Mercenary longbowmen available for hire! Consider contracting them if you want to dish out more damage in combat.',
        'HiredMilitary_Marksmen50' => 'You can hear the sounds of the mercenaries\' arquebuses before you can even see their encampment\'s training grounds. When you arrive, you find the targets riddled with holes.',
        'HiredMilitary_Marksmen5000' => 'You can hear the sounds of the mercenaries\' arquebuses before you can even see their encampment\'s training grounds. When you arrive, you find the targets riddled with holes.',
        'HiredMilitary_Militia50' => 'If you need an urgent supply of well equipped units, these militia seem be perfect for you. Not particularly cheap, but reliable.',
        'HiredMilitary_Militia5000' => 'If you need an urgent supply of well equipped units, these militia seem be perfect for you. Not particularly cheap, but reliable.',
        'HiredMilitary_MountedMarksmen50' => 'While you watch these mounted marksman practice, you cannot help but wonder how well their horses must be trained to not shy from the loud noise. Indeed, as you watch on you confirm that that both riders and horses are at peak capacity.',
        'HiredMilitary_MountedMarksmen5000' => 'While you watch these mounted marksman practice, you cannot help but wonder how well their horses must be trained to not shy from the loud noise. Indeed, as you watch on you confirm that that both riders and horses are at peak capacity.',
        'HiredMilitary_MountedSwordsmen50' => 'The mercenaries\' armour glistens in the sun as does their horses\' barding. They look almost invincible to you.',
        'HiredMilitary_MountedSwordsmen5000' => 'The mercenaries\' armour glistens in the sun as does their horses\' barding. They look almost invincible to you.',
        'HiredMilitary_Recruit100' => 'Diligent recruits are immediately ready for battle. They are not very strong but strong enough to keep the enemy busy for a while.',
        'HiredMilitary_Recruit50' => 'Some of them look a bit old and thin. But as long as they can fight... Who cares?',
        'HiredMilitary_Recruit5000' => 'Some of them look a bit old and thin. But as long as they can fight... Who cares?',
        'HiredMilitary_Soldiers50' => 'The frontlines can be such a busy place - good thing there are these supportive fellows. Alleviate a stressful workday by renting some helping iron-gloved hands.',
        'HiredMilitary_Soldiers5000' => 'The frontlines can be such a busy place - good thing there are these supportive fellows. Alleviate a stressful workday by renting some helping iron-gloved hands.',
        'HiredMilitary_Swordsmen50' => 'You inspect a group of mercenary swordsmen. They look ordinary on first glance, but you quickly realize that they are trained and equipped exceptionally well.',
        'HiredMilitary_Swordsmen5000' => 'You inspect a group of mercenary swordsmen. They look ordinary on first glance, but you quickly realize that they are trained and equipped exceptionally well.',
        'HoliFestivalGrounds' => 'Colors everywhere! That\'s the theme of the Holi Festival. Get some bright paints and enjoy the festivities. We all know the world needs more color!',
        'HoneygladeResidence' => 'The ideal home for those who believe that prosperity should be sweet, sustainable, and surrounded by flowers.',
        'HorsesLvl1' => 'These strong and swift horses are trained to endure the sights, sounds and smells of battle. Since they are not bread for endurance however, cavaliers rely on rotating multiple horses for training and battle.',
        'HumbleExplorer' => '"You don\'t have to go far to find happiness" could be the motto of this explorer. For him, there\'s no need to travel to distant shores, or with extraordinary speed. Appreciating the small things, he excels at short and medium treasure searches.',
        'IcePalace' => 'A gorgeous palace made out of eternal enchanted ice. It has a lovely view too!',
        'IceSculpture' => 'An exquisite sculpture made of ice. A shame all that craftmanship will go to waste as soon as the temperature rises.',
        'IceSkatingLake' => 'A favorite recreational attraction at the colder times of the year.
After spending the day here, settlers return home with warm hearts.',
        'IglooStorehouse' => 'A warehouse made in the Inuit style. Very useful for storing perishable goods, as it keeps them fresh. Very fresh.',
        'ImprovedBakery' => 'Are your plain old bakeries struggling to keep up with your sandwich consumption? Well fear not, as science has the answer to this terrible problem! 
This bakery is equipped with optimized ovens and extra-precise hourglasses.',
        'ImprovedBronzeWeaponsmith' => 'Have you ever had the feeling that the workers in the Bronze Weaponsmith just aren’t efficient enough? Well, you’re right! The workers put all their energy and effort into developing a new improved version of their workyard and now, they’re much faster than before.',
        'ImprovedBuildingBox' => 'Adults need their toys too! This mechanical box includes one or two state-of-the art improved buildings. Who says science has no place in the festivities?',
        'ImprovedLettersmith' => 'For those who believe the letter to be mightier than the sword, the improved lettersmith will fulfill their every need.',
        'ImprovedMill' => 'Mills are nice, but isn\'t there always room for improvement? Our engineers thought so, and devised a much more efficient design that allows it to produce flour much more quickly. They say took years of research, but really they just strapped more donkeys to the wheel.',
        'ImprovedOrnamentalsmith' => 'There’s always room for improvements. That\'s what the architects thought when creating this new Ornamentalsmith, which produces book fittings more efficiently.',
        'IncreaseGuildMemberLimitLvl1' => 'A blank guild membership certificate. Only expert eyes would expose this perfectly counterfeit document as an imitation.',
        'IncreaseGuildMemberLimitLvl2' => 'Old, yellowed and tattered certificates for a guild membership. Fortunately, most of the letters have become illegible over all the years, so the high council will never notice if anyone inscribes another member or guild name.',
        'IncreaseMaxBuildingsLvl1' => 'Ten blank building licences directly from the high court of the royal palace. These will allow you to construct even more buildings in your marvelous city.',
        'IncreaseMaxBuildingsLvl2' => 'The over-worked secretary in the royal palace has lost track of how many building licences you have been given already. A little precious gift might convince him to just hand over a whole batch of blank building licences to you...',
        'IncreaseMaxBuildings_EpicRaid' => 'The high court of the royal palace is highly interested in magic beanstalks. They will even offer you these 5 additional building licences for your city.',
        'InflatableResidence' => 'A residence with walls made of cloth filled with air. Pretty portable, but you need a good set of lungs to set it up.',
        'InflatableStorehouse' => 'A storehouse with walls so bouncy, even if you drop something, it won\'t break - it\'ll just bounce right back up into your hands.',
        'IntermediatePaperLvl1' => 'Not all books turn out to be worth keeping. Sometimes it makes sense just to wipe the slate clean and start over. And frankly, did you ever finish that 1000-pager?',
        'IntrepidExplorer' => 'From tombs to temples, this explorer is always on the lookout for new adventures! She\'s already twice as fast as a regular explorer at any kind of task you give her, but if you send her on an adventure search, she will bring back twice as many rewards.',
        'IronMineEndless' => 'With a special technique, iron ore can be extracted from all kinds of rocks. It took years to develop the method, and it\'s rumored that a certain alchemist involved in the research even went mad during the process. Still, it\'s hard to deny the result is remarkable!',
        'IronMineProdBoost' => 'With this extractor, it\'s easy as pie to extract iron ore from deposits.',
        'IronMine_Mini' => 'A tribute to honor the infamous Iron Mine!',
        'IronOreKnowledge1' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the secrets of working iron.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a manuscript.',
        'IronOreKnowledge2' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the closely guarded secrets of working iron.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a tome.',
        'IronOreLvl1' => 'An overseas mining company is selling large amounts of iron ore. You\'ve never heard of them before, but they appear to be professional and trustworthy.',
        'IronSwordsLvl1' => 'Basic swords, the likes of which are generally handed out to militia in times of need. They can be efficiently wielded with little to no training.',
        'IronWilledGeologist' => 'This fellow showed up here, determined to become the best geologist ever. He\'s practiced his entire life, and has developed a knack for finding bountiful iron deposits.',
        'JaguarBundle' => 'Make preparations for the end of the world with this time-limited and event-exclusive bundle.',
        'Jewelcrafter' => 'A humble workshop focused on handcrafted jewel products.',
        'JewelsBundle' => 'Jewel crafting and prospecting bundle with both new buildings at a more convenient price.',
        'KeenerExplorer' => 'Has gone through pain again and again for her loved ones, but has never once thought about giving up. On the contrary, all her fights have made her stronger, brighter and keener than any other explorer.',
        'KrampusPit' => 'A very deep coal mine. It is still active, but the mined out spaces are great for storing all sorts of goods and keeping them safe from the elements. As a bonus, no one would dare to steal from it with Krampus guarding it.',
        'Laboratory' => 'A most curious building. I have never seen anything like it before. 
It comes with piles of arcane equipment that, I\'ve been assured, can transform one resource into another in the hands of an expert.',
        'LaboratoryForGems' => 'A most curious building. I\'ve never seen anything like it before. 
It comes with piles of arcane equipment that can transform one resource into another - or so I\'ve been assured - in the hands of an expert.',
        'LargeDefBuild' => 'Contains a minimum of 3 random strongholds, with a chance of getting a mixed camp. Has an additional chance of getting a random fourth fortified camp (lvl 2).',
        'LargeEasterBundle2024' => 'This chest is a huge surprise from the Holi Festival. Get your hands on it and reveal some interesting buildings, specialists and buffs.',
        'LargeEasterBundle2025' => 'A chest of sweet goodness to fill your heart and ruin your dental health.',
        'LargeHalloweenBundle2024' => 'Oh no, look at this bag! It comes right from a nightmare. Don\'t close your eyes or it will haunt you in your precious dreams.',
        'LargeHalloweenBundle2025' => 'A chest made of a ghoulish leather, full of Halloween themed goodness. Hopefully the contents are worth bearing the smell.',
        'LetterLvl1' => 'For all who want to produce serial pamphlets rather than fancy poetry books. No time for squiggly scrawling - here\'s how you can produce those piles of documents before tonight\'s deadline.',
        'LevelUp_ExpeditionLevel' => 'If you need a higher PvP level to properly test things, be our guest!',
        'LevelUp_PlayerLevel' => 'We want to test stuff here - can\'t just leave you at level 1 for that, can we?
Gain however many levels you deem necessary.',
        'LevelUp_PlayerLevel10' => 'We want to test stuff here - can\'t just leave you at level 1 for that now, can we?
The same as the other item, just 10x.',
        'LevitatingHauntedWarehouse' => 'This warehouse is flying! It\'s unbelievable. It\'s so haunted that it started to levitate. This is our opportunity to place it in the water!',
        'LightingBlackAndWhite' => 'Someone stole all the colours.',
        'LightingDesert' => 'The sun will shine upon your island, and play tricks upon your mind.',
        'LightingSpooky' => 'The Friar\'s Lantern has already misled a lot of travelers. Be careful!',
        'LightingTundra' => 'The tundra is one of the most beautiful, and most dangerous areas.',
        'LoggingHut' => 'A cozy vacation home, far away from everything. The perfect place to relax and knit ugly winter sweaters.',
        'LonelyHeartInn' => 'An inn that somehow became the favorite place of sufferers of heartbreak to drown their sorrows.',
        'LonerGeneral' => 'The loner general is a rather egotistical character, but fortunately there\'s more to him than that: he\'s an expert in how to lead and attack with offensive units.',
        'LongboatStorehouse' => 'Once a raiding boat, now repurposed as a storage vault for countless stolen riches.',
        'LongbowsLvl1' => 'These exquisite longbows outperform generic bows in both range and penetrating power. While archers need special training to properly use them, they are well worth the effort.',
        'Loottable_GrimoirePages_MysteryBox' => 'An ancient notebook that might contain useful knowledge.',
        'Loottable_HalloweenMysteryBox' => 'A box containing various adventures like "The Nords" or "Island of the Pirates", epic raids like the "The Heroic Little Tailor" or even co-operative ones like "Tomb Raiders".',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxAtTheFootOfTheMountain' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "At the Foot of the Mountain" venture.',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxBuccaneerRoundup' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Buccaneer Roundup" adventure',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxLakesideTreasure' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Lakeside Treasure" adventure',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxMountainLabyrinth' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Mountain Labyrinth" venture',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxRaidingTheRaiders' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Raiding The Raiders" adventure',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxSnowWhite' => 'Simulates the reward loot table from the Snow White venture.',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxTheSiege' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of "The Siege" adventure',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxTombRaiders' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Tomb Raiders" adventure',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxUnknownRegions' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Unknown Regions" venture',
        'Loottable_RewardBoxWhirlwind' => 'Simulates the reward loot table of the "Whirlwind" adventure',
        'Loottable_Valentines2025DecorationMysteryBox' => 'A box containing a mystery Valentines-themed decoration.',
        'Loottable_XmasDecorationMysteryBox' => 'A box containing a mystery Christmas themed decoration.',
        'LoveStruckExplorer' => 'Have you ever met a person who’s so in love that he doesn’t even notice the world around him anymore? That is exactly who the Love Struck Explorer is. He has his head in the clouds, and is only thinking about his beloved one.',
        'LovelyExplorer' => 'Her kind voice helps her gather information about the largest treasures.',
        'LovelyGeologist' => 'His handsome looks help him gather information about easy to mine deposits.',
        'LuxuryResourceBox' => 'A beautiful box containing luxury resource items. It is soft and its golden adornments sparkle in the sun. And it weighs an awful lot.',
        'MIADArcticExplosion' => 'A brand new mini adventure. Do you dare have a go?',
        'MIADBastilleIsland' => 'A brand new mini adventure. Do you dare have a go?',
        'MadScientistGeneral' => 'I don\'t know what to make of this man! It\'s obvious that he\'s some sort of genius, but he seems to have trouble making anything useful. That may be because most of his ideas revolve around explosions...
Still, he\'s looking for work, and you look like you could use more explosions in your army. What do you say?',
        'MahoganyPlanksLvl1' => 'Ready-for-construction planks made of high-quality mahogany. Their durability and beauty make them perfect for any ambitious project.',
        'MahoganyWoodLv1' => 'This unique wood is very robust. Perfectly suitable for building solid constructions that need to stand the test of time.',
        'MajorGeneral' => 'The Major General has seen many battles and is able to command armies of overwhelming size without sacrificing travel speed.',
        'ManEatingPlant' => 'Look at this cute little plant. I\'m sure it’ll develop into a loyal pet, and not a man eating plant who wants to eat its owner...',
        'MarathonGeologist' => 'This geologist is specialized in running. He loves to run. Due to that, he is super fast - but on the other hand, he’s not all that efficient. He feels so bad about it that he tries to compensate with presents.',
        'MarbleLvl1' => 'White and shimmering. High class marble blocks, ready for transport to your storage.',
        'MarbleLvl2' => 'A shady guy is selling a huge amount of marble in a side street of the market. Do not ask him where he got it from. There is talk that the nearby mason and his crew are missing some marble.',
        'MasterEasterExplorer' => 'This explorer doesn\'t just look experienced, he really is. Fast as lightning, he finds treasure and can map all target areas. A must have for every explorer.',
        'MasterEasterGeneral' => 'This general was in many battles and earned honour and fame. Due to his great experience, he is able to command bigger armies than all of his colleagues.',
        'MasterEasterGeneralEgg' => 'This general was in many battles and earned honour and fame. Due to his great experience, he is able to command bigger armies than all of his colleagues.',
        'MasterExplorerLvl1' => 'A native inhabitant of these parts. He knows the area like no other and can help you map these parts in no time. You just need someone to translate his strange tongue.',
        'MasterGeneralLvl1' => 'A Battle Hardened General has led armies to many victories. He can recover twice as quickly from defeat than a normal general.',
        'MasterGeologistLvl1' => 'Ah... those were the good old days. When finding new resources was an adventure. Travelling into the mountains, tapping the stone and placing wooden signposts.',
        'Meadhall' => 'Celebrate like the Nords. A festival hall to start various zone wide effects.',
        'MeatLvl1' => 'A cook is selling cured meat from his storage. He has more than he can possibly put to use, and it\'d be a shame to let quality ingredients go to waste...',
        'MedicGeneral' => 'A medic who was promoted to the rank of general. He cares deeply about his troops, and uses his medical skills to patch them up after battle.',
        'MediumEasterBundle2024' => 'Who would forget a box from the Holi Festival? Now it can be yours! There are quite some nice buildings, specialists and buffs inside.',
        'MediumEasterBundle2025' => 'A box of sweet goodness to fill your heart and ruin your dental health.',
        'MediumHalloweenBundle2023' => 'Everyone forgot about this crate. It got lost in an abandoned building, but it seems to include a lot of useful specialists and buffs.',
        'MediumHalloweenBundle2024' => 'Oh no, look at this bag! It comes right from a nightmare. Don\'t close your eyes or it will haunt you in your precious dreams.',
        'MediumHalloweenBundle2025' => 'A box made of a ghoulish leather, full of Halloween themed goodness. Hopefully the contents are worth bearing the smell.',
        'MiadTikkiIsland' => 'A beautiful, yet small island, whose population is a bit eccentric. They\'ve asked you for help against the bandits that have been giving them a hard time. Help them, so you can return the coin that was stolen from them, and remove the curse surrounding their otherwise peaceful island.',
        'MineralRabbit' => 'A great great great great great great grandfather of one of your settlers buried some wood to save it from bandits. The wood has turned into coal and you can recover it now.',
        'MiniAdventureBox' => 'A box filled with fast, adventurous experiences. For the settler who doesn\'t have enough time or resources, but wants to keep up with the neighbours.',
        'MiraculousGeneral' => 'She is protected by a divine force. This protection is extended to all that fight by her side.',
        'MortarsLvl1' => 'Mortars may be short-ranged and slow, but the explosive power of their projectiles easily outclasses traditional cannons. Because they are somewhat awkward to handle owing to their high arcs of fire, expert besiegers are in high demand.',
        'MotherlyExplorer' => 'The motherly explorer really cares. In fact, she cares so much, she\'ll always bring back 4 times the loot from all treasure, rarity and artifact searches.',
        'MountainClanColossus' => 'An ancient, massive sculpture carved straight into a mountain by the Mountain Clan. It can produce and store copious amounts of riches.',
        'MountainDemolition_L' => 'A crew of serious-looking gentlemen with an unsettling appetite for fire and destruction. 
These guys have the logistics and mental disorder in place to blow up even the largest mountain and create some much-needed building space on your island.',
        'MountainDemolition_M' => 'His ancestors - although short-lived - have passed him down a great deal of knowledge about the art of wrecking stuff. 
As a professional he is able to blow up bigger mountains than his amateur competitors.',
        'MountainDemolition_S' => 'A former cannoneer who even in retirement follows his passion for all things that go *boom*. 
He can help you gain building space by demolishing certain rock formations and smaller mountains.',
        'MultiplierBuffZone1' => 'People crazy in love will do everything better if they can infuse their love into it.',
        'MultiplierBuffZone2_PremiumFriendBuff1Day' => 'If you ever want to show a friend you care, you could send them flowers... Or, if you really care, you could send them this amazing buff! They\'ll definitely appreciate you for it. Don\'t believe us? Check out the effects your friend will be able to enjoy below!',
        'MultiplierBuffZone2_PremiumFriendBuff1DaySoccer' => 'If you ever want to show a friend how much you care, send them flowers. Or, if you REALLY care, you can send them this amazing buff! They\'ll definitely appreciate you for it. Don\'t believe us? Check out the effects your friend will be able to enjoy below!',
        'MultiplierBuffZone2_PremiumFriendBuff_Christmas' => 'If you ever want to show a friend you care, you could send them flowers... Or, if you really care, you could send them this amazing buff! They\'ll definitely appreciate you for it. Don\'t believe us? Check out the effects your friend will be able to enjoy below!',
        'MummifiedGeologist' => 'After several years of being just an ordinary geologist without any peculiarities, he made the mistake of going too far into one of the ancient pharaohs’ tombs. Needless to say, he got cursed, and has had to live his geologist’s life as an undead mummy ever since.',
        'MysteryBoxAdventure' => 'A mysterious box, with unknown inventory. While holding it you get the impulse to travel far away looking for adventures.',
        'MysteryBoxBlackKnights' => 'Open the Mystery Box to receive a reward',
        'NarcissisticGeneral' => 'A general who suffers from a serious case of "excessive personality". She is good at what she does, but her unhealthy rivalry with the Gemini generals makes her insufferable to work with.',
        'NibLvl1' => 'For extensive writing exercises you will need a fair amount of these. Don\'t be stingy here - developed handwriting requires some effort. And remember to keep your wrist relaxed.',
        'NordsResidence' => 'A classic residence of the nords.',
        'NormalResourceBox' => 'A huge box, containing common resource items. It is solid and looks inviting. Seems like a good deal.',
        'NutcrackerGeneral' => 'Don\'t be fooled by the fact that he\'s made from wood! He uses this condition to his advantage - after all, wood is tougher than skin.',
        'OffshoreLighthouse' => 'A reliable lighthouse on a tiny island. During the day, the keeper catches fish as a pastime and sells the surplus at the local market.',
        'OilRefinery' => 'Your settlers have worked hard, and succeeded in understanding the process of refining oil, enabling several new options for its production. From now on, you\'ll even be able to make oil out of fish! Can you imagine? The only thing you’ll need to start producing oil is a teensy-weensy single unit of oil itself. If you haven’t had access to oil yet, why not ask a friend or guild member, or go to the trade market? Now, everyone can produce oil!',
        'Oillvl1' => 'Oil for all your needs. Allows your productions to reach their highest efficiency.',
        'OrePackage' => 'A nice compilation of basic ores to speed up production.',
        'Ostereierbaum' => 'A tree with eggs on it? What’s next? A steak tree? Cows made out of lettuce?',
        'OutdoorCanteen' => 'Here your troops have the opportunity to fill their bellies with a delicious meal before setting out on adventures. You know what they say: "an army marches on its stomach".',
        'OutdoorCanteenAid' => 'A decoration building that reduces the Outdoor Canteen\'s cooldown and increases the Smokehouse\'s production speed.',
        'PalmTreeDeco01' => 'A very beautiful palm tree, which can be placed on your island to prettify it.',
        'PalmTreeDeco02' => 'A very beautiful palm tree, which can be placed on your island to prettify it.',
        'PalmTreeDeco03' => 'A very beautiful palm tree, which can be placed on your island to prettify it.',
        'PermanentBuildQueueSlot' => 'Allows the particularly busy master builder to issue more building orders simultaneously. Your build queue will be extended by one additional slot.',
        'PirateExplorer' => 'A scallywag obsessed with finding treasure and adventure.',
        'PlanksLvl1' => 'Essential for the ambitious builder - a bountiful package of handy planks.',
        'PlanksLvl2' => 'After the refurbishment of all your residences, the good old wooden floor was replaced by a stone floor. So now there\'s a huge amount of planks in good merchantable quality and condition looking for a new owner. Can you find them a new home?',
        'PlatinumOreKnowledge1' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the secrets of working platinum.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a manuscript.',
        'PlatinumOreKnowledge2' => 'Notes recovered from distant lands, uncovering the closely guarded secrets of working platinum.
Can be exchanged at the Mayor\'s house for a tome.',
        'PlatinumOreLv1' => 'Platinum is a very rare metal. It can only be obtained in an exotic area.',
        'PlatinumSwordsLvl1' => 'Considering the rarity of platinum, it comes as no surprise that only the best swords for the most elite swordsmen are forged from it. Their durability is outstanding, and a single sword will not blunt for a lifetime.',
        'PlayerCavExpeditionCampLvl03' => 'A large Cavalry camp to boost the defences of your claimed colonies. Can be placed when building up a colony\'s defences. Troops not included.',
        'PlayerMeleeExpeditionCampLvl03' => 'A large Melee camp meant to boost the defences of your claimed colonies. Can be placed when building up a colony\'s defences. Troops not included.',
        'PlayerRangedExpeditioncampLvl03' => 'A large Ranged camp meant to boost the defences of your claimed colonies. Can be placed when building up a colony\'s defences. Troops not included.',
        'PohutukawaTree' => 'A celebrative decoration from a different culture.',
        'PopulationLvl1' => 'A foreign settler family is looking for a new home. Maybe you can convince them to stay in your kingdom... for a price.',
        'PopulationLvl2' => 'A group of bandits has raided a neighbouring village. Now the inhabitants want to come to your settlement, but you will need money to feed them.',
        'PopulationLvl3' => 'These poor refugees need a place to stay and would be happy if you would give them a chance. Of course, they would agree to help you with your economy and your military in return.',
        'PremiumAccount1DayBlackKnights' => 'With this item you can add 1 day to your premium time. Active premium time gives you multiple benefits. These benefits will be granted as soon as the item is used in the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime180Days' => 'With this item you can add 180 days to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime1Day' => 'With this item you can add 1 day to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime30Days' => 'With this item you can add 30 days to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime360Days' => 'With this item you can add 360 days to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime3Days' => 'With this item you can add 3 days to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PremiumTime7Days' => 'With this item you can add 7 days to your Premium time. Active Premium Time gives you multiple benefits. These will be granted as soon as the item is used from the star menu.',
        'PrincessZoeExplorer' => 'Growing up as a princess taught her diplomatic skills, and gave her the charisma to always get that little extra.',
        'PrintPress' => 'In this print press workshop, a team of skilled Settlers works diligently to operate the machines and produce high-quality prints. These fellows are responsible for keeping everyone’s literary and gossip needs met.',
        'ProductionBoostLvl1' => 'This basket is filled with the most exotic fruit from all over the world. You can marvel at the numerous different tastes, and forget all your stress. With this fruit your workers just can\'t stop working.',
        'ProductionBoostLvl10' => 'A yummy feast that can be given to workers in your friend\'s workyards, or your own. This increases production for a certain amount of time.',
        'ProductionBoostLvl2' => 'Rumours talk of a new kind of drink that has made its way into the kingdom. It is said that anyone who drinks it can work non-stop for 24 hours. You might want to consider this...',
        'ProductionBoostLvl3' => 'Some strange labourers want to work in your factories. They reek, and speaking is not their strong suit, but they work fast and need no sleep.',
        'ProductionBoostLvl4' => 'A tasty looking roasted duck cooked by the guild\'s chef himself!

You can give this amazing meal to your settlers, and they will work harder! You can also offer the meal to your friends!',
        'ProductionBoostLvl5' => 'Cooked using the secret recipe of Piero, the King\'s personal world famous chef, this steaming bowl of pasta will have your whole island begging for more!

You can give this amazing meal to your settlers, and they will work harder! You can also offer the meal to your friends!',
        'ProductionBoostLvl6' => 'Using a secret technique, this friendly scarecrow will help you with the harvest of wheatfields!

You can give this amazing scarecrow to your farmers! Also, you can offer the scarecrow to your friends too!',
        'ProductionBoostLvl7' => 'During an archeological trip, one of our settlers found a brand new and rather special mining cart. The Miners Union decided to make some more and call them "Gold Fever". They\'re going to use the new carts so they can speed up the gold mining process.

You can give Gold Fever to your miners! You can also offer it to your friends!',
        'ProductionBoostLvl8' => 'Fish platters can be given to workers in your friend\'s workyards, or your own. This increases production for a certain amount of time.',
        'ProductionBoostLvl9' => 'Can be given to workers in your friend\'s workyards, or your own. This increases production for a certain amount of time.',
        'ProductivityBuffEW1' => 'Magic Beans may have amazing properties, but they are still "beans"! When boiled, they turn into a liquid whose energizing properties extend beyond living beings and into inanimate objects. Using it on a huge building full of machinery, like the Epic Workyard, seems the smart thing to do.',
        'ProductivityBuffEW2' => 'Studying the cultists\' wicked rituals has yielded some unexpected benefits. This carefully studied chant has proven to increase your epic worker\'s focus threefold.',
        'ProductivityBuffEW3' => 'The experience of long, hard fights against the Jötnar will help your workers boost their productivity.',
        'ProductivityBuffEWBalloonsLv2' => 'Many famous bakers were needed to get this cake done. It is a must have for any celebration in the Festival Hall.',
        'ProductivityBuffLvl12' => 'No-one knows where it comes from - but it certainly boosts productivity!',
        'ProductivityBuffLvl22' => 'Oils machinery to prevent gears from grinding and ensure peak production',
        'ProductivityBuffLvl25' => 'A refined and exotic baker that is willing to lend a hand to improve your bakeries with his methods.',
        'ProductivityBuffLvl27' => 'He may have no head, but this man knows his way around his horses! While he\'s usually somewhat less than co-operative, he\'s actually surprisingly willing to help tend to our horses.',
        'ProductivityBuffLvl28' => 'The sticky and half-molten sweets serve as an inspiration to all smelters... or so they claim. They probably just have a sweet tooth.',
        'ProductivityBuffZoneEW_WitchesFamiliars' => 'These are no ordinary pets. When their owners lend them some of their power, they become very inciting...',
        'Prospector' => 'A workshop that thoroughly inspects mined rocks in search of trace amounts of precious metals and minerals.',
        'ProvisionerBuffLvl3' => 'Sweets from Oriental lands in the south. They\'re sure to boost the productivity of your provisioners.',
        'ProvisionerBuffLvl300' => 'Is your weapon production a bit too slow, even though you\'re using all the right materials? Give your productivity a boost with longer working hours in the combat armoury.',
        'ProvisionerBuffLvl301' => 'Are your settlers tired of producing everything by hand? Give them some mechanical help by boosting the assembly lines of the armoury, and you\'ll increase production a lot.',
        'ProvisionerBuffLvlGuildFestGrounds1' => 'Show your support for your guild by letting out a loud cheer!',
        'ProvisionerBuffLvlGuildFestGrounds2' => 'Show your support for your guild by letting out a deafening cheer!',
        'PumpkinFieldDeco' => 'Why wait for Halloween to have your island populated by pumpkin cemeteries? The ever-lasting elegance of pumpkin breeding can be enjoyed all year round with this replica of the building. Note: This building does not produce any pumpkins!',
        'PumpkinMansion' => 'Often finding itself as the target trick-or-treaters, the pumpkin mansion is ready to receive the Halloween spirit with copious amounts of candy.',
        'QuestStart_ANewStone' => 'A young boy was playing on the beach and found a very beautiful stone. But what kind of stone is it? And is it valuable?',
        'QuestStart_Harbour' => 'Settlers from the continent had to flee to the far-away Tavos archipelago to start a new life there. But they need more settlers to assist them on their epic journey.',
        'QuestStart_MysteriousCoin' => 'For some reason holding it makes you feel uneasy.',
        'QuestStart_OreRefinery' => 'An epic quest to uncover the secrets of metalworking from distant civilizations.',
        'QuestStart_SavetheDeers' => 'The deer population is shrinking! You\'ll need to figure out what\'s causing it, and find some way of restoring the natural balance. Find the source of the problem, and help the deers to recover.',
        'QuestStart_SilkCat' => 'This leather collar looks very expensive. It appears someone has attached a message to it?',
        'QuestStart_TheLittlePanda' => 'He\'s frightened and malnourished.',
        'QuestStart_WeddingInvitation' => 'You recognize the crest of a neighbouring kingdom.',
        'QuestStart_WolfPuppy' => 'A young girl was playing in the forest and found a little, wounded puppy. Help her nurse the puppy back to health!',
        'RabbitFood' => 'Everyone knows that rabbit food is an aphrodisiac. This makes it ideal for increasing the population.',
        'RabbitsLuckCharm' => 'If you have a rabbit lucky charm in your workyard, nothing will break and no workers will be injured.',
        'RangerHut' => 'A high vantage point that allows rangers to take care of the local fauna.',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl1' => 'This improved drill plan includes a new set of orders ("Faster!, Higher!, More!"), a mad drill sergeant and a highly motivating penalty system. Your recruits will be trained in a jiffy!',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl2' => 'A certain Mr. Myers has offered to train your army. He is supposed to get top performance from recruits. You\'ll have to hire him soon though, as he says he\'ll only be in the neighbourhood for Halloween.',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl3' => 'You need to train many new units but you cannot stay in your barrack the whole time? Let your units make some overtime and they will be ready in no time.',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl301' => 'Do you have too many settlers signing up to join your army? Using these new training techniques in the combat academy will make them get through training faster.

Boot camp',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl4' => 'A man in strange garments who calls himself Nash Williams has shown up in our lands. Madly babbling about the threat of some dark army, he offers to aid in the training of your troops. If you want, you\'ll have to hire him soon, because he\'ll be leaving to find some tome after Halloween.',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl5' => 'A creepy fellow who knows how to serve with complete devotion. Your troops could probably learn a lot from him.',
        'RecruitingBuffLvl9' => 'Hugs & kisses are reminders for every soldier that there\'s always someone waiting for them.',
        'RecruitingBuffZoneLvl3' => 'Have you heard about the tradition of egg rolling? It\'s a game that children play all over the world at Easter time.
It\'s a little silly, but our military instructors have found it to make excellent and engaging training for your troops!',
        'RedNoseResourceLvl1' => 'Want to contribute more to the donation campaign? This basket full of red noses should do the trick.',
        'RedNoseResourceLvl2' => 'Want to contribute more to the donation campaign? This basket full of red noses should do the trick.',
        'RefillMysteryBox' => 'A nice, big collection of different deposit refills, including gold ore and universal refills.',
        'RenovationPackFlowerBlossoms' => 'A bundle containing a set of Flower Blossoms building skins.',
        'RenovationPackFlowerBlossomsResidenceBlue' => 'A bundle containing a set of blue Flower Blossoms residence skins.',
        'RenovationPackFlowerBlossomsResidenceGreen' => 'A bundle containing a set of green Flower Blossoms Residence skins.',
        'RenovationPackFlowerBlossomsStorehouseBlue' => 'A bundle containing a set of blue Flower Blossoms storehouse skins.',
        'RenovationPackFlowerBlossomsStorehouseGreen' => 'A bundle containing a set of green Flower Blossoms storehouse skins.',
        'RenovationPackSpiritJourney' => 'A bundle containing a set of Spirit Journey building skins.',
        'RenovationPackSpiritJourneyResidence' => 'A bundle containing a set of Spirit Journey residence building skins.',
        'ResoluteGeneral' => 'A veteran of countless epic battles, he is adept at leading elite groups of highly trained infantry solders. He employs a defensive formation that few have been able to even make so much as a dent in.',
        'ResourceCodex' => 'Used to train your specialists\' gold skills.',
        'ResourceManiscript' => 'Used to train your specialists\' bronze skills.',
        'ResourceTome' => 'Used to train your specialists\' silver skills.',
        'RetirementHome' => 'A buff producer that uses Wool to make Grandma\'s Hand-Knitted Christmas Sock, which is full of gifts.',
        'RetirementHomeAid' => 'A mailbox that goes straight to Santa. Children often visit them after visiting their grand parents.',
        'RevealCollectiblesBuff01' => 'If you have trouble finding that elusive rare collectible that keeps popping-up on your island, some magical creatures can help make things easier.',
        'RevealCollectiblesBuff02' => 'If you have trouble finding the elusive, rare collectibles that are hidden in far away lands, these magical creatures can offer their help.',
        'RinaTheExplorer' => 'Rina is a very passionate explorer, and loves to analyze and collect everything on her journeys. She is very fast, and her only goal has always been to be on adventures.',
        'RomanticExplorer' => 'The romantic explorer loves to go on long treasure searches - but once abroad, he always gets distracted chasing love! While that means he takes twice as long to return, the good news is he\'ll bring back 12 times the rewards.',
        'RomanticRestaurant' => 'Everyone gets hungry just by looking at these delicious meals. There’s something to eat for everyone, and it\'s a beautiful place to meet your favorite person in the world!',
        'RoseArbor' => 'Every rose garden needs an arbor with blooming roses.',
        'RoseTrellis' => 'With this beautiful rose trellis, it\'s possible to create beautiful parks for lovers!',
        'RosyIronMine' => 'This iron mine is not just covered in roses - it’s also very useful! The roses cause this special mine to produce not the ore, but the smelted bar instead! Incredible!',
        'RosyStorage' => 'It\'s just an ordinary storehouse, but look at these beautiful roses. The beauty of the roses, and their soothing smell should be reason enough to have this beautiful storehouse in the village.',
        'RoyalExplorer' => 'The Royal Explorer rules. He\'s incredibly quick, and sometimes even finds tokens during adventure searches, which he loves to collect - but he\'ll still always hand them over to you. Eventually.',
        'S4Barracks' => 'Newer is not always better. These traditional techniques for training out in the fields have been proven to increase soldiers\' capabilities for moving and fighting with armor.',
        'S4Lazaret' => 'Sometimes, the old recipes outshine the new ones. By mixing and preparing some basic materials, and adding a little extra sauce, you can create something truly special. No-one even thought it was possible, but now medipacks can be produced just like in the old days.',
        'S4MayanStorehouse' => 'A very spacious Mayan dwelling from a bygone era, now repurposed for storage.',
        'S4MayanToolmaker' => 'A Mayan toolsmith structure from a bygone era. Don\'t be fooled by its ancient looks - techniques passed down through the generations make it remarkably effective.',
        'S4RomanFisherman' => 'An ancient Roman fishing vessel that now serves as an expert fisherman’s dwelling. It might look improvised, but it is remarkably effective.',
        'S4RomanResidence' => 'Roman architectured housing from a well-remembered era.',
        'S4ThatchedCottage' => 'Nostalgia overwhelmed a builder when he found a blueprint of this cozy and roomy country house. He just had to build it.',
        'SalpeterLvl1' => 'This supply of saltpetre was artificially created by distinguished alchemists. You have very high expectations for its purity, and the samples do not disappoint.',
        'SantaGeneral' => 'It\'s Santa himself! It may not be in his nature to fight, but he can transport your army around the world in the blink of an eye. He is known to make people wait between his random acts of kindness, though.',
        'SausageLvl1' => 'A diligent settler has cooked some sausages for your busy workers. In return, she asks only for a little money to pay for the source materials.',
        'SausageLvl2' => '500 delicious sausages in one insanely long chain! Just think of all the buffs these could be used for!',
        'ScaredExplorer' => 'Incredibly fearful and startled by the faintest of noises, he takes four times as long to complete searches. On the plus side, he\'ll also bring back four times the treasure on treasure searches, and often some omniseeds, too. And that’s not all: thanks to his particularly sensitive nature, he always has a small chance of finding something extraordinary like crystals, premium time items or precious books. Artifact, rarity and adventure searches are excluded from all loot bonuses.',
        'ScenarioBundle1' => 'An impressive bundle to help any and all settlers.',
        'ScenarioBundle2' => 'An awesome and exclusive Scenario Adventure Season bundle.',
        'ScenarioBundle3' => 'Get yourself some refillers, resources and flaming arrows with this time-limited bundle.',
        'Settlers2HQDeco' => 'Increases the population limit.
Functions as a storehouse entry point for production buildings.',
        'SettlersHQ' => 'The Settlers Headquarters, based on the old design from The Settlers 2',
        'ShamanBundle' => 'Make preparations for the end of the world with this time-limited and event-exclusive bundle.',
        'ShopBookbinderBuffLvl2' => 'This resin seems a bit gooey but don\'t let it fool you! It\'s every bit as effective as it is gooey!',
        'ShopIslandDeed_FreeIsland' => 'A Sector Deed. Legitimate and signed by a renowned notary. It allows you to claim a far away sector for your settlement.',
        'ShopIslandDeed_PayIsland' => 'An island ownership deed. The king himself signed it for you, and wrote on the letter\'s foot: "I hope this deed provides you with the building space and deposits you need". Use it on an independent island to claim it for yourself.',
        'ShopProductivityAreaBuffLvl2' => 'Delicious dates, which encourage everyone to do their very best work.',
        'ShopProductivityBuffLvl16' => 'Legends say that the ancient Mayas left this buff for the one true hero, deemed worthy of carrying it. So, make good use of it!',
        'ShopRecoverGeneral' => 'A buff which can help a defeated general to instantly recover. Guaranteed without side effects!',
        'ShopRetailBox2General' => 'A very nice general, who almost cares as much for the 220 units he can carry as he does for his looks.',
        'ShopRetailBoxGeneral' => 'Basically a battle hardened general, but with a veeeery big... helmet!',
        'Shop_AnimalBuff_blackknights' => 'The order of The Black Knights is recruiting. Help them conquer the world.',
        'Shop_AnimalBuff_reindeer' => 'Baskets full of reindeer food. With this many, we can easily populate the island with reindeers for a week.',
        'Shop_AnimalBuff_unicorn' => 'A potion that is said to make you see the world through the eyes of a child. This sense of wonder may attract fantastic creatures whose existence you grew up to doubt.',
        'ShoplanternRamadan' => 'A very beautiful lantern, fit for Ramadan.',
        'SiegeWorkshop' => 'Invest resources to produce buffs that can strike your enemies before they can see you.',
        'SimplePaperLvl1' => 'A good book can start with just a few rough scribbles on a napkin. To ensure your creatives always have said napkin on them, you should provide them with some Simple Paper.',
        'Skyscraper_Residence_Halloween' => 'A creepy variant of the wondrous residence. A must-have for enthusiasts of scary times. 
Instead of tokens, this variant will require pumpkins as upgrade costs.',
        'Skyscraper_Residence_Valentines' => 'The perfect place to live for any settlers that celebrate love and friendship. Snuggle together and enjoy the view from the most romantic of residences.',
        'Skyscraper_Residence_Xmas' => 'A freezing bastion against the winter cold. Could someone please call a heating engineer?
This magnificent and unique winter residence is a must under every Christmas Tree. Requires 4,500 presents to fully upgrade this beauty!',
        'SmallDefBuild' => 'Contains a minimum of 2 random strongholds. Has an additional chance of getting a random third fortified camp (lvl 2).',
        'SmallEasterBundle2024' => 'It\'s just a bag, but someone took it to the Holi Festival and it got painted in some vibrant colors! Opening it does not just make your hands painted, but also reveals some interesting buildings and buffs.',
        'SmallEasterBundle2025' => 'A bag of sweet goodness to fill your heart and ruin your dental health.',
        'SmallHalloweenBundle2023' => 'This dusty bag doesn\'t look promising, but removing the dust reveals some spooky buildings and buffs.',
        'SmallHalloweenBundle2024' => 'Oh no, look at this bag! It comes right from a nightmare. Don\'t close your eyes or it will haunt you in your precious dreams.',
        'SmallHalloweenBundle2025' => 'A bag made of a ghoulish leather, full of Halloween themed goodness. Hopefully the contents are worth bearing the smell.',
        'Smokehouse' => 'A smokery in the style of the Nords. Smokes fish to produce a tasty buff.',
        'Smokehouse_Mini' => 'This tribute honours the island\'s master smokers. Produces 1 Smoked Fish Steak every day.',
        'Snowglobe' => 'This giant globe and its ever-swirling snow capture the Christmas spirit all year long. Everyone that comes close to it is filled with warm feelings of wonder and joy.',
        'SnowyExplorer' => 'When he\'s not passing the time by admiring the Gingerbread House, this explorer really likes going on treasure hunts. In fact, there’s only one thing he likes more - and that\'s presents. He\'ll always bring home 4 times the amount of event resources during events.',
        'SnowyExplorerGems' => 'When he\'s not passing the time by admiring the Gingerbread House, this explorer really likes going on treasure hunts. In fact, there’s only one thing he likes more - and that\'s presents. He\'ll always bring home 4 times the amount of event resources during events.',
        'Soccer2019Explorer' => 'Eager to go on her next adventure, her pace is unrivaled.',
        'SootyGeologist' => 'He has a very peculiar relationship with deep earth minerals. This fellow is able to tell the composition of dirt by just tasting it.',
        'SophisticatedGeologist' => 'The Sophisticated Geologist is - surprise! - sophisticated. Sophisticated… and insanely fast. In fact, we’ve never seen a geologist so fast.',
        'SpecialistBuff' => 'This energy bar gives your specialists the power they need to achieve even the most difficult tasks in next to no time.',
        'SpeedUpPopulationGrowth' => 'Prepared by the local witch, this potion will increase population growth significantly. It is nothing but coloured water, but the placebo effect actually works.',
        'SpeedUpPopulationGrowth2' => 'Shrouded in mystery, this magnificent cheese sandwich has a very special effect on settlers who eat it...',
        'SpeedUpPopulationGrowth5' => 'A famous writer has come to your city to sign his latest book, "Chronicles of a Misunderstood Erudite". Fans from all around will surely come to this event!',
        'SplitCity' => 'A city split by a landslide encounters strange evil-doers and is in dire straits. Will you be able to help them?',
        'SplitCityFall' => 'For a decade, all kinds of evil foes have swarmed into the small town of Kalijenorod all year round. The colder it gets, the nastier the enemies become. 
Even during fall, you can see the immense threat to the people. It\'s unthinkable that children still live there, and families refuse to leave their home.
The onslaught seems to be connected to the disruption that took place a decade ago.
But what is behind this bane?',
        'SpookyBronzeMine' => 'Ghosts of deceased settlers and soldiers keep appearing after you defeat their nemeses, freeing them of their earthly burdens. But instead of haunting the living, it turns out these are actually very friendly spirits, who want to help you in your efforts to conquer the evildoers. As they\'re spirits, they can\'t fight your battles for you - but they can help you produce bronze really quickly! Nobody really knows how the ghosts do it - so just imagine how hard it was for Sonya to convince everybody else that this would work out!',
        'SpringBundle1' => '3 amazing explorers in one neat bundle! Including books to get them ready asap!',
        'SpringBundle10' => 'Sshhh!!! Don\'t tell anyone you found me!
If you absolutely have to, just say something like "Have you found the secret package?" Let\'s play some hide and seek, OK?',
        'SpringBundle2' => 'A whole water town in one bundle! All 5 water buildings in one pack just for you! Including tokens for some upgrades!',
        'SpringBundle3' => 'Can\'t decide which champion you like the most? Why not get all 3 of them at once for the price of 2?!',
        'SpringBundle4' => 'Are your military endeavors lacking a little something? This is it!',
        'SpringBundle5' => 'Looking for something more extravagant? Check out this utility bundle!',
        'SpringBundle6' => 'All the endless mine, in one neat bundle. With a bonus geologist who was stuck in one of the mines!',
        'SpringBundle7' => 'Fancy some improvements?',
        'SpringBundle8' => 'Who doesn\'t like to feel special? Convert coins into something even shinier!',
        'SpringBundle9' => 'Oh, what\'s this? For a boat full of brew, someone\'s willing to provide extra coal, water and storage space...',
        'SpringPark' => 'A pretty park that celebrates the beauty of spring. A perfect place for holding seasonal festivals!',
        'StargazingGeologist' => 'A star obsessed Geologist. He dreams of studying rare earths that fall from the sky. This obsession grants him the abilty to finding Star Shards.',
        'StarterPack' => 'This special offer can only be bought once!
It includes workers and a nice stock of building materials. This is all you need to get a head start in developing your city.',
        'SteelSwordsLvl1' => 'Standard-issue military swords. Forged from high-quality steel, these reliable blades will please every soldier trained in their use.',
        'StoneColdGeologist' => 'I\'ll be honest with you - this man scares me a bit. His single-mindedness towards geology makes him appear almost mechanical. 
But you can\'t argue with results.',
        'StoneCubes' => 'The Miner\'s union has announced it has found a new way to mine stone. Using a special technique, stone is mined in cube shapes, resulting a better yield. They have decided to sell the technique to whomever wants to use it.',
        'StoneDepot' => 'Here\'s where all sorts of rocky goods are processed.',
        'StoneLvl1' => 'High quality stones. Carved from a rock solid mountain with diligence and affection.',
        'StoneLvl2' => 'Not long ago, a horrible earthquake brought fear and trepidation to all your inhabitants. Maybe you could still look for the silver lining in this act of God.',
        'StoneRefillGuild' => 'These stone cubes are special. They can be used on stone deposits to refill them. Awesome!',
        'StorageBasket' => 'A special storehouse that matches the Easter Basket Residence',
        'Stronghold' => 'Let your troops participate in harsh environmental training with the mountain clan.',
        'SummerBoosterBundle' => 'A time-limited, exclusive summer event bundle designed to give you a little boost.',
        'SummerBundle1' => 'A time-limited exclusive summer event bundle to help all settlers out there.',
        'SummerBundle2' => 'A time-limited exclusive summer event bundle to help all settlers out there. Includes the all-new, dark roofed warehouse.',
        'SummerBundle2025_Large' => 'A sunblasted chest containing wonderful goodies',
        'SummerBundle2025_Medium' => 'A sunblasted box containing wonderful goodies',
        'SummerBundle2025_Small' => 'A sunblasted bag containing wonderful goodies.',
        'SummerBundle2026_Large' => 'A large bundle, as refreshing as a summer breeze.',
        'SummerBundle2026_Medium' => 'A medium bundle, as refreshing as a summer breeze.',
